window.AKK_FORENSIC_PSYCHOLOGICAL_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_FORENSIC_PSYCHOLOGICAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: The Vanished: The Last Will","paragraphs":["Fang Rui and his team immediately rushed to the rental apartment where Liu Yaying had attempted suicide.","The apartment was in an urban village, with very poor conditions. It was an illegally converted room, containing a small kitchen, bathroom, and balcony all crammed into one space. Each area was extremely tiny, with very poor lighting.","Given Liu Yaying's current income, she shouldn't have been living in such a place.","\"She rented this place a couple of days ago,\" Zhang said. \"When she first graduated, she lived here with Su Momo for a while. After she became famous, she moved out, but Su Momo lived here for over three years.\"","Liu Yaying had attempted suicide in the bathroom. There was a paper cutter on the floor, with bright red blood slowly flowing across the yellowed white tiles, eventually draining into the floor drain.","Mu Mian examined the suicide scene and found nothing unusual. She collected blood samples from the floor, intending to compare them with Su Momo's.","Fang Rui discovered a stack of money and a bank card on the desk, with a suicide note underneath.","The handwriting was messy, with many tear stains visible:","[I don't know who will find this note, but please hand it over to the police when you do. The cash on the table is your reward for helping. I committed suicide. My life was too painful. I caused the death of my best friend Su Momo. I'm guilty. I killed her, and I should pay for her life with mine.","I have nothing left. There's 100,000 yuan in this bank account. The PIN is the last six digits of Momo's ID number. Please ask the police to donate this money to charity in Su Momo's name, to accumulate some good karma for her. She was such a good person; she deserves good things in return.","Don't notify my family to claim my body. Even if you do, they won't come for me. After I'm cremated, my ashes can be thrown anywhere, even in a trash can. I don't care. A rotten person like me deserves to go to hell and die a miserable death.]","After reading it, Zhang exclaimed, \"Boss, Liu Yaying says Su Momo is dead. How does she know for sure? Does she know where Su Momo's body is?\"","\"I think she might have seen the news and assumed Su Momo died from slitting her wrists. Liu Yaying probably feels that Su Momo committed suicide because her affair with Liang Guangyu was exposed, which pushed Su Momo over the edge,\" Fang Rui analyzed.","Fang Rui increasingly felt that Su Momo might not be dead.","So what exactly was she trying to do?","And could she have an accomplice?","Fang Rui thought of Qi Fang. Zhang had previously suspected her because of the bubble tea incident, but surveillance footage near the tea shop showed her buying tea after 4 PM, and the cake shop's cameras also showed her buying a cake there just before 4 PM.","Although Fang Rui suspected Qi Fang was behind the cursed doll incident, he had no evidence.","Fang Rui found Liu Yaying's phone on the desk.","Li cracked her phone's lock screen password.","Fang Rui went through her phone and found she didn't seem to have many friends. Her contacts list was short, and there were only brief conversations in her chat history. Judging from the timestamps, she probably hadn't cleared her chat history.","A contact labeled \"Bugu's New Owner Miss Zhang\" caught Fang Rui's attention.","Miss Zhang's profile picture was a selfie of a young woman. Her last message to Liu Yaying read: Liar! You promised to give me the puppy, but then you took it back. You big liar!","Liu Yaying had replied: What's wrong? I didn't take Bugu back!","The other party had already deleted Liu Yaying, and a red exclamation mark appeared in the chat box.","Fang Rui scrolled back through their chat history.","The gist of their conversation was that Liu Yaying planned to give the spotted dog to Miss Zhang, explaining that the dog's owner was allergic to dog hair. Miss Zhang expressed her love for the puppy and promised to take good care of it. They reached an agreement, and Liu Yaying gave the puppy to Miss Zhang.","They continued to stay in touch, mostly discussing how to care for the dog. Miss Zhang often sent photos of the dog to Liu Yaying.","The day before the scary doll was found in Su Momo's room, Miss Zhang accused Liu Yaying of taking the puppy back.","After reading the chat logs, Li analyzed, \"Could it be that Qi Fang took the dog back, killed it, and then made the cursed doll to frame Liu Yaying?\"","\"It's possible.\"","In the chat history, Miss Zhang had mentioned her home address. Liu Yaying had personally delivered the puppy and its belongings to her home.","Fang Rui and Zhang found the place, a middle-class residential complex. After learning of their purpose, Miss Zhang said, \"A young woman came to take the dog back. She looked fierce and said she was the dog's owner. She knew the dog's name and all its information. I had no choice but to return the dog.\"","\"Did the woman have any distinguishing features?\"","\"Features? Her appearance was quite ordinary... she had some freckles on her face,\" the girl recalled. \"She was wearing a gray down jacket at the time, nothing special.\"","\"Was it her?\" Fang Rui showed her a photo of Qi Fang.","\"Yes, that's her! She was so fierce at the time, saying how could I steal someone else's beloved dog. My goodness, I was so wronged. It was Miss Liu who told me the dog's owner was allergic to dog hair and couldn't keep it, so she gave it to me. But then she scolded me.\"","\"Alright, thank you for your cooperation!\"","After leaving Miss Zhang's home, Zhang analyzed, \"It seems Qi Fang is highly suspicious. She stole the dog, made the cursed doll, and pushed Liu Yaying out. Now Liu Yaying has attempted suicide – could Qi Fang be behind this too? Maybe Liu Yaying found out something, so Qi Fang had to silence her.\"","\"If she were the culprit, shouldn't she have waited until Liu Yaying was dead before leaving?\" Fang Rui countered. \"And she would have taken Liu Yaying's phone with her.\"","\"That's true!\"","Good news came from the hospital: after several hours of emergency treatment, Liu Yaying was out of danger, but she was still in a deep coma and unable to assist with the police investigation.","Fang Rui decided to adjust the direction of the investigation.","They had previously assumed that Su Momo was seriously injured and kidnapped, so when reviewing surveillance footage, they focused on people carrying heavy objects.","But if Su Momo wasn't injured and could move freely, she could easily evade detection by changing clothes and disguising herself as an extra or backup dancer. The camera at the exit only captured people's backs, not their faces.","\"Zhang, go to the TV station and investigate if any costumes for extras or dancers went missing on the day of the incident. Find out what style of clothes were lost.\"","\"Got it.\"","The police had opened a case to investigate Liang Guangyu's involvement in prostitution. With relevant evidence in hand, they had detained him.","#LiangGuangyuEarnsSilverHandcuffs# once again topped the trending list.","Liang Guangyu's reputation was thoroughly ruined."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: The Vanished: Disappeared Out of Thin Air","paragraphs":["The person in charge of the TV station investigated the costume situation of each program group and temporarily found no cases of missing costumes.","The rehearsal started at 3 PM, so during the time period when Su Momo disappeared, most of the people who left the makeup area were wearing performance costumes. The remaining few in civilian clothes were artist assistants and makeup artists. The police have already found and verified the identities of all relevant personnel.","There were many backup dancers wearing performance costumes, so it wasn't possible to accurately verify their identities. However, they all left in an orderly manner by group and knew each other, and so far no suspicious individuals have been found.","The makeup area is an enclosed space with only one entrance and exit, and everyone must pass through the corridor with surveillance cameras.","According to the police investigation, the person who entered around 3:30 PM was indeed Su Momo, as confirmed by her bodyguard and assistant. After the incident, the police immediately searched the entire makeup area but did not find Su Momo or her body.","She seemed to have vanished into thin air in that area.","At this moment, Su Momo's agent Sun Qin called to urge progress on the case: \"Officer, what are your investigation results? You need to tell us whether Su Momo is dead or alive. Now many of our advertisers and business partners are coming to us wanting to terminate contracts. A TV drama that was already negotiated also wants to replace Su Momo. You must give me definitive information as soon as possible so I can carry out further work.\"","\"We will investigate as quickly as possible.\"","\"What do you mean 'as quickly as possible'? It's been so many days, and you can't even figure out if Su Momo is dead or alive. Your work efficiency is too poor! Please take this seriously and give us results quickly.\"","\"...\"","Clearly, Su Momo's disappearance had already seriously impacted her career.","\"Boss, if Su Momo did this to get revenge on her ex-boyfriend, she's already achieved her goal, so why hasn't she reappeared? Could she really have been killed?\" Zhang voiced everyone's doubts.","Fang Rui also found it strange. If Su Momo didn't reappear soon, her entertainment career would truly be over.","Could it be that she really didn't care about her career anymore?","Fang Rui reviewed the surveillance video again.","He discovered that Liu Yaying entered the makeup area around 3:30 PM, almost following right behind Su Momo. Then she left that corridor at about 4:05 PM.","At around 4:10 PM, someone wearing Qi Fang's clothes entered the makeup area carrying bubble tea, but in less than a minute, she ran out empty-handed, and her back was caught on the corridor's surveillance camera. She was walking very hurriedly.","Fang Rui watched it many times, and judging from the figure and attire, this person did indeed appear to be Qi Fang.","Bored with nothing to do, Mu Mian came to keep Fang Rui company while watching the surveillance videos.","\"Fang Rui, I'm very good at spot-the-difference games. Let me help you look,\" said Mu Mian, with a SpongeBob SquarePants bandage on her head.","Fang Rui looked up and saw the yellow sponge grinning stupidly at him.","Fang Rui gave his seat to Mu Mian.","Mu Mian first watched the video of Su Momo and Qi Fang entering the corridor, then watched the segment of Qi Fang leaving alone.","At first, Mu Mian didn't notice any differences between the two Qi Fangs. Their clothing, appearance, and even walking posture were almost identical. Even their unconscious small movements were the same, such as both instinctively avoiding stepping on the mandala patterns on the floor tiles.","But suddenly Mu Mian noticed that the Qi Fang who was leaving had a scar on her right wrist.","\"Fang Rui, does Qi Fang also have a cut on her right wrist?\"","Fang Rui thought for a moment, not quite sure: \"I don't think so.\"","\"Su Momo has one on her right wrist, you know,\" Mu Mian reminded softly.","Fang Rui opened the surveillance videos from the bubble tea shop and cake shop again.","The bubble tea shop's surveillance caught Qi Fang buying bubble tea there around 4:05 PM. The camera only captured her side profile and body, and her face wasn't very clear, but at first glance, one would think it was Qi Fang.","The cake shop's surveillance also captured Qi Fang, from about the same angle.","Neither shop's surveillance ever captured Qi Fang's full face. At the time, they didn't suspect anything because they saw Qi Fang's freckles in her side profile. Her height and body type also matched.","Fang Rui analyzed: \"Su Momo must have disguised herself as Qi Fang to leave the makeup area, while Qi Fang hid inside. No wonder Zhang said that cup of bubble tea was cold.\"","Looking at it this way, Su Momo's acting skills were really good. Her disguise was so convincing that even the detail-oriented Mu Mian almost couldn't tell the difference.","\"If Qi Fang was hiding in the makeup area the whole time, why did the surveillance camera capture her entering the makeup area with bubble tea again around 5 PM?\" Mu Mian asked, puzzled.","Fang Rui also found it strange. Qi Fang first went out to buy bubble tea, then came back, and then Su Momo left disguised as her. Logically, Qi Fang shouldn't have been able to enter from outside again. But the person captured on camera around 5 PM showed Qi Fang's face, and it was indeed her. This was also an important reason why they didn't notice anything unusual in the surveillance video at the time.","That makeup area was an enclosed space with only one entrance and exit. It was impossible to enter or leave that place without passing by this surveillance camera.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to Qi Fang's home together.","Like Su Momo, Qi Fang was a local. Because Su Momo had disappeared, Sun Qin felt that Qi Fang hadn't taken good care of Su Momo, so she directly gave Qi Fang some money and fired her.","Qi Fang's home was in a residential compound near the hospital. Her parents had divorced when she was young, and neither wanted to raise her, so she was fostered by her grandmother from childhood. Her grandmother was a doctor with decent financial conditions, and after she passed away, she gave the house allocated by the hospital to Qi Fang.","Since Su Momo's disappearance, Fang Rui had been having someone secretly keep an eye on her. She stayed at home every day, hardly going out except to take out the trash, and even had groceries delivered directly to her door by the supermarket. Nothing seemed out of the ordinary.","From Qi Fang's neighbors, they learned that Qi Fang had been odd in personality since childhood, not very sociable, but very filial to her grandmother. After she graduated and came back, she suddenly seemed like a different person.","\"Hey, that granddaughter of Dr. Qi's was really spoiled rotten by her. Can you believe a Chinese literature master's graduate with such good qualifications would quit such a good job because of celebrity worship, idling away her days doing nothing productive!\"","Fang Rui asked, \"She likes Su Momo very much?\"","\"Who's Su Momo? I don't know which celebrity she's chasing after. I heard from others that when her grandmother was still around, she stole money from her grandmother to buy celebrity photos. Those tiny pictures cost thousands of yuan each, and she didn't even blink an eye when buying them. Tsk, who knows where she learned such bad behavior from, she used to be such an obedient child.\"","\"Yes, she used to be so sensible, saying she would take good care of her grandmother. But when her grandmother was seriously ill in bed, she went to a fan meeting instead of seeing her grandmother for the last time. If it weren't for the fact that this house doesn't have a property certificate, she probably would have sold the house to chase after celebrities!\"","Fang Rui felt their description didn't quite match Qi Fang. She seemed quiet and gentle, and quite responsible in her work, not like someone so fanatical.","Zhang muttered softly, \"Boss, could this Qi Fang be a crazy fan of Su Momo?\"","Fang Rui knocked on the door, and someone inside said: \"Just a moment, I'm washing dishes in the kitchen. Give me a minute.\"","After a while, Qi Fang opened the door.","Her home was very messy, with things piled up all over the floor, seemingly not cleaned for a while. There was also a lot of dust on the sofa. Shoes were randomly placed on the shoe rack in the entryway. Fang Rui found it strange - she appeared to live alone, so why were there two styles of shoes on the rack? Some shoes were very colorful, while others were gray and black, with an old-fashioned style, like the pair Qi Fang was wearing.","Fang Rui gave Zhang a look. Zhang had also noticed this oddity, and he immediately clutched his stomach and said to Qi Fang, \"I'm sorry, my stomach suddenly hurts. May I use your bathroom?\""]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: Gone Her: Brainless Fans","paragraphs":["Qi Fang hesitated, but seeing that Zhang was about to burst, she pointed in a direction and said, \"The restroom is on the right.\"","Zhang dashed into the bathroom.","Qi Fang looked at Fang Rui, emotion flashing in her eyes. \"Officer Fang, have you found Momo?\"","\"Not yet. We're here because we have some questions for you.\"","\"What do you want to know? Go ahead and ask.\"","\"Where is Su Momo's dog?\"","\"Dog? You mean Bugu? You should ask Liu Yaying about that. She's been taking care of Momo's dog all along. I think she sent it to a pet hospital for treatment.\"","\"Miss Qi, we've already spoken to the lady who adopted the dog,\" Fang Rui stared at Qi Fang. \"So you don't need to keep making things up. Just tell us the truth.\"","Qi Fang's expression changed. She quickly defended herself, \"I went to get Bugu back myself. Momo asked me to do it, and she told me not to tell Liu Yaying. Liu Yaying has a bad temper and is very strict with Momo. Momo just had a skin allergy, but Liu Yaying insisted it was caused by dog hair and sent the puppy away. I saw how unhappy Momo was, so I secretly checked Liu Yaying's phone and found the dog.\"","\"Where is the dog now?\"","\"I don't know. Momo's bodyguard took it away.\"","\"Which bodyguard? Take us to see him.\" Fang Rui noticed Qi Fang's face turning pale as she seemed to be struggling to find an excuse. He asked, \"You placed that cursed doll, didn't you?\"","\"Of course not. How could I curse Momo?\" Qi Fang immediately defended herself, \"Officer, you can't accuse people without evidence!\"","\"Then tell me where the dog went.\"","\"It died. I threw the body in the trash.\"","\"There are surveillance cameras near your home and the hotel. Let's go check the footage to see if you threw away the dog's body.\"","\"I...\" Qi Fang stiffened her neck, stammering for a while before finally saying, \"I'm sorry, I can't tell you.\"","\"That day, Su Momo was wearing clothes identical to yours, pretending to be you when she left the makeup area, right?\" Seeing Qi Fang about to quibble again, Fang Rui pointed at her right wrist, \"The second 'Qi Fang' who left that area had a scar on her wrist, but you don't have that scar. Are you still going to lie?\"","\"I...\"","\"Miss Qi, where exactly is Su Momo?\" Fang Rui was almost out of patience.","\"I don't know where Momo went either. She forced me to do all this. If I didn't help her, she threatened to report me to the police. Momo already knew that I was the one who placed the cursed doll! I was too jealous of Liu Yaying. I was so good to Momo, helping her manage everything perfectly, and I tried my best to make her happy. But what did I get in return? Momo couldn't see my efforts at all. She was always so nice to Liu Yaying but ignored me. And Liu Yaying always ordered me around like a servant!","I could have endured it. I thought that if I kept being so good to Momo, she would eventually see my dedication. But then I discovered that Liu Yaying was actually with Liang Guangyu, and they had slept together many times. I didn't dare tell Momo the truth, so I could only use this method to drive Liu Yaying away. This way, Momo wouldn't be so heartbroken, and that scum Liu Yaying could stay away from Momo. Someone as good as Momo shouldn't be treated like this!\"","Qi Fang became more and more agitated as she spoke, finally covering her face and bursting into tears.","Fang Rui asked, \"Why did Su Momo fake her death?\"","Qi Fang wiped her tears and said, \"Momo's plan wasn't to fake her death. She just wanted to escape from the New Year's Eve performance. She's done this often before. She doesn't like singing, but her manager forces her to, so she asks me to help her escape. I don't know why there was blood in the makeup room. Could it have been Liu Yaying? Maybe she wanted to ruin Momo's career.\"","\"Liu Yaying attempted suicide by cutting her wrists.\"","\"Suicide? How could this happen? Who made that blood then?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Where did Su Momo go?\"","\"I'm not sure. She might have gone to a small island in the south for a vacation, or to the north to see ice sculptures, or to the west to see the desert. She has many places she wants to visit, and I don't know which one she chose. She hasn't contacted me since leaving the makeup room. I've been trying to find her too.\"","\"Why didn't you tell us the truth before?\"","\"I was afraid it would affect Momo's trip, so I didn't dare tell you. Momo should be fine. She's just hiding because she was deeply hurt by the betrayal of her best friend and boyfriend. She wants some quiet time. I didn't want you to disturb her.\"","Fang Rui looked at Qi Fang, \"Come with us to the station to make a statement. We need to confirm a few things with you.\" For some reason, Fang Rui still didn't quite believe Qi Fang.","\"Alright.\"","\"Why aren't you moving?\"","\"Officer Zhang is still in the bathroom. Let's wait for him to come out before I go to the station with you.\" Qi Fang glanced towards the bathroom and quickly looked away.","Zhang came out soon after.","They let Qi Fang get in the car first, then Zhang pulled Fang Rui aside and whispered, \"Boss, I made a big discovery. There are two pairs of slippers in her bathroom, both women's. The towels and toothbrushes are also in pairs. Someone else is living in that apartment with Qi Fang.\"","\"Hmm.\" Fang Rui had already guessed that Su Momo might have been staying at Qi Fang's place these past few days.","\"At first, I suspected Su Momo was living at Qi Fang's. But I checked those slippers, they're both old, and the towels don't look new either. Su Momo wouldn't wear old slippers or use old towels, would she?\" Zhang analyzed.","Fang Rui frowned. So where had Su Momo gone? She couldn't use her own ID to buy tickets, so she shouldn't be able to travel around freely.","\"Boss, I have another guess. Qi Fang seems to be a fan of Liang Guangyu. I saw a keychain hanging in her entryway, it's merchandise from one of Liang Guangyu's roles, worth over a thousand yuan. This merchandise is expensive and hard to get.\"","Zhang continued, \"There were also traces of posters on her wall, very fresh traces with poster fragments still left. She probably hurriedly tore them down and threw them in the trash just before we arrived. I saw the trash can was full of plastic paper. She must be Liang Guangyu's fan! And a die-hard one at that!\"","Chen Xue had been obsessed with celebrity chasing recently, and Zhang had accompanied her, so he was very familiar with fan culture, including which celebrities were rivals, what kind of merchandise was available, and so on.","Fang Rui applied for a search warrant to investigate Qi Fang's home.","Just as Zhang had said, the trash can was full of freshly torn posters of Liang Guangyu, some even bearing his autograph. Combined with what Qi Fang's neighbors said, the celebrity she had been obsessively following was indeed Liang Guangyu.","Qi Fang's apartment had three bedrooms and one living room. One room was used for storage, while the other two were occupied. One of the rooms was very simply furnished, with just a bed and a quilt, and almost nothing else.","The other room was covered in posters, all of Liang Guangyu. The desk was piled with magazines, all featuring Liang Guangyu's recent photoshoots. There was even a special cabinet in the room, filled with various Liang Guangyu merchandise: plush dolls, badges, standees, photo books, and albums...","All of this confirmed that Qi Fang was indeed a hardcore fan of Liang Guangyu.","\"Boss, do you think Qi Fang might have kidnapped or even killed Su Momo to cover up Liang Guangyu's infidelity?\" Zhang asked."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: The Vanished Her: The Emergence","paragraphs":["The interrogation of Qi Fang was not going well. No matter how they questioned her, she adamantly insisted that she didn't know where Su Momo had gone. She also denied kidnapping Su Momo.","\"I didn't kidnap Momo. She forced me to help her leave the TV station. After she left, I couldn't contact her anymore. I haven't committed any crime! You have no right to detain me. I want a lawyer!\" Qi Fang protested.","Su Momo's manager, Sun Qin, also came to question Qi Fang: \"Qi Fang, please, just tell me where Momo is. How much money do you want? I can give you anything. Is 200,000 yuan enough?\"","\"Stop trying to insult people with money! Momo has gone to do what she wants to do. You've been forcing her to do things she doesn't like, and she's very unhappy!\" Qi Fang shouted at Sun Qin. After shouting, she sat back down, smiling somewhat eerily, \"Momo hates you all. She wants to be alone.\"","Sun Qin was chilled by her smile. She felt that Qi Fang's mental state was a bit unstable.","Fang Rui and his team investigated Qi Fang's properties, but she only owned this one apartment. They also investigated whether she had rented any houses. She had rented a house a year ago but moved out three months ago.","Although there were personal items for two people in Qi Fang's home, those items didn't have Su Momo's DNA on them. They also didn't find any of Su Momo's belongings during the search of Qi Fang's home.","Mu Mian discovered that the DNA from the two sets of personal items was different, belonging to two women, one of whom was Qi Fang. After some thought, she compared the two DNA samples and found that the two individuals were related by blood.","\"Fang Rui, does Qi Fang have any sisters?\" Mu Mian asked.","\"Sisters?\" Fang Rui had a sudden realization. If Qi Fang had a sister, it would explain how the Qi Fang hidden in the makeup area could have come in from outside. The person who came in might not have been Qi Fang, but someone who looked very similar to her.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to question Qi Fang's neighbors again.","\"Qi Fang has a younger sister named Qi Fen. They were born a year apart and were very close as children. When their parents divorced, Qi Fen went with their father. Their father was a lazy good-for-nothing with mental issues, so Qi Fen probably suffered a lot.\"","\"Where did Qi Fen go with her father?\"","\"I think they went to Linzhou City. We're not sure, she hasn't come to see her sister in all these years.\"","Fang Rui quickly investigated Qi Fen's background.","Qi Fen was from Linzhou. She dropped out of middle school and started working, initially in restaurants. Later, she grew tired of work and fell in love with cycling, traveling around on her bicycle.","After meeting her boyfriend, she settled down for a while, living off him. A year ago, she assaulted her boyfriend and was kicked out.","\"The reason Qi Fen assaulted her ex-boyfriend was that he insulted Liang Guangyu,\" Zhang learned about the reason for Qi Fen's detention from the local police station. \"It seems that Qi Fen is the real obsessive fan of Liang Guangyu. Qi Fang might have helped her sister kidnap Su Momo.\"","The most urgent matter now was to find Su Momo. According to Qi Fen's ex-boyfriend, Qi Fen's mental state was very unstable, and she had violent tendencies. If Su Momo had indeed been kidnapped by her, she could be in grave danger.","The surveillance cameras near Qi Fang's home hadn't captured any sign of Su Momo, so she was likely not hidden in Qi Fang's home.","Fang Rui obtained Qi Fen's phone number from her ex-boyfriend, and this number was still in use.","The telecommunications company could roughly locate a user's position based on their phone number. At the police's request, the company helped locate Qi Fen's current position—in a cluster of abandoned buildings in the eastern suburbs.","There were several buildings in that area, and it wasn't possible to pinpoint the exact building based on the phone number. Fang Rui could only have everyone search quietly in different directions, trying not to alert Qi Fen.","\"Ah, boss, I stepped on something!\" Zhang covered his mouth and pointed at his feet.","He looked down and saw a pile of dog feces.","Fang Rui glanced at it and quickly looked away. Judging from the shape, it should have been from a small animal, which reminded Fang Rui of the spotted dog called Bugu.","Was that little dog still alive? Had it also been kidnapped by Qi Fen?","Fang Rui and his team searched several buildings but couldn't find any trace of Qi Fen. Just as they thought the location might be wrong, Qi Fen appeared, walking from a patch of wasteland with grass seeds stuck to her clothes.","At that moment, she noticed the pile of dog feces that Zhang had stepped in, and seeing the footprint, she instantly realized that the police had tracked her here. She immediately ran towards the nearby wasteland.","Fang Rui and Zhang chased after her right away.","Qi Fen, being a long-time cyclist, had excellent stamina. Moreover, she was familiar with the terrain and deliberately headed into the deep grass.","Fang Rui told Zhang to continue the chase while he took a shortcut to block Qi Fen's path.","Qi Fen found herself surrounded.","\"Qi Fen, if you keep running, you'll be suspected of resisting arrest, which will aggravate your crimes!\" Zhang warned.","Qi Fen thought Zhang looked weaker, so she ran towards him, but unexpectedly, Zhang caught her by the collar and quickly subdued her.","\"I didn't expect you to be such a good runner!\" Zhang handcuffed Qi Fen and started escorting her back. After a few steps, Zhang let out a painful cry.","\"Ah, my leg!\"","Zhang had stepped into an animal trap, and his entire leg was covered in blood.","\"I'm really having a crappy day, just my rotten luck!\" Zhang wailed as he was sent to the hospital.","Qi Fen refused to tell the police where Su Momo was. No matter what the police asked, she remained silent.","Fang Rui and his team searched the entire area of abandoned buildings but still couldn't find Su Momo.","\"Woof, woof, woof...\"","Following the sound, they found a spotted dog in the gap between two abandoned buildings. It looked very similar to Su Momo's dog. Its head was tied with a plastic rope, preventing it from leaving.","Seeing people, it barked even more enthusiastically.","Fang Rui and his team untied the rope for the little dog. The dog circled around them a few times, barked \"woof woof\" twice, and then ran forward on its short legs.","\"The dog might know where Su Momo is. Let's follow it,\" Fang Rui said.","The little dog would run a few steps and then look back, making sure Fang Rui and his team were following before continuing towards the wasteland.","After walking for about twenty minutes, they reached a hillside.","\"Help... help...\" A faint cry for help came from the hillside.","They ran over and saw Su Momo tied to a large tree, her lips pale and her whole person looking very weak.","\"Wah... Finally, someone's here. There were two Qi Fangs, they kidnapped me!\" Su Momo cried, \"They're fans of Liang Guangyu and wanted to take revenge on me! They tied me here, wanting wild wolves to eat me alive. They're so cruel! Wah...\"","Su Momo cried for a while and then fainted. Fang Rui and his team quickly carried her to the ambulance.","In the interrogation room, Qi Fen initially refused to admit her crime.","\"Officer, I didn't kidnap Su Momo. It was Su Momo who hired me to kidnap her. She gave me a pendant of Liang Guangyu, one that he had worn personally, very valuable. I couldn't resist the temptation, that's why I pretended to kidnap her.\""]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: The Vanished: The Truth","paragraphs":["\"Where is that pendant now?\"","\"In my pocket.\" Qi Fen felt her pocket, but only pulled out a crumpled tissue and a few coins. She explained embarrassedly, \"I lost it.\"","\"You liked Liang Guangyu so much, how could you lose such a precious item?\" Fang Rui caught the hole in her story.","\"I...\"","\"Qi Fen, we already have evidence of your crime. Su Momo has also identified you as the kidnapper. You'd better tell the truth.\" Fang Rui pointed at the clock on the wall. \"Liang Guangyu's lawyer is working on his bail procedure. In ten minutes, he might pass by that corridor outside...\"","\"Officer, the nature of kidnapping isn't too serious, right? It's at most one or two years in prison, isn't it?\"","\"Sentencing is up to the judge.\"","Qi Fen kept glancing at the clock on the wall and began to ramble about what had happened:","\"My sister and I are both fans of Liang Guangyu. I really hated Su Momo. When I found out Su Momo was Liang Guangyu's girlfriend, I wanted to get rid of her. But murder would get me the death penalty. So I thought about kidnapping her and having someone rape her to ruin her reputation.","My sister didn't agree with my plan because she thought Su Momo was a good person and we shouldn't hurt her. I had no choice but to listen to my sister, otherwise she wouldn't give me money or support me anymore. Later, my sister told me that Su Momo had evidence of Liang Guangyu's infidelity and was going to expose him! We definitely couldn't let her ruin Liang Guangyu. So my sister agreed to help me kidnap her.","Before kidnapping her, we had to get rid of Liu Yaying, otherwise she would always be with Su Momo and we couldn't make our move. My sister knew about her curse doll, so we used that doll to frame Liu Yaying and get her fired. Later, my sister deliberately hinted to Su Momo that she could help her skip the New Year's Eve performance, and Su Momo fell for it. After Su Momo snuck out, I lured her to a secluded place, drugged her, and took her by car to that abandoned building to lock her up.","I thought we'd keep her for a few days to teach her a lesson, so she wouldn't leak the news about Liang Guangyu's affair. Who knew the police would leak this information? You were so irresponsible!","This morning, my sister told me that the police might have discovered what we did. I thought, since we've already committed a crime, why not kill Su Momo. Killing someone with my own hands seemed too cruel, so I tied her to a tree on a desolate mountain, leaving her to freeze to death or be eaten by wolves!\"","To fill the ten minutes, Qi Fen described the events in great detail.","\"Officer, can I go see Liang Guangyu now?\"","Qi Fen was escorted to the detention center. She passed by Liang Guangyu and excitedly said to him, \"Liang Guangyu, I did something big for you. I kidnapped Su Momo for you. I almost killed her. See, I can do anything for you. Liang Guangyu, I love you...\"","Liang Guangyu felt disgusted. His face turned the color of pork liver as he hurriedly left with his lawyer.","Upon learning that her sister had confessed, Qi Fang finally admitted to the crime as well.","\"I kidnapped Su Momo. My sister was just an accomplice. We both like Liang Guangyu very much, and we couldn't watch Su Momo expose him, so we kidnapped her. We originally planned to keep her for a few days and then release her, but things developed beyond our expectations. Suddenly there was blood in that dressing room, which led you to believe it was a homicide, and the situation got out of hand.","Later we panicked and didn't know what to do. We didn't dare to kill her, but we were afraid she'd report us to the police if we let her go, so we just kept her locked up.\"","Qi Fang's account of the incident was similar to her sister's.","\"You didn't put the blood in the dressing room?\"","\"No, I didn't. I was shocked when I discovered the blood. And when you said the blood was Su Momo's, I was completely stunned, not knowing what had happened.\"","\"Could your sister have done it?\"","\"I don't know. My sister and I acted separately.\"","Fang Rui questioned Qi Fen again.","\"I put that blood there. I poured the blood on the floor to make it look like a suicide attempt by wrist-cutting. I wanted Liang Guangyu to think Su Momo was dead, so he wouldn't have to worry about being exposed by her.\"","\"How did you obtain Su Momo's blood?\"","\"I won't tell you.\"","The two sisters, Qi Fang and Qi Fen, admitted to their crimes. The case was more or less solved.","The news of Su Momo being found once again broke the internet.","#SuMomoSuccessfullyRescued#","#SuMomoKidnappedByAntiFan#","#LiangGuangyusCrazyFansAreTerrible#","#RationalFanBehavior#","Su Momo nearly dominated the entire trending list.","In the hospital, Su Momo was eating an apple with her legs crossed, reading a script.","It was a script for a mystery film. Originally, she was cast as the third female lead, playing a forensic doctor, but after her kidnapping experience, the director changed his mind. He thought Su Momo would be perfect for the lead role, a character who also experiences a kidnapping. The director believed Su Momo's real-life experience would enhance her performance, and they could use this angle to promote the film.","Su Momo looked relaxed, not at all like someone who had just been through a life-threatening kidnapping.","The doctor had given Su Momo a full body check-up. Apart from rope marks on her wrists and ankles from being tied up, she had no other external injuries. She was in good health overall.","From the corner of her eye, Su Momo spotted Fang Rui and Mu Mian. She adjusted her posture and smiled at them, \"Officer Fang, Dr. Mu, what brings you to the hospital?\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian were there to visit Zhang, and had passed by Su Momo's room.","Seeing Su Momo act so nonchalant, Fang Rui became even more convinced that there was more to her than met the eye.","\"Miss Su, you weren't actually kidnapped, were you? You planned all this, didn't you?\" Fang Rui analyzed, \"You used the Qi sisters.\"","\"Officer Fang, I don't know what you're talking about.\"","\"Qi Fang said she didn't pour the blood in the dressing room; Qi Fen admitted to it, but her story doesn't match the facts. Did you make some kind of deal with Qi Fen, like giving her some of Liang Guangyu's belongings, so she would willingly follow your plan?\"","\"Officer Fang, you can't solve cases based on guesses alone. You need evidence,\" Su Momo looked up at Fang Rui, \"Even if there was evidence, it's not illegal for someone to arrange their own kidnapping, is it?\"","Fang Rui indeed had no evidence. All the evidence showed that the Qi sisters had kidnapped Su Momo, and they had confessed to the crime. It was possible that they had initially planned to kidnap Su Momo, but Su Momo had turned the tables on them, using their kidnapping to achieve her own goals.","\"It's the police's job to solve cases. You don't need to know the whole truth, and you won't be able to anyway.\" Su Momo's tone was smug, but she waved the script in her hand and said with a smile, \"That's a line from the script. Did I scare you just now? Looks like my acting skills aren't bad.\"","\"Miss Su, that curse doll wasn't placed by Liu Yaying. She didn't curse you,\" Fang Rui said. \"Liu Yaying attempted suicide by cutting her wrists recently. She's in this hospital. She's not in a good state right now. If you have time, maybe you could go talk to her. I think there's been a big misunderstanding between you two.\"","Su Momo took a bite of her apple, her eyes still fixed on the script. \"Thank you for telling me. I'll visit her when I have time.\"","After Fang Rui and Mu Mian left, her new assistant, Little Chen, came in and asked, \"Sister Momo, do you want...\"","Su Momo corrected her irritably, \"Please call me Miss Su.\"","\"Alright, Miss Su, would you like some bubble tea now? Both Sister Yaying and Sister Qi Fang mentioned that you like to drink bubble tea when you're in a bad mood.\"","\"What makes you think I'm in a bad mood?\"","\"I...\"","Su Momo finished the apple and threw the core in the trash bin. \"Little Chen, come with me to see Liu Yaying. I need your help with something.\""]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: The Vanished: Perfect Revenge","paragraphs":["Su Momo went to Liu Yaying's hospital room. She saw Liu Yaying sitting up in bed, leaning against her pillow, her face pale and expressionless as she stared out the window.","When she saw Su Momo, Liu Yaying's expression became agitated. She wanted to rush forward and hug Su Momo, but remembering what she had done, she nervously sat back down on the edge of the bed.","Liu Yaying cried out, \"Momo, that doll wasn't a curse doll, it was meant to bring you good fortune. The master said it would bless your career with brilliance. The bloody doll that appeared later was someone trying to frame me.\"","Su Momo didn't say anything. She no longer cared about the truth of those matters.","\"I didn't mean to send Bugu away. The doctor said you were allergic to dog hair, but you didn't believe it. I had no choice but to secretly send it away without telling you.\"","Su Momo removed her large sunglasses. \"Yaying, all of that is in the past now.\"","\"Momo, I never meant to be with Liang Guangyu. I only slept with him to get evidence of his cheating for you. But you loved him so much, I was worried that even if you knew he cheated, you still wouldn't break up with him. After all, you had once considered giving up your career for him. So I had no choice but to let you find out that I had slept with him, to make you completely disillusioned with him...\"","Liu Yaying was crying messily.","Tears also slowly rolled down from the corners of Su Momo's eyes, but she couldn't feel any sadness.","She thought back to the times she had spent with Liu Yaying, difficult yet full of hope.","None of it could be reclaimed now.","Has anyone ever had a moment when they suddenly saw the true face of the world?","Perhaps from watching too many idealistic TV dramas, people can become rather naive. The old Su Momo had always believed that if you were good to others, they would return that kindness to you. Though there were bad people in the world, she thought good people were still the majority.","So even though she had suffered her father's vicious betrayal, Su Momo still grew up to be a warm and kind person.","Later, she read that suspense script. The female lead in the script also started out pure and kind, but everyone around her used and betrayed her. In the end, she had no choice but to grow up and take up a sharp knife to protect herself.","Su Momo realized that she had been viewing the world through rose-colored glasses before.","She was just like that female lead, and the people surrounding her were all deceiving, using, and betraying her.","The man she loved most was a cheating scumbag, just like her father. Liang Guangyu said he loved her, that his dream was to have a family with her. For this, Su Momo had nearly given up her own career and dreams to marry him. But that man was still in love with many other women.","Her most trusted best friend hated and betrayed her. They had once lived together in the cheapest, dirtiest apartment, helping each other through the darkest moments of their lives. But Liu Yaying had slept with her boyfriend, put a curse on her, and done various underhanded things behind her back to smear her reputation.","Her assistant, whom she thought was kindhearted, was secretly her anti-fan, going to great lengths to collect negative information about her, wanting to destroy her career and even planning to kidnap her.","Her manager, who had struggled alongside her to build her career, had forgotten their original dreams and only wanted to make money now, forcing her to do things she didn't like and take roles she didn't want, binding her with all kinds of cold contracts.","Even the \"Star Home\" charity she had always donated to was just using charity as a way to make money.","Su Momo found that the beautiful world she saw had collapsed.","She wanted revenge on these bad people!","She designed a perfect plan, deciding to go along with Qi Fang's scheme and let her \"kidnap\" herself.","First, she had to reasonably fire Liu Yaying. She deliberately instructed Qi Fang to go to Liu Yaying's room to let her see the doll. She knew that if Qi Fang wanted to kidnap her, she would have to get rid of Liu Yaying first. To Su Momo's surprise, Qi Fang created a bloody curse incident.","Su Momo then enriched her plan.","Su Momo deliberately complained to Qi Fang that she didn't want to perform in the show, and Qi Fang immediately said she could help her leave the TV station—Qi Fang was implementing her kidnapping plan.","Su Momo knew that she couldn't just disappear, otherwise the police wouldn't dig deeply into what had happened to her.","That day, she infused her own blood into props, simulating the blood spatter pattern of a wrist-cutting suicide. Then she poured the blood she had extracted in advance onto the floor, and even lay down in the pool of blood herself, simulating the most realistic scene of a wrist-cutting suicide.","Su Momo had seen what her mother looked like when she committed suicide, and that scene was deeply imprinted in her mind. The first time she learned of Liang Guangyu's infidelity, she had cut her own wrist with a knife, but quickly bandaged the wound herself. She would not repeat her mother's fate.","So she knew exactly what a wrist-cutting suicide scene would look like.","Later, she successfully disappeared from that makeup room. She knew it would immediately cause an uproar, and all those who had betrayed and hurt her would face retribution.","Liang Guangyu would be ruined. Su Momo had already arranged for the press releases. The day after she disappeared, those self-media accounts would widely spread evidence of Liang Guangyu's infidelity. With the massive attention from her disappearance, no one would be able to suppress this scandal.","Liu Yaying would be seen as the other woman, cursed and condemned by everyone. She might worsen her depression out of guilt, and being so fragile, she might even commit suicide. Someone like her was a waste of life anyway, so let her die.","Sun Qin would suffer heavy losses.","Qi Fang would go to prison for kidnapping.","Even her beast of a father would face a small punishment. When he learned of her death, that scumbag would surely be overjoyed, thinking he could get a large inheritance. But he would soon learn that he would get nothing. This feeling of disappointment, of thinking he could get something but ending up with nothing, would torment him for the rest of his life.","As for Su Momo herself, she would gain the sympathy of countless netizens. She could shake off many jobs she didn't want to do, and might even land the lead role in that suspense film she had been vying for, all because of this kidnapping experience.","The plan was nearly perfect, with the only unexpected element being Qi Fang's sister, Qi Fen. Her sister was also a crazed fan of that scumbag Liang Guangyu, and she actually kidnapped her for real.","Qi Fen was mentally unstable and nearly killed her several times.","But it wasn't a big problem. Su Momo bribed Qi Fen with Liang Guangyu's limited edition merchandise. Su Momo told her that the kidnapping charge would only mean one or two years in prison. After she got out, Su Momo would give her a large number of Liang Guangyu's personal items, including clothes he had worn and things he had used.","Qi Fen was as brainless as her sister and agreed to follow her arrangements. She also promised not to reveal anything about Su Momo.","She even taught Qi Fen how to face interrogation. She told Qi Fen not to admit to the crime at first, to make up some lies that were easy to see through, and then to confess when the police put pressure on her. This would seem more realistic.","To make the rescue more authentic, she even had Qi Fen tie up Bugu in the abandoned building, so it could lead the police to find her.","The outcome was perfect. The bad people all received their punishment, while Su Momo remained the kind and beautiful person she had always been.","\"Momo, that's wonderful, that's wonderful, we're still good friends.\"","Liu Yaying's voice brought Su Momo back to reality. Su Momo hugged her back, \"Yaying, you'll always be my good friend.\" Her face rested on Liu Yaying's shoulder, wearing a sincere expression.","Click, a camera flash went off outside the window.","Su Momo released Liu Yaying and put on her sunglasses. \"Miss Liu, I wish you a speedy recovery.\"","\"Momo, you...\"","\"Please call me Miss Su from now on.\"","Liu Yaying looked at Su Momo's cold expression, at a loss. She didn't understand why Su Momo had suddenly become so unfamiliar.","\"Liu Yaying, admit it, all these years you've been jealous and resentful of me. You felt I stole your life.\"","\"I...\" Liu Yaying couldn't deny it, because she had indeed thought that way. But friendship had overcome those malicious thoughts.","Su Momo handed her a card, \"There's 100,000 yuan on this. The password is the last six digits of your ID number. Liu Yaying, you're on your own from now on.\"","Leaving the hospital room, Little Chen immediately came up to her, \"Miss Su, the photos have been taken. I captured the most touching moment.\"","\"Mm, well done.\" Su Momo glanced at the photo, thinking her acting skills were quite exquisite. \"Please call the lawyer for me, I want to modify my will.\"","The next day, the hashtag #Heartbreaking, Su Momo visits critically ill best friend# once again topped the trending topics.","From that point on, Su Momo's career in the entertainment industry shone brightly, but no one ever called her Momo again."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: No Love","paragraphs":["Fang Rui and Mu Mian arrived at Zhang's hospital room.","\"Everyone spread out a bit, don't all crowd together. Zhang can barely breathe,\" Chen Xue waved away the heads clustered around the bed, complaining, \"Who brought those yellow chrysanthemums? That's so inauspicious, take them away! And those lilies too, get rid of them. Zhang is allergic to lilies!\"","Zhang was well-liked, and his room was packed with colleagues who had come to visit. Even the new female accountant from the finance department had brought a bouquet of lilies.","Everyone gathered around to examine Zhang's wounds. Those who knew the truth were stifling their laughter, while the uninformed were whispering amongst themselves.","\"Bro, your leg doesn't look like it was just from a fall. Why are there all these holes in it? What on earth happened?\" Wang poked Zhang's leg, making him howl in pain.","Chen Xue angrily swatted Wang's hand away. \"He's already in this state, and you're still bullying him? What kind of friend are you?\"","\"Come on, Zhang's a tough guy. This is nothing for him,\" Wang sheepishly withdrew his hand.","\"Oh no, I forgot to buy pork trotters to make soup for Zhang. He needs to build up his strength,\" the female accountant looked distraught.","\"Little Shen, why are you worrying? Chen Xue is right here. She's studying medicine, don't you think she knows how to take care of Zhang? You're always fretting over nothing.\"","\"But Chen Xue is a forensic pathologist. She specializes in corpses.\"","\"...\"","Zhang's face turned bright red. He hadn't dared tell everyone that he'd stepped in an animal trap. It would ruin his image.","Mu Mian looked at the room full of flowers and gifts, suddenly realizing she had come empty-handed. Oh no, she'd forgotten to buy a present.","Her gaze moved from the pile of gifts to the enormous, elaborate fruit basket Fang Rui was holding.","Would it be okay to sneak a fruit or two from it?","\"Mu Mian, can you carry this?\" Fang Rui handed the fruit basket to her.","Mu Mian reminded him, \"Aren't you giving it yourself? It'll be awkward without a gift.\"","\"It's fine. My friendship with Zhang doesn't need gifts to prove it.\"","\"That's great then. I could really use a gift.\"","Mu Mian excitedly took the basket, nearly toppling over with it. It was so heavy! In the end, she opted to hug it as she entered the room.","Everyone watched as Mu Mian stumbled in, hugging a fruit basket half her height.","Zhang was moved to tears. \"Mu Mian, I'm so touched! You didn't have to come, let alone bring such a huge fruit basket. Why so formal?\"","Then Zhang glanced at Fang Rui's empty hands, and his tears of gratitude dried up. The boss was so cold-hearted, not even bringing a small gift when he was bedridden.","Seeing Zhang's disappointed expression, Fang Rui was exasperated. Why did a grown man care so much about getting gifts? He wasn't a child.","The others also looked at Fang Rui's empty hands and scolded him, \"Captain Fang, you didn't even help her carry it? How are you going to handle having a girlfriend in the future?\"","\"I wanted to carry it myself,\" Mu Mian clarified, seeing that Fang Rui was being misunderstood. \"Fang Rui bought the fruit basket at the fruit shop downstairs. He got the most expensive one. I forgot to buy a gift, so Fang Rui let me give his gift so I wouldn't be embarrassed.\"","Everyone exchanged knowing looks. \"Well, what's his is yours, right? No need to be so particular about it.\"","\"Exactly!\"","Zhang was touched again. He felt honored that Fang Rui had bought him the most expensive fruit basket. He must really value him!","Mu Mian frowned, not understanding why Fang Rui's fruit basket would be considered hers. Did that mean his corpse would be hers too? But Mu Mian had already promised Fang Rui she wouldn't let him donate his body, so she didn't voice her confusion.","\"Officer Zhang, I heard you were injured by the culprit, but these wounds look strange. Did they attack you with a rake?\" Mu Mian examined Zhang's injuries closely. Worried that others might not know what a rake was, she explained, \"You know, like in Journey to the West? Zhu Bajie's weapon is a rake.\"","Everyone suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha, it really does look like Zhu Bajie took a swipe at him with his rake!\"","Mu Mian didn't understand why everyone was laughing, so she just laughed along.","Zhang grumbled dejectedly, \"Man, I must have stepped in dog poop that day to have such bad luck.\"","Mu Mian pointed to the bandage on her head. \"Hey, I've been having bad luck lately too.\"","Everyone remembered the rumors about Mu Mian and couldn't help laughing again.","Fang Rui glanced at Mu Mian, a bit helpless. Her wound had long since healed, but she loved SpongeBob SquarePants so much that she still wore that eye-catching bandage every day. Fang Rui had tried to remove it for her, but before long, Mu Mian would secretly put it back on.","After making a ruckus in the room for a while longer, they were complained about by the elderly patient next door for being too noisy. Everyone had to leave, letting Chen Xue stay alone to look after Zhang.","Before leaving, Mu Mian saw Chen Xue and Zhang chatting and laughing together in the room, looking very happy.","Mu Mian was puzzled. Zhang's injuries were so severe, why was he still so cheerful? Chen Xue's boyfriend was lying in a hospital bed, how could she laugh? Their emotional states were strange and couldn't be explained by normal logic.","Mu Mian recalled the forensic guide Forensic Doctor Cheng had written for her. He said that people in love have illogical emotions - their tears might express joy, their laughter might mask sorrow. Overcoming hardships and setbacks might even deepen their love... Mu Mian thought love was so complicated!","\"What's wrong, Mu Mian? Your eyebrows are all scrunched up like Crayon Shin-chan.\"","\"Fang Rui, I'm studying an emotion that normal humans possess - love,\" Mu Mian raised her chin, looking a bit proud. She thought Zhou Junwei's experimental design lacked creativity. She wanted to design a perfect experiment to study love.","But before that, she needed to understand what love was.","\"Why study love?\" Fang Rui's heart suddenly sped up. Had Mu Mian finally realized that their relationship was different from her other friendships?","\"Because normal people all have love. Zhang and Chen Xue have love, Forensic Doctor Cheng has love, even Wang found a nurse girlfriend. Even my hacker friend - a severe social phobic - has an adorable girlfriend...\" Mu Mian listed the couples around her and sighed, \"Except for me. I don't have love. Because I'm not normal.\"","Seeing Fang Rui's complicated expression, she carefully reminded him, \"Fang Rui, you don't seem to have love either.\"","\"I do have love,\" Fang Rui corrected her.","Mu Mian tilted her head, looking confused. \"But you don't have a girlfriend.\"","\"That's true, but people without girlfriends can still have love.\"","\"Okay,\" Mu Mian remembered poor Lin Consultant and warned Fang Rui, \"But love without a girlfriend means you can't get married. You'll be lonely forever. Like Lin Consultant. You'll be pitiful.\"","Fang Rui looked at Mu Mian very seriously. \"That's why I have to work hard to make her fall in love with me.\"","\"Fang Rui, it's okay if she can't fall in love with you. I won't get married either. My sister will die before me, so I'll definitely end up alone in my old age. I can keep you company then.\" Mu Mian smiled at Fang Rui.","Fang Rui smiled too. It was okay if Mu Mian couldn't fall in love with him, as long as she was willing to stay by his side forever.","As they passed by the Jiangzhou Grand Hotel, Fang Rui saw police officers and security guards restraining a bruised and battered man.","Fang Rui stopped the car and asked, \"What happened?\"","\"This guy snuck into the hotel to steal. He took a set of jewelry worth millions. We caught him red-handed.\"","The man wailed, \"I didn't steal that jewelry! It was given to me by my daughter, Su Momo. I'm innocent! I'm not a thief! I can prove my identity. I really am the father of the famous star Su Momo. How can it be stealing if I'm taking my daughter's things?\"","\"The evidence is conclusive. We caught you in the act. No use denying it!\"","The police and security guards had already obtained proof of his theft and were taking him to the police car.","Fang Rui suddenly realized that Su Momo had set up a perfect scheme. Everyone who had been unkind to Su Momo received their corresponding punishment.","Su Momo wasn't just seeking revenge on her boyfriend; she was exacting retribution on everyone."]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Happy New Year","paragraphs":["After Su Momo recovered, she went to the police station to give her statement. She identified Qi Fang and Qi Fen sisters as her kidnappers, and her statement matched the sisters' confessions. The case was considered closed.","New Year's Day was approaching quickly.","This was Mu Mian's first New Year in Jiangzhou City. Chen Xue and the others insisted on taking Mu Mian to the square for the New Year's countdown. Even Zhang, who had a leg injury, came with his crutches.","The square was very lively at night, with various colorful lights flashing and beautiful, grand fireworks exploding in the sky.","There were far too many people in the square. Sounds came from all directions, making Mu Mian tense. She frantically tried to avoid people who were getting too close to her.","Fang Rui loosely embraced Mu Mian, shielding her from the surging crowd.","\"Mu Mian, let's leave this place.\"","\"But I promised Chen Xue and the others that we'd count down together.\"","\"Then come hide in my arms.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian reached out and hugged Fang Rui's waist, burying her head in his chest.","Fang Rui was stunned for a moment.","\"Fang Rui, help cover my ears.\"","\"Alright.\"","Nearby, Zhang winked at Chen Xue and whispered, \"See? My method worked, didn't it? They're hugging now, aren't they?\"","Zhang got cocky and nearly fell when he lost his balance on his crutches, but fortunately, Chen Xue caught him.","\"Chen Xue, I'm steady now. You don't need to hold me so tight.\"","\"I know.\"","Wang also hugged his girlfriend, \"Shu, I have social anxiety. There are so many people, I'm scared.\"","\"...\"","After the New Year's countdown event, Fang Rui drove Mu Mian home.","Through the car window, Mu Mian saw Shen Xiyin and Lin Sen walking hand in hand on the sidewalk. Colorful fireworks occasionally exploded in the sky, illuminating the entire night and her sister's radiant smile.","It had been a long time since Mu Mian had seen her sister smile so happily. Her sister used to love smiling. When Mu Mian was still not very responsive to others, her sister would smile brightly at her every day.","\"Fang Rui,\" Mu Mian's voice sounded a bit dejected.","\"What's wrong?\"","\"I might have to face a lonely old age sooner than expected,\" Mu Mian sighed.","Her sister's friends had warned her before that one day her sister would start a family with someone else, and there would be no place for her in that family. So she had to learn to be independent and take care of herself.","Sigh, she might be all alone in the future. But Mu Mian didn't like loneliness; she didn't want to grow old alone. She thought that if worst came to worst, she could negotiate with her sister and Lin Sen to let her sleep on the floor in their new home. She would only take up a tiny bit of space and promised not to disturb them.","Fang Rui also saw the couple outside the window. Not long ago, he had been mocking Lin Sen for his breakup, but unexpectedly, within just a few days, Lin Sen had won Shen Xiyin back.","\"Mu Mian, you won't grow old alone. Didn't you say you'd stay with me?\"","\"Yes, but what if you get a girlfriend too? Normal people like you will all get married.\"","\"I can marry you in the future.\"","Another huge firework exploded in the sky, illuminating the entire night.","\"That's not possible. We autistic people can't get married. My former therapist said so. This is what she told the parents of another autistic patient,\" Mu Mian imitated Ms. Mischel's tone, \"'If even you as parents can't love her unconditionally, how can you expect another man to love her, take care of her, and not abandon her? You're not fulfilling her love, you're just trying to get rid of a burden.'\"","\"She's wrong.\"","\"Fang Rui, you should believe the therapist's words. Ms. Mischel is the most authoritative autism therapist.\"","When Mu Mian got home, she found that Shen Xiyin hadn't returned yet. Mu Mian sat on the sofa, feeling a bit angry. Why didn't her sister tell her she had a boyfriend?","She was so tight-lipped, she wouldn't have told anyone. Did her sister plan to elope with Lin Sen and abandon her?","Mu Mian saw that everyone was sending New Year's greetings in the WeChat group. She also sent a carefully edited greeting, then decided to share this gossip she had discovered herself.","Mu Mian: [Shocked.jpg] Let me tell you all a little secret, it seems Lin Sen has a girlfriend now. He won't be growing old alone. Guess who his girlfriend is?","Chen Xue: Remove the \"it seems.\" Mian Mian, you actually think this is a secret? [Face palm.jpg]","Zhang corrected her: Mu Mian, why are you still calling him Lin Sen? You should call him brother-in-law now.","Mu Mian: ... Why do you all know about this?","Chen Xue: Comrade Mu Mian, you should reflect on why you didn't know about this.","Mu Mian: No one told me...","Mu Mian: @Fang Rui Did you know too?","Fang Rui: Yes.","Zhang: Did this need to be told? Couldn't you see it with your own eyes? Haven't you noticed that Lin Sen has been smiling radiantly every day for over a month now, which seriously contradicts his usual cold demeanor?","Lin Sen: @Mu Mian Yes, you should call me brother-in-law from now on. @Zhang Please don't excessively project yourself onto others. If you don't know what this means, please open your browser and search for it.","Mu Mian: Self-projection refers to the externalization of internal psychology, that is, judging others by oneself, projecting one's own emotions, will, and characteristics onto others, imposing them on others, and believing that others are the same. So Officer Zhang's strange smile over the past month can be described as radiant, huh?","Wang: I think \"licentious\" might be a more fitting description. Hehe.","Chen Xue: ...","Zhang: ...","Lin Sen sent several large red envelopes in the group chat, and then the word \"Congratulations\" flooded the screen.","When Shen Xiyin returned home, she was carrying a huge gift box. The box was grass green, tied with beautiful ribbons and a bow.","Mu Mian's eyes lit up when she saw the gift, \"Sister, is this a New Year's gift for me? I see my name on the card on the box.\"","\"Yes. Mian, Happy New Year!\"","\"Happy New Year.\"","Mu Mian excitedly opened the box. Inside was a SpongeBob SquarePants themed Lego set, including SpongeBob and his pineapple house.","\"Sister, how did you know I wanted this gift?\" Mu Mian liked SpongeBob because he always smiled sincerely at others, whether they were normal or not.","Shen Xiyin glanced at the SpongeBob band-aid on Mu Mian's forehead, just smiled, and didn't answer.","Receiving a gift she liked made Mu Mian feel less angry.","Shen Xiyin sat down on the sofa and said, \"Mian, your sister has a boyfriend now. You know him, it's Lin Sen.\"","\"I already knew that.\" Mu Mian eagerly started assembling her Lego set and curiously asked, \"Sister, didn't you say you wouldn't marry Lin Sen? Why are you with him now? Are you going to get married?\"","Her sister's friends often told her sister that she should get married. Mu Mian thought that for normal people, marriage must be a very important thing.","If her sister was going to get married, she would happily congratulate her, even if it meant she might be alone in the future.","\"Mian, I used to think the future was very important. If something was going to have a bad ending, it should be stopped in time and ended. But when you were kidnapped, I suddenly realized that the future is unpredictable and uncontrollable. We never know what will happen tomorrow. All we have is the present. I've always wanted to be with him, so I reconciled with him.\"","\"Will you marry him?\"","\"I don't know. The future is uncertain, anything could happen. But one thing is certain, your sister won't abandon you. No matter what happens, I'll be with you until you no longer need me,\" Shen Xiyin's voice was very firm.","\"Then you can't lie to me, okay? Deceiving autistic patients is unethical.\"","Mu Mian breathed a sigh of relief. She had been very worried that if her sister married Lin Sen, she would be abandoned. Just like her hacker friend, whose mother got married and abandoned him. He was very lonely for a while and almost imagined another version of himself to talk to. Fortunately, he later had her as a friend.","Mu Mian asked curiously, \"Sister, so do you and Lin Sen have love now?\"","Shen Xiyin smiled, \"Yes.\"","Mu Mian's face lit up with excitement, \"Then can you and Lin Sen accompany me to the psychology lab at Jiangzhou University?\"","Shen Xiyin frowned and asked in confusion, \"Why do you want to go there?\"","\"Sister, I want to study love too. I want to know how the brain of someone in love differs from a normal person's brain. That way, I'll know if I have love or not. Can you and Consultant Lin be my test subjects?\"","Mu Mian thought Zhou Junwei's idea of studying love was good, but his methods were too extreme. So Mu Mian designed her own experiment to study love.","\"Love is a very complex emotion. It can't be accurately defined by science, nor can it be quantified and studied. It's a combination of many emotional states. Xiao Mian, you can't study love, you can only experience it.\"","Mu Mian quickly finished assembling SpongeBob and started on the pineapple house. \"But other emotions can be studied. Fear, happiness, sadness... these can all be researched. Love must be possible to study too! I think Zhou Junwei is right, all human emotions come from the brain, so by observing changes in the brain, we should be able to see love.\"","\"Xiao Mian, why are you suddenly so interested in love?\"","\"You and Chen Xue both have love, and the forensic manual Forensic Doctor Cheng gave me has a large section describing love. It seems to be a very important thing. I think I should have it too. Zhou Junwei said that people with autism can have love,\" Mu Mian said. \"But first, I need to know what the definition of love is, what standard needs to be met.\"","\"Xiao Mian, that's not the right order. You need to experience love first, then you'll know what it's like,\" Shen Xiyin reminded her. \"Before encountering love, no one can accurately describe what it is.\"","\"Alright!\" Mu Mian finished assembling the Lego set and took a photo. She gave up on the idea of studying love.","Mu Mian sent a message to Fang Rui: [Photo attached] This is the New Year's gift my sister gave me. Isn't it pretty?","Fang Rui: It's very pretty, but don't you think something's missing?","Mu Mian: What's missing?","Fang Rui: Mu Mian, Happy New Year.","Outside, huge fireworks were bursting again, filling the sky with brilliant and dazzling flowers of light."]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: Flowers for Algernon","paragraphs":["The next day, when Mu Mian arrived at the office, she found several boxes piled on her desk.","\"Chen Xue, who put these things on my desk?\" she asked.","\"I think it was Captain Fang. He brought them over early this morning,\" Chen Xue came over and glanced at the boxes, shaking her head. \"Geez, he really doesn't know how to give gifts. He didn't even wrap them.\"","Mu Mian picked one up and looked closely. She realized they were several Lego sets, all SpongeBob SquarePants themed: Patrick Star and his rock house, Squidward and his clarinet, the Krusty Krab and Mr. Krabs...","Mu Mian finally understood what had been missing. The photo from yesterday was missing SpongeBob's friends.","Just like Mu Mian now, who was no longer the lonely Mu Mian she used to be. Besides her sister, she now had Fang Rui and many other friends.","Mu Mian corrected Chen Xue, \"Fang Rui is very good at giving gifts.\"","After Su Momo's disappearance case was closed, they had another quiet period.","Before the Spring Festival, Zhang's leg had finally recovered. Although the wound still hurt, he could basically walk now.","In the past, Mu Mian didn't celebrate the Spring Festival because it was just her and her sister at home, and they didn't need to wait for anyone to reunite. But the Spring Festival atmosphere in China was very strong, so Shen Xiyin decided to bring their aunt Shen Min back from the nursing home to celebrate together.","Mu Mian went to wait for Shen Xiyin at the psychology clinic where she worked, and then they would go pick up their aunt together.","The receptionist recognized Mu Mian and told her to wait in the lounge area.","\"Chen, I've tidied up the sand tray room. Can I leave work early today? It's my roommate's birthday and we have a dinner party,\" Mu Mian heard Bai Jing say as she came out of the sand tray room.","\"You're Xiyin's assistant, you should ask her directly about these things.\"","\"Dr. Shen will definitely agree.\"","\"Then it's fine.\"","Feeling Mu Mian's gaze, Bai Jing looked at her. \"Mu Mian, what a coincidence. Are you here to see your sister?\"","Mu Mian found it strange that Bai Jing was her sister's assistant. Wasn't she a social worker in the community?","Just then, Shen Xiyin finished her work and came to find Mu Mian. When Bai Jing saw Shen Xiyin, she immediately went up and linked arms with her, saying coyly, \"Dr. Shen, are you really not coming to Qiao Wan's birthday party? She really wants you to attend.\"","Shen Xiyin calmly withdrew her arm. \"I'm sorry, I don't have time.\"","\"Alright, but you must come to my birthday party next time, okay?\"","\"We'll see when the time comes.\"","Bai Jing left the clinic with her bag.","Seeing Mu Mian staring at Bai Jing's back, Shen Xiyin asked, \"Mian, do you know Bai Jing?\"","\"I do.\" Mu Mian thought for a moment and decided to warn her sister. \"She's a dangerous person. Sister, you need to be careful around her.\"","\"Most of the people I deal with at work are dangerous individuals. It's nothing unusual. Her dysfunctional family background has made her personality somewhat twisted and dark, but if someone is willing to guide her with care, she can become a normal person.\"","Shen Xiyin had also noticed that Bai Jing's personality had flaws. She might have paranoid personality disorder, but Shen Xiyin was willing to give her a chance. The purpose of psychological therapy was to help those with defects to grow.","Shen Xiyin drove Mu Mian to the high-end nursing home.","\"Mian, you go talk to Aunt first. I'll go meet with her attending physician to understand her condition and see if we can bring her home for a while.\"","Mu Mian nodded, holding a bouquet of flowers. \"Okay.\"","Shen Min was still sunbathing on the lawn. She held a book in her hand but wasn't reading it. Her gaze was empty, but not like that of a dementia patient. She looked more like a sage, quietly contemplating something.","\"Aunt.\"","\"You're blocking my sunlight.\" Feeling the sunlight being blocked, Shen Min's gaze fell on Mu Mian, and she smiled. \"Mu Mian, have you found my Momo?\"","Mu Mian was surprised that her aunt remembered her. But her aunt had forgotten that Momo was already dead.","\"I'm sorry, Aunt. I haven't found Momo yet.\"","\"Momo is a police officer with strong counter-surveillance abilities. It's normal that you can't find her. Spring Festival is coming, and my Momo will definitely come to see me.\" Shen Min said to a nearby caregiver, \"Nurse, can you help me get my photo album? I seem to have forgotten what Momo looks like. I need to refresh my memory.\"","\"Sure.\"","Shen Min asked Mu Mian to sit down beside her. They sunbathed together for a while. Just when Mu Mian thought Shen Min wasn't going to speak, she handed the book in her hand to Mu Mian. \"This is for you.\"","The book was titled \"Flowers for Algernon.\"","Mu Mian accepted the book. \"Thank you for the gift. I've already read this book. It's a soft science fiction novel. I think the premise is quite unrealistic. There's no surgery that can increase intelligence yet.\"","The novel described a brain surgery that could increase intelligence. Algernon was a white lab mouse that received the surgery and became as intelligent as a human. The male protagonist, Charlie Gordon, also underwent the surgery, gradually transforming from intellectually disabled to a genius. But this brought various troubles. He discovered how ugly and unbearable the real world was... He gained wisdom but also experienced various negative emotions.","When Charlie's intelligence peaked and began to decline, the experiment failed, and he eventually returned to his intellectually disabled state...","Shen Min said to herself, \"I can't let Momo become smart.\"","\"Why can't she become smart?\"","\"Because she will die.\"","Mu Mian was confused. She thought her aunt might be having an episode again.","After saying this, Shen Min closed her eyes and continued sunbathing. Her expression was peaceful, as if she was quietly waiting for her Momo to come see her.","Shen Xiyin watched Shen Min and Mu Mian from a distance. She didn't dare to approach, fearing that if she did, her aunt would remember the cruel reality. Perhaps, letting her aunt live in a fantasy was a good thing.","In the end, they didn't bring Shen Min home. Her attending physician didn't agree to let her leave the nursing home, worried that she might lose control of her behavior and do something destructive.","On New Year's Eve, Mu Mian thought the dinner would be like before, just her and her sister. But then the doorbell rang.","Shen Xiyin was cutting vegetables and said to Mu Mian, \"Mian, can you get the door?\"","Mu Mian opened the door to find Lin Sen standing there, holding a large bouquet of roses in one hand and a gift box in the other.","Mu Mian was stunned. Why was Consultant Lin at their house on New Year's Eve instead of staying at his own home?","Lin Sen handed Mu Mian a gift box. \"Mu Mian, this is for you.\"","Mu Mian was delighted to receive the gift. She hugged it, smiling brightly. \"Thank you, brother-in-law.\"","\"You're welcome.\"","Lin Sen saw Shen Xiyin in the kitchen and followed her in.","\"Xiyin, do you need any help?\"","\"I think I do. You know I'm not very good at cooking,\" Shen Xiyin glanced at Mu Mian, who was playing with her phone, and lowered her voice, \"Mian only cares about the shape of the food, not the taste. So my cooking skills haven't improved much over the years.\"","\"Then let me cook.\"","\"Alright, but I still need to cut the vegetables. Mian has strict requirements for the shape of various ingredients.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian was updating the latest gossip in the group chat.","Mu Mian: Shocked.jpg Do you know where Consultant Lin is right now?","Chen Xue: At your house! Let's skip this topic. Wang, didn't you say you were going to send red envelopes? Hurry up.","Wang: Oh, the network is bad. I can't send the red envelopes.","Mu Mian: Aren't you all surprised?","Zhang: Wang, how come your network isn't lagging when you're grabbing red envelopes? Come on, send the red envelopes!","Mu Mian private messaged Fang Rui: Fang Rui, why aren't they interested in gossip anymore?","Fang Rui: Maybe because they all have partners now...","Mu Mian: You don't have a partner. Why aren't you curious about why Consultant Lin is spending New Year's at my house?","Fang Rui: After Lin Sen's parents divorced, neither of them wanted him. He used to spend New Year's alone, occasionally coming to my house. Now that he has a girlfriend, he's definitely spending New Year's at her place.","Lin Sen came out with dishes and saw Mu Mian looking at him sympathetically.","\"Mu Mian, what's wrong?\"","\"Brother-in-law, you should come to our house for New Year's from now on.\" Mu Mian thought for a moment, felt that this logic wasn't rigorous, and added, \"Or I'll go to your and my sister's new home for New Year's.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian thoroughly enjoyed this New Year's Eve dinner. The presentation of the dishes perfectly matched her aesthetic taste, and the flavors were much better than usual. Mu Mian found it strange – how could the taste change so dramatically with the same ingredients and cooking methods?","If one could ignore the fact that Mr. Lin and her sister were constantly communicating through mind-reading, isolating her, this meal would have been perfect.","Mu Mian thought that her sister's friend might be wrong. Even if her sister had a new family, there would surely be a place for her in it.","After their thirty-fifth exchange of meaningful glances without speaking, Mu Mian silently complained that it would be nice if this new family were a bit livelier.","Mu Mian turned on the television to watch the Spring Festival Gala.","Not long after, Mu Mian unplugged the TV.","Good heavens, it was so noisy.","The Spring Festival Gala... was just too awful to watch!"]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: The Death of the Virgin: Dying with a Smile","paragraphs":["The Special Crime Unit had another quiet spell. They had been investigating only minor cases during this period.","One morning, the police received a report of a homicide at \"Star Home,\" a private welfare institution in the old town district.","Fang Rui and his team followed the navigation for a while, turning onto a bumpy small road. After several twists and turns, they finally saw two small buildings.","\"Star Home\" was located on the edge of the old town district, consisting of two three-story buildings and a large lawn. The entire complex was enclosed by high red brick walls, with the entrance being a black iron gate. The gate had colorful paint writing: Star Home.","The outer walls were covered with moss and vines, giving it a vibrant appearance.","Outside the walls was a large wasteland, unpaved with cement. It had rained the previous day, leaving the ground full of puddles.","\"Boss, there are footprints by the wall,\" Wang pointed to the muddy area not far away, which had many messy footprints. He estimated, \"That shoe print is at least size 42, looks like an adult male's footprint.\"","Fang Rui looked over and noticed mud on the wall as well, suggesting someone might have climbed over during the heavy rain.","Wang quickly went to collect footprint samples with his equipment.","\"Officers, you're finally here,\" Acting Director Chen Xinran greeted them at the door. She wore a black long dress, had shoulder-length short hair, and a cross on her chest. She looked young, but was actually nearly fifty years old.","\"Where's the deceased?\"","\"The victim is our director Zhang Xuemei. She died in her office, stabbed multiple times in the chest,\" Chen Xinran said nervously. \"There's blood all over the floor, it's terrifying.\"","She steadied herself and continued, \"Officers, I've locked that room and contained the news. I hope during your investigation, you won't tell the other children about Director Zhang's death. These children were very close to her, and they'll need time to accept this. I plan to have the teachers give them a lesson on the meaning of life first. Once they understand what death means, we'll break the news to them.\"","\"We understand. We'll keep it confidential from them throughout.\"","Director Chen led Fang Rui and his team into the welfare home.","The exterior walls were colorful, painted with many dreamy scenes: colorful whales swimming through clouds and stars, various colorful mushrooms waving on the ground, a giant wooden house filled with adorable children...","The interior walls were also covered in paintings, with childish brushstrokes lacking clear lines but bold in color use. The content was imaginative and full of creativity, likely drawn by the children.","Mu Mian quietly explained to everyone, \"That whale is called Alice, also known as the 52-hertz whale. Whales communicate with each other through sound frequencies, usually between 15 to 25 hertz. This one's voice is always around 50 hertz, meaning it can never contact its companions. It's the loneliest whale in the world.\"","Mu Mian used to be like this lonely whale, unable to find the frequency to connect with the outside world. But her sister found her frequency and connected with her. She was no longer a lonely whale.","Mu Mian once had someone create a 52-hertz sound. When her father took her to the beach, she put the recording in a drift bottle and secretly threw it into the sea. She hoped that the whale could hear this sound, so it wouldn't be so lonely.","\"Yes, that's why this whale can also represent autistic children,\" Chen Xinran observed Mu Mian for a moment and quickly realized that Mu Mian was also an autistic person. But Mu Mian was a fortunate autistic individual, at least able to work normally now.","\"Are all the residents here autistic?\" Mu Mian asked.","\"Seven or eight years ago, yes. That's why it's called 'Star Home,' because autistic individuals are also called star children. But now, with improved economic conditions and treatment options, it's rare for parents to abandon autistic children. So we now accept all kinds of children, focusing on those with disabilities.\"","At this moment, a handsome little boy came bouncing over. He said to Chen Xinran, \"Mama Chen, why hasn't Director Mama woken up yet? Woof, woof, blah blah blah,\" the little boy's neck twitched, and he made some strange noises. Then he scratched his forehead and continued, \"Didn't Director Mama say to sleep early and rise early? Woof, how can she lie, woof, and secretly sleep in? Blah blah blah.\"","While speaking, the boy made faces and occasionally let out strange noises, then continued talking.","Chen Xinran crouched down and explained to the little boy, \"Guoguo, Director Mama is sick. She needs to rest well, and you shouldn't disturb her, okay?\"","\"Okay. Mama Chen, I'll tell the others not to disturb Director Mama's rest,\" Guoguo nodded obediently. His neck twitched, but this time he tried hard to suppress his strange noises.","Guoguo thought these uncles and aunties were here to donate money or goods, so he wanted to leave a good impression.","Mu Mian looked at the little boy and asked, \"Does he have Tourette's syndrome?\"","Tourette's syndrome (also known as Tic disorder) commonly includes symptoms such as muscle spasms, involuntary movements, repetitive muttering, distorted movements, and facial muscle spasms.","Chen Xinran nodded, \"Yes. It's also because of this that his parents abandoned him at the train station. Later, the police contacted our director, and she, being very kind-hearted, took him in. He's a very smart and sensible child, with no intellectual problems, but because of this condition, he can't attend school. We tried sending him to school before, but he was bullied by classmates and teachers, so he had to drop out. The children here, for various reasons, can't live normal children's lives...\"","The institution housed over thirty children, ranging from three to twenty years old, all with various disabilities. At the moment, they were sitting on the lawn, drawing or playing with toys, with several staff members accompanying them.","The murder case hadn't affected their lives yet.","\"Sister Chen, it's terrible, Yuanyuan is missing,\" volunteer teacher Li Min ran over, saying anxiously, \"Could something have happened to him? He can't speak, so he can't call for help if he's in danger...\"","Chen Xinran's expression also became worried, \"Yuanyuan likes to hide in closets, have you checked there?\"","\"We have! We've searched the game room and rest area, but we can't find Yuanyuan anywhere.\"","\"Don't panic, go to the security room and check the surveillance footage to see where Yuanyuan is.\"","\"Okay.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Director Chen, do you need our help to search?\"","\"It's alright, Yuanyuan is an autistic child, and he often hides like this. Our place isn't that big, we'll be able to find him quickly with the surveillance footage.\"","Zhang Xuemei's office was on the second floor of the first building.","Chen Xinran unlocked the door with a key. As soon as it opened, Mu Mian smelled the scent of blood, then saw a woman lying in a pool of blood, with a knife stuck in her chest.","The woman's face was pale due to excessive blood loss, but her wrinkled face wore a kind smile, as if she hadn't been murdered but had died naturally.","Zhang exclaimed, \"This is too bizarre, why did she die with a smile?\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: The Death of the Virgin: The Bloody Boy","paragraphs":["The office was small but filled with various items: a large bookshelf packed with fairy tale books and several dolls; a wooden filing cabinet; a brown desk with books on autism intervention and files for all the children.","The room was tidy, with no signs of a struggle. However, the window was open, allowing rain to drift in and wet the wooden floor, leaving a puddle.","Fang Rui walked over. There were no security bars on the window; anyone could climb in once the glass was opened. There was a bit of mud and half a footprint on the windowsill.","Under the desk was a red, deflated balloon.","\"Hmm, it might have been a burglar,\" Chen Xinran said. \"I've been urging the director to install security bars, but she refused to save money. She said she was so poor that even if thieves came, they could only steal some books. I wish I had insisted on installing them for her.\"","\"Director Chen, what did you do before?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"I was an autism intervention teacher. About seven or eight years ago, I was a volunteer here, but as I spent more time with these children and grew attached to them, I decided to stay. I had a child before, but he passed away in an accident. I thought I could share the love I had for him with these poor children, and perhaps it would bring blessings to my child as well.\"","Fang Rui noticed something seemed to be missing from the desk. There were two circular marks, as if something had been there for a long time, but now those objects were gone.","\"Director Chen, what used to be in these two spots?\"","\"Here... I think there were two little pig dolls. Maybe a child gave them to her,\" Chen Xinran thought for a moment, then opened her phone and found a photo. \"Look, like this. This photo was taken when Director Zhang was interviewed by a reporter.\"","Fang Rui looked at the photo. The two dolls were about 20 centimeters tall, pink, and pig-shaped. Nothing special about them.","If there really was a thief, why would they steal such ordinary dolls?","Mu Mian noticed that the victim's eyes were wide open, staring at a particular spot. Mu Mian lay down beside her, following the victim's gaze, and saw the cabinet.","\"Mu Mian, the floor is so cold. Why are you lying down? You'll catch a cold.\"","Mu Mian reached out to Fang Rui, \"Fang Rui, give me a hand.\"","Fang Rui pulled Mu Mian up. Mu Mian walked to the cabinet and, wearing gloves, gently pulled open the cabinet door.","With a creak, the old door opened.","\"Ah, there's another victim?\" Zhang exclaimed.","A blood-covered little boy was revealed before them.","The boy wore a sweatshirt with a rainbow horse print. He had pitch-black, hollow eyes and looked like a frozen statue, showing no expression or movement.","Mu Mian checked his breathing, \"He's alive, not a corpse.\" She briefly examined his body with her eyes, \"No stab wounds, the blood isn't his.\"","\"Yuan Yuan.\"","The boy showed no reaction.","Chen Xinran rushed over and hugged the boy, \"Yuan Yuan, why are you here? Su Laoshi and the others have been looking for you for so long, they couldn't find you anywhere. She was worried sick. Yuan Yuan, what's wrong?\"","Mu Mian looked at Chen Xinran with disapproval, \"Acting Director Chen, you're contaminating potential evidence.\" Fearing she might sound cold-hearted, she added, \"If you want to hug him, at least put on a raincoat and gloves first.\"","\"Yuan Yuan is probably in shock. He used to be non-verbal, but he would react when he saw me. Now he's completely unresponsive, likely traumatized from witnessing the murder. We need to provide crisis intervention for him. I'm sorry, but I need to handle his situation first.\" Without waiting for Fang Rui and the others to agree, Chen Xinran ran out carrying Yuan Yuan.","Zhang looked at the bloodstains in the cabinet and came up with a shocking theory: \"Do you think it's possible that Yuan Yuan stabbed the director? The director, not wanting to scare Yuan Yuan, maintained a smile even as she was being stabbed. She didn't want to frighten him.\"","Although Zhang's guess was far-fetched, Wang and Chen Xue found it somewhat plausible. How else could they explain why the victim died with a smile?","\"Following your logic, it's also possible that the director knew Yuan Yuan was hiding in the cabinet, and she didn't want to scare him, so she kept smiling even as the killer stabbed her, trying to reassure Yuan Yuan?\" Fang Rui offered his own theory.","\"Ah, boss, your guess makes much more sense,\" Zhang said admiringly.","Mu Mian sighed, \"Eh.\"","\"Mu Mian, what's wrong?\" Fang Rui could tell from Mu Mian's smug expression that she was silently critiquing something.","\"Your guesses are so heartwarming. Your kindness limits your thinking, preventing you from considering other possibilities.\"","Fang Rui said resignedly, \"Mu Mian, why don't you just share your theory?\"","\"I won't. I only speak with evidence.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian examined the body's surface. The victim had been stabbed three times in the stomach and once in the chest. She also measured the body temperature, which was slightly higher than room temperature, about 25.2°C.","\"The victim likely died between 10 and 11 PM last night,\" Mu Mian said.","Fang Rui went to the security room to check the surveillance footage.","Old Liu, the security guard, was in his fifties, wearing a black brand-name tracksuit and looking energetic. However, he walked with a noticeable limp.","\"Officer, was it Director Zhang who... ? I didn't see her come in this morning. Unless she was sick, she would always be here to have breakfast with the children,\" Old Liu said, his face full of concern.","Old Liu didn't know how to operate the computer, so he let Fang Rui access the surveillance footage himself. As Fang Rui worked, he casually chatted with Old Liu, \"Uncle Liu, what kind of person was your director?\"","\"Our director was a top-notch good person. She used to be very wealthy, owning a KTV business. She was quite the female entrepreneur in the 90s. But her child was diagnosed with autism, and she nearly went bankrupt trying to cure him. Her husband was a useless freeloader who ran away when things got tough. She persisted in treating her child alone, but in the end, she couldn't save him. She lost sight of him for a moment, and he ran onto the road and was hit by a truck. Sigh, why don't good people get rewarded?","Afterwards, she established this welfare home, specifically for autistic orphans. Even children with parents who couldn't afford to raise them, she would take in. She even spent money to learn about autism intervention, just to better care for these children.","Later, Star Home became famous, and many companies and kind-hearted individuals donated to us. The director used the extra money to set up a charitable foundation dedicated to helping autistic children with their treatment. She was even selected as a moral role model in Jiangzhou City a year ago...\"","Old Liu went on and on about Director Zhang's achievements.","\"I was also taken in by her. I've had a deformed right foot since childhood and was abandoned by my parents. I grew up in an orphanage. As an adult, I couldn't find stable work and could only wander around this area, doing odd jobs to scrape by. Director Zhang took pity on me and let me work as a security guard, paying me over a thousand yuan a month. It's not much, but I get room and board here, so I hardly spend anything. She even bought me pension insurance, so when I retire, I can receive a few hundred yuan each month. She's truly a great person. I hope heaven opens its eyes and rewards good people.\"","Zhang listened with a moved expression and chimed in, \"Indeed, why don't good people get rewarded?\"","\"Uncle Liu, why is the surveillance footage from 8:05 PM yesterday to 9:17 AM today missing?\" Fang Rui interrupted their conversation."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: The Death of the Virgin: The Thief","paragraphs":["\"Officer, I forgot to tell you. Last night, due to heavy rain, there was a power outage. It started around 8 PM and power wasn't restored until after 7 AM this morning. The surveillance cameras probably didn't record anything last night.\"","Old Liu looked at Fang Rui and Zhang guiltily. \"But I guarantee, no one broke in last night. I didn't sleep at all because I was worried someone might come to steal things during the blackout.\"","The security room was clean and tidy, with a visitor log on the desk and neatly arranged folders. Earlier, when going downstairs, Fang Rui noticed that all the fire safety equipment in the building had inspection tags and had been regularly checked, with Old Liu as the inspector. It was clear that this security guard was very conscientious.","Fang Rui noticed the dark circles under his eyes and felt he probably wasn't lying.","He was about to leave when he spotted a pair of brand-name sneakers under Old Liu's bed, covered in mud.","\"Uncle Liu, did you go out after the rain?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"No! My legs aren't in good shape, so I don't usually go outside.\"","\"Uncle Liu, what size shoes do you wear?\"","\"Size 42. Why, do you have some shoes you don't want to donate to me?\" Old Liu asked excitedly. He rarely bought clothes, usually wearing discarded clothes from others to save money.","Zhang said, \"I also wear size 42. I have quite a few old shoes that aren't worn out, just out of style. If you need them, I can bring them for you. It would be a shame to throw them away.\"","\"That would be great, thank you! I don't mind. All my clothes and shoes are donated by kind people.\" Old Liu pointed to his tracksuit, boasting, \"Some are even brand names, you know.\"","Fang Rui pointed to the shoes under his bed and asked, \"Can I borrow those shoes for a moment? One of my colleagues' shoes broke.\"","\"Oh? Will they fit him?\" Old Liu hesitated, but quickly added, \"Sure, if your colleague doesn't mind.\"","Old Liu was about to grab the shoes, but Fang Rui beat him to it, picking them up.","\"Why is there so much mud on the soles? I don't know when that got there. Let me clean them for you first,\" Old Liu said nervously, trying to grab the shoes.","\"No need, we don't mind.\"","Outside the security room, Fang Rui placed the shoes in an evidence bag.","\"Boss, do you think the footprints outside were made by these shoes?\" Zhang asked.","\"Mm-hmm.\"","Fang Rui took the shoes to find Wang outside the wall.","There were many chaotic footprints near the wall, so Wang hadn't finished collecting evidence. Judging from the size and pattern of the footprints, they seemed to belong to the same person.","\"Wang, what size are the footprints?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"They appear to be size 42.\"","Fang Rui carefully examined the right footprint, which was very even. He compared the pattern of the footprint on the ground with the pattern on the shoes in his hand; they were identical.","The footprint in the mud was very even. If Old Liu had stepped in the mud wearing these shoes, the right footprint should have been uneven, as Old Liu limped and his right foot tilted to the side. The footprint should have been deeper on the right and shallower on the left.","\"Boss, these footprints are strange,\" Wang analyzed. \"Even if a normal person walked in well-fitting shoes, the footprints shouldn't be this even. Most people have their own walking habits, which should cause different depths in different parts of the shoe print. But here, all these footprints are very even, indicating that the person was applying equal pressure across the entire shoe while walking.\"","Zhang said, \"Does this mean the person has flat feet?\"","\"...It's not about whether the feet are flat or not,\" Wang pointed to the footprints. \"Look at these prints that are closer together; the person was probably walking faster. Shouldn't the prints in the mud be shallower? And those prints that are further apart, shouldn't they be deeper? But the depth is all the same, which doesn't make sense.\"","Fang Rui summarized, \"Like someone deliberately made these prints?\"","\"Exactly that feeling!\"","Zhang also caught on, \"Boss, could someone have stolen Old Liu's shoes to frame him?\"","Fang Rui walked around the wall again. He examined the mud on top of the wall; its color matched the mud at the base. A large patch of moss at the wall's base had been kicked off, exposing the bare wall. Nearby vines had also been trampled.","However, the moss and vines higher up the wall were undisturbed.","They also discovered an oval-shaped depression in the moss at calf height on the wall. There was a long skid mark on the ground.","\"Someone must have slipped and accidentally hit the wall, leaving that dent,\" Zhang said.","\"Judging by the size, it doesn't look like it was made by an adult male's knee,\" Wang analyzed.","Fang Rui called the power company and learned that there had been no power outage in the area last night. Nearby residents also confirmed there had been no blackout.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to check the electric meter again. It was normal, with no signs of tampering.","\"Who checked the electric meter at the time?\" Fang Rui returned to the security room to ask Old Liu.","\"Sister Chen went to check. She said the power was out because of the heavy rain.\"","\"Which Sister Chen?\"","\"Chen Xinran. Though the WeChat group just announced she's now the acting director.\"","Fang Rui went to examine the half shoe print on the windowsill again; its pattern matched Old Liu's shoes.","Chen Xinran was in the treatment room with some volunteers. Yuanyuan's condition was terrible; he had no response other than blinking. But when Chen Xinran and the volunteers discussed his condition outside the door, Yuanyuan quickly crawled into the toy cabinet.","\"Yuanyuan, we're Mama Chen and Teacher Li. Can you open the door, please?\" Chen Xinran crouched down and patiently spoke to the little boy in the cabinet.","Yuanyuan desperately held the cabinet door shut. They didn't dare use too much force and could only call to Yuanyuan softly from outside.","But Yuanyuan still held the cabinet tightly shut, not letting anyone open it.","Chen Xinran stood up, supporting herself on her knees, and said to the volunteer Li Min, \"Teacher Li, we can't do anything about Yuanyuan's condition. Please ask Teacher Jiang to come and see if she has any ideas.\"","Li Min nodded, \"I've already contacted her. She said she'd come as soon as possible.\"","Chen Xinran then turned to Fang Rui and his team: \"Officer Fang, I was dealing with an urgent situation earlier and couldn't properly receive you. I'm free now, shall we talk in my office?\"","Chen Xinran's office was also small but elegantly decorated, with calligraphy paintings on the walls and orchids on the windowsill. Her windows didn't have security bars.","Zhang thought to himself that if a thief really wanted to steal something, they should start with this office.","Chen Xinran poured rose tea for everyone.","Fang Rui specifically asked Chen Xue to come along. He gave Chen Xue a look, and she winked in response. Holding her cup of tea, she walked to Chen Xinran's side and pretended to accidentally spill tea on her skirt.","\"Oh, I'm so sorry, my hand cramped. Are you alright? Let me help you clean up.\" Chen Xue took out a tissue, appearing flustered as she wiped the skirt, but actually pulled up the skirt slightly, revealing Chen Xinran's knee.","Her right knee was bruised black and blue, as if it had been hit."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: The Death of the Madonna: Fatal Smile","paragraphs":["\"Director Chen, please come with us. There are some things you need to explain to us. For example, why did you try to disguise the crime scene as a burglary?\" Fang Rui said.","Chen Xinran's face turned pale. She instinctively retorted, \"Officer, what are you talking about? I called the police as soon as I saw the body. When would I have had time to stage the scene?\"","\"How do you explain the injury on your knee?\"","\"I fell when I was holding Yuanyuan earlier.\"","\"Where did you fall? Please show us. The surveillance cameras are working again now. We can easily check the footage and find out what really happened.\"","Chen Xinran gave up her attempts at deception and left with Fang Rui and his team. Before leaving, she appointed the volunteer Li Min as the acting director. Li Min was in her early thirties and was one of the more experienced staff members.","\"Li Min, please take good care of the children.\"","\"Where are you going, Chen? I can't handle this alone. You must come back as soon as possible.\"","\"Alright, I'll be back soon.\"","Back at the police station, Chen Xinran confessed to her crime.","\"Officers, I really didn't kill anyone! I don't know how Director Zhang died!\" Chen Xinran wrung her hands nervously. \"I needed a large sum of money. I asked Director Zhang to lend it to me, but she refused. So I had the evil idea of sneaking into her office to steal money. It was raining heavily last night, wasn't it? When I was checking the electric meter, I suddenly thought, if I could trick them into a power outage, there would be no surveillance, and I could enter her office to steal the money.\"","\"How did you know there was money in her office?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"She's loaded! What kind of person do you think our director is? A saint?\" Chen Xinran sneered.","Zhang replied, \"The newspapers say she's a selfless moral model. Although she has no children of her own, she's a good mother to many orphans...\"","\"Haha, only you would believe that! Do you know how much money kind-hearted people donate to our orphanage every year? The Jiangmiao Group alone donates millions every year. Where do you think that money goes?\"","Chen Xinran wore a mocking smile, \"It all goes into Zhang Xuemei's own pocket. She always brainwashes us with grand, empty words about charity and accumulating good karma, while paying us only two or three thousand a month. Meanwhile, she's raking in the cash. I just asked to borrow a few tens of thousands for an emergency, and not only did she refuse, she even lectured me.\"","\"Are you saying she's been embezzling funds all along?\"","\"You've seen our orphanage, just two small buildings. The children's living expenses aren't that high. How much money could it possibly cost? Where did the rest of the money go? Obviously into her own pocket.\"","Zhang said, \"But we didn't find any assets under her name, and there were only a few thousand yuan in her bank account.\"","\"Young man, are you naive? If you embezzled millions, would you keep it in your own bank account? You'd obviously convert it to cash and hide it. At the time, I suspected the money was hidden in her bookcase. She treasured that bookcase and wouldn't let anyone touch it.\"","\"So, did you manage to steal any money?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Of course not! I searched her study with a flashlight for over an hour. The bookcase was full of books, which I checked one by one, but I didn't find a single cent. Her office was surprisingly bare, with nothing of value. I had searched her dormitory before, but found no money there either. I really can't figure out where she hid all that money.\"","Zhang said, \"Could it be that she never embezzled any money at all?\"","Zhang had inspected Director Zhang's dormitory. The clothes in her wardrobe were old, some even yellowed from washing, but clean and tidy. The quilt and bed sheets had several holes, which were covered with embroidered flowers. She even refused to throw away broken coat hangers. Would such a person embezzle public funds? Zhang thought of a corrupt official from a TV drama and realized it wasn't impossible.","\"Was her office not locked at the time?\"","\"No, her office was never locked. I thought she was very bold, not locking the office with so much illegal money inside. Now I think that money probably wasn't in her office at all.\"","\"Please give us a full account of what happened.\"","\"The orphanage lost power after 8 PM last night. While Old Liu was on his rounds, I stole his shoes and made many footprints outside the wall. I even damaged some vines and moss to make it look like a thief had climbed over. I also left footprints on the windowsill. After doing all this, I searched the study with a flashlight for the illegal money. Around 10 PM, I heard movement downstairs, so I quickly slipped out of the office. Officers, I didn't steal anything. My actions weren't illegal, right?\"","Zhang reminded her, \"There's a charge called attempted theft. The specific sentence will be up to the judge.\"","Chen Xinran's face turned ashen.","Fang Rui asked, \"You said you heard something last night. What kind of sound was it?\"","\"It sounded like Director Zhang's footsteps, so I quickly left her office.\"","\"When did you discover she was dead?\"","\"Around 7 AM this morning. She usually gets up very early, but this morning she hadn't appeared for a long time, so I went to her office to look for her. That's when I found her stabbed to death. I was completely shocked.\"","Fang Rui remembered the two missing stuffed pigs and asked, \"Did you steal the stuffed pigs from her office?\"","\"Why would I steal children's toys? Those two pigs were so ugly, with their paint peeling off. What would I do with them? Probably some kid snuck in and took them.\"","Chen Xinran couldn't help but ask, \"I made so many preparations. How did you figure out I was involved?\"","\"You left too many clues. For example, those unnecessary footprints...\"","Before ending the interrogation, Fang Rui asked, \"Why didn't you get rid of Old Liu's shoes?\" It was foolish to try to frame Old Liu with footprints, given that he had a limp.","\"I did throw them away. I put them in the trash can. He's the only male in the orphanage, so I could only steal his shoes.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang exchanged a puzzled look. Why, then, had those shoes reappeared under Old Liu's bed?","At the next morning's meeting, Mu Mian reported the autopsy results.","\"The time of death was the night before last, between 10 PM and 11 PM on March 21st. The cause of death was excessive blood loss.\"","\"There was a hematoma with vital reaction on the occipital region of the victim's head, which was likely caused by falling to the ground,\" Mu Mian displayed photos of the deceased on the screen. \"There were four knife wounds on the victim's body, all made by the same weapon - the fruit knife found in the victim's chest. Based on the location of the stab wounds and the blood spatter pattern at the scene, we can deduce that when the killer stabbed the victim, she was lying flat on the ground and didn't resist.\"","\"Several fingerprints were found on the knife, all belonging to the same person. Judging from the size of the prints, they appear to be from a child,\" Wang said. \"I suspect they might belong to the little boy found at the crime scene. However, I haven't been able to obtain his fingerprints yet. The orphanage staff won't let us see him, saying they're afraid it might traumatize him.\"","\"Could Yuanyuan have killed the victim?\"","\"But Yuanyuan is only eight years old. How could he overpower Director Zhang and stab her to death?\"","\"Could Director Zhang have fallen and been knocked unconscious?\"","\"We also detected an overdose of nitrous oxide in her system,\" Mu Mian interrupted their discussion. \"This gas has a slightly sweet smell, mild anesthetic effects, and can cause laughter. That's why it's also known as laughing gas.\""]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: The Death of the Virgin: A Mother's Guilt","paragraphs":["\"Mu Mian, are you saying that the reason the deceased maintained a smile was because she was inhaling laughing gas before she died?\" Fang Rui asked.","Nitrous oxide has many uses. It can be used as an anesthetic or as a propellant for whipped cream. Although its production is regulated, it's not classified as a drug and is relatively easy to obtain. In recent years, there have been several cases in Jiangzhou City of disability and death caused by inhaling laughing gas, mainly among young people.","\"Yes. Her brain had already undergone pathological changes, so she had likely been addicted to it for some time,\" Mu Mian said. \"This gas tricks the brain into producing a feeling of euphoria while causing the facial muscles to lose control, forming an eerie smile. The deceased maintained her smile because of this gas.\"","Mu Mian continued, \"The murder weapon was an ordinary fruit knife. These knives are very common and sold in many department stores.\"","Fang Rui remembered Chen Xinran mentioning that the deceased had particularly treasured that bookshelf. Could that be where she hid the laughing gas?","\"Mu Mian, come with me to the deceased's office. Let's see if we can find where she hid the laughing gas,\" Fang Rui said.","\"Alright.\"","Fang Rui and the others returned to Director Zhang's office.","Mu Mian searched the office, and her gaze was quickly drawn to the red balloon under the desk.","The balloon was somewhat deflated and looked no different from an ordinary balloon. It had fallen under the desk.","Mu Mian picked up the balloon and slowly brought it to her nose.","Fang Rui, who had been searching the bookshelf, saw Mu Mian's action and rushed over to cover her nose.","\"Fang Rui, I can't breathe! I hate the feeling of suffocation.\"","\"Mu Mian, what were you trying to do?\" Fang Rui was exasperated. Balloons are the main tool for inhaling laughing gas, and it likely contained toxic gas. Mu Mian was really a handful!","\"I wanted to smell if it was cream-scented. Just a quick sniff, it wouldn't be a problem. It was originally used as an anesthetic...\" Seeing Fang Rui's darkening expression, Mu Mian quickly changed her tune, \"Alright, I'll take it back for testing.\"","Zhang quickly took out an evidence bag, letting Mu Mian put the balloon inside, and stated that he would keep it in his custody.","\"Officer Zhang, you don't trust me at all!\" Mu Mian complained, \"I'm a forensic expert, I wouldn't put myself in danger!\"","Fang Rui began listing Mu Mian's \"glorious\" deeds: \"Last March, you were taken to the roof by Chen Hui; last June, you got your hand scratched by Ye Zeling; you were also kidnapped by Zhou Junwei...\"","Mu Mian sheepishly changed the subject: \"Fang Rui, hurry up and collect evidence. Don't slack off during work hours.\"","Fang Rui looked at Mu Mian and said emphatically, \"Mu Mian, you can't do such dangerous things in the future, or I won't bring you along on investigations next time!\"","\"I didn't do anything dangerous... Alright, I promise!\" Mu Mian gave up arguing, \"Fang Rui, don't be angry anymore. When you're angry, I feel like the air pressure here is so low, I can hardly breathe.\"","\"...\"","Zhang held his head in his hands. Mu Mian had even learned to make jokes, albeit cold ones!","\"Boss, there's a fruit bowl over there,\" Zhang pointed to a bowl tucked away in the corner with several unpeeled apples. \"Could the fruit knife used to kill the victim have been in that bowl before?\"","Fang Rui noticed that one of the apples had been half-peeled. The killer might have picked up the fruit knife from the bowl and stabbed the victim. It was likely a crime of passion.","\"Possible.\"","The bookshelf was full of books, but Fang Rui's attention was drawn to several angel figurines on the top shelf. The angels were made of plastic, about a palm high, with white wings inserted in the back. The craftsmanship was crude, with unevenly applied paint.","Fang Rui picked up one of them, feeling that the weight was off. This type of plastic figurine shouldn't be so heavy.","He shook it and found that the figurine was hollow with an opening at the bottom. He pulled out the plastic plug and two small silver canisters fell out.","\"Found it,\" Mu Mian came over, picked up one of the canisters, and said, \"Laughing gas is usually stored in steel canisters like these.\"","There were seven angel figurines in total, each hiding small canisters inside.","They also found two notebooks disguised as books. The covers were fairy tales, but inside were handwritten pages. One was a diary, and the other seemed to be an account book recording the orphanage's income and expenses.","Fang Rui briefly flipped through the diary. Director Zhang used delicate words to describe her guilt and longing for her deceased son. She seemed to have never emerged from the shadow of her son's death.","The latest diary entry was written on March 19th, two days before the incident. It read:","\"Today marks 9,495 days since my child passed away. I dreamed of him again last night, he was covered in blood and waving at me. He asked me why I didn't save him. I didn't know how to answer him. I killed him. I could have saved him, but I was tired of those days of endless giving without any emotional return, tired of having to watch over him every moment. I had lost my own life, I was on the verge of breakdown.","If he had grown up and I couldn't move him anymore, couldn't change his diapers, what would I have done? A child like that, not normal, living would only be suffering... As I hesitated, that car killed my child. My poor child. It's mommy's fault, mommy didn't protect you! If mommy had another chance, I would rush to protect you without hesitation, even at the cost of my own life.","Child, if you really hate mommy so much, then take me away. Mommy is living in too much pain.\"","She mentioned multiple times in her diary:","\"The devil, it was the devil who tempted me.","She told me this thing could make me happy, but it doesn't. I'm still in pain. But I can't get rid of it anymore. I've already made a deal with the devil. If falling and sinking can let me see my child again, I'm willing to continue dealing with the devil.\"","From Director Zhang's diary, it seems she started inhaling this gas a year and a half ago, and someone deliberately lured her into depending on it. But her diary didn't name that person.","Who could it be?","Fang Rui then flipped through the account book, which detailed every income and expense clearly. Star Home received millions in corporate donations each year, but most of this money was donated through the foundation to other families with autistic or disabled children in need. From the accounts, the income and expenses basically balanced out.","Fang Rui speculated that the killer might have been trying to control Director Zhang through this method to gain benefits.","\"Zhang, take this account book and investigate to see if there are any issues with the accounts in it.\"","\"Alright.\"","After leaving the director's office, they passed by the treatment room.","Several volunteers and an elderly woman with graying hair were standing in the treatment room, all looking very anxious.","Seeing Fang Rui, Li Min came over and asked, \"Officer Fang, where did Sister Chen go? Why hasn't she come back yet? Yuan Yuan still refuses to come out of the cabinet. He hasn't eaten or drunk anything for two days. If this continues, he'll become dehydrated.\"","They tried to open the cabinet, but as soon as they did, Yuan Yuan would burrow deeper inside, hitting the cabinet walls without stopping, constantly banging against the wooden boards. His resistance was very intense, and they couldn't restrain him even with several people.","\"Hasn't a therapist come?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Teacher Jiang is an experienced autism intervention specialist, but even she is at a loss now,\" Li Min sighed, pointing at the elderly woman. \"Yuan Yuan's condition was already quite severe, and now that he's been traumatized, he's completely out of control.\"","Mu Mian recognized Teacher Jiang. She had dinner with her and her sister last time.","\"Little Mian, long time no see. What are you doing here?\" Teacher Jiang also saw Mu Mian and greeted her warmly.","\"Work.\"","Mu Mian looked at the tightly closed cabinet, seeming to see a lonely and helpless soul hiding inside.","\"Can I give it a try?\" Mu Mian said, \"The 52-hertz whale is unable to hear the sounds of other whales, unless it encounters another whale that can produce a 52-hertz sound.\""]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: The Death of the Virgin: A Common Frequency","paragraphs":["Everyone had left, leaving only Mu Mian and Yuanyuan in the cabinet in the treatment room.","Mu Mian tiptoed carefully to the cabinet and gently knocked on its door.","There was no response from inside.","Mu Mian patiently knocked again.","Still no response.","Mu Mian knocked for a long time until her hand grew tired. She thought that perhaps she and Yuanyuan were just not on the same wavelength.","With a creak, the cabinet door opened.","\"Hello, may I come in and visit your home?\" Mu Mian asked, tilting her head.","Yuanyuan looked at Mu Mian for a long time before finally nodding.","Mu Mian crawled into the cabinet and closed the door behind her.","The two of them were squeezed into the cramped space.","It was pitch black inside the cabinet, but for some people, a narrow, dark space is a source of security.","Next to the treatment room was an observation room with a one-way mirror that allowed a view into the treatment room. Fang Rui watched as Mu Mian crawled into the cabinet, feeling a bit worried. He wasn't sure if Yuanyuan was potentially aggressive, and if he were to harm Mu Mian, Fang Rui wouldn't be able to rescue her in time. He also wasn't certain if Mu Mian had claustrophobia.","\"No need to worry too much. I understand Yuanyuan's condition; he has a very good temperament and isn't aggressive,\" Teacher Jiang smiled at Fang Rui. \"Are you Mu Mian's boyfriend?\"","\"Not yet, I'm just her colleague at the moment.\"","\"She relies on you a lot.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Teacher Jiang, were you once Mu Mian's therapist?\"","\"Not exactly, although I did provide her with short-term treatment when she was very young. She had just been diagnosed with autism then, and she was like Yuanyuan is now – unable to speak and rarely responding to external stimuli. But she was very fortunate; her condition improved significantly.\" Teacher Jiang took out his phone, searched for a while, and found a photo. \"I have a picture of Mu Mian when she was little. Would you like to see it?\"","Fang Rui looked at the photo for a while. The young Mu Mian was a miniature version of her current self, but little Mu Mian's eyes were very vacant. She was quietly staring at the patterns on the floor, like a lifeless puppet.","\"Teacher Jiang, do you know Ms. Mischel?\"","\"Yes, she was also one of Mu Mian's therapists.\"","\"Why did she tell Mu Mian that people with autism can't get married?\"","\"Did she say that? That's impossible. People with autism can definitely get married. I have a patient who did. However, relatively speaking, fewer of them do get married.\"","About ten minutes later, the cabinet door slowly opened, and Mu Mian came out holding Yuanyuan's hand.","Although Yuanyuan's gaze was still blank and there were traces of tears at the corners of his eyes, he was no longer as resistant to people and things outside the cabinet.","\"Yuanyuan.\" Li Min ran over and hugged him.","Yuanyuan reached out and hugged Li Min back. He rested his head on her shoulder and soon fell asleep. He had been in a highly tense state for the past two days, and now that he had relaxed, he felt very tired.","\"Mu Mian, thank you for your help,\" said Teacher Jiang.","The other staff members also expressed their gratitude to Mu Mian.","\"Fang Rui, Yuanyuan told me through his drawings that the deceased was killed by a big red mushroom,\" Mu Mian walked up to Fang Rui and held up her palm, saying, \"Yuanyuan wanted to use magic to save her, but his magic failed. He was very sad and afraid that others would blame him, so he hid in the cabinet out of fear.\"","Fang Rui held Mu Mian's hand and looked carefully, but there was nothing on it.","\"Fang Rui, you're so silly! The drawing is in my brain, not on my palm,\" Mu Mian tilted her head and looked at him. \"Do you want to see it? I can draw it out for you.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian found some paper and a pen, and quickly drew a picture. There were many lines representing raindrops on the glass window, a woman lying on the floor, a huge mushroom above her head, and a little boy standing nearby holding a magic wand with a helpless expression.","\"I asked Yuanyuan what the mushroom was, but he didn't know. He might have forgotten, or maybe he just doesn't want to remember,\" Mu Mian sighed.","Teacher Jiang looked at the drawing Mu Mian had made and furrowed his brow. \"Yuanyuan must have witnessed the crime scene. The intense shock caused his memory to distort, and he reconstructed the scene in a fairy tale-like manner. It seems that only through hypnosis can we uncover the memory he has disguised.\"","Yuanyuan's emotions were still unstable, so they decided to wait until he recovered a bit before attempting hypnosis.","Fang Rui took the mud-covered shoes and went to question Old Liu, the security guard, again.","\"Uncle Liu, you picked these shoes out of the trash can, didn't you?\" Fang Rui questioned. \"You deliberately placed them in a conspicuous spot for us to find, right?\"","Old Liu didn't try to hide it and frankly admitted, \"Yes, I intentionally let you find them. This morning, I saw Chen Xinran go to pull the circuit breaker, and I felt something was wrong. I quickly checked around and found Director Zhang dead in her office. Director Zhang must have been killed by Chen Xinran! She has always coveted the director's position and had been spreading rumors before, saying that Director Zhang was embezzling funds. How could Director Zhang, such a good person, embezzle money? Later, I found my shoes in the trash can, which further confirmed my belief that Chen Xinran killed the director and was trying to frame me!\"","\"Why didn't you tell us directly at the time?\"","\"Who would believe the words of an old man like me? Chen Xinran is the acting director. If she found out I was tattling, she'd fire me immediately.\"","Old Liu became more agitated as he spoke, spilling everything about Chen Xinran, \"The reason Chen Xinran stayed here instead of leaving was to wait for Director Zhang to retire so she could take over this welfare institution and use it to make money. Chen Xinran even found a drunk boyfriend, and she had been borrowing money from everywhere to spend on that man. She must have killed Director Zhang to become the director.\" Old Liu's tone was very certain.","\"What was the relationship between Director Zhang and Chen Xinran like?\"","\"Pretty good.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Didn't Director Zhang know about Chen Xinran's ambition to take over? Didn't you tell her about Chen Xinran spreading rumors?\"","\"I told Director Zhang, but she didn't believe me! She thought I was stirring up trouble. I don't know why, but Director Zhang trusted Chen Xinran completely. Even when I gave her recordings of Chen Xinran badmouthing her, she still refused to believe Chen Xinran was a bad person.\"","Fang Rui suspected that the person who had been controlling Director Zhang with that gas was likely Chen Xinran. She hadn't told the truth during the interrogation.","\"What's Chen Xinran's boyfriend's name?\"","\"Zhang Damin. He runs a mahjong parlor in the nearby town.\" Fang Rui noted down the information about this person.","On the way back, Fang Rui curiously asked, \"Mu Mian, what did you say to Yuanyuan in the cabinet?\"","\"Nothing much. I thought he might feel lonely hiding in the cabinet alone, and if someone was willing to go in and keep him company, he might feel better.\" Mu Mian looked at the blue sky outside the car window, her voice very soft. \"The day my parents died, I also hid in a cabinet. The narrow space made me feel safe. I hid in the dark cabinet for four hours and seven minutes, but no one found me. My sister and the others were busy with other things. I came out on my own because I was too hungry...\"","Fang Rui was stunned. Everyone had wanted to pull Yuanyuan out of the cabinet, but no one had thought of going into the cabinet to keep him company.","Mu Mian continued, \"Fang Rui, Yuanyuan has several needle marks on his arm. Those shouldn't be from vaccine injections. I suspect someone has been abusing Yuanyuan. Yuanyuan also told me through his drawings that someone often pokes the children here with needles.\""]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: The Death of the Virgin: Abuse","paragraphs":["Back at the bureau, Mu Mian reproduced the other drawings that Yuanyuan had made.","The first drawing depicted: A little boy curled up in a narrow oval cabinet lying on its side, with several eyeballs embedded in the side of the cabinet. Outside the cabinet stood two monsters in long robes, their faces fierce as they stared intently at the boy inside.","The second drawing showed: A naked little boy lying on the ground, with countless hands reaching out from the walls and floor. Long, thin fingers held needles, all poised to stab into his body.","The third drawing portrayed: A huge room filled with many children, each with a bowl of beads in front of them. Behind them stood a hairy monster holding a spoon, seemingly forcing the children to swallow the beads.","After seeing these drawings, everyone felt a chill run down their spines.","\"Good heavens, could this be a coffin?\" Zhang pointed at the cabinet in the first drawing and said, \"Who puts cabinets on their side like that? This orphanage must be incredibly dark to abuse children in such a way.\"","The children at \"Star Home\" were closely monitored by the staff, making it difficult for Fang Rui and his team to interact with them alone, let alone investigate whether they were being abused.","Child abuse cases were not easy to investigate openly. Firstly, there was no substantial evidence, and if it turned out to be false, the orphanage would likely file a complaint against them. Secondly, even if child abuse was occurring, it would need to be handled delicately.","Star Home was not only home to over thirty children but also the hope for many families with disabled children. If a hasty investigation damaged Star Home's reputation and they couldn't raise charitable donations, many families would lose their support.","Fang Rui made an agreement with Teacher Jiang to bring Yuanyuan to her autism intervention center for hypnotherapy in two days. They could use this opportunity to conduct a full body examination on Yuanyuan to check for signs of abuse.","Zhang and Chen Xue were outside the classroom, secretly luring the mischievous Guoguo out with candy.","Although Guoguo had coprolalia, he was clever. He slipped out while the teacher was playing music for them, using the chaotic sounds to mask his uncontrollable outbursts and avoid detection.","\"Pretty sister, are you, woof, woof, going to give me candy?\" Guoguo struggled to control his tics but still made strange noises. He quickly covered his mouth, afraid of being disliked by Chen Xue and Zhang.","\"Yes, all these candies are for you,\" Chen Xue handed him a large handful of sweets. \"Guoguo, sister has some questions to ask you, is that okay?\"","\"Go ahead and ask, I'm honest Guoguo, I'll definitely tell you,\" Guoguo unwrapped a piece of candy and eagerly started eating.","Chen Xue first examined his arms. Apart from scars from vaccination shots, there were no needle marks or other scars.","Chen Xue breathed a sigh of relief and asked, \"Guoguo, does anyone stick needles into you?\"","\"When we get vaccines, they do. It hurts a lot. But Mommy Director says we have to get them, it's for our own good, to prevent diseases.\"","\"What about other times?\"","Guoguo's eye twitched, \"No needles. Except for Mommy Director's sewing needle, we don't have any needles at home. Woof, woof. Mommy Director uses her needle to embroider pretty flowers and our names on our clothes. Pretty sister, where did Mommy Director go, woof? I haven't seen her for many days.\"","Looking into Guoguo's sincere eyes, Chen Xue's eyes also grew moist. She said, \"Mommy Director went to a faraway place. She'll be back a bit later.\"","\"Then she shouldn't come back too late. I'm afraid I might fall asleep at night, woof, woof, and then I'd have to wait until tomorrow to see her. Woof, I'll try hard not to fall asleep. I stayed awake all last night, I wanted to wait for Mommy Director, woof, to come back.\"","\"Guoguo, what I mean is, Mommy Director won't be back for many days.\"","\"Pretty sister, how many days is 'many days'?\"","\"Sister doesn't know either.\"","\"Okay. Mommy Director must have her own things to take care of. We'll be good and wait for her to come back here.\" Guoguo said understandingly.","Chen Xue continued to ask, \"Guoguo, does anyone lock you in cabinets?\"","\"No. Mommy Director doesn't let us climb into cabinets. She says it's very dangerous, woof, if we get locked in, we might die if we can't get out. There are monsters in the cabinets, woof, that eat naughty children. But Yuanyuan can climb into cabinets, the monsters don't eat children like him.\"","\"Is Yuanyuan often locked in cabinets?\"","\"Yuanyuan likes to climb in by himself. He doesn't talk, so we don't know what he's thinking.\"","Chen Xue asked, \"Do they force you to eat strange things?\"","\"Yes. We're often forced to eat yucky carrot cubes and small green vegetables, and we're not allowed to spit them out after eating.\"","\"Have you eaten anything round, like beads?\"","\"You mean little tangyuan? They're delicious. But Mommy Director says we can't eat too many, glutinous rice is hard to digest.\"","Chen Xue and Zhang discovered that there didn't seem to be any child abuse occurring at the orphanage, and the deceased Director Zhang appeared to be a very loving person.","Zhang asked, \"Guoguo, have you always lived here? Do you go anywhere else to play?\"","\"I've always lived here, but Yuanyuan, Xiao Bai, Zhu Zhu, and others go somewhere else with Mommy Director. I don't know where.\"","Zhang remembered that these children all had autism.","\"Alright, Guoguo, thank you. Please don't tell anyone that we talked to you, okay?\"","Guoguo looked troubled at the large pile of candy in his hands, \"Okay. Can I share the candy with the other kids?\"","\"Of course you can.\"","As Chen Xue and Zhang were about to leave, they found Guoguo tugging at their clothes. \"Pretty sister.\"","\"What is it, Guoguo?\"","\"They said my mom went to a faraway place. I kept waiting, waiting for many years, but she never came back to find me. Later they said my mom had died. Is Mommy Director also dead? Is that why she's not coming back?\"","Chen Xue didn't know how to answer this question. She gently hugged Guoguo.","The results of the financial investigation into \"Star Home\" came out quickly. All donations to \"Star Home\" went through official accounts, and most of the outgoing funds were transferred to foundations under \"Star Home's\" name.","Director Zhang had previously been in business and kept very clear accounts. The destination of every transfer could be traced.","She didn't own any property, nor had she ever rented a house. She had always lived in the orphanage's dormitory. No valuable items or cash were found in her office or living quarters.","From the financial records, it appeared that Director Zhang had not embezzled any public funds.","Director Zhang's phone has not been found to this day. The police searched the entire orphanage but couldn't find the missing phone. Director Zhang rarely used computers, and no suspicious clues were found on her computer.","The diary found at the scene was confirmed through handwriting analysis to be written by Director Zhang, and based on ink analysis, the actual writing times mostly matched the dates written on the paper.","The diary entries began ten years ago. She didn't write frequently, sometimes writing one entry every month or two, and the entries were not long.","After reading her diary, everyone felt that although Director Zhang couldn't shake off the psychological shadow of her son's death, she had redirected her attention to other autistic children. By taking care of them, she filled the void and found inner peace for a long time.","Everything changed a year and a half ago. At that time, Director Zhang seemed to be facing some difficult choices. She began to frequently think about her deceased son, wrote in her diary more often, and her mental state deteriorated."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: The Death of the Virgin: The Dark Side","paragraphs":["\"Director Zhang was truly a selfless and devoted person,\" Zhang said with tears in his eyes after reading the diary. \"To make up for the guilt she felt towards her son, she treated all the other autistic children as if they were her own. It's so admirable.\"","Chen Xue nodded in agreement: \"Indeed. And she only used nitrous oxide to ease her own pain a little. Chen Xinran is just awful, spreading rumors everywhere that she embezzled funds. That woman is too much.\"","Fang Rui and his team discovered that Chen Xinran's boyfriend, Zhang Damin, had previously been in rehab for drug addiction. He had also served time in prison for fraud, having been caught by police selling alum disguised as drugs to addicts. Due to the large amount of money involved in the fraud, he was eventually sentenced.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to Zhang Damin's mahjong parlor to find him. As soon as they showed their badges, he took off running, but Zhang quickly tackled him to the ground.","Zhang Damin tried to defend himself: \"Officers, this is just a legitimate mahjong parlor.\"","\"If it's legitimate, why did you run?\"","\"Well, I've developed a conditioned response from being arrested before. I'd run with my tail between my legs even if I just heard a police siren on the street.\" Zhang Damin said glibly, rubbing his bald head.","\"You know Chen Xinran, don't you?\"","\"Yeah. That old woman won't leave me alone. If she didn't keep giving me money, I wouldn't give her the time of day.\"","\"We've arrested her. During questioning, she revealed some things about you,\" Fang Rui said.","\"That old woman confessed? Is she trying to pin this on me?\" Zhang Damin said angrily. \"How dare she try to blame me for her own misdeeds!\"","\"Yes, she confessed everything.\"","\"Well, you still can't arrest me,\" Zhang Damin said smugly. \"I didn't ask her for money this time, so it doesn't count as a sale. You can't charge me with fraud!\"","\"So, you admit to providing nitrous oxide to Chen Xinran?\"","\"Officers, you already know everything, so why are you still asking?\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui handcuffed Zhang Damin to the doorknob. He and Zhang searched the mahjong parlor but found no illegal items. They did, however, find several phones and motorcycle batteries.","Seeing the pile of stolen goods, Zhang Damin's face reddened slightly. He tried to explain: \"Those... those were left here by people who lost at mahjong.\"","\"Lost? So you're running an illegal gambling den here?\"","\"No, no, they borrowed money from me and couldn't pay it back, so they left these things as collateral.\"","\"Oh, so who exactly left these items? Give us a list of names.\"","Zhang Damin's face fell. \"Officers, you already know everything, so why are you making me jump through hoops?\"","\"We want to see how you'll try to weasel out of this. It's the same old excuses every time. I'm tired of hearing it,\" Zhang sighed, digging in his ear.","\"...\"","After bringing Zhang Damin back to the station, he confessed everything: \"Six months ago, Chen Xinran came to me asking for drugs. I couldn't get the real stuff. If I could, I wouldn't have sold fake drugs before. At first, I thought about giving her some fake stuff to scam her for money. But an online friend told me he could get something legal, what you call nitrous oxide. So I had him get me some, and I gave it to Chen Xinran.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Are you sure it was six months ago?\"","\"Definitely. I had just been released from detention then.\"","\"Did she say what it was for?\"","\"They often make cakes at their care home. She said it was for whipping cream.\"","\"You just said she asked you for drugs, now you're talking about whipped cream?\" Fang Rui interrupted his nonsense. \"We've come this far, so stop wasting my time with your slick talk.\"","Zhang Damin shrank back, frightened. \"She wanted to frame the director of their care home. She used that stuff to ruin the director's reputation so she could take over as director. She promised me a lot of money if it worked out. But then she went back on her word and didn't give me a penny. Officer, since she didn't pay me, it doesn't count as an illegal transaction, right...\"","Fang Rui questioned Chen Xinran again.","\"Your boyfriend Zhang Damin has already confessed everything,\" Fang Rui said. \"You bought nitrous oxide from him to frame Director Zhang, didn't you?\"","\"Zhang Damin is not my boyfriend. He's the one spreading rumors to ruin my reputation. No, I never did anything like that! He tried to scam me and now he's slandering me.\"","\"He's in the next room. Do we need to bring him in for a face-to-face confrontation?\"","\"I... What he sold me wasn't nitrous oxide at all, just some empty bottles. He's a fraudster! He's framing me!\"","\"Fake? Then why was Director Zhang inhaling nitrous oxide before she died?\"","\"It wasn't me. I never gave her that stuff. How could she have it?\"","\"Director Zhang didn't embezzle funds either, did she? You spread rumors to destroy her reputation, right?\"","\"No! She really did embezzle money. She received a whole box of cash, at least several hundred thousand yuan, but it never went into the care home's bank account. I saw it with my own eyes, it couldn't have been fake!\"","Fang Rui noticed a hole in her story: \"Are you saying someone donated a whole box of cash to your care home? Does that seem logical to you? Donations are tax-deductible, who would donate in cash? Or are you suggesting someone bribed your director with a box of cash?\"","Zhang chimed in: \"Director Zhang is dead. Why are you still spreading rumors about her embezzling? Are you taking advantage of the fact that the dead can't speak?\"","\"I'm not lying this time!\" Chen Xinran slammed her hand on the table in agitation. \"Bring me my phone. I have evidence!\"","Zhang quickly brought Chen Xinran's phone.","Chen Xinran snatched the phone and found a video file in a hidden folder. She played it and held it up for Fang Rui and the others to see.","\"Look, isn't she accepting money?\"","The video was shot from a low angle, as if hidden. In the video, there was a large box of 100 yuan bills in front of Director Zhang. She casually checked if the money was real, then closed the box.","\"Director Zhang, now that you've taken my money, you must arrange everything as we discussed,\" said a haughty voice.","Fang Rui and Zhang both felt the voice was familiar.","\"I understand,\" Director Zhang said quietly. \"I don't have any other choice, do I?\"","\"Pleasure doing business with you.\"","The camera shook chaotically for a moment before finally settling on a cold face.","\"Isn't that Lin Qianjie's stepmother, Jiang Yun?\" Zhang exclaimed. He had a strong impression of Jiang Yun because Chen Xue had said she was Mu Mian's mother, but she had cruelly abandoned such an adorable child.","Fang Rui found it strange. Jiang Yun was a typical businesswoman who put profit above all else. She wouldn't give money away for no reason.","Chen Xinran said, \"Officers, I'm not lying to you, am I? She really did embezzle funds.\"","\"When did this happen?\"","\"Six months ago. It was because of this that I saw through Zhang Xuemei's hypocrisy. She brainwashes us every day with her sanctimonious face, while behind our backs she's using these children to line her own pockets. If she can do it, why can't I?\"","Chen Xinran had been blinded by jealousy. Originally, she had been happy working at the care home. Even though the salary was low, she was willing to care for these disadvantaged children. She had even genuinely admired Director Zhang. But when she discovered Zhang Xuemei's true nature, she felt foolish for all her past efforts.","The police contacted Jiang Yun again, but her secretary said she was very busy and that any questions could be directed to her. However, no matter what the police asked, the secretary politely replied that she was unaware of those matters.","Fang Rui felt that Director Zhang's death was likely connected to that money."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: The Death of the Virgin: The Magic Wand","paragraphs":["The next morning, according to plan, Yuanyuan was to be taken to the \"Star Benefit Station Children's Rehabilitation Center,\" an autism intervention institution founded by Teacher Jiang, to undergo hypnosis to awaken his deeper memories.","Fang Rui, Mu Mian, and Zhang arrived at the institution early to wait for them.","\"Mu Mian, did you often visit places like this when you were young?\" Zhang asked curiously while looking around. This was his first time seeing so many children with autism.","Zhang had thought all autistic children were gentle and lovable like Mu Mian, but reality was different. Some autistic children could be aggressive, hitting others without reason, and forcefully throwing toys when angry.","Mu Mian shook her head, \"I didn't like going out when I was little. My father would bring therapists to our home. I met many therapists. Most of them were noisy and boring. After I grew up, my sister would often take me to various therapy centers and support groups, saying I might make friends that way. But it didn't work.\"","Mu Mian's tone was calm, but Fang Rui could hear the sadness in her voice. He remembered when he first met Mu Mian, she had said, \"I'm troublesome, I don't have any friends.\" The Mu Mian back then must have really wanted to have friends.","\"But now I have many friends,\" Mu Mian said with a hint of pride.","\"Yes, quite a few. Four of them, and I'm number four,\" Zhang teased.","\"...\"","After about ten minutes, two staff members from Star Home and the acting director Li Min arrived with Yuanyuan.","They let Yuanyuan sit in the rest area to play with toys while he adjusted to the unfamiliar environment. Yuanyuan seemed very familiar with the surroundings and showed no signs of discomfort. He sat obediently on the stool and skillfully began playing with the Lego toys on the floor.","Mu Mian pretended to build Legos with Yuanyuan while secretly examining his arms. Earlier in the cabinet, it had been too dark, and she had only felt unusual needle marks on his hands.","Both of Yuanyuan's hands had needle marks on the back, which appeared to be from blood drawing needles based on the wounds.","There were also needle marks on the inside of his wrists, likely from arterial blood draws.","There were many needle marks, and the wounds were fresh.","Why were they collecting Yuanyuan's blood? And judging from the number of needle marks, Yuanyuan must have been having blood drawn frequently. Otherwise, there would be no need to alternate between both hands.","Mu Mian shared this discovery with Fang Rui and Zhang.","Fang Rui analyzed: \"In Yuanyuan's drawings, there were many needles pointing at him. Could those be blood drawing needles? He's had blood drawn so frequently that he exaggerated the blood drawing scenes in his drawings.\"","\"That explains the third drawing too. The round beads might be pills. Could Yuanyuan be forced to take medicine every day? He hates taking medicine, so he drew the people forcing him as monsters,\" Zhang analyzed. \"But how do we explain the coffin? Why would Yuanyuan be locked in a coffin?\"","Mu Mian thought for a moment and said, \"When getting an MRI, you need to be pushed into an oval-shaped enclosed chamber. Could that oval-shaped cabinet be the MRI chamber? So Yuanyuan wasn't locked in a cabinet, but was getting an MRI scan.\"","If viewed in a medical context, all three drawings made sense. Yuanyuan hadn't been abused; he just misinterpreted medical examinations and treatments as abuse.","\"But Yuanyuan doesn't seem to have any physical illness, so why would he need injections and medicine?\" Zhang wondered.","Fang Rui asked one of the staff members.","\"Director Zhang said Yuanyuan was a bit anemic, so she took him to the hospital for a check-up. The doctor said the problem was serious, that Yuanyuan had anemia. Director Zhang was very concerned about this and often took Yuanyuan for follow-up visits...\"","\"If Yuanyuan really has anemia, why would doctors draw his blood so frequently? Aren't they worried about making his condition worse?\" Zhang questioned. \"And why would anemia require an MRI?\"","\"That's how hospitals are. They do all sorts of tests, necessary or not. Medical insurance doesn't cover these examinations, so hospitals just make excuses to do as many tests as they can. They're always trying to squeeze money out of common people.\" This staff member had lost a son to leukemia and had spent several years in hospitals with him, so she harbored resentment toward hospitals.","Zhang nodded in agreement. He remembered when he was hospitalized for his leg injury, he had undergone numerous tests - blood work, CT scans, everything. He had wondered at the time why he needed CT scans of his leg and head when he hadn't suffered any fall injuries.","When the Star Home staff went to accompany Yuanyuan, Mu Mian whispered, \"Yuanyuan's complexion is very rosy. He doesn't look like someone with anemia. They're lying.\"","Fang Rui thought about Jiang Yun again. She reportedly had a biological son who had never been seen in public. He had heard rumors that her son wasn't quite normal, which was why Jiang Yun kept him hidden. Could her son be autistic like Mu Mian?","The Jiang family owned many medical enterprises. Could she have made some deal with Director Zhang to use the children at Star Home for drug experiments?","Teacher Jiang took Yuanyuan into the therapy room, while the others went to the observation room next door, watching through one-way glass.","Yuanyuan's case was special. He couldn't express himself verbally, but fortunately, he was very good at drawing and could express his thoughts and emotional experiences through lines and colors.","Teacher Jiang handed Yuanyuan a piece of white paper and a box of colored pencils. \"Yuanyuan, I'm going to ask you some questions in a moment. Can you answer Teacher Jiang using the pencils?\" she asked.","Yuanyuan nodded obediently.","\"That day you saw Director Mom lying on the ground, right? Do you remember what she looked like?\"","Yuanyuan picked up a black pencil and first drew a person lying on the ground. The clothes and hair were simple sketches without detail, but the face was drawn very meticulously, down to individual eyelashes. The smiling face was instantly recognizable as the deceased Director Zhang.","\"What else did you see?\"","Yuanyuan took out a red pencil from the box and drew a large red mushroom above Director Zhang's head. It was enormous, even bigger than Director Zhang herself.","Using the black pencil again, he drew a window in the upper left corner with many rain streaks.","\"Where were you, Yuanyuan?\"","Yuanyuan used the black pencil to draw a little boy next to Director Zhang, then used a silver-gray pencil to draw a magic wand.","\"Yuanyuan, where did that mushroom come from?\" Teacher Jiang asked gently.","Yuanyuan pointed to the floor, indicating it grew from the ground.","\"Yuanyuan, where did your magic wand come from?\"","\"Magic wand... do you want to see my magic wand?\" Yuanyuan suddenly spoke, pronouncing each word slowly.","Yuanyuan looked up at Teacher Jiang. His face was pale, his pupils very dark, and when he stared directly at someone, his appearance was frightening.","\"Yuanyuan, you can speak?\" Teacher Jiang said joyfully. \"It seems the treatment is working.\"","Yuanyuan tilted his head and showed an eerie smile.","The next moment, Teacher Jiang felt a sharp pain in her chest. She instinctively touched it and found her hand covered in blood. Looking down, she saw a small knife stuck in her chest.","In that instant, Yuanyuan had somehow produced a sharp knife and forcefully stabbed it into her chest."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: The Death of the Virgin: Nightmare","paragraphs":["The people in the observation room were shocked, and Fang Rui immediately rushed into the treatment room.","Teacher Jiang was lying on the floor covered in blood.","Yuanyuan looked at his blood-stained hands, slowly extending his fingers to smear the blood over the painting, covering all the images on it.","It was a folding knife with a short but sharp blade. Teacher Jiang's wound wasn't deep, but she had lost a lot of blood, and her condition was serious. Fang Rui asked Zhang to call an ambulance to take Teacher Jiang to the hospital for emergency treatment.","\"Yuanyuan, what's wrong? Why did you stab Teacher Jiang?\" Li Min hugged Yuanyuan and asked softly.","Yuanyuan didn't respond, reverting to his autistic state where he only blinked without any other reaction.","They couldn't hear any sound from the observation room, only see their movements. They didn't know what Teacher Jiang had said to provoke Yuanyuan into attacking her.","\"Yuanyuan... he can speak...\" Teacher Jiang mumbled.","Everyone looked at Yuanyuan in shock.","He still appeared quiet and well-behaved.","\"Yuanyuan, tell us, why did you stab Teacher Jiang?\"","Yuanyuan didn't respond to her.","Fang Rui turned to Li Min, \"Why did Yuanyuan have a folding knife?\"","Li Min panicked, \"I don't know. We don't have such dangerous items in our welfare institute. When he came, we changed Yuanyuan's clothes. He couldn't have had something like that on him.\"","Teacher Jiang was sent to the hospital. The doctor said her injuries were severe, but currently not life-threatening. However, further observation was needed, and they couldn't rule out the risk of her condition worsening to endanger her life.","It was already afternoon when they returned to the bureau.","Mu Mian analyzed, \"When Yuanyuan stabbed Teacher Jiang, his lips moved slightly. Reading his lips, he seemed to be saying: 'Magic wand... Do you want to see my magic wand?'\"","\"Teacher Jiang's lip movements also seemed to be asking about a magic wand.\"","Fang Rui suddenly had an absurd guess, \"Could the 'magic wand' Yuanyuan mentioned be referring to the knife?\"","Zhang was about to say it was impossible, but then realized this guess made sense. The magic wand Yuanyuan drew was silver-gray and relatively short, very likely his fairytale version of the knife.","\"So, could Yuanyuan be the one who killed the victim?\" Zhang analyzed, \"No wonder Yuanyuan was covered in blood at the time. But how could an autistic child suddenly use a knife to kill someone?\"","Fang Rui said, \"So, it's very likely that an adult was manipulating him to kill.\"","\"The mushroom in that painting was red,\" Mu Mian suddenly said, \"We previously thought the mushroom represented the killer, but a red mushroom could also be that balloon. Yuanyuan saw Director Zhang inhaling laughing gas from the balloon. This time she might have overdosed and collapsed on the ground. Yuanyuan might have thought Director Zhang was poisoned by a toxic mushroom, so he picked up the fruit knife, wanting to save her. Someone might have told Yuanyuan that stabbing people with a fruit knife was magic, so Yuanyuan wanted to use this method to rescue her...\"","The blood spatter at the crime scene indicated that the person who stabbed Director Zhang was very short. They had suspected Yuanyuan before, but everyone still found it hard to believe that a quiet, well-behaved autistic child would kill someone.","Zhang said, \"Who could be the one who told Yuanyuan that stabbing people with a knife was casting magic? Could it be Chen Xinran? She seemed to have a good relationship with Yuanyuan, and she also had a motive for murder.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang interrogated Chen Xinran again.","\"Officers, I've already confessed everything I should. I've admitted my guilt honestly. Why are you questioning me again?\" Chen Xinran looked exasperated. She just wanted to face her legal judgment quickly and serve her sentence quietly.","\"What's your relationship with Yuanyuan like?\"","\"How is Yuanyuan now? He's such a timid child. Encountering something like this must have scared him terribly. Officers, please ask Li Min and the others to take good care of him. That child is so pitiful.\" Chen Xinran said anxiously.","\"Did you tell Yuanyuan that the knife was a magic wand that could be used to save people?\"","\"What knife? What magic wand?\" Chen Xinran looked confused, \"Why would I tell Yuanyuan such things? Yuanyuan can't understand fairy tales, so I basically never tell him fairy tales.\"","Chen Xinran's expression didn't seem like she was lying, but this woman was full of lies, and Fang Rui didn't quite believe her.","\"But his painting style is very fairytale-like.\"","\"Then I don't know about that. Yuanyuan was often taken out by Director Zhang to see therapists. His painting wasn't taught by us, but by outside therapists.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Do you know the names of those therapists?\"","\"I don't know. But they're all from Teacher Jiang's institution. You can ask Teacher Jiang.\"","Teacher Jiang was currently lying unconscious in the hospital.","After finishing the interrogation of Chen Xinran, Fang Rui went to Mu Mian's office to find her.","\"Mu Mian, do you think Teacher Jiang might also have been a target of the killer?\" Fang Rui quickly denied his own speculation, \"No, that's not right. How could the killer be sure that the one hypnotizing Yuanyuan would definitely be Teacher Jiang? If it was another therapist, wouldn't the killer have targeted the wrong person?\"","\"The killer might have set up a trigger word after knowing that Teacher Jiang would hypnotize Yuanyuan. Once Teacher Jiang triggered the keyword, Yuanyuan would stab her with the knife,\" Mu Mian speculated, \"But I don't understand why the killer would want to kill Teacher Jiang. She's a good person. That day when she invited me and my sister for dinner, I ordered a double portion of seafood rice, and she didn't say anything.\"","Fang Rui looked at Mu Mian helplessly.","\"Fang Rui, why do I feel like you're mocking me?\" Mu Mian said, displeased.","\"It seems that every person you've certified as good turns out not to be so good.\"","Mu Mian felt Fang Rui's criticism was reasonable. She indeed couldn't distinguish between good and bad people very well. But it wasn't her fault; those bad people were all quite nice to her.","\"So, what bad things could Teacher Jiang have done?\" Mu Mian wondered.","Fang Rui felt that the key word connecting everything was autism. Director Zhang was taking care of several autistic patients, Teacher Jiang was an autism therapist, and the killer was the autistic child Yuanyuan. But what could be the motive for the killer to use Yuanyuan to harm them?","Late at night, it started raining heavily again in Jiangzhou City.","Mu Mian had a nightmare. She dreamed that she had turned into a little red mushroom with long mushroom tentacles holding a magic wand, lying in a dark coffin.","Mu Mian hated this suffocating feeling. She struggled desperately, kicking open the coffin lid with her feet. She crawled out of the coffin and took a deep breath, but looking down, she realized the coffin was placed on a cliff, with a pitch-black abyss below.","In the abyss, as dark as a black hole, there were many faces - her father and mother, Jiang Yun, and her sister. They were all waving at her, wanting her to jump down and join them.","Mu Mian wanted to be with them, but the cliff was so high. Her fear of heights made her think that growing old alone might not be so bad after all.","At that moment, a hand reached out from the abyss, grabbing her ankle and pulling her down forcefully.","Mu Mian fell from the coffin. The sensation of falling was so real that Mu Mian could even feel the wind whistling past her ears.","\"Fang Rui, help! I'm so scared. Can you catch me?\"","Mu Mian suddenly woke up, finding herself drenched in cold sweat.","It was raining outside, a soft pitter-patter. Perhaps it was the lingering fear from the dream, or perhaps the sound of rain irritated her, but Mu Mian felt inexplicably uneasy.","It seemed as if something big was about to happen.","Mu Mian couldn't sleep, feeling restless. So she took out her phone and sent messages to all her friends.","\"Are you asleep? Come out and chat for five cents.\" This was what Zhang always said when he wanted to gossip. Mu Mian found it amusing and saved it. Today she finally got to use it.","Maybe everyone was asleep, as no one replied except Fang Rui.","\"Mu Mian, are you having insomnia again?\" Fang Rui was also having trouble sleeping. In the evening, Zhang's takeout discount coupon was about to expire, so he insisted on treating everyone to milk tea, but ended up giving Fang Rui a cup of black coffee. After drinking the coffee Zhang gave him, he couldn't sleep.","\"No, I woke up from a nightmare. It was so scary.\"","\"What nightmare?\"","Mu Mian briefly described the dream she just had. She said, \"Hey, it's all because of what Yuanyuan said. It made me have nightmares.\"","\"Mu Mian, since neither of us can sleep, do you want to come out... and watch the rain?\" Fang Rui's voice was a bit nervous.","Watch the rain? What a strange activity, Mu Mian silently thought to herself. But she desperately needed to do something to distract herself, anything would do, so she said, \"Sure.\"","Mu Mian changed her clothes and went out. Fang Rui was already waiting for her in the hallway. They walked downstairs together, but the rain was pouring heavily, so they could only stand at the entrance of the building.","It was pitch black outside, and they could only see the dense raindrops through the dim yellow streetlights. Fang Rui suddenly felt that watching the rain was a silly idea.","There were so many more romantic things to do, like watching a movie, strolling in a park, going on a trip, or even just taking a walk on a nice day would be more romantic than watching the rain.","The cold wind blowing on Mu Mian's face made her feel of unease subside a little.","At that moment, Fang Rui's phone rang. It was the operator calling.","\"Detective Fang, there's been a murder in the villa district downtown. The victim was stabbed multiple times. I've sent you the address. Please get there as soon as possible.\"","\"Alright.\" Fang Rui glanced at the address, his brow furrowing slightly. This address seemed to be Lin Qianjie's villa.","\"Fang Rui, let's go quickly. We should leave right away.\"","Zhang also called: \"Boss, you got the call, right? Whatever you do, don't bring Mu Mian to the crime scene! Keep it from her!\""]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: The Death of the Virgin: New Dead","paragraphs":["\"Officer Zhang, why won't you take me along?\" Mu Mian leaned towards the phone, complaining, \"I'm a forensic expert. How can you not bring me when a body has been discovered?\"","\"Mu Mian, why are you eavesdropping on the boss's phone call? Wait a minute, why are you two together in the middle of the night?\" Officer Zhang seemed to have stumbled upon some juicy gossip.","Fang Rui, not wanting to listen to Officer Zhang's chatter, hung up the phone. He had a good guess as to why. The victim was most likely Jiang Yun.","\"Mu Mian, you're very tired now. Why don't you go back to sleep?\"","\"No! I've figured it out. The victim is Ms. Jiang. It's nothing special, everyone dies eventually,\" Mu Mian's expression was calm. \"Fang Rui, let's hurry over there, or the body won't be fresh anymore.\"","\"Mu Mian, if the deceased is your relative, you need to recuse yourself,\" Fang Rui reminded her.","\"But she's not my relative, neither legally nor emotionally. I don't need to recuse myself.\"","\"Mu Mian, are you really not upset?\"","\"Of course not!\"","Fang Rui felt that Mu Mian was lying because her hand, tucked in her coat pocket, was clenched tightly. He sighed, realizing that Mu Mian had now mastered the skill of lying.","The call to the police had been made by Sister Chen, the Lin Family's housekeeper, and Uncle Zhang, the security guard. Sister Chen had discovered the body and was guarding the crime scene in the living room. The servants, chef, and family doctor were anxiously waiting at the main gate along with the security guard.","The servants, chef, and family doctor usually lived in the staff quarters next to the villa. They only learned about the incident when the security guard informed them.","Uncle Zhang approached them, \"Officers, it's terrible. Someone broke into the villa and killed Ms. Jiang. They've also kidnapped Yan Yan.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Who is Yan Yan?\"","\"Ms. Jiang's son. Yan Yan has autism. We must find him quickly. If he's traumatized, his condition could worsen,\" the family doctor said anxiously.","Mu Mian's hand clenched even tighter. So she had an autistic child. Why wasn't Yan Yan abandoned? Was it because Yan Yan's condition wasn't as severe? Was Yan Yan a smarter, more lovable child?","\"Where's the victim? Please take us there,\" Fang Rui said.","They followed the security guard into the villa. Upon entering the living room, they saw a scene of chaos. The floor was covered in ceramic shards, and a woman lay in a pool of blood. Her chest had been stabbed multiple times and was a bloody mess. Her face, usually stern and cold, now wore a smile. She was smiling, her wide-open eyes fixed on a certain spot.","Mu Mian saw clearly that the woman was indeed Jiang Yun. She had never smiled at her before, but now she was smiling so warmly, her eyes full of love.","Fang Rui and his team were surprised. Jiang Yun's manner of death was almost identical to that of Director Zhang.","They followed Jiang Yun's gaze to a bookshelf. The lower half of the bookshelf consisted of a row of cabinets.","\"Could there be another autistic child hidden in there?\" Officer Zhang speculated.","Mu Mian walked over, intending to open the cabinet, but Fang Rui grabbed her hand and pulled her behind him.","\"Mu Mian, he might be aggressive,\" Fang Rui said. \"Let me do it.\"","Fang Rui slowly opened the cabinet. Inside, curled up, was a blood-covered boy about fifteen or sixteen years old. He had very small eyes and a vacant stare, and he was tightly gripping a fruit knife. Sensing the light, he opened his eyes and stared blankly at them.","Mu Mian looked at Yan Yan. He wasn't cute at all. His eyes were very small, his mouth was very large, and his face was covered in acne. He didn't look intelligent either.","\"Yan Yan, why are you hiding in here?\" Sister Chen immediately ran over, but when she saw the blood on Yan Yan, she quickly stepped back, mumbling in horror, \"How could this happen? Yan Yan is such a good boy, how could he kill someone?\"","Seeing Sister Chen, Yan Yan raised the knife and obediently walked out of the cabinet.","Sister Chen was startled by his movement. She quickly hid behind Officer Zhang, shouting, \"Officer, help! Help! Is he going to kill again?\"","Yan Yan saw how scared she was of him and sadly lowered his head.","Fang Rui carefully gripped Yan Yan's hand and took the knife from him. Yan Yan was very obedient, offering no resistance as he handed the knife to Fang Rui.","Seeing this, Sister Chen approached again, feeling guilty. She crouched down and softly asked Yan Yan, \"Yan Yan, you didn't hurt your mother, did you?\"","Yan Yan nodded.","\"Then why were you holding the knife?\"","\"No... knife,\" Yan Yan struggled to squeeze out a few words. He pronounced each word with great effort, but his voice was muffled and unclear. Without careful attention, it was impossible to understand what he was saying. \"Ma...gic... wand! Mom... dead, I save her!\"","\"Who told you this was a magic wand?\" Fang Rui asked.","Yan Yan's expression changed instantly. He suddenly lunged at Fang Rui, opening his mouth wide to bite Fang Rui's arm. Fortunately, Fang Rui quickly grabbed his chin, and Officer Zhang swiftly moved to restrain him.","Once he realized he was under control, Yan Yan returned to his docile state.","\"Yan Yan has likely been hypnotized. 'Magic wand' seems to be the trigger word. When we mention it, they become aggressive,\" Fang Rui analyzed. \"So it will be difficult to learn from the two children who is actually controlling them to kill.\"","Sister Chen was terrified, frozen in place with shock.","\"Did Yan Yan's mother love him very much?\" Mu Mian suddenly asked.","\"Yes. Ms. Jiang was very busy, but she would set aside one day each week to come here, talk with Yan Yan, play with toys, and occasionally take him to the amusement park. However, due to Yan Yan's special condition, he wasn't well-suited to be exposed to many people, so Ms. Jiang never publicly acknowledged Yan Yan. She wanted Yan Yan to grow up happily. She was a good mother.\" Ms. Jiang was very generous to Sister Chen, paying her a monthly salary of 100,000 yuan, so naturally, Sister Chen had a good impression of her and only spoke of her virtues.","In reality, Jiang Yun didn't love Yan Yan that much. Otherwise, she wouldn't have left Yan Yan in this villa, only seeing him once a week. During their meetings, she would only give him gifts, rarely helping him bathe, eating meals with him, or reading him bedtime stories. She might have truly loved Yan Yan, but her love was purely material. Yan Yan didn't lack material things; what he lacked was companionship.","\"Why do you all call her Ms. Jiang? Shouldn't it be Mrs. Lin?\" Officer Zhang asked curiously.","\"Mr. Lin passed away five years ago. He left all his assets to Ms. Jiang and Yan Yan. After Mr. Lin's death, Ms. Jiang told us not to call her Mrs. Lin anymore. She said she didn't like that title and didn't want to be seen as a man's appendage. Ms. Jiang is a strong, independent woman. She has managed the company very well.\"","Fang Rui noticed signs of a struggle in the living room. There were bloody ceramic shards on the floor. This crime scene was slightly different from the one at the orphanage.","Mu Mian examined the body's surface. The victim had been stabbed ten times, and each wound was very deep. The killer must have used all their strength to inflict these wounds. She discovered a wound on the back of the victim's head where the scalp had been cut open. White ceramic fragments were stuck to the cut scalp."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: The Death of the Virgin: Dissecting Mom","paragraphs":["\"Based on the body temperature, the victim's time of death was estimated to be between 11:30 PM last night and 12:30 AM today. Similar to Director Zhang's case, analysis of the stab wound patterns indicates that the perpetrator stabbed the victim multiple times after she fell to the ground,\" Mu Mian explained, pausing briefly before continuing, \"There's also a wound on the victim's head with signs of vital reaction, indicating it was inflicted while she was still alive.\"","Zhang analyzed, \"So the crime might have happened like this: the victim was first knocked unconscious with a vase, fell to the ground, and Yan Yan, thinking she was dead, tried to use the 'magic wand' - which was actually the fruit knife - to save her, ultimately resulting in the victim being stabbed to death!\"","Chen Xue countered, \"But if the killer had already struck the victim with a vase, why not just kill her directly? Why go through the trouble of manipulating Yan Yan to kill her? Doesn't that seem unnecessary?\"","Fang Rui noticed vase fragments under the body as well. This suggested that either the vase broke first and then the victim fell, or someone had turned the body over.","Fang Rui asked Sister Chen, \"Were you in the villa tonight? Did you hear the sound of a vase breaking?\"","\"Around 11 PM, Yan Yan suddenly wanted to eat strawberry cake. I was planning to buy it for him tomorrow, but he threw a tantrum, and Miss Jiang always spoils him. So she asked the driver to take me to buy some. It was late and raining, so it took a while to find a shop that sold strawberry cake. When I returned, around 1 AM, I found Miss Jiang lying on the floor covered in blood, and Yan Yan was nowhere to be seen, so I immediately called the police.\"","\"Did anyone come to the villa while Sister Chen was out?\" Fang Rui asked the security guard.","\"I don't think so. After Sister Chen left, no one came in. Only Miss Jiang and Yan Yan were in the villa. It's possible a thief climbed over the wall to steal something. We have many cameras installed inside and outside the villa, you can check the surveillance footage.\"","\"Is it just you and Yan Yan in this big villa usually?\"","\"Yes, Yan Yan is very averse to strangers. The chef, cleaning staff, and family doctor all live in the servants' quarters next door. Yan Yan hates noise, so this villa has extra soundproofing. They probably couldn't hear anything.\"","Mu Mian found the smile on Jiang Yun's face disturbing. She covered her face with a white cloth, hiding the smile.","\"Mu Mian, could she have inhaled laughing gas?\" Fang Rui suggested. He wanted to tell Mu Mian that Jiang Yun's expression was just due to the effects of drugs, not because she favored another autistic child.","\"There are no balloons here, no small steel cylinders for laughing gas, and her facial muscles aren't stiff... It's not due to drugs. The reason is quite touching, just as you guessed earlier. It's because of love. She was afraid of scaring Yan Yan, so she smiled to comfort him, even though she was bleeding and in pain all over...\" Mu Mian's voice was calm, devoid of any emotion, but everyone somehow felt she was very sad.","Mu Mian had thought Jiang Yun just disliked autistic children because they were too troublesome, as few people like them. But it turned out Jiang Yun was so kind to another autistic child. It wasn't that she disliked autistic children; she just didn't like Mu Mian.","But why didn't she like her? Her dad, mom, and sister all said she was a genius, the most adorable child in the world. Ms. Mischel also said she was the best-recovering autistic patient she had ever encountered.","As Chen Xue and Zhang were about to comfort Mu Mian, she said, \"Let's hurry and get the body into the car. While it's still fresh, I want to complete the autopsy before dawn.\"","\"...\" Perhaps she wasn't so sad after all.","There were surveillance cameras at the villa's main gate, entrance, and near the bookshelf on the first floor, but the spot where Jiang Yun was killed happened to be in a blind spot. Fang Rui and his team spent the whole night reviewing the footage, but it showed no one had broken into the villa.","The camera facing the floor-to-ceiling window near the bookshelf showed Yan Yan taking a knife from the coffee table at 11:41 PM. About three minutes later, he reappeared in the frame holding a bloody knife, pacing anxiously before disappearing from view.","\"Could it be that Yan Yan first hit the victim with the vase, then stabbed her to death with the knife?\" Zhang speculated, \"With cameras at every entrance, this seems to be the only possibility left.\"","\"No, there are other possibilities,\" Fang Rui said.","In the autopsy room, Mu Mian calmly used a scalpel to cut open the victim's scalp, folding it back to reveal only a small subcutaneous tear with minor bleeding corresponding to the wound.","\"Mu Mian, this doesn't seem to be caused by a vase strike,\" Chen Xue analyzed, \"It doesn't look like an impact injury.\"","Mu Mian didn't respond. She took out the most expensive imported electric saw from the tool cabinet, one that could cut through bone without producing debris and was sharp enough to quickly saw through even the hardest bones.","\"Mu Mian, let me do it,\" Chen Xue reached for the saw, but Mu Mian avoided her.","\"Chen Xue, everyone dies. It's nothing special, just an inviolable law of nature. If her body must be autopsied, I want to be the one to do it.\"","\"But Mu Mian, you look...\"","\"Chen Xue, I'm a professional forensic pathologist!\"","Mu Mian switched on the saw and began cutting through the victim's skull. The blade spun rapidly, accompanied by a roaring sound.","Wearing light blue safety goggles, Mu Mian's expression was hidden from Chen Xue. But she remained professional, quickly and steadily sawing through the victim's skull.","Mu Mian removed the skull cap and cut open the dura mater, exposing the brain tissue. There was a small hematoma attached to the occipital lobe. A slight hematoma was also present in the corresponding frontal area.","\"It's a contrecoup injury!\" Chen Xue exclaimed, \"This head wound was caused by a fall. She might have fallen onto the vase fragments, which cut her scalp, making us think she was hit with the vase. No wonder I thought it was strange at the scene. If the victim had been struck with a vase before falling, based on the force analysis, she should have fallen face down. Also, that vase was quite thick; it shouldn't have shattered from just hitting someone.\"","Contrecoup injuries typically occur in falls, trips, or incidents like hitting one's head against a wall. It refers to bleeding and contusion in the brain tissue corresponding to the wound site, with similar injuries on the opposite side of the brain, but without scalp damage or skull fracture on that side.","This happens because when the head is in rapid motion and suddenly stops, the skull stops first, but the brain continues moving due to inertia, hitting the inner wall of the skull and causing bleeding and contusion on the opposite side. Contrecoup injuries are generally diagnostic of deceleration injuries to the head.","In the past, Mu Mian would have cut open the victim's body and meticulously examined all the internal organs, dissecting everything possible. But today, she suddenly didn't want to continue the autopsy.","The cause of death was clear, and the origin of the head wound had been determined.","Mu Mian carefully replaced the skull cap, returning all the tissues to their original positions. Finally, she took out a needle and thread and sutured the scalp back together.","Her stitching was perfect.","Jiang Yun's once sleek black hair had been completely shaved off, leaving her bald and unsightly. Mu Mian thought she should buy a wig later to put on Jiang Yun, which would hide the ugly, worm-like suture line.","But Mu Mian was exhausted. The wig would have to wait.","\"Mu Mian, are you very upset? Do you need a hug?\" Chen Xue asked.","Although Mu Mian had been pretending to be indifferent about Jiang Yun, Chen Xue knew she cared deeply about her birth mother. The reason Mu Mian had joined the Jiangzhou City Police Department in the first place was to use the internal ID system to find her mother's address.","How could she not care about the mother she had tried so hard to find?","\"Chen Xue, I'm very tired. I want to go home and sleep. Tell Fang Rui and the others that the cause of death was excessive blood loss. The victim fell; she wasn't attacked with a vase.\"","\"Do you want me to drive you home?\"","\"I've already called a car.\"","\"Alright, then get some rest!\" Chen Xue said, still concerned. \"Mu Mian, let me drive you home after all.\"","But Mu Mian had already left the autopsy room."]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: The Death of the Virgin: The Incident Process","paragraphs":["The investigation of the case quickly made progress.","Jiang Yun's assistant told them that Jiang Yun had installed many hidden cameras in the villa to monitor the work of the servants and prevent Lin Qianyan from being abused. These cameras were installed covertly, known only to the assistant and Jiang Yun.","The surveillance videos were uploaded to the cloud in real-time and could be viewed by logging into the account. Jiang Yun rarely watched these surveillance videos, and the assistant had almost forgotten the account password.","One of the hidden cameras captured the entire incident:","At 11:33, Jiang Yun walked over to the shelf. She wanted to pick up a toy from the floor but stepped on a glass marble and accidentally knocked over an antique vase on the shelf.","After regaining her balance, she intended to call the servant from the neighboring room to clean up, but after a few steps, she slipped on another marble and fell to the ground, hitting the back of her head on the broken vase pieces.","At this moment, Yan Yan saw Jiang Yun fall. He slowly walked over, ignoring her, and his first reaction was to pick up the glass marbles on the floor, about five or six of them, and put them in his pocket.","He kicked Jiang Yun's hand, and seeing no response, he took the fruit knife from the coffee table and violently stabbed it into Jiang Yun's chest.","Jiang Yun let out a painful cry.","Hearing her scream, Yan Yan revealed an excited smile. He stabbed her many more times, with blood continuously splattering onto his face.","Then he glanced at the camera on the bookshelf. He walked into the camera's range and suddenly changed his demeanor. He put on a panicked expression and deliberately performed in front of the camera before hiding in the cabinet of the bookshelf.","Jiang Yun looked in the direction he left, slowly losing consciousness, but she still managed to force a smile.","This surveillance video could prove that Yan Yan was the one who killed Jiang Yun.","After watching this, everyone felt chills down their spines. Yan Yan even had a smile on his face while killing his mother, and he deliberately performed in front of the camera. But he didn't know there was a hidden camera.","\"Could Yan Yan have been in a hypnotized state when he killed?\" Zhang speculated, \"Otherwise, it's hard to explain his bizarre behavior.\"","Although they had found the killer, similar to the case at the welfare home, Yan Yan's actions were likely instigated by someone behind the scenes. Otherwise, how could an autistic person suddenly stab someone?","Fang Rui asked Sister Chen again, \"Who has Yan Yan been in contact with recently?\"","\"Yan Yan rarely goes out. He doesn't have many friends. The only people he sees are just us.\"","\"Doesn't he receive treatment?\"","\"He does have regular intervention therapy. There's a therapy room upstairs. Teacher Jiang comes every Monday and Thursday to give Yan Yan treatment.\"","\"Are there no other therapists?\"","\"No! But Teacher Jiang occasionally brings assistants. The assistants are different each time, but they're all staff from her institution.\"","Fang Rui took away the surveillance videos from the villa. That person must have had close contact with Yan Yan, otherwise, they couldn't have controlled Yan Yan to kill. And that person had also been in contact with Yuan Yuan from \"Star Home\". The most likely suspect was still a therapist from Teacher Jiang's institution.","The entire second floor, except for Yan Yan's room, was therapy rooms. The decoration was almost a copy of Teacher Jiang's institution's setup.","Fang Rui and Zhang entered Yan Yan's room. The interior was very cozy, with stars and moons painted on the ceiling, light blue walls, and all furniture wrapped in foam to prevent Yan Yan from getting hurt.","Many drawings were scattered on the floor. Unlike Yuan Yuan's fairy tale style, Yan Yan's drawings looked creepy, mostly depicting mutilated human and animal bodies, such as a teddy bear with its eyes gouged out or a doll with its left leg severed. He liked black and red colors, often using these two colors to fill the background.","His drawings had no lines, composed of thick and chaotic color blocks, giving a strong sense of discomfort.","\"Has Yan Yan's drawing style always been like this?\" Zhang asked Sister Chen.","\"Yes, Yan Yan likes to draw, but I think his drawings are strange. Teacher Jiang said it's normal, that it's a post-modern art style. She even said Yan Yan has artistic talent and could become an artist in the future.\"","Fang Rui collected all of Yan Yan's drawings and put them in evidence bags. They also looked through Yan Yan's drawers, which were also filled with drawings of the same dark style.","\"Why are there photos of Mu Mian in his drawer?\" Zhang exclaimed, holding up a photo.","The photo showed Mu Mian waiting for a car at the entrance, seemingly taken secretly. Two large red crosses were drawn heavily on the photo with an oil pastel, and on the back was scrawled in red: Kill her!","\"Could his next target be Mu Forensic Doctor? He seems to particularly hate her,\" others chimed in.","Fang Rui put that photo into an evidence bag. He was a bit worried. Could the mastermind also hate Mu Mian? But Mu Mian didn't know them, why would they have such malice towards her?","Zhang found a cookie box under Yan Yan's bed. They opened it to find it full of torn-up drawings.","These drawings were completely different from Yan Yan's style. They were in a fairy tale style, with bright lines and pleasant color schemes.","Fang Rui casually flipped through the pieces of the drawings, his attention caught by a small whale. The shape and color of the whale were very similar to the one on the wall of \"Star Home\".","\"Isn't this the whale from the welfare home?\" Zhang asked, confused. \"Has Lin Qianyan been to the welfare home? No, did he draw these? The style doesn't match.\"","At this moment, Chen Xue's phone call came in: \"It's not good! Mu Mian is missing!\"","After Mu Mian left the autopsy room, Chen Xue was worried and, estimating that Mu Mian should have arrived home by now, called Shen Xiyin to ask if Mu Mian had returned home. Shen Xiyin said no. They waited another hour, but Mu Mian still hadn't returned home. At this point, they realized something was wrong.","Chen Xue tried calling Mu Mian, but she didn't answer. Later, Chen Xue discovered that Mu Mian's phone was left on her office desk.","But Mu Mian was nowhere to be found.","\"Yan Yan is tied up with restraints downstairs, he couldn't possibly harm Mu Mian. Could it be that the mastermind personally took action and kidnapped Mu Mian?\" Zhang said anxiously, \"Mu Mian is so unlucky!\"","However, Fang Rui felt that perhaps Mu Mian hadn't gone missing at all.","Although Chen Xue was panicked, her mind was clear. She first went to the security room to check the surveillance footage and found that Mu Mian hadn't left the police station at all, not even this floor. The hallway surveillance showed that after Mu Mian entered the forensic office, she hadn't come out.","But Chen Xue had been in and out of the office many times, and she hadn't seen Mu Mian inside.","When Fang Rui returned, Chen Xue reported this to them.","\"Could Mu Mian have some way to become invisible on the surveillance?\" Chen Xue speculated, \"Otherwise, how could she vanish into thin air?\"","Fang Rui looked down at the file cabinet behind Mu Mian's desk and said to Chen Xue and Zhang, \"You all go out first. I know where Mu Mian is.\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: The Death of the Virgin: Unloved","paragraphs":["Chen Xue and Zhang exchanged a glance. Where could Mu Mian be? Surely she wouldn't be childish enough to hide in a closet like Yuanyuan and the others? Then they realized their thinking was limited - Mu Mian very well could be in there.","After Zhang and the others left, only Fang Rui remained in the room.","He walked to the closet and noticed a bread bag on the floor. He smiled, realizing Mu Mian probably hadn't gone hungry.","Fang Rui knocked on the closet door. No response.","He knocked again.","\"Fang Rui, you're knocking on the wrong one. It's the closet on this side,\" Mu Mian said softly. \"That one's full of files, I couldn't fit. My legs were going numb so I switched sides.\"","Fang Rui opened the closet to find Mu Mian curled up inside, clutching a small pink bag - a gift from Jiang Yun that she had thrown away in front of her sister, but later secretly retrieved from the garbage downstairs after much searching when her sister wasn't looking.","Feeling the harsh light, Mu Mian turned away from Fang Rui.","Beside her were piles of small bread loaves and a bottle of water, as if she planned to live in the closet long-term.","\"Fang Rui, I don't want to come out yet. I'm thinking things through,\" Mu Mian said.","\"You don't have to come out. But Mu Mian, can you make some room for me to squeeze in and keep you company?\"","Mu Mian turned back, her eyes red-rimmed. She looked at Fang Rui in surprise, but he was already trying to get into the closet. Mu Mian shifted over and nodded, \"Okay.\"","Fang Rui was too tall and broad to fit easily. He struggled for a while but couldn't get in.","\"Mu Mian, what should I do? I can't fit,\" Fang Rui said sheepishly.","Mu Mian found Fang Rui's current state rather amusing - such a big guy desperately trying to squeeze into the closet, his head in but legs still out. The narrow closet simply couldn't accommodate him.","\"Fang Rui, you don't need to come in.\" Mu Mian shifted from inside the closet to its edge.","Fang Rui sat on the floor, leaning against the closet. \"I'll have to keep you company from out here then.\"","\"Fang Rui, I feel so guilty. I shouldn't be sad about Miss Jiang's death. At my parents' funeral, I didn't cry. I even snuck behind the tombstone and ate some of the offerings. I was so hungry. My Eldest Aunt caught me and said I was a cold-blooded monster. I didn't understand - she had wanted my father dead to take his inheritance, yet she cried so bitterly at his death. Meanwhile, I didn't shed a single tear.\"","Mu Mian recalled her first experience with a loved one's death. \"I told her everyone dies eventually, it's no big deal. She would die someday too; it's an unchangeable law of nature. She glared at me and ran away screaming. Everyone else looked at me strangely. That day, I realized I wasn't normal.\"","Jiang Yun's death had awakened Mu Mian's memories of that funeral. Her past memories were usually black, static, and colorless, but now they became more vivid, with color and movement. She even remembered her Eldest Aunt's twitching facial muscles and unpleasant body odor.","\"Fang Rui, should I have acted more upset at the funeral?\" Mu Mian asked guiltily. \"My parents were much kinder to me than Miss Jiang, but I wasn't sad for them. Now I'm grieving for Miss Jiang's death.\"","\"You must have been sad then too, you just didn't know how to express or understand your emotions,\" Fang Rui consoled her. \"If you weren't sad, why would you have hidden in a closet?\"","\"Fang Rui, I prefer how I used to be. Even when I was sad then, my heart didn't hurt. I could just hide in a closet, and my brain could control my emotions. But now I'm overwhelmed by this immense sorrow. I feel like I'm suffocating.\" Mu Mian felt panicked, not understanding what was happening to her. Logic told her she didn't like Miss Jiang, yet she was devastated by her death to the point of losing control.","Her logic and emotions were misaligned.","Mu Mian handed Fang Rui a photo. It showed a young Jiang Yun holding a baby, smiling with a loving gaze at the infant.","\"Because of that photo, I thought she loved me a little. I made up so many excuses to explain why she abandoned me, even though all her actions were so illogical. I still had hope. I thought she must have had her reasons, but today I realized I can't fool myself anymore.\"","Tears streamed from Mu Mian's eyes. \"She really didn't love me. It wasn't that she disliked autistic children - she just disliked Mu Mian. Even so, I still don't want her to be dead.\"","Fang Rui held Mu Mian tightly.","\"Fang Rui, why didn't she like me?\" Mu Mian choked out.","\"Some mothers just don't love their children. But it's not your fault, and it doesn't mean you're not good enough.\"","\"Mm, I'm a genius. Many people love me. It doesn't matter if she's not one of them,\" Mu Mian said lightly.","Shen Xiyin arrived after receiving Chen Xue's call. Standing outside the door, she watched Fang Rui embracing Mu Mian and suddenly realized that Mu Mian might have developed the ability to feel and express emotions like a typical person.","Everything changed when she started looking for her mother. Perhaps from that moment, Mu Mian had already begun to change. Her self-awareness had qualitatively developed, and she became curious about her origins, leading her to search for her mother.","Later, through a series of events, Mu Mian learned to lie and became curious about love. Today, she finally experienced a substantial emotional response to death.","Mu Mian was gradually becoming more like a typical person.","This was good!","\"Sister, don't misunderstand. This is just a normal comforting gesture,\" Zhang quickly explained.","\"Zhang, you're calling her 'sister' too!\" Chen Xue nudged Zhang, then promoted Fang Rui to Shen Xiyin, \"Sister Xiyin, are you satisfied with Captain Fang as a brother-in-law? He's a great person and takes good care of Mian Mian... Most importantly, Mian Mian really likes him.\"","\"I can see that.\" Mu Mian was starting to not need her anymore. Shen Xiyin felt both gratified and a little sad.","\"So you support them being together?\"","\"I support all of Little Mian's choices.\" That's why even knowing Mu Mian would certainly be disappointed after finding Jiang Yun, she still didn't stop her.","With Fang Rui's comfort, Mu Mian quickly composed herself.","\"Chen Xue, I'm sorry. I heard you calling me, but I was thinking things through and couldn't respond.\"","Zhang muttered quietly, \"But you responded to the boss, and he didn't even say anything, just knocked on the closet.\"","\"...\"","\"It's okay, I was mainly worried something had happened to you. Next time, let me know in advance.\"","\"Chen Xue, what could happen to me? I'm very cautious and won't easily have accidents.\"","\"...\" Zhang remembered the photo with the big X drawn on it. The accidents Mu Mian could have were far from ordinary!","Learning that Shen Xiyin was skilled in art therapy, Zhang figured since she was already here, they should ask her to analyze Lin Qianyan's paintings to see if there were any clues.","Zhang handed Lin Qianyan's paintings to Shen Xiyin. \"Dr. Shen, can you see if there's anything wrong with these paintings? We all felt very uncomfortable after looking at them.\"","Shen Xiyin flipped through the large stack of paintings, her brow furrowing deeper as she examined them. She said, \"If the artist of these paintings isn't suffering from schizophrenia, then he's very likely to have antisocial personality disorder.\""]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: The Death of the Virgin: Evidence in the Painting","paragraphs":["\"But he's an autistic patient,\" Zhang said.","Shen Xiyin asked, \"Who is the artist of the painting?\"","\"Lin Qianyan, Jiang Yun's son,\" Chen Xue replied.","Shen Xiyin paused as she was flipping through the paintings. She looked closely at that particular painting, then showed it to the others: \"Doesn't the person in this painting look like Mu Mian?\"","The content of the painting was: a girl lying in a pool of blood, her hands and feet had been cut off, the facial features were very clear, and it looked a bit like Mu Mian.","Everyone fell silent because it really did look like Mu Mian, and a photo of Mu Mian had also been found in Lin Qianyan's room. Lin Qianyan knew what Mu Mian looked like, so this certainly wasn't a coincidence. But they didn't understand why this autistic child would harbor such hostility towards Mu Mian.","\"Why would he paint me like this?\" Mu Mian complained, \"I've never offended him!\"","They reviewed surveillance footage for an entire day and finally discovered a suspicious person: Li Min, the acting director of \"Star Home\". Every few days, she would bring Yuanyuan along with Teacher Jiang to this villa. Sometimes Director Zhang would bring Yuanyuan over. But Yuanyuan came very frequently.","Li Min used to be a therapist at Teacher Jiang's institution. After resigning, she volunteered at \"Star Home\", helping autistic children with intervention therapy. She was very responsible in her work and was well-liked by the children.","\"Chen, what were they coming here to do?\" Fang Rui pointed at Li Min and Yuanyuan in the surveillance footage, asking the Lin family's housekeeper.","\"Yuanyuan came to keep Yanyan company. Miss Jiang was afraid he'd be lonely, so she occasionally invited children from the welfare home to come play. Yanyan didn't like those children, but he quite liked Yuanyuan.\"","Li Min was one of the few people besides Teacher Jiang who had contact with both children. Now that Teacher Jiang had been attacked, Li Min was the prime suspect.","\"But how can we prove that she induced Yuanyuan and Yanyan to kill? It's hard to leave evidence of verbal manipulation,\" Zhang sighed.","\"Indeed, and given Yuanyuan and Yanyan's special circumstances, and the fact that they're both children, even if they pointed out that Li Min told them the knife was a magic wand, this testimony might not hold up in court. We need substantial evidence,\" Chen Xue said.","Fang Rui first asked Zhang and Wang to go to the welfare home to get Li Min's drawings and handwriting samples.","He and Mu Mian stayed in the office to piece together the torn drawings.","There was a thick stack of paper scraps in the cookie tin. The drawings had been torn into very small pieces, making it difficult to reassemble them, but fortunately, Mu Mian was skilled at puzzles.","Fang Rui handed her the paper scraps, and Mu Mian matched their positions based on the shapes of the edges and the content on the scraps.","As each drawing was completed, they sealed it with laminating paper to prevent it from being messed up.","Working late into the night, Mu Mian and the others finally finished piecing together all the scraps, totaling thirty-nine drawings.","\"Finally finished. I don't want to do any puzzles for a long time, except for corpses,\" Mu Mian took off her gloves and rubbed her sore eyes. \"Judging by the painting styles, these drawings should be by two different people.\"","The drawings had already been separated into two piles based on technique and style. One pile was very thick, with thirty-five drawings, while the other had only four.","The thirty-five drawings were likely drawn by Yuanyuan, with an immature technique.","The other four drawings had a style similar to Yuanyuan's, both with a fairy tale style, fluid lines, and reasonable color combinations, but with mature drawing techniques.","Fang Rui picked up one of the four drawings. It was very sparse, with only a fruit knife drawn on it.","Another drawing depicted a hand holding a knife stabbing into a woman's chest, with splashing blood drawn as red magical effects.","Among the thirty-five drawings, there was also a similar one. The content of that drawing was: a boy holding a fruit knife, stabbing it into a woman's chest, but without any blood drawn.","The woman had a face they were familiar with.","Fang Rui invited Li Min to the interrogation room.","Li Min sat in the chair and asked in confusion, \"Officer, I'm not a criminal, is it necessary to take my statement in a place like this?\"","Zhang didn't answer her question, \"Miss Li, do you know Lin Qianyan?\"","Li Min thought for a moment and asked, \"You mean Yanyan? Yes, I know him. I occasionally bring Yuanyuan to play with him. His mother often donates to our welfare home.\"","\"Do you know what a magic wand is?\"","\"Why do you ask? A magic wand is used to cast spells.\"","\"If we found a more professional hypnotist to hypnotize Yuanyuan, do you think he would remember who told him the knife was a magic wand?\" Fang Rui said.","\"He probably would! But how can you be sure that what Yuanyuan says under hypnosis is the truth? Children love to lie, you know.\"","\"Miss Li, it was you who told Yuanyuan and Yanyan that the fruit knife was a magic wand, and that stabbing it into a person's body could bring the dead back to life, right?\"","Li Min displayed an expression caught between laughter and tears, \"Officer, your imagination is too rich. Those two children are autistic, but they're not stupid. How could they believe such nonsense?\"","\"What if someone made them see it with their own eyes?\" Fang Rui placed a drawing in front of Li Min. \"You personally demonstrated it for them, didn't you?\"","The content of the drawing was Li Min lying on the ground, with a boy stabbing a knife into her chest, but there was no blood from the wound. This knife was probably a retractable one.","\"This is a child's drawing. What can it prove?\" Li Min glanced at the drawing and quickly looked away, defending herself.","\"How do you know this is a child's drawing?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"I've studied art therapy, so I'm familiar with these things. Analyzing the lines, composition, and technique, this should be drawn by a child.\"","\"If that's the case, why didn't you recognize this as Yuanyuan's drawing? You spend a lot of time with Yuanyuan, couldn't you tell this was his work?\" Fang Rui continued to question.","\"Of course I can tell this is Yuanyuan's drawing. Officer, there's no need to dwell on these issues. Children's drawings often mix reality with imagination, they can't be used as evidence to deduce the truth of a case.\"","Li Min's tone was calm, as if she was certain Fang Rui and his team couldn't find any evidence.","\"If children's drawings don't count, what about an adult's?\"","Fang Rui took out the other four drawings and laid them in front of Li Min.","Li Min's pupils dilated instantly, looking at those drawings in disbelief. She had torn these drawings up and thrown them away, how could they appear here again? The garbage should have been disposed of long ago. Did the police dig these things out from the waste treatment plant?","\"The Technical Department has already compared them. The technique and the way the lines are drawn in these four drawings match your painting style. These four drawings were done by you.\"","Li Min leaned back slightly, saying calmly, \"Why couldn't it be someone else imitating my painting style? Technique is easy to imitate. Even works by famous artists can be imitated so well it's hard to distinguish the real from the fake. My drawings would be even easier to imitate. What can this prove?\"","\"But your fingerprints are also on these drawings,\" Fang Rui said."]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: The Death of the Virgin: The Truth","paragraphs":["Li Min was shocked and dismayed.","\"You can deny it, but if Yan Yan and Yuanyuan both identify you as the person who told them the knife was a magic wand during questioning the day after tomorrow, combined with these drawings as evidence, I think it will be enough to prove you're the murderer.\"","Li Min fell silent, her mind wrestling with inner conflict. Finally, she made a decision.","\"Enough. There's no need to torment these children anymore. I admit I did it. I wanted to kill Zhang Xuemei and Jiang Yun, those two devils. They were too cruel, using these autistic children for drug experiments!\" Li Min stood up excitedly, accusing, \"Yuanyuan was almost killed by them.\"","\"What drug experiments?\"","\"Jiang Yun's pharmaceutical company developed a drug to treat autism. The drug had passed animal trials, and the next step was clinical trials. That's when they set their sights on the autistic children at Star Home and those supported by Zhang's foundation. This drug's side effects were still unknown. If used long-term, the consequences could be unimaginable.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang fell silent. They had imagined many motives, but never thought Li Min killed to protect these children.","\"I can plead guilty and clearly explain the entire process of the crime, but as a deal, you must thoroughly investigate the drug trials conducted by the Star Benefit Station Children's Health Center and Jiang Yun Pharmaceuticals. If you don't agree, I won't say a word, and you'll never know the truth.\"","\"If there really were illegal drug trials, we'll definitely investigate,\" Fang Rui promised.","\"I started working at Star Home because of Director Zhang's inspiring story. I idolized her and wanted to be like her. I never imagined she would do such an evil thing for money. My spiritual pillar collapsed.\"","Li Min's brother was also autistic. When he was ten, he drowned in a pond due to her negligence. Li Min had always felt guilty about this, so she chose to major in special education in college. Director Zhang's story resonated with her, so she chose to follow her.","\"At first, I wanted to kill them directly. But why should I sacrifice my life for these two devils? Later, I realized that minors who commit murder aren't held criminally responsible, let alone autistic children like Yuanyuan and Yan Yan. So I told Yuanyuan and Yan Yan that the knife was a magic wand that could cast spells to save people.","No hypnosis was needed, just simple psychological suggestion. To make them believe, I pretended to faint, and then Yan Yan stabbed me with the prop knife I had prepared. I immediately opened my eyes and 'came back to life.' They believed what I said. But I didn't expect Yuanyuan to draw that scene, which became evidence to convict me.\"","Fang Rui looked at the torn drawing, frowning slightly, \"Didn't you tear up these drawings?\"","\"I didn't tear up this one that Yuanyuan drew. I know when he drew it. I tore up these four. At the time, drawing these pictures was to help them better understand how to use the magic wand. Later, I tore them up and threw them in the trash can in Yuanyuan's room. I didn't expect you to find them.\"","Fang Rui realized that someone seemed to have deliberately led them to discover these clues to convict Li Min.","Li Min described the details of the crime.","\"That rainy night, I found the power was out, which was the perfect opportunity for murder. I had Yuanyuan hide in Director Zhang's closet beforehand, telling him we were playing hide-and-seek, and he could come out when he heard a bang.","On the day Director Zhang's son died, it rained heavily. Under my inducement, she indulged in nitrous oxide to numb herself. She would inhale nitrous oxide whenever it rained. I had replaced her cylinder earlier, and this time the concentration was higher than ever. She quickly passed out. The sound of her falling attracted Yuanyuan, who picked up the fruit knife I had left nearby and stabbed Director Zhang.\"","\"Good children pick up trash when they see it. Yuanyuan picked up the nitrous oxide cylinder on the ground, just like Yan Yan would conscientiously pick up marbles on the ground.","Killing Jiang Yun was more troublesome because I couldn't get close to her. Fortunately, when Yan Yan asked me how to keep his mother from leaving, I told him that if he scattered marbles on the ground and his mother broke her leg after falling, she wouldn't be able to leave. He did exactly that, but after Jiang Yun fell unconscious, Yan Yan would use magic on her, killing this devil.\"","Zhang listened, feeling his scalp tingle. Li Min had actually used the children's innocence to commit murder.","Li Min sincerely pleaded, \"Officers, I've confessed my crimes in detail. Can you investigate those drug trials and arrest all those people?\"","\"We'll investigate this matter thoroughly. Do you have any more detailed information you can provide?\"","\"No, I only know the drug was developed by Jiang Yun's company, but I don't know the company name. However, Teacher Jiang definitely knows. She would assess the children who had been given the drug to see if their condition improved.\"","Li Min stood up and bowed deeply to Fang Rui and the others, \"I thank you on behalf of those children.\"","The media somehow got wind of the news and extensively reported on these two murder cases involving autistic children. They portrayed Yuanyuan and the others as evil children who killed their mothers, sparking online discussions about whether autistic individuals are prone to violence.","After Li Min's arrest, they changed their previous conclusions, defining Li Min as a devil and portraying Yuanyuan and Lin Qianyan as innocent youths who were induced to commit crimes. Netizens condemned Li Min en masse and sympathized with these two innocent young boys.","Yuanyuan might have been induced, but was Lin Qianyan really innocent?","Fang Rui recalled Lin Qianyan's expression when he killed, the photos of Mu Mian in his room, and the drawings he made. Shen Xiyin said he might have antisocial personality disorder. Fang Rui suddenly had a bold idea.","Lin Qianyan had been staying at the detention center for the past two days, not because he was being held, but because his nanny, Sister Chen, was too afraid to take care of him. To prevent him from suddenly becoming aggressive and harming himself or others, he was kept there.","Jiang Yun had previously made a will stating that if she died, all her assets would go to Lin Qianyan. She also designated her nephew, Jiang Yinian, as Lin Qianyan's sole guardian. Jiang Yinian had the right to manage all the assets, but he must ensure that he would take care of Lin Qianyan until his natural death.","Jiang Yinian drove to the detention center to pick up Lin Qianyan.","The prison guard had seen the news and knew that the young man in front of him was about to inherit all of the Lin family's assets. Seeing Jiang Yinian's impatient and displeased expression, he joked, \"You've suddenly come into a huge fortune, why aren't you happy?\"","\"So what? I've also inherited a lot of trouble. I don't need that much money, and I don't like having responsibilities forced upon me.\"","\"...\" Too pretentious!","The guard took him to see Lin Qianyan.","\"Cousin Yinian.\" As soon as he saw Jiang Yinian, Lin Qianyan excitedly rushed towards him.","Jiang Yinian held his hand back, saying impatiently, \"Lin Qianyan, I've told you many times, you can't hug me.\"","Lin Qianyan asked coldly, \"Then can Mu Mian hug you?\"","\"She wouldn't hug me.\"","Lin Qianyan said dissatisfied, \"If it were Mu Mian, you'd definitely let her hug you, right? You and mom both like her. She has a sister and so many friends, while I only have a cold and empty villa. This world is too unfair.\""]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: The Death of the Virgin: The Bad Kid","paragraphs":["\"Lin Qianyan, you don't need to compare yourself to Mu Mian. She was carefully raised by me and Xiyin. You'll never measure up to her. Don't you dare harm her,\" Jiang Yinian warned.","\"But your Xiyin doesn't want you anymore. And the excellent Mu Mian doesn't like you either. How pitiful you are,\" Lin Qianyan smiled coldly at Jiang Yinian. \"Cousin Yinian, we're the same kind of person. You have no right to look down on me.\"","\"Lin Qianyan, if you still want me to take you home, shut your mouth!\"","\"The truth is always hard to hear. If you want me to say nice things, don't provoke me! I don't want you to take me. I want Captain Fang and Mu Mian to take me home.\"","Jiang Yinian gritted his teeth and said, \"Lin Qianyan, don't cause trouble for me.\"","\"Cousin Yinian, whether you like me or not, you'll have to put up with me in the future to get the Lin Family's property. You'll get used to it.\"","Lin Qianyan turned to the prison guard, \"Hurry up and contact Fang Rui and Mu Mian to come here. They must arrive within an hour, otherwise I won't leave. I'll also sue you for illegally detaining a minor with autism.\"","The prison guard was dumbfounded. Was this really someone with autism?","Fang Rui received a call from the prison guard, first listening to his complaints, \"Captain Fang, you're so inconsiderate, leaving this troublemaker with us. You and Mu Mian need to come pick him up quickly, or he's threatening to sue us for illegal detention.\"","\"Didn't his family come to pick him up?\"","\"He says it must be you and Mu Mian, or he won't leave.\"","Fang Rui drove over with Mu Mian to the detention center entrance.","Lin Qianyan was already waiting there. Seeing Fang Rui park the car, he said to Jiang Yinian, \"Cousin Yinian, you can go now. I have something to say to Captain Fang and Mu Mian.\"","\"Suit yourself,\" Jiang Yinian glanced at Mu Mian, then looked away and drove off.","Fang Rui was shocked. He had guessed Lin Qianyan wasn't simple, but he didn't expect him to speak so fluently, unlike someone with autism.","Without waiting for their agreement, Lin Qianyan opened the car door and sat in the back seat.","Before Fang Rui could ask anything, Lin Qianyan spoke first, \"Drive. Take me back to that villa from before.\"","\"Won't you have nightmares if you go back there?\" Fang Rui mocked.","\"Of course not. You must be very curious why I can speak normally, right? I don't have language problems. When I was little, to make that nasty woman Jiang Yun and that beast Lin Ye talk to me, I pretended I couldn't speak. That way they would spend more time with me, teaching me to talk. As a result, the therapist assessed me as having delayed language development. They probably thought I was an idiot and stopped talking to me. Later, I just couldn't be bothered to talk to them, so I stopped speaking.\"","Lin Qianyan's tone was flat, but Mu Mian could still hear the sadness in it.","Mu Mian looked at Lin Qianyan with sympathy in her eyes. So Jiang Yun didn't love Yanyan that much either. Yanyan had it even worse than her; she had foster parents and a sister, her upbringing wasn't lacking in love. But Lin Qianyan only had himself; he could only pretend to be sick to get a little attention.","The former Lin Qianyan must have been very eager for love.","\"I don't have autism. I just developed much slower than other children, but those useless therapists diagnosed me with autism. But it doesn't matter, I don't like the outside world anyway. So I continued to pretend to be autistic. At first, it was to get their attention, later it was because I didn't want to go out. Now I find that the identity of an autistic person is quite useful.\"","\"Why are you telling us all this?\" Fang Rui asked, puzzled.","\"I want to prove that I'm more normal than Mu Mian,\" Lin Qianyan looked at Mu Mian, his eyes full of jealousy.","\"She doesn't love me either,\" Mu Mian sighed.","\"No, she loves you. I saw the photo. She was holding a baby, that was you. She was smiling, her eyes full of love. But she never smiled at me. She only had perfunctory love for me.\"","Lin Qianyan had always thought Jiang Yun was just cold by nature, but after finding this photo in her room, he completely broke down. It turned out his mother loved another child.","His father also favored his useless brother. Even though Lin Qianjie argued with his father every day and was always causing trouble outside, his father still loved him. The nanny who took care of him only treated him well for money. Even Cousin Yinian liked Mu Mian more, even though he knew Lin Qianyan was normal while Mu Mian was autistic.","No one was willing to favor him.","That huge villa was like a tomb where he was buried in loneliness, with no one caring about him.","When he learned of Mu Mian's existence from Cousin Yinian, seeds of jealousy took root in his heart. For a while, he desperately wanted to kill Mu Mian. But he soon realized that the one he should kill was that nasty woman Jiang Yun; she was the source of all misfortune.","Mu Mian comforted him, \"That's just an illusion. She said I was her nightmare; she didn't want to see me. She hated me very much.\"","Fang Rui felt that this woman Jiang Yun was truly sinful. She had never given love to either child, deeply hurting both of them.","\"She also said I was her nightmare,\" Lin Qianyan mumbled. \"She needed a son, that's why she had me.\"","\"You weren't actually induced by Li Min. You deliberately killed your mother, didn't you?\" Mu Mian asked.","Lin Qianyan's face showed a smug smile: \"Shouldn't you thank me? If I hadn't helped you preserve the evidence, you wouldn't have been able to prove Li Min's crime, right?\"","Fang Rui had already guessed that Lin Qianyan deliberately hid all the fragments of the paintings under the bed, waiting for the police to find them and ultimately prove that Li Min was the mastermind, which even Li Min herself believed.","\"That woman Li Min thought she was so clever. She thought I was autistic, so she tried to deceive me with those fake words. But autistic people aren't idiots; even Yuanyuan wouldn't fall for her lies. But Yuanyuan believed me. I made Yuanyuan believe that the knife was a magic wand that could save people. Yuanyuan said his orphanage mother loved him very much. I didn't have such a mother, so Yuanyuan couldn't have one either. His mother had to die.\"","\"Yes, I deliberately killed Jiang Yun. That woman was too annoying; she appeared once a week. I hated that woman very much. I had wanted to kill her for a long time. Li Min's appearance made me feel I could kill her in a cruel way openly. Li Min thought she was manipulating me to kill, little did she know I was the one manipulating everything. Autistic children don't actively commit crimes, so there must be an adult behind it. This way, even evil children can become innocent.\"","Fang Rui remembered Shen Xiyin saying that Yanyan had antisocial personality disorder. Now it seemed her judgment was very accurate. Yanyan had strong aggression, extreme self-centeredness, and no empathy. Who knows what negative impact such a child would have on society when he grows up.","But he was still a minor, and the law couldn't judge him.","Lin Qianyan glanced at Fang Rui's face-down phone. He took out a device from his pocket and boasted, \"This is an audio interference device. All the sound you just recorded has turned into noise. Did you think I said those things to leave evidence for you to catch me? I'm not that stupid. Besides, even if you had evidence, so what? The law can't judge an underage autistic person.\"","Fang Rui felt helpless; they really couldn't do anything about him.","\"Mu Mian, I'm smarter than you. I designed a perfect crime, and you've all been fooled by me,\" Lin Qianyan said proudly. \"Mu Mian, you're so pitiful. You don't have a mother anymore.\"","\"Lin Qianyan, that was your mother. The one who lost a mother is you,\" Mu Mian said softly. \"You also made Yuanyuan lose the orphanage mother who loved him. Yuanyuan was your only friend, and you hurt him. You've also lost Yuanyuan as a friend.\"","The smug smile on Lin Qianyan's face froze. He glared at Mu Mian fiercely, \"I don't need a mother, I don't need friends. I'm doing very well on my own.\"","\"Then why are you jealous of me?\"","Lin Qianyan didn't answer this question.","Fang Rui stopped the car, and Lin Qianyan got out angrily.","\"Lin Qianyan,\" Mu Mian called out to him, handing him a thick notebook. \"This is my social guide. It's for you.\"","Lin Qianyan glanced at the notebook, then shifted his gaze away and said to Mu Mian, \"I don't need it. Mu Mian, goodbye.\"","Lin Qianyan slowly walked into the villa."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: The Death of the Virgin: The Case Closed","paragraphs":["Based on the clues provided by Li Min, the police quickly located Zhanhong Pharmaceuticals, the pharmaceutical company developing autism medication.","However, Zhanhong Pharmaceuticals turned out to be a shell company. The legal representative wasn't a mainland resident, and the research staff developing the drug had already fled overseas. The entire company had become an empty shell, with even the laboratory stripped bare.","They had signed a drug trial contract with Star Home, which was properly formulated, and they had paid substantial fees for the trials. The parents of other autistic children participating in the trials had also signed contracts with the company, receiving generous trial fees and free autism intervention therapy. As a result, they had no intention of suing the company.","One child's mother said, \"Even if there's just a tiny hope of a cure, we're willing to try! They didn't force us; we volunteered for the trials! We would have done it even without payment, let alone with the substantial amount they gave us, allowing our children to receive free intervention therapy. They're not committing a crime; they're doing charity work.\"","\"Aren't you worried about side effects?\" Zhang asked.","\"He's already in such a terrible state, how could it get any worse? None of you have an autistic child, so you can't understand how we feel. Officer, please stop investigating. If that company really develops a drug to treat autism, I'd trade my life for it.\"","Fang Rui had originally planned to visit Teacher Jiang in the hospital to see if he could get any clues from her, but bad news came from the hospital. Due to a lung infection, her condition had worsened, and she had passed away the night before.","Her son and daughter had cremated her body early that morning and quickly divided her estate.","All leads regarding the drug had been cut off.","The murder cases at Star Home and the Lin family villa were officially closed.","\"There's still one thing unresolved,\" Fang Rui said.","\"What's that?\"","\"The money Director Zhang received has disappeared. But we haven't found it.\"","\"Could it be buried in the lawn?\" Zhang speculated. \"Should we go dig at the orphanage?\"","Since the murder, Star Home had been in a state of unrest, and Old Liu, the security guard, had become busier. After the murderer was caught, the orphanage got a new director, and Old Liu finally got a day off.","He deliberately changed into shabby clothes, carried a worn-out cloth bag, and limped to a poorly decorated gold shop.","He felt the pig in his bag, then looked around cautiously. Seeing no one paying attention to him, he slipped into the gold shop.","\"Boss, do you buy gold? Pure gold,\" Old Liu asked in a low voice, leaning in.","The shop owner looked Old Liu up and down and said, \"Yes, how much do you have?\"","Old Liu made a gesture for seven.","\"Seven grams?\"","\"Seven hundred grams.\"","The owner grinned, thinking this man must be bluffing. How could someone with 700 grams of gold dress so shabbily?","Seeing his disbelief, Old Liu took out a pink pig from his bag. \"Test it yourself, see if it's pure gold. This is my family heirloom. I have another one at home. If the price is right, I'll sell that one to you too.\"","Upon seeing the pig, the owner's expression changed. He said, \"I believe you. I'll test the purity of the gold right now. Please have a seat. Xiao Ye, what are you staring at? Serve tea to this gentleman.\"","Old Liu was quite pleased with himself. He had calculated that 700 grams of gold could be exchanged for over 300,000 yuan. He was about to become a rich man.","After Old Liu finished his fourth cup of tea, he finally realized something was wrong. Why did it take so long to verify the purity of the gold?","\"Boss, I'm in a hurry. I won't exchange it now. Please return the gold pig to me.\"","\"Don't rush, sir. We'll have the price estimated soon. Please wait a bit longer.\"","Old Liu sensed something was amiss. He decided to leave without the pig, but as he turned around, he saw Fang Rui and Zhang staring at him.","\"Uncle Liu, long time no see,\" Zhang said with a mischievous grin.","\"Officer Fang, Officer Zhang, are you here to buy something too?\"","Zhang replied, \"We're not buying anything. We're here to arrest someone.\"","Old Liu broke out in a cold sweat, nervously wiping his brow. \"Arrest who?\"","\"You, of course!\" Zhang took out handcuffs and cuffed Old Liu.","\"I... What crime did I commit? I didn't kill Director Zhang. Why are you arresting me?\" Old Liu let out a pig-like squeal, shouting at passersby, \"Help! The police are beating me! The police are arresting me illegally! I haven't broken any laws. Why are you arresting me?\"","The shop owner handed the pig over to Fang Rui. \"Captain Fang, your guess was spot on. Someone really did come to sell the gold pig.\"","\"Thank you for your help, sir.\"","\"It's nothing. Fighting crime is everyone's responsibility.\"","Old Liu saw Fang Rui holding the gold pig and immediately turned ashen.","\"How... how did you know this pig was made of gold? How did you know I stole it?\" Old Liu began to stammer.","\"I guessed. When you deliberately exposed Chen Xinran, I felt something was off about you, but I had no evidence, so I could only wait and see. I had informed every gold shop that if anyone came to sell a gold pig or part of one, they should tell me,\" Fang Rui explained.","Old Liu's face turned ashen. He had thought the case was closed and this matter was over. No one would know that two pigs were missing, let alone that those two pigs contained gold. But he never expected the police had been watching him all along.","Back at the station, Old Liu confessed to the course of events and admitted to the theft.","\"I occasionally helped Director Zhang clean. One day, I picked up one of the pigs to dust it off and found the weight was off. This small pig was very heavy! So I scraped off the paint on the surface and found it was gold underneath. Plus, Chen Xinran said Director Zhang had received several hundred thousand in bribes, but none of us had ever seen that money. I suddenly realized where the money was.","The night Director Zhang died, after Chen Xinran left, I snuck in and stole the two pigs. Even if Director Zhang reported it, they would only arrest Chen Xinran. And it just so happened that Director Zhang died, so no one would know the truth.\"","Zhang was furious after hearing this. \"Director Zhang was so good to you, and this is how you repay her?\"","\"Good to me? Paying me just over a thousand yuan a month, treating me like a beggar! She's a great philanthropist, why should she expect us to be selfless like her? Besides, she was just pretending to be charitable, making money from charity.\"","Zhang fell silent. He couldn't understand how the staff at Star Home, a charitable organization, could have such dark hearts.","\"If I had known, I would have melted the gold and sold it bit by bit over time. I'd sell it out of town!\" Old Liu cursed. \"I never thought I'd be on edge for half a month and end up with nothing. What rotten luck!\"","The Star Home case was officially closed.","Star Home soon had a new director, but the children still missed the director mom who had gone to a faraway place.","Stars twinkled in the night sky as a group of children crouched at the entrance of the orphanage.","\"Guoguo, will Director Mom come back?\"","\"No, Director Mom has gone to live her own life. Woof, we need to take care of ourselves, woof, and not, make Director Mom worry,\" Guoguo, who knew the truth, choked out.","\"Guoguo, you're lying.\"","\"Director Mom loves us so much, she couldn't possibly not come back.\"","\"Director Mom will come back tonight. I'm not going to sleep; I'll wait for her to return.\"","\"I won't sleep either.\"","\"Me neither.\"","\"Let's all wait for Director Mom to come back together.\"","\"Director Mom, please come back soon. We all miss you so much,\" someone shouted at the starry sky.","The stars twinkled, as if responding to the children."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: The Death of the Virgin: Moral Dilemma (Li Min Side Story)","paragraphs":["Li Min grew up in a family that favored boys over girls. After having five daughters, her parents finally had a son.","But fate seemed to play a cruel joke on them. This long-awaited son turned out to be mentally disabled. He couldn't speak or understand others, and would throw things around when agitated. Despite this, because he was a son, he remained the center of the family, cherished by everyone.","Li Min was only three years older than him but shouldered the burden of caring for her brother. Though her parents favored her brother, they were also exhausted by their disabled son and pushed all responsibility onto young Li Min.","Li Min's feelings toward her brother were conflicted. She loved him because she had raised him, and he depended on her. At the same time, she resented him because his existence robbed her of all free time. Her parents even considered pulling her out of school to care for him full-time. Only after her desperate pleas and her sisters' intervention did they abandon this idea.","Li Min's love for her brother gradually faded, and hatred took over.","So one day, when she saw some mischievous village boys teasing her brother, Li Min hid and let them humiliate him.","She watched as they pushed him into a pond. Her brother screamed helplessly while the boys laughed. When they had their fun, they left, leaving her brother struggling in the water.","Li Min panicked and ran to the pond's edge to pull him out, but suddenly remembered her parents' words:","\"We shouldn't let Min continue school. Too much education makes girls willful, and she won't want to care for her brother anymore. When she's older, we'll find her a live-in son-in-law, any man will do as long as he's willing to look after Qiang Qiang. This way she can stay home and care for Qiang Qiang.\"","Why should her life be tied to her disabled brother? It wasn't fair.","If her brother died, she would be free. Her brother deserved to die.","With these thoughts, Li Min withdrew her outstretched hand.","\"Sister, I'm scared,\" her brother looked at her in bewilderment and despair, slowly sinking into the pond.","Li Min became frightened again. She tried to reach for her brother but couldn't find him. She ended up sinking into the pond herself.","Adults passing by heard the commotion and jumped in, pulling them both out. She survived, but her brother died.","When the soaking wet Li Min was brought home, her parents beat her viciously, nearly breaking the fire poker before they stopped.","\"Why did Qiang Qiang die? Why couldn't it have been you, you worthless girl?\"","Li Min glared at them fiercely. \"Go ahead, keep beating me. Beat me to death if you dare! Your only son is dead, and my sisters are all married. If you kill me, who will care for you in your old age?\"","Her parents were shocked, seeming to realize something. From then on, they changed their attitude and treated Li Min very well.","They reasoned that since they had no son, when Li Min grew up, they could find her a live-in son-in-law who could serve as a half-son to them.","The cause of her brother's death was quickly determined. Those boys who had teased him had pushed him into the pond where he drowned. Li Min's parents went to their homes and made a scene, receiving a substantial compensation.","With the comfort of money, her parents weren't as heartbroken over their son's death. After all, he had been disabled.","They soon forgot about him, but Li Min couldn't. She kept remembering those desperate eyes and hearing a voice saying, \"Sister, I'll be good and wait at home for you to return from school.\"","Li Min's body was free, but her soul wasn't. She had caused her brother's death. She was guilty.","Later, she studied special education and learned a lot of professional knowledge. She realized her brother wasn't stupid, he had autism. After graduation, she worked as a teacher at an autism intervention center, hoping to make up for her guilt by caring for these children.","Later, moved by Director Zhang's story, she quit her job and became a volunteer at \"Star Home\".","Director Zhang was the kindest person Li Min had ever met. She was incredibly patient, treating almost all the children as her own. She would patiently read them fairy tales and check on them in the middle of the night. The children all called her \"Director Mom\".","One night, Li Min saw Director Zhang in the dormitory hallway. Seeing her, Director Zhang smiled and asked, \"Min, are you having trouble sleeping again? Do you need someone to talk to?\"","Li Min's nose stung with emotion. She sat down with Director Zhang on chairs in the play area and started talking. Li Min couldn't help but tell Director Zhang about her and her brother.","\"Was that pond deep?\" Director Zhang asked.","\"Very deep.\"","\"Min, memories can be deceptive. Even if you had grabbed your brother then, you might not have been able to save him. The pond was too deep. If you had tried to save him, he might have pulled you in too. It wasn't your fault. It was those boys who pushed your brother into the pond. You feel guilty, so you've magnified your own responsibility. But protecting and caring for your brother wasn't your responsibility, it was your parents'.\"","\"Everyone blamed me!\" At that moment, Li Min burst into tears.","Director Zhang hugged her, comforting her like a child. \"Min, the ones who should feel guilty aren't you, but your parents.\"","Director Zhang then shared her own story with Li Min.","\"I once had an autistic son too. I loved him dearly. For him, I got divorced and sold all our property. But caring for him was so difficult. Sometimes he would lose control of his bowels, other times he would suddenly throw tantrums and break things. I had to watch him 24 hours a day. But I was so young, I wanted my own life too.","One rainy night, he ran downstairs again. I followed him down, and then I saw bright lights coming towards us. It was a large truck. I knew what was about to happen, and I knew that if I grabbed my son right then, he could still live. But I hesitated. I was afraid of living like that for the rest of my life. In those few seconds that I hesitated, the truck hit and killed my son...\"","Li Min stared at Director Zhang in shock. \"So you're trying to make up for your guilt towards your son?\"","\"Yes. I'm atoning for my sin.\"","\"But what if your memory is deceiving you too? What if you really couldn't have grabbed your son in time?\"","Director Zhang fell silent.","That late-night conversation brought them closer together.","But Li Min never expected that Director Zhang's true face would soon be revealed to her.","Director Zhang had actually made a deal with a pharmaceutical company, allowing these autistic children to become test subjects. She even connected the company with more parents of autistic children.","Li Min confronted Director Zhang. \"We're not sure if those drugs have side effects. What if something happens to the children after they take them?\"","\"Li Min, nothing will happen.\"","\"How can you be sure? Did you ask the children's opinion? Are they willing to be guinea pigs? Autism can't be cured! How could these drugs possibly work?\"","\"How do we know they won't work if we don't try?\" Director Zhang argued. \"Li Min, if Yuanyuan and the others could choose, do you think they'd rather be idiots for life, or take a life-threatening gamble for that 1% chance of becoming normal? I'm telling you, they'd rather die than stay like this forever. They want to be normal, and I'm helping them.\"","\"That's just what you think, not what they want! You're a hypocrite. Back then, you watched your own son get hit by a car just to get rid of your burden. You could have saved him but chose not to. And now, you're clearly doing this for money, but you're using such an absurd excuse to justify yourself.\"","Director Zhang fell silent. She didn't defend herself.","Li Min knew Director Zhang wasn't doing it for money. If she wanted to embezzle funds, she had many ways to do so. But Li Min didn't understand why Director Zhang would believe the pharmaceutical company's lies.","When Yuanyuan repeatedly sought her help, expressing his fear of the drugs and medical examinations through drawings, she finally made up her mind to kill Director Zhang and the mastermind behind it all, Jiang Yun.","She had to protect these poor children!","She successfully used those two children to kill them. However, she sank into deeper self-condemnation - how was she any different from Director Zhang and the others when she used Yuanyuan and Yan Yan to commit murder?","She too had become a demon."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: The Death of the Virgin: The Selfish (Jiang Yun Side Story)","paragraphs":["As Jiang Yun watched Lin Qianyan's knife stab towards her, she thought of her childhood. Perhaps, it was she who had passed on the evil and coldness to Lin Qianyan.","Jiang Yun was a love child. Her father was quite wealthy, but he was afraid of his wife and dared not acknowledge her as his daughter. Her mother was a beautiful but useless woman who drank every day and beat her when she couldn't get money.","The adults around her would curse her behind her back, calling her the daughter of a mistress and shameless. Jiang Yun never refuted them. At night, she would puncture their bicycle tires or throw caterpillars into their children's backpacks.","Later, they all said that Jiang Yun was a well-behaved and sensible child. Every time her mother got drunk at the bar, it was Jiang Yun who carried her home. When her father didn't pay alimony, she even had to work part-time while studying to support the family.","Jiang Yun studied hard, got into the best high school, and then the best university. She saved money and eventually went abroad for further studies with her own earnings.","She finally escaped that nightmare place and her useless mother.","Before meeting Mu Mian's Father, Jiang Yun's life was dark. She had done many bad things. For example, knowing she could only come second in exams, she secretly cut the brakes of the first place student's bicycle, causing him to break his hand and miss the exam. That time, Jiang Yun got the highest scholarship...","At that time, she participated in Mu Mian's Father's graduation experiment for a hundred dollars. That's how they met.","Mu Mian's Father was a psychology student. He was very smart and saw through Jiang Yun's selfish and cold soul at a glance. But he still fell hopelessly in love with her.","At first, Jiang Yun hated this clingy person. She was busy, spending all her spare time working to earn a living.","Jiang Yun told Mu Wenzhou all the bad things she had done and then said, \"Mu Wenzhou, I'm like a scorpion. Anyone who gets close to me and tries to love me will be hurt by me. You'd better stay away from me.\"","\"Jiang Yun, you had no choice back then. You did what you had to do to survive. Otherwise, you wouldn't have made it.\"","Mu Wenzhou hugged her, embracing that wounded soul.","In that moment, endless grievances welled up in her eyes. Yes, she had no choice. Just like a scorpion using its sting to protect itself, it was an instinct formed for survival.","Later, they got married, bought a house, and Jiang Yun got pregnant.","Jiang Yun eagerly awaited the birth of this child. At that time, she felt that no matter what the child was like, she would love her and give her the best. She wanted to make up for all the childhood she had missed with Mu Mian.","When Mu Mian was a baby, she was very different from other children. She rarely cried or responded to adults' actions. She seemed to live in her own world.","When other children of the same age could speak fluently, Mu Mian couldn't say a single word. No matter how hard Jiang Yun tried to talk to Mu Mian, she wouldn't respond. She didn't cry or make a fuss, like a doll.","Later, Mu Mian was diagnosed with autism.","The evaluator said Mu Mian had low intelligence, sensory integration disorder, and stalled language development. They had to prepare for the possibility that Mu Mian might be like this for life.","Jiang Yun gradually fell apart. She didn't want to be tied down by such a child. She had her dreams and career. She didn't want to spend her life taking care of a fool, no, even worse than a fool. At least those mentally retarded children would give their parents emotional feedback, but Mu Mian was like a walking corpse.","Mu Mian's Father, however, thought differently. He was a psychotherapist and believed that as long as they kept expressing love to Mu Mian, she would eventually feel it. Mu Mian wasn't devoid of emotions; she just hadn't found the frequency to communicate with the outside world. As long as they kept sending her love signals, they would eventually connect.","Even if they couldn't connect, Mu Mian, no matter what she was like, would still be their most beloved child.","Jiang Yun thought he was too naive. Of course, it wasn't him who had to take care of Mu Mian at home, facing such a cold child. He could afford to say such grandiose words.","To treat Mu Mian's autism, they began to struggle financially, living in poverty.","Later, Jiang Yun couldn't take it anymore and proposed a divorce to Mu Mian's Father.","\"Jiang Yun, you probably have postpartum depression. You need treatment, not a divorce.\"","\"No, Mu Wenzhou. I've always been a selfish and cold-hearted person. I've had enough of the hard life with you, and I've had enough of Mu Mian. I have my dreams. I don't want to be trapped here.\"","\"Alright, let's get a divorce. Don't worry, I'll take good care of Mu Mian.\"","Mu Mian's Father signed the papers without hesitation, even borrowing several thousand dollars from a friend for her. He smiled and said, \"Jiang Yun, you don't need to feel guilty. Everyone has the right to choose their own life. Go and achieve your dreams.\"","In that moment, Jiang Yun felt utterly guilty. But what could she do? If she didn't escape, she would go mad.","After returning to China, Jiang Yun met Lin Ye. At that time, Lin Ye was an unloved son of the Lin Family, excluded from the inheritance. Jiang Yun used the power of the Jiang Family and her own schemes to help him rise to power and eventually inherit the Lin Family's wealth.","Jiang Yun had been a love child of the Jiang Family, suffering from contempt. So her dream was to climb to the top and become a powerful person. Meeting Mu Wenzhou was an accident. His love had briefly numbed her, but the trauma of childhood couldn't be healed.","She didn't love Lin Ye; he had many women outside, and she didn't care. Her love was buried abroad, in the small house with Mu Wenzhou and Mu Mian.","So her only expectation for the unborn Lin Qianyan was that he must be a boy.","He was indeed a boy, but unexpectedly, he was also abnormal. By the age of three, he still couldn't speak. The therapist diagnosed him with autism.","In that moment, she felt that fate was playing a cruel joke on her. Why did she have to give birth to another abnormal child? But this time, she accepted her fate. After all, she only needed a son; his condition didn't matter.","She hired the best nanny to take care of Lin Qianyan and occasionally played the role of a loving mother, playing with him. She didn't love this child, but she had no choice; she needed a son.","Lin Ye's ex-wife also gave birth to a son, Lin Qianjie. That child was rebellious and didn't like Jiang Yun. But Jiang Yun was good at manipulating people. She first showed weakness, softening Lin Qianjie's attitude with sweet words, then sowing discord between him and his father, making Lin Qianjie completely side with her.","She indulged all of Lin Qianjie's bad behaviors, suppressing his occasional desire to improve, eventually turning him into a complete failure.","Occasionally, she would think of Mu Mian and Mu Wenzhou. But she didn't dare to find out about their current situation. Her cousin told her that Mu Mian's Father had died, and she was adopted by the Shen family. Later, Jiang Yinian found her and said, \"Auntie, I saw Mu Mian, she...\"","\"Enough, don't mention that name in front of me,\" Jiang Yun interrupted him.","Jiang Yun put all her energy into her career.","Lin Ye's women became more and more numerous, and one even got pregnant, wanting to take her place. At this point, Jiang Yun suddenly realized that Lin Ye was no longer useful. So she tampered with Lin Ye's medicine, causing him to have a stroke and die in bed while having an affair with another woman.","She went from being Mrs. Lin to Ms. Jiang, becoming the true power holder.","She had thought about finding Mu Mian, but she realized that wouldn't make Mu Mian's life better, so she gave up. If Mu Mian had been raised by her, she would probably have become a selfish and cold-hearted person too.","In the courtroom, it was the first time she saw the grown-up Mu Mian. She was lovely, cautiously testing her, but she disappointed Mu Mian. She had never been a good mother.","Jiang Yun was surprised to find that Mu Mian had become a normal person. She could speak, she could draw, and she even became a forensic scientist.","But all of Mu Mian's changes had nothing to do with her.","She thought, since Mu Mian could become a normal person, so could Lin Qianyan. She wanted those experts to study Mu Mian and find out the reason why she was cured of her autism, but Shen Xiyin protected her so well that she had no way to proceed.","On her deathbed, Jiang Yun thought of the time when Mu Mian was just born. At that time, the man she loved was also by her side, and they dreamed of a beautiful future together.","Her lips curved into a smile.","But if time could flow backward, she would still choose to divorce and leave Mu Mian. Her life belonged only to herself."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: Can Get Married","paragraphs":["After the case at Star Home was resolved, Mu Mian and her colleagues took a few days off.","Jiang Yinian invited Mu Mian to attend Jiang Yun's funeral, but she declined. No matter what expectations and emotions she had once harbored for Ms. Jiang, they no longer mattered on the day of her death.","Mu Mian disliked funerals! The deceased were reduced to ashes, and crying loudly wouldn't make them hear anything. Why bother?","On the last day of their vacation, Zhang frantically called for help in the group chat. After a long time, only Mu Mian, full of excitement, and Fang Rui, looking sleepy and irritable, showed up.","\"Only you two came?\" Zhang looked behind them, finding it empty. He had been shouting in the group chat for a while, but only Mu Mian and Fang Rui had come. And in such matters, they were the least helpful.","\"Where's the body?\" Mu Mian stood in the luxurious hotel lobby, bewildered.","\"There's no body.\"","\"Then why did you call me here? I only know how to dissect bodies.\" Mu Mian sighed. Zhang had sent a location in the group chat earlier, saying, \"Everyone, hurry up, someone's going to die.\" Mu Mian quickly went to Fang Rui's place, dragged him out of bed, and had him drive her over.","\"If you don't help me, you might only see my corpse tomorrow.\" Zhang whined.","\"But Officer Zhang, I'm not interested in your remains.\"","\"Mu Mian, isn't it time to stop bickering when things are this urgent?\"","Fang Rui impatiently interrupted him, \"Then please get to the point.\"","\"The thing is, last night, I went to Chen Xue's rented place for dinner, and unexpectedly, her mom showed up and caught me red-handed. She didn't say much at the time, but if looks could kill, you'd be seeing a corpse right now. Before letting me go, her mom coldly said, 'Let's have lunch together tomorrow.' Chen Xue told me that all her aunts and uncles would be there, and she asked me to bring a few people to boost the numbers. That's why I called you guys.\"","Zhang's parents were on a trip and wouldn't be back soon. Also, calling relatives over seemed too formal, and Chen Xue mentioned that her mom hadn't yet agreed to their relationship. Zhang had no choice but to ask his colleagues for help.","Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui, \"There will be about fifteen aunts and uncles, plus Chen Xue's mom. Fang Rui, can you handle so many people? Maybe we should just leave. I'm scared!\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Boss, please don't leave! Mu Mian, 'aunts and uncles' is just a term, not a specific number! And you're not here to fight; you're here to eat.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"So how many people are there exactly?\"","They soon found out. Chen Xue's mom arrived with a large group of aunts, about fifteen or sixteen of them, bustling in. Chen Xue covered her face, looking helpless.","Chen Xue's mom owned a shop and had some money. She had already booked a large private room that could accommodate twenty people.","On the way to the room, the aunts all looked at Fang Rui with satisfied smiles. Then they saw a young girl hiding behind Fang Rui, her hand tightly gripping his arm. Their smiles froze, and their gazes slowly shifted to Zhang, whose smile faded.","Although Zhang was decent, his physique and build couldn't compare to Fang Rui's. Too bad Fang Rui already had a lovely girlfriend.","Once seated, Zhang introduced himself confidently, \"Hello, aunts. I'm Chen Xue's boyfriend, Zhang Qiang. You can call me Little Zhang. It's my first time meeting you all, so I'll toast you with tea.\"","Soon, the aunts changed their minds.","Zhang was good at dealing with these aunts. He poured tea and chatted with them, making everyone laugh. He also didn't neglect Chen Xue, often serving her food and handing her tissues, showing meticulous care.","In contrast, Fang Rui was a mute. Not only did he not initiate conversations, but he also didn't respond when the aunts tried to engage him. He even ordered a dish of Kung Pao Chicken and ate it alone, which was quite rude.","The aunts shook their heads.","Fang Rui picked out the chicken from the Kung Pao Chicken and placed it in Mu Mian's bowl, who then ate it.","\"Young people these days are picky eaters,\" an aunt said sarcastically.","\"That's right. With better conditions now, they can afford to be picky. Back in our day, having something to eat was good enough.\" The aunt next to Mu Mian directly addressed her, \"Little Mu, even if your boyfriend spoils you, you can't be so picky. It's important to have a balanced diet and eat everything.\"","Mu Mian whispered to the aunt, \"Yes, being picky is bad, but I'm not picky. Fang Rui is very picky; he only likes the cucumbers and carrots in Kung Pao Chicken. I like the chicken, so I help him eat it.\"","\"...\"","The aunts were even more dissatisfied with Fang Rui. He was so inconsiderate to put disliked food in his girlfriend's bowl. In contrast, Zhang was incredibly considerate.","Mu Mian ate while occasionally glancing at the table, ready to flee if they decided to attack Zhang. She chose a seat by the door for this purpose, though it meant she and Fang Rui had to move dishes every time the waiter served them.","Fortunately, the atmosphere at the table was good, and Chen Xue's relatives grew more satisfied with Zhang, especially in contrast to Fang Rui and Mu Mian.","After finishing dessert, Chen Xue's mom said to Zhang, \"Little Zhang, I'm not a conservative person. If you want to be with Chen Xue, that's fine, but you two need to settle down soon. Chen Xue is a good girl, and you mustn't mistreat her.\"","\"Yes, Chen Xue is a wonderful person,\" Mu Mian chimed in. \"Auntie, I'll keep an eye on him to make sure he doesn't bully Chen Xue.\"","Chen Xue's mom teased Mu Mian, \"Little Mu, with your small frame, I doubt you can beat Little Zhang.\"","\"True. But I'm smarter than him. And I can have Fang Rui help me beat him.\" Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui, \"You'll help me, right? Even though you know Little Zhang longer, I feel like we're closer.\"","\"Hahaha.\" Everyone laughed.","Mu Mian didn't understand why they were laughing, so she laughed along.","Chen Xue's mom looked at Fang Rui, \"When do you plan to get married?\"","\"Not that soon,\" Fang Rui replied.","After the meal, Chen Xue's mom and the aunts went to play mahjong, Chen Xue and Zhang went on a date, and Mu Mian and Fang Rui planned to go home and spend the rest of their vacation in bed. But Mu Mian received an email sent two hours ago.","Dear Cherry,","I'm flying back to Florida at four o'clock this afternoon. I want to have lunch with you before I leave. Would you like to come to a restaurant near the airport?","The sender was Ms. Mischel.","Mu Mian quickly replied to the email. She hadn't seen Ms. Mischel in a long time. Although they couldn't have lunch, Mu Mian thought they could meet at the airport.","\"Fang Rui, can you take me to the airport?\"","\"Sure.\" Fang Rui saw the word \"dear\" and asked jealously, \"Who are you going to see? Are you going to have another friend pop up?\"","\"It's Ms. Mischel.\"","Fang Rui suddenly remembered that it was this lady who had told Mu Mian that people with autism shouldn't get married.","\"Let's hurry to see her then. We can't let her leave.\"","\"Fang Rui, don't walk so fast. It's only two o'clock now, and it only takes half an hour to get to the airport. We have plenty of time.\"","When they arrived at the airport, Fang Rui saw an elegant foreign woman sitting in the waiting area, reading a book.","\"Cherry,\" Ms. Mischel could speak Chinese, but not very fluently, \"You seem to have grown up a lot.\"","She wanted to reach out and hug Mu Mian, but she remembered that Mu Mian was resistant to physical contact, so she tried to pull her hand back.","Mu Mian hugged her first, \"It's been two years since we last met, so a hug is okay.\"","Ms. Mischel smiled, \"Cherry, your sister was right, you've changed a lot.\"","\"Hello, Ms. Mischel,\" Fang Rui greeted her.","\"Hello,\" Ms. Mischel was a bit surprised, she looked at Mu Mian and exclaimed, \"Cherry, is this your boyfriend? You've found love?\"","\"I don't have love yet,\" Mu Mian sighed, \"People with autism find it hard to have love.\"","\"Who told you that? People with autism can have love. Do you remember Amy? She later got married and she's very happy.\"","Mu Mian asked confusedly, \"But you said people with autism can't get married. You told Linda's parents not to let her get married, don't you remember?\"","\"That's because Linda's boyfriend didn't love her, he was a liar, so they couldn't get married.\"","Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui excitedly and said, \"Fang Rui, I can get married, I don't have to live alone forever.\"","\"Mm-hmm.\"","Ms. Mischel looked at Mu Mian affectionately and asked, \"So, Cherry, do you have someone you want to marry?\"","\"Ms. Mischel, your plane is about to take off, you should hurry to board,\" Mu Mian pointed at Ms. Mischel's watch, reminding her of the time.","\"Cherry, I hope the next time I come back to China, it's for your wedding,\" Ms. Mischel glanced at Fang Rui, smiled at him, and then took her handbag to board the plane.","\"Cherry, goodbye.\"","\"Ms. Mischel, goodbye!\"","After Ms. Mischel walked away, Fang Rui curiously asked, \"Mu Mian, why didn't you answer Ms. Mischel's question directly just now?\"","\"Fang Rui, I'm hungry.\"","\"You ate a big bowl of rice and half a plate of chicken at lunch.\" Fang Rui felt Mu Mian's ability to change the subject was getting stronger.","Mu Mian pleaded, \"I want seafood paella.\"","\"Alright.\"","Mu Mian happily followed behind Fang Rui. She had thought about marrying Fang Rui, so she could legally obtain his body, but she had promised never to mention those two words in front of Fang Rui again, so she didn't want to answer that question.","But how could she get Fang Rui to willingly marry her?"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Sleeping Murder: Surrender","paragraphs":["After the vacation, Mu Mian just arrived at the office when she found it crowded with people, both familiar and unfamiliar female colleagues. Each of them held a cup of milk tea, with Chen Xue in the middle.","\"Little Mu, the forensic scientist, Chen Xue is getting married, you know that, right? Here, have some milk tea. Chen Xue said you like this.\" Wen from the finance department handed Mu Mian a cup of milk tea. Seeing Mu Mian's surprised expression, she continued, \"Okay, you didn't know! You share an office with Chen Xue, and you didn't know anything?\"","\"Yes, I'm not very well-informed.\"","\"Then next time there's gossip, I'll share it with you on WeChat. Ah, we haven't added each other on WeChat yet. Let's do it now. I'll scan your code.\"","Chen Xue quickly explained, \"Mu Mian, I only found out about this recently.\"","\"Zhang's friend circle said his mother-in-law is very satisfied with him. They've met the family, so they must be getting married!\"","\"Zhang is so lucky to marry such a good girl like Chen Xue.\"","\"Alright, alright, when Zhang and I get married, we'll definitely invite everyone to the wedding. It's time to get back to work, everyone should return to their offices.\" Chen Xue quickly ushered the gossiping colleagues out, \"Everyone, disperse, don't disturb Mian.\"","\"I wasn't disturbed,\" Mu Mian clarified softly.","\"You were!\"","\"Ah, it's so noisy! There are too many people, the oxygen is so thin, I'm going to suffocate!\"","\"......\"","The gossip was over, and the milk tea was almost finished. Everyone returned to their offices.","Chen Xue turned around and saw Mu Mian looking at her with envy.","\"Mu Mian, what's wrong?\"","\"How did you get Zhang to agree to marry you?\"","Chen Xue blushed and said in a high-pitched voice, \"We're not getting married, it's all just rumors. What do you mean 'get Zhang to agree to marry me'? He proposed to me, and I might not even agree, let alone me proposing to him. He's dreaming!\"","\"You don't plan to get married?\"","\"Of course, we will, but not now. We've just started dating, we don't want to rush into marriage. Marriage and dating are two different things.\" Chen Xue felt something was off with Mu Mian. Mu Mian usually didn't gossip about such things, \"Mu Mian, why are you so interested in the topic of marriage?\"","\"I used to think that people with autism couldn't get married, but yesterday, Ms. Michell told me that I can get married.\"","\"So?\" Chen Xue took a sip of milk tea and casually asked, \"You're not thinking of getting married, are you?\"","Mu Mian nodded seriously, \"Yes. I want to marry Fang Rui.\"","Chen Xue spat out her milk tea onto her desk, \"Mian, are you still thinking about Fang Rui's body?\" Chen Xue could only think of this reason. Otherwise, why would Mu Mian suddenly want to get married? She hasn't even dated, what marriage? The process isn't right.","Mu Mian felt Chen Xue was wrong. If it were a year ago, Mu Mian wanted to marry Fang Rui to get his body, but now it seemed to be more than that. Love movies say that getting married means you can be with that person forever. She wants to be with Fang Rui forever.","Mu Mian didn't answer Chen Xue's question, \"Chen Xue, what should I do to get Fang Rui to agree to marry me?\"","\"Go find Fang Rui now and ask him if he'll marry you.\"","\"Now?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Do I need to use sophisticated language skills? Like quoting poetry or other rhetorical devices.\" Mu Mian asked.","\"Can you?\"","\"No!\"","\"So no need, just ask directly.\"","Mu Mian left the office.","Chen Xue finished a bun and was about to start on the second when Mu Mian walked in.","\"Did he agree?\"","\"There's a case, someone came to confess to a murder, Fang Rui is currently understanding the details. Chen Xue, what do you think the body will look like this time? The murderer confessed themselves, so the victim's family probably won't let me dissect the body. This murderer is too honest.\"","Chen Xue bit the straw, perhaps, in Mu Mian's heart, bodies are still more important.","In the interrogation room, a beautiful young woman sat nervously on a chair. Her eyes were dark and bloodshot, her hair was messy, and she looked like she hadn't slept for days, very haggard.","\"What's your name?\"","\"Zhang Mingli.\"","\"Your age and occupation?\"","\"Twenty-five years old, freelance, I'm an architectural designer, usually taking commissions to draw interior design plans.\"","\"Why are you here to confess?\"","She licked her cracked lips and said in a trembling voice, \"Comrade police, I think I accidentally killed someone!\"","\"Think? Are you not sure if you killed someone?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes, I'm not sure if I killed someone, but my mind has an extra memory, I pushed a man down the stairs with my own hands, he rolled down and bled a lot. He's dead!\"","\"When did this happen?\"","\"I don't remember.\"","\"What was the scene like?\"","\"I can't remember. I only remember that day the sun was very good, but the house was very cold.\"","\"Where is the crime scene? Take us there.\" Fang Rui said.","\"It's my new home... Comrade police, but the body is missing. I don't know where that body went.\" Zhang Mingli said in terror, \"I clearly remember the body was on the floor, but it's gone!\"","\"Do you know the deceased?\"","Zhang Mingli shook her head, \"No. I can't remember his face. He has no face. But I seem to be very afraid of him!\"","\"Then why was he in your house?\"","\"I don't know. I don't know why he came to my house, and I don't know why I killed him. But I'm very sure, I killed him.\" Zhang Mingli held her head, saying in terror, \"Comrade police, what should I do, I killed someone, am I going to jail?\"","Fang Rui and Zhang exchanged glances, they felt this woman's mental state might be problematic.","\"Comrade police, I'm not crazy, what I said is true! You have to believe me!\" Zhang Mingli pitifully looked at Fang Rui and Zhang, \"I admit my crime, and I accept the judgment of the law. But you can't think I'm crazy!\"","\"How about this, Miss Zhang, can you take us to the crime scene?\" Fang Rui said.","Hearing Fang Rui believed her, she calmed down a bit and asked, \"Okay. Can I take you there now?\"","\"Can you give me the contact information of your relatives?\" Fang Rui said, \"If you really are the murderer, your relatives need to sign some documents, so it's better to inform me in advance.\"","\"My mother just passed away, my aunt is out of town, there's only my uncle in Jiangzhou City, his name is Zhang Taotao, you can contact him.\" Zhang Mingli wrote her uncle's phone number on a piece of paper.","\"You rest here for a while, we'll go to your house with you later to see if we can find the body.\"","\"Okay, Comrade police, thank you so much!\"","After leaving the interrogation room, Fang Rui contacted Zhang Mingli's uncle.","\"Hello, we are the police station, are you Mr. Zhang, Zhang Mingli's uncle?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes, what happened to Mingli? This child usually behaves well, how did she end up at the police station?\" The person on the other end of the phone asked anxiously.","\"What is Zhang Mingli's usual mental state like, does she have any mental illness?\"","\"This child is quite normal! Just a bit introverted, not very talkative. Ah, she grew up in a single-parent family, her mother was like that, it's normal for her to have a strange personality.\"","\"What was wrong with her mother?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Her mother was a mental patient. She recently passed away from stomach cancer. Mingli moved back to Jiangzhou because of this.\"","\"Okay, thank you!\"","After hanging up the phone, Zhang said, \"Boss, Zhang Mingli might be mentally ill too. Look, she can't remember anything when we ask her.\"","\"It's possible. But we still need to go to the crime scene to see if there really was a murder.\""]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Sleeping Murder: Reality or Fantasy","paragraphs":["Zhang Mingli took Fang Rui and the others to Beiyuan Garden Residential Area. It was an old residential complex built in the 1990s. The buildings were closely spaced, resulting in poor natural lighting. Upon entering the stairwell, there was an immediate sense of darkness and gloom.","Zhang Mingli lived on the fourth floor. Her apartment was a duplex with two levels, so despite being on a lower floor, the ceiling felt low upon entering, making the space feel somewhat cramped.","There was a bagua mirror hanging on the door, covered in dust, appearing to have been there for years.","\"It was right here. He was lying here, covered in blood,\" Zhang Mingli pointed at the floor near the stairway entrance, speaking frantically. \"I was standing upstairs at the time. I watched him roll down and fall here, where he slowly closed his eyes. He died.\"","Zhang opened the curtains and turned on the lights, but found nothing on the floor. The floor tiles were grayish-white and worn, with some even cracked, but there were no traces of blood.","Mu Mian sprayed luminol reagent on the floor, but no fluorescence appeared. There were no signs of chemical corrosion on the floor, ruling out the possibility that the perpetrator had used bleach or similar substances to clean up blood, indicating that there had never been any blood on the tiles.","\"No blood,\" Mu Mian whispered to Fang Rui and the others. \"No traces of bleach detected on the floor either, so we can rule out blood being cleaned with bleach. It seems there was never any blood on these tiles.\"","\"The tiles look old, with lots of dust in the gaps. They don't appear to have been replaced recently,\" Wang said. \"We can basically rule out tile replacement.\"","Mu Mian sprayed luminol reagent in every corner of the house, but found no fluorescent reactions except for some small spots on the white walls, which were from mosquitoes that had been killed.","As Mu Mian walked out of the room, she hesitated, feeling something unsettling about the house.","\"Mu Mian, what's wrong?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"I think my OCD is acting up. Something's not right about this house!\"","\"Is it because of the tiles?\"","Fang Rui noticed that the tiles in the bedrooms were different from those in the living room, with different patterns. Except for the bathroom, all other rooms had matching tiles. Normally during renovation, the living room and bedrooms would use the same tiles, but this house was different.","However, the living room tiles didn't look newly replaced either. They felt loose underfoot, with several cracked pieces, and the style and pattern weren't contemporary – they appeared to be from over a decade ago. The building itself was quite old.","\"Yes. The bedroom tiles are different from the living room. That's why this house feels so uncomfortable to me,\" Mu Mian complained, then pointed to the large bay window in the second bedroom. \"And why build such a platform in the house? It's difficult to close the windows, it's so high I can't even climb up there. The design of this house is so impractical!\"","\"I feel the same way. This house feels very gloomy!\" Zhang commented. \"It's so eerie, no wonder Ms. Zhang developed mental issues living here.\"","Zhang Mingli stood in the living room, visibly anxious. The murder scene seemed to replay constantly before her eyes, but she couldn't remember why she killed someone or who the victim was.","Suddenly, there was a knock at the door.","Zhang Mingli jumped in fright.","\"Ms. Zhang, don't be afraid. We're still here,\" Zhang reassured her.","Zhang opened the door to find Zhang Mingli's uncle, Zhang Taotao, a man in his fifties wearing black-framed glasses and having a scholarly appearance. He addressed Zhang Mingli: \"Mingli, what's wrong? How did you end up at the police station?\"","Zhang Taotao was a high school chemistry teacher nearing retirement. He barely needed to work anymore, so when he heard about Zhang Mingli's situation, he rushed over immediately.","\"Uncle, I killed someone! I pushed someone down the stairs, they fell to their death, but the body is gone,\" Zhang Mingli's eyes darted around wildly as she spoke in terror. \"There's a ghost! Uncle, this house is haunted. I can't stay here anymore. I don't want to live here.\"","\"Alright, you don't have to stay. Come live with your uncle,\" Zhang Taotao embraced her. \"I told you before to come live with me, but you insisted on staying here. Now look what's happened – you ended up in a haunted house, and look how frightened you've become.\"","After Zhang Mingli calmed down, Zhang Taotao addressed Fang Rui and the others: \"Officers, I apologize for my niece's behavior in making a false report. She told me earlier that this house was haunted. I told her not to stay here, but she insisted, and now she's been frightened out of her wits. How could a young woman like her possibly kill someone?\"","\"No, Uncle, I did kill someone!\" Zhang Mingli insisted.","\"Mingli, child, you say you killed someone, but who did you kill?\" Zhang Taotao interrupted. \"Haven't the police officers searched the entire house? Did they find any body?\"","Zhang Mingli began to doubt herself, looking at her hands while mumbling, \"Did I really not kill anyone? Uncle, am I going crazy like Mom?\"","\"Mingli, didn't you get checked at the psychiatric hospital last time? The doctor said you're fine, just under too much stress, which is why you're thinking too much.\"","Zhang Taotao turned to Fang Rui and the others, saying, \"Officers, I'll take my niece home now. She's been under too much stress lately and might be having some mental health issues. She needs proper rest.\"","\"Alright, take her home.\"","Fang Rui and the team thoroughly searched the house again but found nothing suspicious.","The house's decoration was old, apparently from many years ago, and the furnishings hadn't changed much recently.","There was a security camera in the corridor outside Zhang Mingli's apartment. They went to the security office to retrieve the footage from the past two weeks.","Back at the station, each person was assigned to watch several days of footage at 16x speed until around seven or eight in the evening. The surveillance footage showed that in the past two weeks, apart from Zhang Mingli's uncle, delivery personnel, and utility workers, no other men had visited her home. Only two women had visited, and everyone who entered had also left – no one had disappeared.","\"There haven't been any missing persons reports recently either. It seems Ms. Zhang really is experiencing mental health issues,\" Zhang rubbed his tired eyes. \"Still, it's good that there wasn't actually a murder.\"","Everyone went home after work. Fang Rui drove Mu Mian home, and she remained silent throughout the journey.","Seeing Mu Mian's deep contemplation, Fang Rui asked, \"What's wrong?\"","\"Nothing!\"","At 1:08 AM, Fang Rui was suddenly awakened by knocking at his door. He knew only Mu Mian would knock at this hour. He opened the door with messy hair, \"Mu Mian, can't this wait until tomorrow?\"","\"Fang Rui, do you think the body could be hidden in the bay window?\" Mu Mian asked with dark circles under her eyes, trying to keep them open. \"Let's go dig for the body with some tools.\"","\"Mu Mian, do you know what time it is?\" Fang Rui could barely keep his eyes open.","\"1:09 AM.\"","\"So, go back to sleep now, and we'll talk about this tomorrow.\" Fang Rui grabbed Mu Mian's shoulders and pushed her to her apartment door, then turned to go back to sleep.","\"Fang Rui, you can sleep tomorrow.\"","\"This case hasn't been officially opened. If we go digging for a body now, we'd be illegally entering private property. That's against the law, understand?\"","\"I know. I understand the law. But...\"","\"Then go back to sleep now, and tomorrow we'll contact Ms. Zhang and check that bay window again, okay?\"","\"Okay.\"","Fang Rui closed his door, returned to bed, and was about to sleep when something occurred to him. He quickly got up and opened the door, finding Mu Mian still standing outside, as he'd suspected.","\"Fang Rui, why aren't you going back to sleep?\"","Mu Mian was happy to see Fang Rui come out again. She had been counting seconds, wanting to know how long it would take for him to return. The number would be her waiting time. It only took 18 seconds for Fang Rui to come back out.","She felt lucky – she only had to wait 18 seconds.","\"Mu Mian, shouldn't I be asking you that question? Why aren't you going back to sleep?\" Fang Rui asked with resignation.","\"You said you'd only tell me the important thing tomorrow. But I can't sleep, so I'll just wait here.\" Mu Mian waved her hand at Fang Rui, \"Fang Rui, you should go back to sleep. I'm not tired, so I'll just keep waiting here.\"","\"Mu Mian, Miss Zhang is sleeping, we can't reach her right now. Besides, there might not even be a body there. So, please be good and go back to sleep. We can check it out tomorrow, okay?\"","\"That's not what I wanted to talk about. I wanted to say something else.\"","\"What is it?\"","Mu Mian looked at him with sincere eyes, \"Fang Rui, would you marry me?\""]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: Sleeping Murder: Concrete Sealing of the Corpse","paragraphs":["Fang Rui's drowsiness vanished completely. He felt as if he'd been struck by lightning, completely petrified.","He had been waiting for Mu Mian to realize she liked him, but he never expected her to jump straight to a marriage proposal. This progression was far too chaotic.","\"What did you say?\" Fang Rui asked nervously.","\"Fang Rui, will you marry me?\" Mu Mian raised her voice, her words echoing through the entire hallway. \"Did you hear me clearly this time?\"","\"Is it because marrying me would give you legal rights to my corpse?\" Fang Rui slowly regained his composure, knowing he couldn't analyze Mu Mian's behavior by normal standards.","Now it was Mu Mian's turn to fall silent. She didn't know how to answer this question. Because that was indeed one of the reasons. But more than that, she wanted to be with Fang Rui forever. Besides her sister, no one understood her better than Fang Rui. Her sister was going to marry Mr. Lin, so she wouldn't be able to stay with her forever.","\"Good night, Mu Mian.\"","Fang Rui returned to his home and closed the door. He feared that if he stayed any longer, he would have agreed to marry her. But he couldn't do that - Mu Mian didn't understand what marriage meant, so he couldn't agree to marry her. Otherwise, he would become exactly the kind of deceiver Mrs. Michelle had warned about.","Mu Mian felt confused. Fang Rui hadn't agreed, but he hadn't refused either. Moreover, his expression had been strange; he had looked very unhappy.","Mu Mian felt somewhat dejected, as Fang Rui didn't seem to want to marry her.","She waited outside his door for a while longer, but this time Fang Rui didn't open it. She waited for 999 seconds, but he still didn't appear. Mu Mian sighed - her life was so difficult. When she wanted Fang Rui's corpse, he wouldn't give it to her, and now when she wanted to marry him, he wouldn't agree to that either.","Never mind, she thought, she'd just stay single forever. If no one else wanted to be with Fang Rui, she could still stay with him. Mu Mian suddenly didn't feel so sad anymore, because she believed Fang Rui would have a hard time finding a partner as excellent as her.","Mu Mian went home and continued sleeping. She slept sweetly.","Fang Rui, however, couldn't sleep at all.","The next day, Fang Rui waited outside with dark circles under his eyes, looking completely exhausted, for Mu Mian to go to work.","Mu Mian emerged energetically with her bag. Seeing Fang Rui's condition, she asked curiously, \"Fang Rui, did you have insomnia? Why couldn't you sleep? Did you drink Zhang's coffee again?\"","Why... it was all because Mu Mian had proposed to him in the middle of the night! Why was she, the culprit, so energetic while he was the one who couldn't sleep?","Looking at Mu Mian's innocent face, Fang Rui replied, \"I suppose so.\"","\"Next time, let me drink it instead. I often have insomnia, so I'm used to it.\"","\"Okay.\"","After the morning meeting, Chen Xue cornered Mu Mian and asked curiously, \"Mian Mian, did you do something to make Captain Fang look like that? What did you do?\"","\"Chen Xue, we still haven't checked everywhere yesterday. We should remove the tiles and check underneath them,\" Mu Mian said, changing the subject.","\"Did you propose to him yesterday?\"","\"I think the body might be buried in that bay window. That huge bay window doesn't match the room's decoration style at all. It must have been renovated later,\" Mu Mian continued deflecting.","\"That bay window doesn't look recently built; it appears to have been there for a long time. Besides, sealing a body in cement would be easily discovered. Hardened cement can't mask the smell of decomposition, but there wasn't any unusual odor in that room. It's unlikely the body is hidden there,\" Chen Xue analyzed.","She still believed that Zhang Mingli had mental health issues, which was why she thought she had killed someone. The victim probably didn't exist at all.","\"But it's really perfect for hiding a body.\"","\"Then let's dig it up and see.\"","\"Chen Xue, I did propose to Fang Rui last night, and he rejected me,\" Mu Mian suddenly said.","\"He rejected you? Did he say why?\"","\"No, he just looked unhappy. I don't understand why. I'm so excellent, and we're so compatible. Why wouldn't he want to marry me?\"","Chen Xue thought she understood why. Among all of Mu Mian's reasons for marriage, love wasn't one of them. If Chen Xue were Fang Rui, she would have been frustrated by Mu Mian's denseness too.","Fang Rui had called Zhang Mingli, who said they could inspect the house however they wanted, even if it meant damaging the furniture and structure, as she was planning to renovate the house soon anyway.","They returned to Zhang Mingli's house. Mu Mian first asked Fang Rui and the others to remove the tiles near the stairway.","After removing the tiles, the floor was uneven and dirty.","Mu Mian sprayed luminol reagent on the exposed surface. Soon, the reagent that had seeped into the cement joints began to emit tiny spots of fluorescence.","Everyone was surprised - there were indeed bloodstains under the tiles.","\"There really are bloodstains,\" Mu Mian said. \"It seems there might actually be a body hidden in the house.\"","They all went to the second bedroom, where they had previously thought nothing of the bay window, but now the rectangular platform looked increasingly like a coffin.","The window seat was covered with a carpet. They lifted it to reveal tiles underneath, the same color and pattern as those in the living room but different from the room's decor.","They began breaking apart the cement platform. After working for a while, they discovered a layer of white substance under the cement.","\"This looks like dried latex,\" Zhang said after examining a piece.","They found that the platform had first been coated with latex, then covered with a 2cm layer of cement. They also found several pieces of torn yellow paper in the latex layer.","\"These look like talismans, and there's writing on them.\"","Soon after, they also found a bagua mirror and a peach wood sword.","\"There couldn't be something sealed in here, could there?\" Zhang exclaimed.","\"If a body were only sealed in cement, it would emit a strong decomposition odor because cement isn't completely airtight and can't contain the smell. But if you add a layer of latex, the seal becomes much stronger, and the odor would be trapped inside,\" Mu Mian explained. \"That might be why they used latex.\"","Initially, they had broken open the cement platform just to check, but now their spines were tingling - could there really be a body buried underneath?","They continued breaking it apart and discovered thick wooden boards with intricate carvings.","After removing the outer cement, they found what appeared to be a wooden box, but the wood had already rotted.","Zhang asked puzzled, \"What's this black stuff?\"","Chen Xue said, \"It looks like charcoal.\"","\"It's activated charcoal,\" Mu Mian said. \"But it must have been here for many years. The body, if there is one, wouldn't be fresh either.\"","The wooden box was also filled with cement. As they gradually broke apart the cement chunks, they saw something that looked like a human-shaped sculpture within."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: Sleeping Murder: The Haunted House","paragraphs":["“There's a corpse inside. Be careful when digging,” Mu Mian pointed to the nail exposed in the concrete block and began directing them to excavate the body. “Officer Zhang, don’t dig here, dig over there. First, don’t worry about the concrete on the surface of the body. We’ll move the concrete-encased body back to the lab, and I’ll clean off the surface concrete there.”","Zhang and the others followed Mu Mian’s instructions and unearthed an irregularly shaped concrete block.","Mu Mian carefully used a shovel to chip away at the concrete covering the dead person’s arm. She found that the skin was dark brown, dried out, and had turned leathery. There were also white substances on the concrete.","“It’s impossible to determine the time of death right now,” Mu Mian said, “but based on my experience, this body has been buried here for no less than ten years, most likely even longer.”","“No less than ten years? Then the victim couldn’t possibly have been killed by Miss Zhang, could she? Miss Zhang was probably still a child ten years ago,” Zhang exclaimed in surprise. “So why did she come to confess to murder?”","Everyone was puzzled.","“Maybe Miss Zhang knows the inside story. She deliberately came to the police station to confess, hoping to draw our attention and make us discover this body,” Chen Xue speculated.","Zhang and Wang thought it made sense.","Mu Mian was puzzled. “If Miss Zhang was already at the police station, why didn’t she just tell us directly that there was a body here?”","“Maybe the murderer threatened her not to say anything.”","“But if she came to the police station to report the case, wouldn’t that anger the murderer? She might as well have written us an anonymous letter and secretly revealed the truth to us. That way, the murderer wouldn’t know who turned him in,” Mu Mian still couldn’t understand her motives. Why make things so complicated?","After Mu Mian’s question, everyone was also confused about why Miss Zhang confessed.","“Could it be a coincidence? After moving into this place, the oppressive structure of the house caused Miss Zhang’s mental state to deteriorate, leading her to report the case and confess. It just so happens that a murder occurred in this house more than ten years ago,” Fang Rui analyzed.","“But could it really be that much of a coincidence?”","“Once I dig out the body, we’ll definitely find more clues,” Mu Mian said. “The person who buried the body handled it very professionally. We must catch them, and I’d like to have a good chat with them!”","Chen Xue agreed, “Exactly. No wonder this platform didn’t show any signs of collapse or cracking. There’s a wooden box inside providing support. I guess the cement wasn’t poured full, leaving some space, so the gas expansion wouldn’t affect the surface of the platform. Otherwise, the gas produced by the decaying body would definitely cause the concrete platform to deform.”","“The cement burial scenes in TV dramas are all about pouring concrete directly. It turns out that this method of disposing of a body is not feasible!” Zhang exclaimed. “Those TV dramas are so unprofessional.”","Chen Xue said, “Of course. Not only do you need to consider the issue of the stench, but also the gas produced by the decaying body that can cause cracks and deformation in the concrete. So burying a body in concrete is not a clever way to dispose of a body; the concrete actually accelerates the decay of the body.”","“I know many clever ways to dispose of a body!” Mu Mian said excitedly. “Do you want me to share them with you? Theoretically, they should be able to perfectly dispose of a body, but I haven’t practiced them, so I don’t know if there would be any issues during execution.”","“...Let’s stop there. I’m afraid I won’t be able to eat,” Zhang quickly interrupted Mu Mian.","“Alright,” Mu Mian reluctantly suppressed her desire to share her knowledge and continued to take photos of the concrete block, documenting the scene.","Chen Xue continued, “The person who buried the body was very smart. They considered both problems. First, they used activated carbon to absorb the odor, and then reinforced the sealing of the platform with latex to prevent the odor from escaping. Most people who bury a body in concrete would just pour concrete on top without thinking so much.”","“It seems this murderer is quite intelligent. If it weren’t for Miss Zhang’s actions, we probably would never have known that there was a body buried here,” they said as they placed the concrete-encased body into a body bag.","This residential area is mainly for the elderly, with mostly older people and children living there, so elevators were installed.","However, the elevators were small and run-down, dirty inside, and shook violently every time they reached a floor. With a body at their feet, Zhang and Wang felt a chill down their spines.","Mu Mian thought of the various accident cases she had seen involving elevator malfunctions, where the victims had died horribly. She was a bit scared and clung tightly to Fang Rui’s hand.","“Don’t worry, Mu, this elevator is old but definitely safe. It won’t malfunction, you can rest assured!” Wang said.","“How can you be so sure? You don’t know anything about elevators,” Mu Mian clung to Fang Rui’s arm. She still felt the elevator was very unsafe.","Zhang chimed in, “We understand developers. The residents here are mostly elderly and children. If the elevator had any accidents, they could cause the developer to go bankrupt!”","“...”","Fang Rui comforted Mu Mian, “Don’t be afraid, we’ll protect you.”","“Yeah. Even if something happens, we’re all together, so we won’t be alone,” Mu Mian thought, and she wasn’t nervous anymore.","“...”","As Zhang and Wang struggled to carry the body out of the building, a group of elderly men and women gathered around, pointing and whispering.","“Is there another thief in our community? Why are the police here?”","“Judging by the commotion, it doesn’t seem like they’re catching a thief!”","“Isn’t there a girl living on the fourth floor? Could this be her body they’re carrying? No, I saw her yesterday, how could she be gone today?” Sister Wang muttered.","“Tsk tsk, these two young men are so weak, they can’t even carry a girl’s body!”","“I’ve always said that the house on the fourth floor is unlucky. That girl didn’t listen to my old woman’s advice and insisted on living there. Look, now something has happened,” Sister Wang sighed.","“Yes, yes, that house hasn’t been lived in for a long time.”","Fang Rui asked an elderly woman who seemed knowledgeable, “Auntie, who used to live in that house?”","The woman glanced at Fang Rui but didn’t speak.","Zhang stepped forward and asked enthusiastically, “Sister, who used to live in that house?”","“Just call me Sister Wang,” the woman began to pour out everything she knew to Zhang. “A family of three lived there a couple of years ago. Later, they said the landlord was a pervert, secretly installing cameras in their house. They were scared to death and moved out overnight, not even taking their rent and deposit. The house hasn’t been rented out since, and I suspect it’s haunted.”","“Do you know Zhang Mingli from the fourth floor?”","“Yes, she bought that house about a month ago. I wanted to warn her that the house is haunted, but every time I tried to talk to her, she walked away and ignored me. I never got the chance to tell her,” Sister Wang complained.","Seeing that Zhang Mingli didn’t have a boyfriend, Sister Wang had originally planned to get close to her and then ask if she wanted to go on a blind date. She had many high-quality men to introduce, ensuring she could find a good match. But Zhang Mingli ignored her.","“How do you know that house is haunted?” Fang Rui asked."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: Sleeping Murder: Mummified","paragraphs":["Auntie vividly recounted the ghost story: \"In the past, our neighborhood often had thieves coming to steal things. About two years ago, a thief saw that the house was always empty, so he pried open the burglar-proof window to steal. Who knew he heard a female ghost crying inside, and he even claimed to have seen a whole group of ghosts chasing him. He was so scared that he jumped out of the window, luckily landing on a rain canopy on the first floor, only suffering a minor injury.","Since then, no thief has dared to come to our neighborhood to steal. And because of this, that house has been completely unrentable. Miss Zhang is from out of town, probably tricked by a real estate agent, to buy that house.\"","\"Do you know who the landlord of that house is?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"I don't know! I just moved here a few years ago. It's strange, I don't think I've ever seen the landlord of that house. Not to brag, but I know everyone in this neighborhood.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang went to the security guard to inquire about the situation.","The security guard said he also didn't know the owner of that house. He often saw the previous tenants though. Fang Rui saved the contact information of that tenant.","This residential area was built in the 1990s as resettlement housing, part of the demolition compensation, and the owners didn't have property certificates, making the property rights very chaotic. About eight years ago, the local government introduced a policy, and only then did the owners of these resettlement houses start to get their property certificates.","Fang Rui and his team then found the property manager, \"Does the resident in the leftmost unit on the fourth floor of Building 7 pay the property fees on time? Do you have his contact information?\"","\"Yes, we just collected the property fee not long ago. That family always doesn't pay, and it was only after I called to urge them that they reluctantly paid. Let me find it.\" The manager flipped through the payment record book while chatting with Fang Rui, \"Officer, did something happen to that house?\"","\"Why do you ask?\" Zhang inquired, \"No, it's just that the owner's things were stolen, and we're investigating.\"","\"You don't have to hide it from me. What thief would dare to steal from that house? That house is inauspicious! It's on the 4th floor, on the shady side, lacking in the five elements, and the feng shui is bad.\" The manager, an old man, was very superstitious about feng shui, muttering, \"The orientation of that house is extremely inauspicious! It's not suitable for living, light can lead to bankruptcy, heavy can lead to family breakdown.\"","\"Grandpa, don't be too superstitious. You should believe in science.\"","\"You young people don't understand, this isn't feudal superstition, it's the treasure our ancestors left us to help us avoid misfortune.\"","\"...\"","\"Found it. He's surnamed Wang, named Wang Dadong.\" The manager pointed to the handwritten number in the book, \"This is his phone number. His phone is often unreachable, you have to call several times before he picks up.\"","Zhang dialed the number, but after many attempts, no one answered. Sending him a text message also went unanswered.","On the dissection table lay the cement block. Mu Mian and Chen Xue hammered and chiseled for a long time, only clearing out one leg of the deceased, and there was still a lot of cement left on it.","\"Chen Xue, aren't we like archaeologists? We're excavating a mummified corpse.\" Mu Mian's arms were a bit sore, but she was still full of energy, \"I often went to museums to see mummies before, but always through glass, I couldn't touch them. I looked it up online, I couldn't find a legal way to touch a mummy, even if I became an archaeologist, because mummies are all in museums now, there are no mummies in the pyramids anymore.\"","\"There's also a very famous mummified corpse in China called 'Loulan Beauty,' I'll take you to see it next time we have a holiday.\" Chen Xue thought they could go on a trip together next time. Mu Mian hadn't seen the great landscapes of the motherland yet, she could take her to see them.","\"Really take me? I'll resist the temptation and make sure not to steal it.\"","\"Uh... although it's called Loulan Beauty, it's not pretty at all... okay, any corpse is irresistibly attractive to you.\" Chen Xue looked at the shriveled leg, her eyebrows slightly furrowed, \"Wait, how could there be a mummified corpse in cement? Cement would corrode the body, accelerate decay, how could the body become a mummy?\"","\"Chen Xue, I've already said it, the murderer is very professional in handling the body.\" Mu Mian reminded softly.","This was a very arduous task. Mu Mian, though full of fighting spirit, had arms that were too sore to cooperate. She had to stop and rest. Chen Xue had long since given up.","\"Mianmian, I can't stay late with you tonight.\" Chen Xue said regretfully, \"Otherwise, let's continue cleaning tomorrow? If your hands are sore, they'll shake, and you might damage the body.\"","\"It's okay, I've found someone to stay late with me.\" Mu Mian washed her hands and planned to go to the cafeteria with Fang Rui to eat.","Chen Xue smiled, changed her clothes, picked up her bag, and said to Mu Mian, \"Tonight, I'm going to meet Zhang's parents. Mianmian, I'm a bit nervous.\"","\"Why nervous? Everyone likes you. You're very excellent!\" Mu Mian comforted her. Chen Xue had a good reputation in the bureau, people often came to the office to play with her, they also often brought delicious food, and Mu Mian also ate various local specialties, of course, junk food too.","\"Mianmian, you don't understand, the hardest relationship in the world is the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law relationship, I'm afraid Zhang's mom won't like me.\" Chen Xue was a bit inferior in her feelings, growing up in a single-parent family, her profession being a forensic doctor, a slightly conservative family might find fault with her.","\"Chen Xue, you're marrying Zhang, why do you care about his parents?\" Mu Mian asked puzzled.","\"Marriage is a very complicated thing, it's not just about two people, it's about two families, no, three families, and then there will be our own little family. So you can't get married lightly.\" Chen Xue sighed, \"Mianmian, wish me luck!\"","\"Chen Xue, good luck!\"","Chen Xue left the office with her bag.","\"Chen Xue, you are very, very, very excellent, if someone doesn't like you, it must be that person's problem.\" Mu Mian said behind her.","\"Thank you, Mianmian.\"","Mu Mian took her lunch box and went to the cafeteria with Fang Rui to eat.","After getting the food, Mu Mian, as usual, put what she didn't like to eat into Fang Rui's bowl, and put what Fang Rui didn't like to eat into her own bowl.","After exchanging dishes, Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui and said seriously, \"Fang Rui, it was my oversight to propose marriage to you so rashly. It turns out that marriage is such a complicated thing, I'm not sure if I want to get married now.\"","The colleagues who were originally concentrating on eating suddenly felt that the food in front of them wasn't appetizing, they all put down their chopsticks and looked at Fang Rui with varying expressions.","\"Why do you think it's complicated?\" Fang Rui ignored their gazes and asked puzzled.","\"Because Chen Xue said marriage is about three families, including my parents' family, well, I don't have parents; your parents' family, but your mom likes me a lot, so I don't have to worry about the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law relationship; and our own family... this one is just us two.\" Mu Mian found that her marriage wasn't complicated at all.","\"See, it's not complicated.\" Fang Rui said with a smile.","\"Then why don't you want to marry me?\"","\"Mu Mian, eat quickly, we still have to work overtime after eating.\" Fang Rui pointed at Mu Mian's watch, \"Don't you want to dig out the body quickly?\"","\"I do!\" Mu Mian immediately buried her head in eating. As she chewed the food, she suddenly realized that Fang Rui was diverting the topic.","Mu Mian thought, when she had time, she would write a report, titled \"Analysis of the Reasons Why Fang Rui Doesn't Want to Marry Mu Mian.\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: Sleeping Murder: Mu Mian User Manual","paragraphs":["After clearing away the debris to expose the head of the corpse, Mu Mian and Fang Rui discovered that the deceased's teeth were pink.","\"We have rose teeth here, which suggests the deceased likely died from asphyxiation, or at least experienced a period of suffocation,\" Mu Mian analyzed.","The surface of the body, even the mouth and nose, was covered with some white crystals.","The deceased was a male.","Mu Mian used a scalpel to scrape off some of the white crystals, planning to send them for testing.","\"These white crystals look like clumped salt,\" Fang Rui picked up a few and observed them closely.","\"Salt is a good preservative,\" Mu Mian agreed.","\"The deceased's head seems to have wounds,\" Fang Rui noted.","\"Yes, there are wounds on the left forehead, the back of the head, and behind the ears. Judging from the shape of the wounds, they were likely caused by hitting the steps of a staircase. He probably rolled down the stairs before he died,\" Mu Mian explained.","\"Zhang Mingli said she pushed the deceased from upstairs, causing him to roll down the stairs. The deceased's experience is exactly as she described,\" Fang Rui was a bit surprised. He speculated, \"Could Zhang Mingli be a witness to this murder? She might have amnesia or was too young at the time of the incident to remember. But now, returning to the scene, she has recalled it.\"","\"It's possible. When the murder occurred, Miss Zhang was just a child. She might have witnessed the killing process and, due to the intense shock, lost her memory. When she returned to this house, she remembered the scene but, due to inaccurate memory, she distorted the killer into herself, mistakenly thinking she had killed someone.\"","Fang Rui suddenly remembered that Zhang Mingli had a mother with schizophrenia. He made a bolder conjecture: \"Could it be her mother who killed the person? Her mother might look very similar to her, so she mistakenly thought she had killed someone?\" Fang Rui even suspected that her mother went insane because she accidentally killed someone.","But if that were the case, why didn't Zhang Mingli know she had lived in this house before? Even if she had amnesia, wouldn't her uncle know? It seems they need to investigate the previous owners of this house thoroughly.","\"Your guess makes sense, but we don't have any evidence,\" Mu Mian was still more interested in the corpse. She restrained her urge to dissect it immediately. Chen Xue had certainly never dissected a corpse like this before. She wanted to wait until tomorrow when Chen Xue came to work and dissect it together with her. Let Chen Xue gain some experience.","Of course, a more important reason was that she was very tired now. This state was not suitable for dissecting a corpse.","Around one in the morning, they drove home.","Mu Mian took out her key to open the door, but the door opened by itself. Shen Xiyin had heard Mu Mian's footsteps and came to open the door for her.","\"Sister, I encountered a mummified corpse today. It was buried in cement, and I dug for a long time to get it out. You were right not to let me become an archaeologist; it was a wise decision. Digging up corpses is too tiring,\" Mu Mian couldn't wait to share the corpse she encountered with Shen Xiyin.","\"Xiaomian, then go get some rest quickly.\"","\"I need to adjust my schedule. I'll sleep in twenty minutes later tomorrow. The paper I was supposed to read tomorrow morning, I'll move it to the evening.\"","\"Alright, then I'll wake you up twenty minutes later tomorrow.\"","\"No need, I'll set an alarm myself.\"","Mu Mian turned back to look at Fang Rui, \"Fang Rui, goodnight. See you tomorrow.\" After saying that, Mu Mian walked towards her room.","\"Goodnight.\"","After Mu Mian entered her room, Fang Rui said to Shen Xiyin, \"Miss Shen, you don't need to worry too much about Mu Mian. I'll protect her. What happened last time won't happen again.\"","Shen Xiyin smiled at him and said, \"It's not that I'm worried she'll get into trouble. It's just that I'm used to sleeping after Xiaomian falls asleep. I think I should change this habit.\"","\"Are you going to marry Lin Sen?\"","\"Your way of speaking seems a bit influenced by Xiaomian. Of course not, whether I get married or not won't affect Xiaomian's life. I just feel that she no longer needs me.\" Shen Xiyin felt both relieved and a bit lost.","Mu Mian was the most important piece of her life. She didn't know if in the future, she could find another piece to fill the void.","Shen Xiyin took down a notebook from the bookshelf and handed it to Fang Rui, \"I'll give this to you; I think you might find it useful.\"","Fang Rui saw that the notebook was titled: \"Mu Mian's User Manual.\"","He flipped through it casually. It was divided into sections on clothing, food, housing, and transportation, recording various habits of Mu Mian. There was even an appendix that listed Mu Mian's various behaviors and language corresponding to her thoughts. It even had color illustrations depicting Mu Mian's various actions and small stories.","There were two types of handwriting in it, one light and elegant, the other powerful and vigorous. The first part mixed both handwritings, but the latter part only had the light and elegant one.","\"I'm very happy that Xiaomian can have love,\" Shen Xiyin said with a smile, \"When she was in that stage where she didn't talk much, we once wondered if Xiaomian would ever have love. So we started writing this manual, hoping to help that person better understand her. She's a bit troublesome, but she's also very simple; she's easy to take care of.\"","When Shen Xiyin mentioned \"we,\" she seemed to think of something and then withdrew her smile.","\"Sister, are you saying that she likes me?\"","\"Isn't that obvious?\"","Fang Rui's heart instantly bloomed with joy. Shen Xiyin was the most understanding person of Mu Mian, and her words must be correct.","\"Thank you!\"","After seeing Fang Rui off, Shen Xiyin also planned to go to bed. At that moment, Mu Mian came out of her room again, half-asleep, and walked up to Shen Xiyin.","\"Sister, I just said goodnight to Fang Rui but forgot to say it to you. Sister, goodnight.\"","\"Xiaomian, goodnight.\"","Mu Mian squinted her eyes and dragged her feet back to her room.","Shen Xiyin thought that even if Mu Mian no longer needed her, she would still be the most important person in Mu Mian's life.","The next day, Mu Mian sat listlessly in the office. She looked at the time; it was already 9:05, and Chen Xue still hadn't come to work. Although Chen Xue always came late and often arrived just in time, she was never late. Had something happened to her?","Just as Mu Mian was about to call Chen Xue, she walked in. She had a drooping face, her eyes were red, and she looked more exhausted than Mu Mian, who had stayed up all night.","Mu Mian sighed; digging up corpses was indeed a physically demanding task, looking at how tired Chen Xue was. Fortunately, Mu Mian was prepared; she had bought two cups of extra strong black coffee.","\"Chen Xue, I bought you some coffee. Drink it first, and then we'll go dissect that corpse,\" Mu Mian took a sip of the black coffee, it was so bitter, she stuck out her tongue to relieve the bitterness, but then she drank several more sips. She needed the coffee to perk herself up.","\"No thanks, life is already bitter enough; who would drink such a bitter thing,\" Chen Xue said softly, her head lowered.","\"But aren't you the one who loves coffee the most? You wouldn't be picky about whose coffee you drink, would you?\" Mu Mian felt that today's Chen Xue was very unusual.","\"I won't drink it anymore.\"","\"Then I'll give it to Fang Rui. Don't waste it.\"","\"...\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: Sleeping Murder: Amnesia","paragraphs":["In the autopsy room.","The cement that had wrapped the corpse was almost completely cleaned off. The body was in a curved position, with legs curled up near the abdomen. The surface of the corpse was covered with a layer of white crystalline substance.","The deceased had no clothing or any items that could prove their identity.","\"This is sodium chloride, or salt. From the analysis of its composition, it appears to be coarse salt used for pickling vegetables,\" Mu Mian explained. \"The killer sprinkled a lot of salt on the body's surface.\"","Chen Xue said, \"No wonder the body has mummified.\"","Mu Mian opened the deceased's chest cavity, revealing the internal organs. To their surprise, the victim's organs were in a semi-decomposed state. In theory, even if the body's surface was preserved, the fluids inside the organs themselves have corrosive properties, such as gastric acid and intestinal fluid, and after death, the body undergoes autolysis.","Mu Mian quickly discovered why - there was an oily substance in the stomach. The chest cavity was also coated with a film of oil. The killer had poured oil into the body, soaking the internal organs in oil to slow down the body's autolysis.","Mu Mian used a cotton swab to collect samples of the substance.","\"Chen Xue, could you take this for testing?\" Mu Mian handed the test tube containing the swab to Chen Xue.","Chen Xue stared at the notebook in her hand, unresponsive.","\"Chen Xue?\"","\"Sorry, I was lost in thought. Mian Mian, what did you want me to do?\" Chen Xue snapped back to reality.","\"Chen Xue, do you want to take some time off to rest? You look exhausted,\" Mu Mian said with concern. \"In your current state, I don't feel comfortable giving you work.\"","\"...Alright, I'll take leave and go home.\"","\"What's really going on with you?\" Mu Mian cut off a piece of cartilage from the deceased to test for DNA later.","\"Mian Mian, I'm starting to regret becoming a forensic pathologist.\"","Mu Mian looked at Chen Xue in shock, asking incredulously, \"Why? Being a forensic pathologist is such a great profession, getting to work with so many corpses. You regret it? I regret not choosing this profession sooner.\"","\"Mian Mian, others don't think like that. They think dealing with corpses every day is unlucky.\"","\"Why does their opinion matter?\" Mu Mian cut open the deceased's dried-up thigh, exposing the leg bone.","\"What if they're Zhang's family? Zhang's mother says being a forensic pathologist is too inauspicious, dealing with corpses all day will affect their family's feng shui. They say if I want to be with Zhang, I must quit my job.\"","Mu Mian went to the toolbox, contemplated for a moment, and finally chose an electric saw. Holding the saw, she suggested, \"Then don't be with Zhang, so you can continue being a forensic pathologist. Although Officer Zhang is a nice person, Sister Wen says there are plenty of good men in the world, you can find someone better.\"","\"Mian Mian, I really like him.\"","\"How can he compare to your work?\" Mu Mian said, puzzled. \"Being a forensic pathologist is such a great profession, you can't give it up.\"","\"If you had to choose between your work and Fang Rui, what would you choose?\" Chen Xue asked.","\"But I don't need to make that choice. If it weren't for this job, I wouldn't have met Fang Rui.\" Mu Mian started the electric saw and cut off one of the deceased's bones along with the joint for age testing. The body was too heavy to move around, so cutting the bone directly was easier.","The bone age could help estimate the approximate age of the deceased. This would help better identify the unknown male corpse.","\"Mian Mian, actually, I never really wanted to be a forensic pathologist. I wanted to be a doctor. When I filled out my college applications, I chose all medical-related majors, with forensic medicine as my last choice, which I filled in randomly. Unfortunately, I got assigned to that major. I didn't have the courage to retake the entrance exam, so I had to stick with it,\" Chen Xue began to open up. \"So, I don't really love this job, it's just a job.\"","\"Well, then why are you conflicted? Just choose Officer Zhang,\" Mu Mian said. \"People should do what they love.\"","Mu Mian's words suddenly enlightened Chen Xue. Love or career - which is more important? Of course, it's her career!","Chen Xue suddenly made a firm decision, \"Mian Mian, I've figured it out. I choose my work. I'm going to break up with Zhang!\"","Mu Mian thought Chen Xue was being fickle and couldn't understand her thinking. \"But you don't like being a forensic pathologist, and you like Officer Zhang.\"","\"Few people truly love their jobs. But if I'm going to quit, it should be for myself, not for someone else.\"","\"Isn't there a third option? You could try to make Zhang's mother like the forensic pathologist profession,\" Mu Mian suggested.","\"That's impossible!\"","\"Alright then.\"","Fang Rui brought Zhang Mingli back to the interrogation room.","\"Miss Zhang, we did indeed find a corpse in that house,\" Fang Rui said while observing Zhang Mingli's expression.","\"There really was a body...\" Zhang Mingli covered her mouth, laughing and crying simultaneously, \"I really killed someone! It wasn't a hallucination, it was real! Thank goodness, thank goodness, I'm not crazy, I'm normal.\"","Zhang Mingli had lived in inexplicable fear since childhood, afraid she would become insane like her mother, so when she thought everything was a hallucination, she completely broke down. She would rather be a murderer than become insane and be locked up in a mental hospital.","Zhang was stunned - it was his first time seeing someone so hopeful about having killed someone!","\"But that person died over a decade ago,\" Fang Rui reminded her.","\"Died over a decade ago? Impossible! I pushed him down just last week. I remember it clearly.\" Zhang Mingli fell back into panic.","\"Do you remember why you pushed him down the stairs?\"","\"Why... I don't know. My head hurts, I can't remember!\" Zhang Mingli clutched her head, her expression pained. \"Yes, why did I push him?\"","\"Miss Zhang, please calm down! Don't think about it anymore. Here, have some water first.\" Zhang poured a glass of water for Zhang Mingli, trying to calm her emotions.","Fang Rui also changed his approach. After Zhang Mingli's emotions stabilized, he asked, \"Miss Zhang, do you remember where your father went?\"","\"My uncle said that when my father saw my mother go insane, he ran away with another woman and took all our family's assets. I don't know where he went, and he hasn't come back to find us all these years.\"","\"Your uncle said that? Don't you remember anything from your childhood?\""]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: Sleeping Murder: Complex Relationships","paragraphs":["Zhang Mingli said, \"When I was six years old, I had a high fever that damaged my brain, so I don't remember many things. My mother developed schizophrenia because of this incident - she thought I had died from the fever, and the shock affected her mentally.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang exchanged glances. They increasingly felt that the murder case might have occurred during Zhang Mingli's childhood. The reason for her memory loss was probably not due to the fever - if her brain had been damaged by the fever, Zhang Mingli should have had intellectual problems, not just memory loss. It was more likely that she lost her memory because she witnessed the murder.","\"Everything from before you were six was told to you by your uncle?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"My aunt told me. But she probably heard it from my uncle, as she rarely came back since she lived far away. Before my mother got sick, she and my mother didn't get along well. After my mother became ill, my aunt put aside their past grievances and reconciled with her.\"","\"After your mother got sick, did you stay with your aunt?\"","\"Initially, I lived with my uncle, but my aunt-in-law and cousin didn't like me. After six months, they sent me to my aunt's house. My aunt was divorced, financially well-off, and had no children, so she treated me like her daughter - it was like a semi-adoption. My aunt would bring me back every few months to see my mother, but mother's condition was severe. She didn't believe I was her daughter and would chase me away every time she saw me. Eventually, I visited less frequently.\"","\"Do you know where your father went?\"","\"My uncle said that beast abandoned my mother and me, running away abroad with his mistress. Twenty years ago, our house was scheduled for demolition, and we suddenly had a lot of money. He took all the assets and left the country. I can't contact him, but his relatives on his side can reach him.\" Zhang Mingli's expression showed disgust when mentioning her father.","\"That apartment is so old, and the location isn't great. Why did you buy it?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"After my mother passed away, I wanted to stay and develop my career in Jiangzhou City. I planned to buy a house and looked at many properties but wasn't satisfied with any of them. However, when I saw this apartment, I fell in love with it immediately. I contacted the owner, and they were very cooperative - we completed the transfer procedures within days. I paid for the apartment in full.\"","Zhang Mingli also found it strange - the apartment seemed to have some magical pull on her. As soon as she saw it, she inexplicably fell in love with it, feeling that it gave her a sense of home.","Zhang couldn't help but think sarcastically - of course the owner would be cooperative, it was a haunted house after all. They must have been overjoyed to find someone willing to take it off their hands.","\"Have you met the owner? Do you have their contact information?\"","\"Yes.\"","The phone number Zhang Mingli provided was the same as the one from the property management office, but they had called many times without getting through.","\"Can we see the purchase contract?\"","\"Sure, I can show you right now. I have scanned copies on my phone.\"","From the contract, Fang Rui and his team learned the owner's home address. The attached property deed copy showed that the owner was Wang Dadong, and the deed was issued eight years ago.","Fang Rui asked Zhang Mingli for a hair sample for DNA testing. If the DNA matched, the body was likely her father's.","\"You suspect the deceased is that beast?\" Zhang Mingli said in shock. \"That's impossible, right? My cousin said he sent money to my grandmother from abroad just last year.\"","\"Has he ever returned from abroad?\"","\"No. My cousin said he hasn't come back once in all these years. He didn't even return when my grandfather died, claiming he couldn't get his passport sorted out.\"","After Zhang Mingli left, Zhang suddenly thought of something: \"Boss, if the deceased is Zhang Mingli's father, and her father disappeared more than twenty years ago, could the victim have been dead for over twenty years? If so, we won't be able to prosecute the killer!\"","Criminal cases have a statute of limitations, with murder cases having a maximum prosecution period of twenty years. If the victim's death occurred more than twenty years ago and no case had been filed previously, the prosecutor's office would not pursue charges. This meant that even if they discovered the truth and found the killer, they couldn't do anything about it.","The time of death for this unidentified male corpse was difficult to determine. The technical department had collected samples of cement blocks, rotted wood, and latex pieces to analyze and estimate the approximate time the body had been buried.","Mu Mian extracted DNA from the deceased's cartilage. After comparing it with Zhang Mingli's hair sample, the results showed no blood relation between them.","Chen Xue exclaimed, \"So the deceased isn't Zhang Mingli's father? Doesn't that mean all our previous deductions were wrong?\"","\"Not necessarily. This only proves that the deceased has no blood relation to Zhang Mingli - he's not her biological father,\" Mu Mian said. \"I don't share blood relations with my parents either, but they're still my mom and dad.\"","\"But Zhang Mingli's parents were both in their first marriage, and she was registered in the household registration system a year after their marriage,\" Chen Xue analyzed. \"This possibility seems unlikely. Unless Zhang Mingli's mother had an affair.\"","Mu Mian compared the deceased's DNA with samples in the police missing persons database but found no matches.","Through examining the deceased's bone age, Mu Mian determined that the victim was approximately 33-37 years old at the time of death. However, among the filed missing persons cases, there were no male victims in this age range, though there were several females.","This meant that after the victim's disappearance, their family never reported it to the police.","\"It's strange that a middle-aged man disappeared without a trace, and his family didn't report it,\" Chen Xue pondered.","\"That's actually quite normal. Most filed missing persons cases involve women and children. Middle-aged men rarely go missing,\" Mu Mian explained.","\"That makes sense. When they disappear, it's usually to escape debts or elope with someone. Their families probably wouldn't want to report it out of shame.\"","During lunch, Mu Mian and Chen Xue found seats first. Shortly after, Zhang arrived with his tray. When Chen Xue saw Zhang approaching, she immediately picked up her tray and left, deliberately choosing a seat as far from Zhang as possible.","Zhang was bewildered, completely unaware of what had happened. He looked at Mu Mian, but she was also at a loss, unsure whether to follow Chen Xue - if she left, Officer Zhang might think they were isolating him.","\"Mu Mian, what's wrong with Chen Xue today? Why is she ignoring me and walking away when she sees me?\"","\"You really don't know why?\" Mu Mian thought Zhang was quite dense not to figure it out.","\"No idea!\"","\"Officer Zhang, you might end up dying alone,\" Mu Mian sighed, looking at him. She then picked up her tray and ran to join Chen Xue.","Zhang was completely confused. When Fang Rui sat down beside him, Zhang asked, \"Boss, Mu Mian said I'll die alone - what does that mean? Has she taken up fortune-telling?\"","\"Chen Xue wants to break up with you.\"","\"Break up... that's impossible, our relationship is so good... wait, why does Chen Xue want to break up with me?\" Zhang suddenly panicked. Why break up out of nowhere?","\"What have you done recently?\"","\"Nothing special. I even took her to meet my parents, we had dinner together, and they quite liked her.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Did you leave during the meal?\"","Zhang suddenly remembered something. During the meal, his mother had sent him out to buy milk tea.","\"Now you know the reason?\" Fang Rui picked up his tray and left too.","\"...\"","Chen Xue left after barely eating anything. Only Mu Mian was left eating, but soon Fang Rui sat down across from her.","\"Fang Rui, the deceased isn't Zhang Mingli's biological father - they have no blood relation,\" Mu Mian paused, then continued, \"But it's possible her mother had an affair. We need to rule out this possibility. Can you find any close relatives of the father listed on Zhang Mingli's household registration?\"","\"Zhang Mingli's grandmother is still alive.\"","\"That's great. But if he really isn't Zhang Mingli's father, then we'll be looking for a needle in a haystack.\""]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Sleeping Murder: The Backyard Owner","paragraphs":["The landlord of that apartment, Wang Dadong, had been unreachable by phone. After Fang Rui and Zhang visited his home, they learned from his wife that he had been arrested and detained during an anti-prostitution operation.","Zhang remarked with exasperation, \"We've been looking everywhere for him, only to find out he'd already gotten himself arrested.\"","Wang Dadong was forty-three years old, unemployed, and lived in a rundown rental unit in an urban village. He had a son in middle school, and the family of three was cramped into a one-bedroom apartment. His son could only sleep in a partitioned area of the living room, and they were living in quite difficult circumstances.","His wife was short and plump, with a fierce demeanor. She complained, \"This good-for-nothing man can never hold onto money. Whenever he gets his hands on any cash, he wastes it on all sorts of nonsense. When he gets out, I'm going to break his legs!\"","\"Small amount of money? Didn't he just sell an apartment?\" Zhang asked, puzzled.","\"What? He sold an apartment? That's impossible! Where would he get an apartment from? If he had one, would we be squeezed into this rental unit?\" Wang Dadong's wife exploded in rage. She grabbed a mop from beside the door, intending to rush to the detention center to beat her husband, but Zhang stopped her.","\"You didn't know about this?\" Fang Rui handed her the purchase contract to look at. \"But his name is on the property deed.\"","\"This... it's his name and ID, and his fingerprint too... Could he be kept by some rich woman? A piece of trash like him definitely couldn't afford an apartment!\" Wang Dadong's wife broke down. After all these years of frugal living, she discovered her husband had an apartment and had kept it secret from her. She covered her face and began to sob.","What a miserable marriage this had turned out to be!","Zhang glanced at the photo on Wang Dadong's ID card and thought this scenario seemed unlikely.","\"Boss, I don't think that apartment really belongs to Wang Dadong,\" Zhang said.","\"It probably isn't his,\" Fang Rui agreed, but he was confused. If the killer had kept the apartment vacant, wouldn't the body have remained undiscovered forever? Why did they decide to rent it out before, and why suddenly sell it now?","After leaving Wang Dadong's home, they went to the detention center to find him.","When Wang Dadong saw them, he complained, \"Officers, I've already confessed. Why are you still interrogating me? I really haven't done anything else illegal. I only made a deal with Jiaojiao, I don't know any other women, and I didn't do business with them.\"","\"Wang Dadong, did you sell an apartment recently?\"","\"What apartment? How could I have an apartment to sell?\" Wang Dadong said with a smirk, but suddenly remembering something, he quickly changed his tune, \"Oh right, I did sell an apartment. Got over a million yuan for it.\"","\"Why doesn't your wife know about this?\" Zhang asked.","\"A man's business doesn't need to be shared with some woman. I can make my own decisions, why should I tell her?\"","Fang Rui placed a photo in front of Wang Dadong, \"We found a corpse in the second bedroom of that apartment.\"","The photo showed a bay window that had been pried open, revealing the body inside.","\"A corpse? Officers, you're trying to trick me, right? How could there be a body in a perfectly good apartment?\" Wang Dadong's face turned pale. \"Besides, I've already sold the apartment to Zhang Mingli. If there's any issue, you should find her.\"","\"This body is from over a decade ago. You were the previous owner, so naturally we need to talk to you.\"","Seeing that the apartment was involved in a murder case, Wang Dadong quickly tried to distance himself.","\"Officers, this apartment isn't really mine, I'm just the nominal owner. It belongs to my cousin Wang Yuanfang. She wanted to buy a second property at the time but didn't want to waste her first-time buyer status, so she put it under my name. She gave me a few thousand yuan, and I agreed. I barely ever went to that apartment. I couldn't possibly have killed anyone, officers, I'm innocent!\"","\"We never said you killed anyone. Why are you so agitated?\"","\"It must have been my cousin who killed someone. She's an extremely vicious person, won't even take care of her own parents. I wondered why she gave me so much money and put the apartment in my name - turns out it was a murder house!\" Wang Dadong spat in disgust, anger rising within him. After his cousin got rich, she became increasingly arrogant, ordering him around, and now it turned out she had set him up!","\"Do you have your cousin's home address and contact information?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes.\"","\"What does your cousin do for a living?\"","\"She's a high school Chinese teacher. But don't let that fool you - after she made some money, she forgot all about morals and decency. When her elderly mother was seriously ill, she actually said, 'Why won't this old thing just die already?' What kind of person would say something like that?\"","\"When did she come into money? How did she get rich?\"","\"About twenty years ago, she suddenly had enough money to buy houses and cars. No one knows where it came from. Her husband is also a high school teacher. They used to be dirt poor, couldn't even afford to raise their child, always borrowing money from us. Then somehow they suddenly became wealthy. Must have embezzled public funds.\"","\"Is her husband's name Zhang Taotao?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes! That's his name. Officers, how did you know?\" Wang Dadong said with schadenfreude, \"Don't tell me her husband is the killer? Tsk tsk, who would have thought Teacher Zhang, with all his proper appearances, was actually a murderer. Haha, my cousin is going to be a murderer's wife now. Let's see how smug she acts after this.\"","Fang Rui suspected that Zhang Taotao's money might have actually belonged to Zhang Mingli's mother. Seeing that Zhang Mingli's mother had gone insane and Zhang Mingli had lost her memory, he probably embezzled their assets and sent Zhang Mingli to be raised by her aunt.","If that was the case, the deceased was likely Zhang Mingli's father listed on her household registration.","\"Stop rambling. Focus on reforming yourself in here. Your wife has a hard enough time managing the household,\" Zhang interrupted, unable to hold back his advice. \"When you get out, find a job. You have a child now, so earn money properly and take care of your family.\"","\"What family is there to take care of? If you had a wife like mine, would you want to go home? Even my kid doesn't acknowledge me. What's the point of going back? I'm better off staying here.\"","Zhang struggled to contain his urge to curse at him."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: Sleeping Murder: Identification Confirmed","paragraphs":["The DNA test results comparing Zhang Mingli's grandmother and the deceased quickly came back. Zhang Mingli's grandmother was confirmed to be the mother of the deceased, and the age of Zhang Mingli's father, Li Bao, matched that of the deceased.","Zhang Mingli's grandmother had given birth to four daughters and two sons, and she lived with her eldest son. This evidence strongly suggested that the deceased was indeed Zhang Mingli's father, Li Bao.","When Zhang Mingli's grandmother received the call asking her to come to the police station to identify the body, her first reaction was that it was a scam call.","\"You heartless scammer! My son is living well in America. It's your son who's dead, trying to deceive an old lady like me. You have no conscience!\" Zhang Mingli's grandmother, though in her seventies, still had a strong, forceful voice.","\"Grandmother, you say your son is in America. Has he ever video called you or come back to visit?\"","\"My son can't come back from abroad, but he always sends money and clothes from overseas. During Chinese New Year, he even sent me a red envelope with several hundred yuan. You're just a scammer!\"","Li Qiang, Zhang Mingli's uncle, was listening to the conversation nearby and took the phone: \"Mother, let me talk to them.\"","\"Qiang, they're saying Bao is dead.\"","\"Mother, you already said they're scammers. Let's ignore them.\"","He took the phone and walked outside before speaking: \"Officer, you're saying my brother is dead?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Ah, I knew something had happened to Bao. Otherwise, why wouldn't he have come back all these years? He was always the most filial one! Officer, I'll come to the police station shortly to identify the body. Please contact me directly for any matters, don't contact my mother. I'm worried she won't be able to handle the news.\"","\"Alright.\"","When Li Qiang arrived at the morgue, Mu Mian pulled open the freezer drawer and said, \"This is your brother's body.\"","Li Qiang didn't cry or make any excessive movements. He just stood there, looking down at his brother's body. All these years, he had believed his brother was really working abroad, thinking he was doing well, even though he never called home or sent any news.","When he heard about his brother's death, everything that hadn't made sense suddenly became clear. So his brother had been dead all along.","\"How did my brother die?\" Li Qiang asked.","\"Preliminary findings indicate the cause of death was asphyxiation,\" Mu Mian replied.","In the past, Mu Mian would have told him that his brother had been pushed down the stairs, suffered a head injury, and then the killer had preserved the body with coarse salt and tung oil before encasing it in concrete. But now Mu Mian knew that victims' families didn't really want to know the details of how their loved ones died.","Fang Rui and Zhang took Li Qiang to the interrogation room to take his statement.","\"Officers, was my brother murdered? But he was just an elementary school teacher, honest and kind, well-liked by everyone. How could anyone want to murder him?\"","\"Mr. Li, please don't worry. We need to understand some details from you,\" Zhang handed him a glass of water. \"When did you completely lose contact with your brother?\"","\"It was around August 2004, during the summer break. My brother's wife, Zhang Huanhuan, suddenly called home saying my brother was having an affair and was making a huge fuss about getting divorced. None of us knew what was happening at the time. At first, we didn't believe it - my brother had always been an honest person, and they had such a good marriage. But that year our family had just received a house and a large sum of money from relocation compensation, so we wondered if the money had changed him. We tried our best to calm my sister-in-law down, and eventually she agreed not to divorce.","We planned to have a family meeting to properly talk to my brother, but he wouldn't answer my calls. When I went to his house to look for him, I heard that Mingli was in the hospital, so I went there to see her. After I left the hospital, I received a text from my brother saying he had gone abroad with Juan and told us not to look for him.","Three months later, he sent another text saying he had settled down in America and not to worry about him. After that, we never received any more messages from him. My sister-in-law's family came to our house and caused a huge scene. Feeling guilty, we gave them a large sum of money to finally settle the matter.\"","\"But your mother said your brother often sends money from abroad?\" Zhang questioned.","\"Ah, that was just to make my mother feel better. She loves my brother the most, and if she knew he was missing, she would have worried herself sick. I often buy things myself or withdraw cash, package them up with fake shipping labels, and tell my mother they're from my brother. To make it more convincing, I even deceived my wife and children - they all believe my brother regularly sends money home.\"","\"Didn't you think about reporting it to the police?\"","\"During the first few years after he went missing, I really believed he had gone to America. He used to talk about how great and free America was, saying he would definitely visit if he had the money. I thought maybe he really had gone there. Later, I started feeling something was wrong - even in America, he could still make phone calls home. I thought maybe he had met with foul play in America, but I had no connections there and didn't know how to report it. I never imagined he hadn't left the country at all.\"","\"Do you still have those text messages?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Yes. I keep that phone charged regularly and maintain the phone plan. I was afraid my brother might call and I wouldn't be able to receive it,\" Li Qiang said. \"The phone is at my house. I'll go get it right away.\"","\"How was your brother's relationship with his wife?\"","\"It was good. They fell in love naturally. You young people might not know, but twenty-some years ago, most marriages were arranged - it was rare for people to find their own partners. My sister-in-law was also an elementary school teacher. They taught at the same school and gradually fell in love. That's why I could never understand how my brother could have an affair and abandon his family to go abroad.\"","\"How was your brother with his daughter, Zhang Mingli?\"","\"He absolutely adored her. Let me put it this way - back then, how many men would smile after their wives gave birth to a daughter? When Mingli was born, my brother announced it to everyone with such joy, you'd think his wife had given birth to a son. Before the relocation compensation, they were very poor, but they would scrimp and save to give their daughter the best of everything. That's why I never really believed my brother would abandon his wife and child over an affair.\"","Zhang couldn't help but sigh inwardly - if Li Bao had known Zhang Mingli wasn't his biological daughter, he probably wouldn't have smiled at all.","\"Did your brother show any unusual behavior before he disappeared?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Unusual behavior? He kept calling me during that period, but wouldn't say what was wrong when I asked. He was always trying to get me to drink with him. My restaurant was just starting up then, and I was extremely busy, so I didn't pay much attention to him. Thinking back carefully now, maybe my brother really was having an affair at that time.\""]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: Sleeping Murder: Property Seizure","paragraphs":["\"How was your brother's financial situation?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"At that time, he had just received an apartment and 100,000 in cash. Don't underestimate that amount - it was a huge sum back then.\"","\"Was the apartment in Beiyuan Garden?\"","\"Yes, it was there.\"","\"What happened to his assets after he disappeared?\"","\"My sister-in-law claimed that my brother had taken all their money and they wouldn't let us see Mingli. We felt guilty at the time, so we gave my sister-in-law custody of Mingli and the apartment, plus 50,000 yuan for child support,\" Li Qiang said. \"Later, when we heard my sister-in-law had gone insane, I wanted to take Mingli to live with us, but her uncle always prevented us from seeing her. We felt my brother was partly responsible for my sister-in-law's mental breakdown, and since my business was doing well then, I gave her uncle another 150,000 yuan for her medical expenses.\"","Zhang sighed, thinking how Li Qiang would be devastated if he knew Zhang Mingli wasn't actually his brother's biological daughter, and all that money had gone straight into her uncle's pocket.","Seeing Zhang's complex expression, Li Qiang asked puzzled, \"Officer, what's wrong?\"","\"Nothing. Let's go to your house to find that phone.\"","\"Alright. Officers, please tell my mother you're here for a census, and don't mention anything about my brother, okay?\"","\"No problem.\"","Li Qiang drove his own car leading the way, while Fang Rui and Zhang followed in their vehicle.","\"Boss, Zhang Mingli's uncle is truly despicable. Not only did he embezzle the mother and daughter's property, but he also extorted money from the Li family,\" Zhang couldn't help but complain. \"I thought he was a decent person when I first saw him, but I never expected him to be so vicious. And that house rightfully belonged to Zhang Mingli, yet he sold it back to her and made another fortune. He's truly a genius at making money!\"","\"I even suspect he might be involved in this murder case,\" Fang Rui analyzed. \"Zhang Mingli's mother had schizophrenia - how could she have handled the body so calmly and thoroughly? Could someone have helped her?\"","\"Right! Zhang Taotao was even a chemistry teacher. God, this is terrifying when you think about it.\" Zhang suddenly felt a chill down his spine. He had originally thought Zhang Taotao was just wickedly occupying a widow and orphan's property, but now he wondered if there was more to it.","\"Boss, if he buried the body, why would he sell the house to Zhang Mingli? Wasn't he afraid she might remember something? He wouldn't risk his life just for money, would he?\" Zhang questioned.","Fang Rui thought for a moment and said, \"If he only helped bury the body, the maximum sentence wouldn't exceed ten years, and the statute of limitations should be no more than fifteen years. The limitation period has already passed. So even if we discover his crime and find evidence against him, we still can't convict him.\"","Zhang fell silent. It's not scary that bad people do bad things; it's scary when bad people are smart.","Li Qiang's home was a small villa. When Fang Rui and Zhang arrived, his elderly mother was sitting by the door sunbathing. The blanket on her legs had fallen to the ground, and Li Qiang picked it up, dusted it off, and placed it back over her legs.","Li Qiang led them to the second floor and opened a door, saying, \"This was my brother's room. After he said he was going abroad, I brought all his things from his house back here. Everything's here. See if you can find any clues.\"","\"Mr. Li, you're very good to your brother,\" Zhang noticed there was no dust in the room, showing it was regularly cleaned.","\"He's my own brother,\" Li Qiang said chokingly. He had kept this room intact, hoping that one day his brother would return and find that he would always have a place in this home, no matter how long he'd been gone.","There weren't many items in the room, just some books and clothes. Zhang checked the clothes, shaking each piece and feeling through the pockets.","\"Officer, you don't need to check those clothes, there's nothing in them, I've already looked through them.\"","Fang Rui casually flipped through the books, which were all teaching materials with no writing in them. As he was looking, a piece of paper fell out.","He picked it up and read the scrawled message: \"Li Bao, your wife is having an affair, your daughter isn't yours.\"","The paper was crumpled, looking like it had been crushed and then tucked into the book.","\"Which bastard wrote this? My brother and his wife were so in love, how could she have an affair? Mingli is such a smart and lovely child, anyone can see she's my brother's daughter,\" Li Qiang said indignantly.","Zhang couldn't help but think to himself: But Zhang Mingli really isn't!","\"Were these books brought back from your brother's house?\"","\"Yes. At the time, my sister-in-law had thrown all my brother's things in the garbage, but I secretly retrieved them.\"","Li Qiang found a black Nokia phone in the drawer. After charging it for a while, he opened the text messages.","\"These are the last two messages my brother sent me before losing contact.\"","The message read: \"Brother, I love Juan so much, I would die for her. Zhang Huanhuan is crazy and won't leave me alone, so I have to go abroad with Juan. Brother, don't worry too much about me and mom, I've taken all the money with me, so I won't be short of cash. I'll contact you once I'm settled.\"","The last message read: \"Brother, Juan and I are in America now, everything's good here, don't worry about me and mom.\"","After reading the messages, Fang Rui checked other texts Li Bao had sent to Li Qiang. He noticed that in other messages, Li Bao referred to their mother using the word \"niang,\" but in these two messages, he used \"ma.\"","\"How did your brother usually address your mother?\"","\"In our area, we usually say 'niang.' We don't say 'ma.'\" Li Qiang suddenly realized something and asked, \"Do you suspect these two messages weren't sent by my brother? Was he already dead by then?\"","Zhang nodded gravely.","\"Do you know who Juan is?\"","\"No. We asked Bao's friends, but they didn't know anyone with 'Juan' in their name. There wasn't anyone like that at the school where he taught either.\"","After leaving Li Qiang's house, Zhang said, \"Who could have written that note? Why would they tell Li Bao about this? Was it to create conflict between the couple? Could the writer be the lover?\"","\"It's possible that this note caused their marriage to break down, and Zhang Mingli's mother accidentally pushed her father during an argument,\" Fang Rui speculated.","Fang Rui had originally wanted to summon Zhang Taotao to the police station for questioning. But even if there was evidence that Zhang Taotao had seized Zhang Mingli's property, that would be a civil dispute, which they couldn't handle. Currently, there was no evidence linking Zhang Taotao to this murder case.","After dinner, Fang Rui and Zhang drove directly to Zhang Taotao's house.","A young man opened the door. He was handsome, with features somewhat similar to Zhang Mingli's.","His temper wasn't good though, and he asked impatiently, \"Who are you? Who are you looking for?\"","\"Is Zhang Mingli here?\"","He became even more agitated and turned to shout into the house: \"Zhang Mingli, don't you have any sense of being a guest in someone else's home? This is my house, please don't let your questionable friends come visiting, okay?\"","Zhang Mingli quickly ran over: \"Mingyuan, don't be so rude! Officer Fang, Officer Zhang, is there any new development in the case?\"","Seeing they were police officers, Zhang Mingyuan immediately put on a friendly face, \"Officers, I apologize for my poor attitude earlier. Please come in, let me make you some tea.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui noticed that Zhang Mingli and Zhang Mingyuan's features were very similar, and standing together, they looked exactly like sister and brother."]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Sleeping Murder: Malice","paragraphs":["Seeing Fang Rui continuously observing Zhang Mingyuan, Zhang Mingli tried to defend her cousin: \"Officer, I'm sorry, my cousin is young and doesn't know better. Please don't take offense.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Young? How old is he?\"","\"Twenty-five.\"","\"He's not much younger than you then,\" Fang Rui retorted casually.","\"We were born on the same day. I was born a few minutes earlier. When we were little, everyone called us dragon-phoenix twins,\" Zhang Mingli tried to ease the tension.","Officer Zhang also observed the siblings and suddenly realized why Fang Rui had asked about their age. He exchanged a glance with Fang Rui, who gave him a subtle signal. Officer Zhang nodded, indicating he understood the instruction.","\"Miss Zhang, where is your uncle? We'd like to ask him some questions.\"","\"He and my aunt went for a walk. They'll be back soon. Please have a seat.\"","\"Alright.\"","Zhang Mingyuan, currently unemployed and preparing for the civil service exam, was somewhat intimidated by Fang Rui, so he kept asking Officer Zhang various questions.","\"Brother Strong, is police work very tough? Is the pay good? What are the benefits like? How many tens of thousands can you make in a year?\"","Officer Zhang responded perfunctorily while eyeing his thick hair, and when Zhang Mingyuan wasn't paying attention, quickly and precisely plucked a few strands of his hair.","\"Ouch! What the hell are you doing? That hurts!\"","\"Sorry, sorry, I saw a white hair and wanted to help you remove it. It's gone now,\" Officer Zhang said jokingly.","\"How could I have white hair? Where was it?\"","\"I threw it away,\" Officer Zhang said, standing up with his fist closed. \"I need to use the bathroom. Where is it?\"","\"Over there.\"","About five minutes later, Zhang Taotao returned with his wife Wang Yuanfang. His wife was plump with a smile on her face, appearing to be an easy-going person.","Upon seeing Fang Rui and his colleague, Zhang Taotao frowned and said disapprovingly, \"Why do you keep coming to question Mingli? She has nothing to do with that case. She was just a child then. How could she possibly be a murderer?\"","\"How do you know Zhang Mingli was a child when the incident occurred?\" Fang Rui questioned.","\"Mingli told me.\"","Zhang Mingli frowned. She had only told her uncle that the police had found a body, but hadn't mentioned what condition it was in. Why did her uncle know so much about it?","\"What we told Miss Zhang was that the deceased had been dead for at least ten years. At that time, Miss Zhang would have been fourteen or fifteen - not exactly a child, right?\"","\"Officers, aren't you just arguing semantics? How is fourteen or fifteen not still a child? Mingli is twenty-five now, and she's still a child in my eyes,\" Zhang Taotao explained calmly.","Wang Yuanfang chimed in, \"Officers, if you have any questions in the future, you can ask us outside. Coming to our home so often affects our reputation. You police should consider us ordinary citizens too.\"","Fang Rui asked directly, \"Mr. Zhang, according to our investigation, the second month after Zhang Mingli's father Li Bao ran away with his lover, your sister was admitted to the hospital for schizophrenia. We'd like to know how her assets were handled?\"","Zhang Mingli also looked at Zhang Taotao. She had asked similar questions before, but her uncle always said that her beast of a father had taken all the assets when he left.","\"That beast Li Bao took all the money and ran. What inheritance? I even advanced the money for my sister's medical expenses.\"","\"But Li Qiang said he gave you two hundred thousand yuan gradually to take care of Zhang Mingli and her mother. How did that become money you advanced? Mr. Zhang, we've already investigated the bank withdrawal records,\" Fang Rui decided to test him, \"Your brother-in-law's bankbook shows...\"","Zhang Taotao raised his voice, interrupting Fang Rui, and said to his son, \"Mingyuan, go out with your sister to buy some fruit and snacks. We don't have anything to serve our guests. Mingli, go with Mingyuan.\"","\"Dad, can't Zhang Mingli go by herself?\"","\"Just go when I tell you to. Why so many questions?\"","Zhang Mingli guessed that her uncle wanted to get rid of her. Her aunt had once told her that her uncle and aunt weren't good people, they just leeched off relatives. Her aunt had passed away, her mother had passed away, and her uncle was her only remaining relative. Even if she knew her uncle might have seized things that belonged to her, she couldn't bring herself to confront him.","\"Mingyuan, let's go.\"","After they left, Zhang Taotao said to Fang Rui and his colleague disapprovingly, \"Officers, this is our family matter. You have no right to interfere in our family affairs.\"","\"We may not have jurisdiction over your family matters, but we have the right to investigate the whereabouts of a murder victim's assets.\"","\"You're saying the deceased is my brother-in-law? Impossible...\" Zhang Taotao exaggeratedly opened his mouth in surprise.","Fang Rui said, \"Mr. Zhang, shouldn't you first explain to us why you didn't recognize your sister and brother-in-law's former home?\"","\"I... that house was sold by my brother-in-law. It was so long ago, and I didn't visit their home often, so it's normal that I didn't recognize it.\"","\"Then you know Wang Dadong, right?\" Fang Rui looked at his wife. \"You couldn't possibly not know your cousin? Your cousin has already confessed everything.\"","Wang Yuanfang became flustered, looking helplessly at her husband.","\"That house was transferred to me by my sister. Once it was transferred to me, it became mine. I can put it under whoever's name I want and sell it to whoever I want!\" Zhang Taotao remained composed. \"Go ahead and investigate all you want!\"","Zhang Taotao took out a property transfer agreement and threw it on the table. \"Look, this transfer document was written by my sister herself, and we had it notarized in court. Everything was legal and proper.\"","Fang Rui noticed the date on the agreement was the week before Zhang Mingli's mother entered the psychiatric hospital.","Fang Rui said, \"Legal and proper? How can you prove Zhang Mingli's mother was mentally sound at that time? You know that any contract signed by a schizophrenia patient is invalid, right?\"","Zhang Taotao's face paled. He berated, \"You police should just focus on solving cases. Why are you meddling in my family affairs?\"","\"Upholding legal justice is also part of our job. Mr. Zhang, we will advise Miss Zhang Mingli to sue you to recover her rightful property.\"","When money became involved, Zhang Taotao's emotions became unstable. He cursed, \"Didn't Zhang Mingli's crazy mother's treatment cost money? Didn't Zhang Mingli need living expenses? What's wrong with me taking one house?\"","\"Just one house?\" Fang Rui questioned.","\"Are you police taking out your frustration on an ordinary citizen because you can't solve the case? Let me tell you, I am Zhang Huanhuan's brother and Zhang Mingli's uncle. Their assets are mine! She won't dare sue me. If she dares to sue me, I'll break her legs!\"","Officer Zhang walked behind him, observing for a long time until he finally spotted a short hair that had fallen on his clothes. When no one was paying attention, he secretly picked up the hair and wrapped it in a tissue."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: Sleeping Murder: Conspiracy","paragraphs":["Fang Rui didn't want to engage in this meaningless argument with him. As they were about to leave, when they opened the door, Zhang Mingli was standing there alone, tears streaming down her face.","\"Miss Zhang, you...\" Zhang felt that their previous conversation had been cruel to Zhang Mingli.","Zhang Mingli hastily packed some luggage and left her uncle's house.","Zhang handed her a tissue and consoled her: \"Miss Zhang, if you want to sue your uncle, we can help provide evidence.\"","\"Thank you, but I don't want to sue him. He's my only relative now. If he wants those assets, he can have them. Consider it the price of cutting ties with him - I'll never associate with him again,\" Zhang Mingli wiped her tears, \"Don't worry about me, I'm strong. I'll go find a hotel to stay at.\"","Fang Rui couldn't help but remind her: \"Miss Zhang, do you really think there's any familial bond between you and your uncle?\"","\"That's right, your uncle seized your property and abandoned you with your aunt, he might even have...\" Zhang swallowed the rest of his words.","Zhang Mingli fell silent. Over the years, her uncle would always call to check on her, acting like a caring uncle, showing concern, but in reality, he only made empty promises without any actual support.","Her aunt always said her uncle was hypocritical, and back then Zhang Mingli would defend him. Now thinking about it, if her uncle really wanted to take care of her, he wouldn't have left her with her aunt.","\"Actually, since I was little, I've had a recurring dream where there's a loving couple who are very kind to me, and in the dream, I'm very happy,\" Zhang Mingli started crying again, \"I think they were my parents, but they weren't good to me at all. My mother went mad, she would always curse at me, saying I wasn't her child, that I was illegitimate; my father ran away with another woman, he abandoned me. But I don't know why I still keep having this dream.\"","That's why when Zhang Mingli saw that house, she bought it without hesitation. That house made her feel like she was returning to a warm, happy home, even though none of her relatives were there.","\"Thank you for listening to all this. I feel better now.\" Zhang Mingli took a deep breath, looked at Fang Rui and Zhang, and suddenly said firmly, \"Officer Fang, Officer Zhang, I want to recover my memories from before I was six years old.\"","\"Perhaps you could try hypnosis to recover those memories,\" Fang Rui suggested.","Watching Zhang Mingli get into a taxi with her suitcase, Fang Rui and Zhang followed the taxi in their car, only leaving after they saw her enter the hotel.","Zhang sighed: \"I hope the truth isn't what we suspect, otherwise it would be too cruel for Miss Zhang!\"","Mu Mian compared Zhang Mingyuan's DNA with the deceased's, and the results showed they were father and son; she then compared Zhang Mingli's DNA with Zhang Taotao's, and the results showed they were father and daughter.","When Chen Xue saw the report, she was stunned: \"What's going on? Zhang Mingli's uncle is actually her biological father? Her mother's affair partner couldn't be... no, no, her cousin is her father's biological son. Were Zhang Mingli and Zhang Mingyuan switched at birth?\"","Chen Xue realized this case was becoming increasingly complex.","\"A baby boy and a baby girl wouldn't likely be switched by accident. Unless it was intentional,\" Mu Mian said.","Combining the clues that Fang Rui and his team had already uncovered, Chen Xue formed a terrifying theory.","During the morning meeting, Mu Mian reported this discovery.","Everyone fell silent.","Zhang analyzed: \"Have you noticed, Zhang Taotao is a high school teacher, and twenty years ago was when the one-child policy was strictest. Someone in his position as a teacher couldn't have had a second child. So it's very possible that Zhang Taotao and his wife switched the children, so he could have a son. Even though this son wasn't his biological child, being his sister's child meant they still shared blood ties. My God, how evil can someone be?\"","Chen Xue angrily said: \"So even though they knew Zhang Mingli was their biological daughter, and they had the opportunity to raise her, they still sent her to her aunt to be raised. They're beasts! Not even raising their own daughter.\"","\"I suspect it's because Zhang Mingli's aunt was a businesswoman, wealthy, divorced with no children, and never remarried. Think about it, if Zhang Mingli was raised by her, after her aunt's death, wouldn't the property go to Zhang Mingli?\" Zhang said excitedly, \"We found out earlier that Zhang Mingli's aunt passed away recently, also from cancer, and left all her property to Zhang Mingli.\"","Chen Xue analyzed: \"So Zhang Taotao coaxed Zhang Mingli back, probably to seize the property her aunt left her. My God, Zhang Taotao is terrifying, truly trying to squeeze everything from his own family!\"","Mu Mian watched Zhang and Chen Xue analyzing back and forth, feeling somewhat happy, thinking Officer Zhang and Chen Xue probably wouldn't break up now, as they were finally talking to each other again.","The others remained silent. They had seen many brutal cases and many vicious criminals, but they still felt afraid of someone like Zhang Taotao.","Zhang angrily said: \"Is there really no way to arrest this beast in human clothing, Zhang Taotao? My God, he's so calculating! It's terrifying!\"","Chen Xue agreed: \"We must find a way to let the law punish him! Such an evil person, preying on women like a parasite. Look how many people he's hurt. Just because he didn't have a son, he switched someone else's, destroying their family while living comfortably himself.\"","Everyone vented their anger.","After everyone calmed down, Mu Mian said: \"We found tung oil in the victim's body. Tung oil has specific sales locations. If we could find the sales records from back then, we could prove he was involved in this murder.\"","Fang Rui said: \"Miss Zhang agreed to undergo hypnosis to recover her memories, maybe she'll remember something.\"","Fang Rui felt the case from back then couldn't be that simple. Li Qiang said his brother and sister-in-law had a good relationship, so even if they had conflicts, it shouldn't have escalated to violence.","\"There's also that bagua mirror,\" Zhang said.","\"What about the mirror?\"","\"Different fortune tellers have different bagua mirrors, with different engravings and such. If we could find the fortune teller from back then, maybe they'd remember who commissioned this mirror.\"","Wang gave Zhang a thumbs up: \"I didn't know you understood metaphysics.\"","\"Well, it's just that my mom is really into all this stuff, and I...\" Zhang's voice trailed off as he saw Chen Xue's face fall."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Sleeping Murder: Clues","paragraphs":["After establishing a clear direction for the investigation, Fang Rui assigned the tasks. He and Mu Mian would investigate the source of the tung oil, Zhang and Chen Xue would look into the bagua mirror, while others would interview the schools and neighbors where Zhang Mingli's parents had worked, hoping to find a breakthrough through the victim's social connections.","Chen Xue immediately objected, \"I don't want to work with him! Besides, I'm a forensic expert. I only handle autopsies, not field investigations.\"","Zhang's previously cheerful expression crumbled. He had been trying to talk to Chen Xue for days, but she would walk away whenever she saw him, never giving him a chance to explain.","He had a huge argument with his mother and moved out of his home into the dormitory. While he was fighting against his family's wishes, Chen Xue had already given up on him.","\"Chen Xue, we're short-handed right now, so please help out. The statute of limitations for this case is approaching, and we need to find evidence to identify the killer quickly,\" Fang Rui tried to comfort her, \"You wouldn't want the murderer to escape justice, would you?\"","Chen Xue fell silent, knowing she couldn't let personal feelings affect her work. She was about to suggest teaming up with Mu Mian instead, but Mu Mian was already excitedly discussing investigation plans with Fang Rui.","What a fair-weather friend.","Chen Xue glanced at Zhang, who was looking at her hopefully, and reluctantly agreed.","Mu Mian and Fang Rui drove off to investigate the source of the tung oil.","Tung oil comes in two forms: raw and processed. Raw tung oil is used in medicine and chemical industry, and is rarely sold to individuals. Processed tung oil is refined from raw tung oil and is mainly used in varnishes and other coatings.","Twenty years ago, before online shopping existed, hardware stores and paint shops would sell tung oil.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian interviewed elderly residents near the crime scene, asking about any old shops that used to sell tung oil. They provided some shop names and addresses.","When they checked these locations, they found that the shops had either closed down or relocated. They finally found one old shop, but it had no sales records or accounting books.","This lead seemed to be a dead end.","Zhang and Chen Xue were driving aimlessly around the streets. When they passed the same intersection for the third time, Chen Xue finally spoke up.","\"Zhang Qiang, weren't we supposed to be looking for the fortune teller? Why are we driving in circles?\"","Zhang replied dejectedly, \"I was waiting for you to tell me where we should start looking.\"","\"Zhang Qiang, aren't you the police officer here? Why are you asking me?\"","\"Zhang Taotao used to live in the Jiangzhou No. 13 Middle School staff housing complex. If he was looking for a fortune teller, he probably started searching near his home. Let's start with the most famous fortune tellers.\"","After analyzing, Zhang paused and added, \"Skilled fortune tellers are usually quite old, so they might have passed away. Even if they're still alive, they must be very elderly now.\"","\"Then let's hurry!\"","There was an old street near Jiangzhou Middle School that was home to many funeral industry workers, offering everything from feng shui and fortune-telling to burial clothes and funeral wreaths.","After asking around the shops, Zhang and Chen Xue learned about a famous fortune teller known as the \"Living Immortal.\"","He earned this nickname not only because of his accurate predictions and great skills but also because he was over ninety years old – living so long naturally made him a \"Living Immortal.\"","When Zhang and Chen Xue entered his shop, they saw an elderly man with white hair sitting there, looking spirited, with bubble tea on his table and a phone in his hand as he scrolled through short videos.","Hearing footsteps approach, the old man looked up and carefully observed Zhang and Chen Xue. He asked, \"Young believers, are you here to learn about your love destiny? From your facial features, I can see you have a deep connection. However, your relationship path will be rocky, and might not end well...\"","Chen Xue's heart skipped a beat, remembering that Zhang's mother had also said their zodiac signs were incompatible.","\"Master, we're police officers, not here for relationship readings,\" Zhang showed his badge, \"We have some questions for you.\"","Zhang believed fortune-telling was just feudal superstition, and that no one could predict the future. He thought the master was deliberately trying to frighten them about their relationship to scam money from them.","\"Officers, I haven't broken any laws! My predictions are accurate, and I never engage in fraud. I earn my living through genuine skill!\"","Zhang took out the evidence bag containing the bagua mirror and asked, \"Master, do you know where this mirror was made?\"","\"At a mirror factory, of course.\"","\"...\"","Chen Xue asked, \"Is there anything special about this bagua mirror? How can you tell which master made it?\"","\"Ordinary bagua mirrors are all similar, but ones that have been blessed are different. Let me take a look.\"","The master took the mirror and examined it carefully before saying, \"This is a convex bagua mirror, used to ward off evil spirits.\"","Bagua mirrors come in two types: concave and convex. Concave mirrors attract wealth, while convex mirrors ward off evil. The mirror's border contains the heavenly stems and earthly branches, the Nine Star System, the Early Heaven Bagua, and the twenty-four solar terms. It must be used with a stone tablet talisman or hand seals.","Chen Xue and Zhang exchanged glances, realizing that Zhang Taotao had planned to use this mirror to ward off the victim's negative energy.","\"You've come to the right person. I made this bagua mirror,\" the master opened his seal book, \"The book contains the Nangong Jumo seal, and the person who requested this blessing must have been born in the sixth lunar month. The handwriting isn't very flowing – it must be from when I was in my seventies.\"","\"Master, do you remember who commissioned it?\"","\"It's been so many years, how could I remember?\" the master shrugged.","Zhang thought this lead was probably another dead end.","The master took a sip of his bubble tea and said, \"But I recorded every penny I earned. I can check my records.\"","\"Please do so right away.\"","The master pulled out a thick account book and started looking through it.","\"Master, it should be from nineteen years ago, please look further back.\"","The master leisurely flipped through the account book. Zhang glanced at it and noticed the master had earned quite a lot over the years.","\"Master, you even keep accounts?\"","\"Of course, every penny I earned was exchanged with my lifespan. I have to keep track of it.\"","\"And you still lived to be over ninety...\"","The master shot Zhang a disapproving look before continuing to flip through the book. His hand suddenly stopped, \"Found it, this should be it.\"","The entry read: Fifth day of the sixth lunar month, 2024; two bagua mirrors, one peach wood sword; 1,000 yuan; Believer Wang.","Zhang's face fell, \"Are you sure it was Believer Wang, not Believer Zhang?\"","\"I wrote down whatever surname they gave me, I don't know if it was true or false.\"","\"Aren't your predictions supposed to be accurate?\"","\"Yes, I can tell fortunes, but I'm not a mind reader.\"","Chen Xue said, \"Master, I notice you have an excellent memory. Do you remember what this Wang Jushi looked like?\"","Chen Xue had noticed that while other clients paid just a few hundred yuan, Wang Jushi had paid 1,000 yuan. With such a high price, the master must have remembered him.","\"I do remember. He had a black mole at the corner of his mouth, right here. From that position, I predicted he would face imprisonment. His facial features suggested he wasn't a good person, so I demanded one thousand yuan, and he paid without hesitation.\"","\"Is this him?\" Zhang showed him Zhang Taotao's photo.","\"Yes, that's him. I remember him clearly because his facial features indicated a very poisonous nature.\"","Zhang's face lit up: \"Master, would you be willing to testify to this?\""]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: Sleeping Murder: The Exchange of Evil","paragraphs":["Fang Rui and Mu Mian's investigation into the source of tung oil wasn't going well. Tung oil wasn't a controlled substance and had many sources - people could even collect tung seeds from the mountains and press them for oil themselves.","Seeing Fang Rui's disappointment, Mu Mian consoled him, \"Fang Rui, what Zhang Taotao did by switching babies at the hospital was illegal. If we can find evidence of him swapping the two children, we can still put him in prison.\"","\"That might not work. There was a similar case before where a poor mother switched her baby with a rich family's child at the hospital. Twenty years later, when confronted, the mother denied switching the babies and instead sued the hospital for negligence, eventually receiving compensation. Zhang Taotao will definitely blame the hospital unless—\"","Fang Rui paused mid-sentence. He pulled over to the side of the road and searched for the news article about the baby switch on his phone. He discovered that the hospital involved was Jiangzhou University Third Affiliated Hospital - the same hospital where Zhang Mingli was born.","\"Fang Rui, what is it?\"","\"Let's investigate that hospital.\"","Zhang Mingli was born in the obstetrics department of Jiangzhou University Third Affiliated Hospital. After understanding Fang Rui's purpose, the hospital staff agreed to help them locate the medical records from that time.","The hospital had digitized their medical records, so the staff quickly found Zhang Huanhuan's medical file.","The hospital staff said, \"On November 13, 1998, Zhang Huanhuan was admitted to Room 706. On November 14 at 3:09 PM, she entered the delivery room and gave birth to a daughter.\"","The staff printed out Zhang Huanhuan's admission certificate, prenatal examination reports, and discharge papers, handing them to Fang Rui.","Fang Rui asked, \"Who shared the room with her?\"","The staff checked the ward records and replied, \"It was a double room. The other mother was Wang Yuanfang. She was admitted on the morning of November 14, and entered the delivery room at 3:23 PM the same day, giving birth to a son.\"","\"Who were the doctor and nurse who delivered Zhang Huanhuan's baby?\"","\"The doctor was Li Qing, our best obstetrician, who passed away two years ago. The midwife was Wang Pandi, who has retired.\"","\"Do you have her home address?\"","\"One moment, I'll need to check.\"","The staff quickly printed out Wang Pandi's employment records.","\"Has your hospital ever had incidents of babies being switched?\"","\"We were wrongly accused in that case. It wasn't our hospital's fault. The mother deliberately switched the babies herself because she knew her son had a genetic disease, and she noticed that the mother in the next bed was wealthy, so she had ulterior motives. Over twenty years ago, hospital security wasn't as strict - babies were only identified by wristbands, so it was easy to switch identities by swapping the bands.\"","\"Who were the doctor and nurse involved in that delivery?\"","\"Doctor Li Qing and Nurse Wang Pandi...\" The staff member suddenly realized something.","\"How easy would it be to switch a boy and a girl?\"","\"That would be impossible! Right after birth, the mother is told the baby's gender. While same-sex babies might be switched, different sexes couldn't be - unless the nurse was involved.\"","Fang Rui gave Wang Pandi's name and ID number to Li, asking him to investigate any connection between Wang Pandi and Wang Yuanfang.","Li quickly reported back: \"Wang Pandi is Wang Yuanfang's paternal cousin.\"","Fang Rui had Wang Pandi brought to the police station immediately.","She was a woman in her sixties, short and slightly hunched, with a kindly appearance.","Wang Pandi asked confusedly, \"Officers, what crime have I committed? Why have you brought me here?\"","Fang Rui silently placed two DNA test reports in front of Wang Pandi.","\"What's this?\" Wang Pandi was farsighted and held the documents at arm's length. Upon seeing the results, her brow furrowed briefly, but she quickly feigned ignorance. \"Why are you showing me these reports? I can't understand them.\"","\"You were an obstetric nurse. Are you saying you can't understand a DNA test report?\"","\"I understand the report, but I don't know these people.\"","\"Isn't Zhang Taotao your brother-in-law? Don't you know him?\" Fang Rui questioned.","\"Oh, now I remember, my cousin's husband is also called Zhang Taotao. Ah, I'm getting old and forgetful, I can't remember many things anymore.\"","Fang Rui said, \"In 1998, Wang Yuanfang and Zhang Huanhuan shared a room, but their babies were switched. The babies were different sexes, making it unlikely to be an accident. You deliberately switched them, didn't you?\"","\"The babies were switched?\" Wang Pandi feigned surprise, saying, \"How could that happen? I never made mistakes in my work. It's impossible. Maybe the parents switched them themselves?\"","Fang Rui placed another stack of files before her, \"The hospital has given us the list of all the pregnancies you handled, and we found two other cases where babies were switched. The suspect in one of those cases was your distant in-law...\"","Wang Pandi turned pale and covered her face, crying, \"I had no choice, they forced me to do it. I got into that hospital with fake credentials, and they threatened to expose me if I didn't help them. I had finally made it to a city hospital, I couldn't let them ruin my career... My sister-in-law was also struggling, how could a family like hers raise a child with congenital heart disease? I had to help her...\"","\"So you destroyed other families instead?\" Zhang said angrily. \"You separated parents from their children - where was your professional ethics?\"","Wang Pandi kept crying, covering her face, \"I had no choice, I was forced into it.\"","\"How was Zhang Huanhuan's baby switched?\"","\"Li Bao didn't care about having a daughter, but my cousin's husband desperately wanted a son. Wasn't it better to switch them? Both children would have happy lives. I was helping them...\"","Fang Rui laughed bitterly at her logic, \"Ms. Wang, judging by your name, you were also a victim of son preference. Why did you become their accomplice?\"","\"I...\" Wang Pandi didn't know how to answer. While she hated her name and the preference for sons, when she had her own child and discovered it was a girl, her first instinct was to abort. She had been assimilated by these evil thoughts, just as she had accepted her name.","\"Please explain what happened back then.\"","\"My cousin and her husband Zhang Taotao came to me, asking me to help check the gender of my cousin's baby. I didn't want to at first, but Zhang Taotao threatened to expose my fake credentials if I didn't help. I had no choice but to arrange for someone to check the baby's gender.","When they learned it was a girl, they initially wanted to abort. But my cousin's health was poor, and if she aborted this baby, she might never be able to conceive again. That's when Zhang Taotao came up with the scheme to switch babies. He was very particular about it, so we couldn't find a suitable match for a while.","Soon after, Zhang Huanhuan was found to be three months pregnant. Their due dates were two weeks apart, which normally would have made switching impossible, but Zhang Taotao forced me to get labor-inducing drugs for his sister, causing her to deliver early. He deliberately convinced his sister to share a room with his wife.","On that day, knowing his sister was about to give birth, Zhang Taotao sent Li Bao away, then switched the babies after birth. I helped by falsifying the medical records. The children were related by blood anyway and looked similar, so no one suspected anything all these years.\"","Wang Pandi, now elderly and superstitious about karma, had been tormented by her conscience for years, so she confessed everything.","\"Officers, I was coerced. Zhang Taotao was the mastermind; all the ideas were his. I was just an accomplice.\"","\"Do you have evidence that he was the mastermind?\" Fang Rui asked."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: Sleeping Murder: Confrontation","paragraphs":["\"I have evidence. Zhang Taotao wrote me an IOU. At the time, he promised to pay me 2,000 yuan in service fees, but he couldn't afford it, so he said he'd owe it first, and I had him write an IOU. Afterward, he kept refusing to pay, and I didn't dare make a big deal out of it since I was an accomplice, but I've kept the IOU all this time at my home.\"","Fang Rui and his colleagues quickly retrieved the IOU from Wang Pandi's house.","\"Now we can finally send that scumbag Zhang Taotao to prison!\" Zhang exclaimed excitedly.","However, Fang Rui felt it wouldn't be that easy, as an IOU alone couldn't prove Zhang Taotao was the mastermind.","Zhang Taotao was brought to the interrogation room.","He crossed his arms over his chest, looking impatient. \"Officers, I've already told you, my sister willingly gave me all her property, and she even signed a property transfer agreement. I didn't defraud her. Besides, property disputes are civil cases, not under police jurisdiction, right? Tell Zhang Mingli to come find me herself!\"","\"We brought you in because you're suspected of committing two criminal offenses,\" Fang Rui said.","Zhang Taotao angrily replied, \"What crime did I commit? What criminal cases? Officer, don't falsely accuse an innocent person.\"","\"Do you know Wang Pandi?\"","Zhang Taotao's expression froze, but he quickly composed himself and said, \"Yes, she's my wife's cousin. My wife doesn't get along with her; they have a grudge.\"","Fang Rui placed the two paternity test reports in front of him.","\"Officer, what do you mean by this?\" Zhang Taotao asked with trembling lips, his mouth agape. \"Isn't Ming Yuan my son? How is this possible? We look so much alike. My God, Ming Yuan and Ming Li were switched at birth? What were the hospital nurses doing? How could they make such a mistake?\"","Zhang couldn't help but think to himself that Zhang Taotao was quite the actor - if they hadn't already gathered evidence of his crimes, they might have actually believed him.","\"Wang Pandi has already confessed that you switched the babies because you wanted a son.\"","Zhang Taotao angrily slapped the table. \"Slander! She's slandering me! How could I have had the opportunity to switch the babies? Ming Li and Ming Yuan are different genders - unless the nurses switched them, how could I have done it? Officer, Wang Pandi is falsely accusing me. She has a bad relationship with her cousin, and she's trying to frame me. She's so vicious.\"","\"She has an IOU written by you.\"","\"Yes, I borrowed 2,000 yuan from her. The reason is written on the IOU - it was to buy a house. I didn't pay her back because her father and my father-in-law had financial disputes, so that 2,000 yuan was used to offset that. My wife's family all knows about this. You can ask them. Wang Pandi must hold a grudge against me and deliberately switched my child.\"","\"Your child was switched before the IOU was written,\" Fang Rui reminded him.","\"Ah, I was too angry to think straight. Anyway, she's just trying to frame me. This woman is just jealous that my family is doing better than hers.\"","An IOU alone wasn't enough to prove Zhang Taotao had instructed Wang Pandi to switch the children.","Zhang Taotao was well aware of this fact. As long as he firmly denied any knowledge, he could shift the responsibility for the baby switch to the hospital, then sue them and get compensation.","After all, the police couldn't possibly find evidence that he had switched the children, since Wang Pandi had done everything.","Zhang was infuriated by his smug smile. \"You're also suspected of involvement in a murder case. We suspect your sister accidentally killed her husband, and you helped bury the body.\"","\"Officer, even if you want to falsely accuse me, at least be logical about it. First you say I switched my sister's baby, then you say I helped her bury a body. Am I schizophrenic? If I had switched my sister's baby, I could have just sent her to prison and taken my child back to raise. Do the police solve cases by making up stories? You don't have any evidence.\"","Zhang took out the bagua mirror: \"Do you recognize this mirror?\"","\"Of course, my sister asked me to help make two bagua mirrors and a peach wood sword, so I found a master to make them. Is there something wrong with this mirror?\" Zhang Taotao examined the mirror and tossed it lightly onto the table. He tilted his head back with a smug expression.","Zhang was stunned; he hadn't expected the evidence he had worked so hard to find would be so easily dismissed.","\"Officers, do you have any other evidence? If not, let me go home quickly - I need to make dinner for my son.\"","\"Your son? Didn't you just learn that Zhang Mingyuan isn't your son? Why are you still thinking about making him dinner?\" Fang Rui mocked.","\"The bond of raising a child is stronger than blood ties. I've raised Ming Yuan for so many years - even if he's not my biological son, he is now. Ming Li is my daughter now too. One of these days I'll have her acknowledge her ancestral roots, and I can fulfill my duties as a father.\"","Zhang Taotao stood up, looking down at Fang Rui and Zhang with triumphant eyes. His plan had been so perfect - it would have been a shame if there were no witnesses. The fact that the police had discovered his masterpiece but could do nothing about it gave him an immense sense of achievement.","This is what you call a perfect crime!","Next, he would reconnect with Zhang Mingli, and then he could openly demand that she hand over all her property to his precious son Ming Yuan.","After Zhang Taotao left, Zhang angrily said, \"Can we really do nothing about this scumbag? Look how smug he is. It's infuriating!\"","Fang Rui called a case analysis meeting.","Although Zhang and Chen Xue had broken up, they shared the same attitude toward Zhang Taotao.","\"Wang Pandi has confessed everything. Isn't that enough to prove Zhang Taotao was the mastermind?\" Chen Xue said angrily.","\"According to our investigation, Wang Pandi has significant grudges with Zhang Taotao and his wife, so her confession can only be used as supporting evidence. The IOU states the money was borrowed to buy a house, so it can't be used as evidence either.\"","\"The crime happened so long ago that many pieces of evidence are gone. We can't prove Zhang Taotao was involved in burying the body,\" Chen Xue sighed.","Everyone fell silent. After all the evil things Zhang Taotao had done, would he really get away with it?","\"I suspect there are important clues in the memories Zhang Mingli lost,\" Fang Rui looked at Lin Sen. \"Can you help Zhang Mingli recover those memories?\"","\"If it's psychogenic amnesia, I can try,\" Lin Sen paused. \"But even if Ming Li remembers everything, her testimony probably can't be used as direct evidence.\"","Chen Xue looked at Mu Mian.","Mu Mian had been idly reading a medical journal. Feeling Chen Xue's gaze, Mu Mian said, \"Don't worry, I'll work hard to find evidence, but let me finish this page first.\"","\"...\"","After the meeting, Mu Mian went back to examining the victim's body.","Chen Xue sighed nearby, \"We've examined this body inside and out several times, but haven't found any evidence. Mian Mian, we're not really going to let Zhang Taotao get away with this, are we?\"","\"Wherever there's a crime, there must be evidence!\" Mu Mian said softly.","The victim's chest cavity had been doused with tung oil, which had dried into a dark red film.","Mu Mian examined the oil film inch by inch.","\"What's this?\"","Mu Mian used tweezers to pick up something black.","Chen Xue stared at the tweezers for a moment, then said, \"It must have been an insect when it was alive.\""]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Sleeping Murder: Finding Memories","paragraphs":["After Zhang Mingli learned about everything Zhang Taotao had done, she agreed to undergo hypnosis therapy to recover her lost memories.","The hypnosis session was arranged at the house where the incident occurred.","\"Miss Zhang, your brain shows no signs of damage or disease. Your condition appears to be psychogenic amnesia. Our brains have a defense mechanism that protectively suppresses certain memories to shield us. These memories aren't lost; they're just buried in your subconscious. Are you certain you want to recover these memories?\" Lin Sen asked again for confirmation. \"It could be quite distressing.\"","\"That's alright, I can handle it.\"","\"Then let's begin.\"","Lin Sen had Zhang Mingli sit on the sofa and guided her through breathing exercises until she was completely relaxed.","\"You're feeling very relaxed now... You're walking through a long tunnel with light at the end. Follow that light. At the end of the tunnel is your childhood... What do you see?\"","\"I see my father cooking and my mother teaching me to write... After dinner, father is playing games with me while mother washes the dishes... I'm laughing happily. I feel so content. This is my home.\"","\"Is there anyone else in the house?\"","\"No.\" Zhang Mingli's expression suddenly changed. \"Wait, yes, someone's here. He's here again...\"","\"Who is he?\"","\"My uncle. He's here again asking my parents for money. Father refuses to lend it, and mother is scolding father.\"","\"What happens next?\"","\"My head hurts... I can't remember...\" Zhang Mingli clutched her head, clearly in pain.","\"Can you see the stairs?\"","\"Yes. It's very dark there. I'm scared. I don't dare go over.\"","\"The lights are on now. Can you see the light? Do you have the courage to go up?\"","\"I... I see my parents upstairs looking at me. They're asking me to come up.\"","\"Can you climb the stairs?\"","Zhang Mingli nodded, \"I'll try. I'm on the first step.\"","\"Good, keep going slowly.\"","\"I've gone up. I can see my parents, but they can't see me.\"","\"Why can't they see you?\"","\"I'm hiding behind the sofa. I'm playing hide-and-seek with father. Mother and uncle suddenly came back, and they're all arguing with father. Father can't win the argument, and he's crying, feeling wronged.\"","\"Why are they arguing?\"","\"Father doesn't want mother to lend money to uncle. He's saying I'm not his daughter. That's not true, I am father's daughter.\" Zhang Mingli shook her head desperately, tears streaming down her face. \"Father is wrong, how could I not be his daughter?\"","\"Take deep breaths... Breathe in deeply, then out... What do you see now?\"","\"Mother says father is slandering her. Uncle says father is making excuses because he wants to divorce mother. Father slapped mother... Mother is crying. Father tries to comfort mother, but uncle says father had an affair and spent all his money on his mistress, that father wants to divorce mother. Mother is furious and is packing her suitcase to leave...\"","\"What happened then?\"","\"Father fell down the stairs! Mother pushed him!\"","\"Where was your uncle?\"","\"Next to mother.\"","\"What did he do?\"","\"He was smiling...\" Zhang Mingli clutched her head. \"I remember now. Father tried to hold mother back, but she shook off his hand... Father lost his balance and fell down the stairs. There was so much blood... Uncle saw that father was dead, and he was smiling with joy...\"","Zhang Mingli suddenly opened her eyes, cold sweat on her forehead, breathing heavily like a fish out of water.","\"I remember now. Mother caused father to fall,\" Zhang Mingli covered her face and sobbed. \"Uncle told mother that she had killed father, and if she turned herself in, she'd go to prison and wouldn't be able to take care of me. Uncle said he could help her dispose of the body so the police would never find out...\"","At that time, Zhang Mingli discovered she wasn't her father's daughter and witnessed her mother causing her father's death. Under such intense trauma, she forgot everything before the age of six. When her mother saw her behind the sofa, Zhang Mingli had already fainted, and when she woke up, she remembered nothing.","However, Zhang Mingli's testimony alone wasn't enough to implicate Zhang Taotao. She had been too young when it happened, and too much time had passed. Her testimony wouldn't be considered reliable, especially given her history of amnesia. The accuracy of her memories would be questioned.","\"Zhang Mingli once said her mother never acknowledged her as her daughter. Could it be that her mother didn't actually have schizophrenia?\" Zhang analyzed. \"Could she have known the truth? Might she have left us clues before she died?\"","Fang Rui and the others visited the mental hospital where Zhang Mingli's mother, Zhang Huanhuan, had stayed.","\"Zhang Huanhuan's condition wasn't severe, but she showed strong aggressive tendencies, attacking her relatives indiscriminately,\" her attending physician explained. \"She was lucid most of the time, could take care of herself, and spoke logically and coherently.\"","\"Did she ever say anything unusual?\"","\"She often claimed her daughter wasn't her child. But this is a common symptom of schizophrenia called Capgras syndrome, where patients believe their relatives have been replaced by imposters. It's a type of delusion. Oh, and she always felt ghosts were following her, so she liked hiding under her bed. She said she could see her husband's ghost that way.\"","\"Could you show us Zhang Huanhuan's former room?\"","\"Of course.\"","Entering the ward, Fang Rui and Zhang saw various mentally ill patients, most with vacant stares or foolish grins.","Passing one room, Fang Rui saw Lu Tian sitting on a bed, quietly reading a colorful picture book.","\"Boss, look, that's Lu Tian,\" Zhang pointed at the room. \"She seems to be doing well now.\"","Among all the patients with various symptoms, Lu Tian appeared remarkably normal.","Sensing Fang Rui and Zhang's gaze, Lu Tian looked at them, smiled, then returned to her book.","Due to her violent tendencies, Zhang Huanhuan had been kept in a high-security ward in a private room. Since her discharge, no other patient had occupied the room.","The cleaning staff had already cleaned the room; there were no personal effects left, and even the bedding had been changed.","Fang Rui and Zhang carefully examined the entire room but found no clues.","Not giving up, Zhang crawled under the bed to check and discovered words carved into the bed board:","\"Zhang Taotao deserves to die.\"","The writing was faint, apparently scratched out gradually with fingernails. She had covered the entire underside of the bed with it.","\"It seems Zhang Huanhuan discovered Zhang Taotao's true nature. That's why she carved these words under the bed,\" Zhang sighed. \"Why couldn't she have left us more specific clues?\"","They removed the bed board for closer inspection.","Fang Rui discovered that besides \"Zhang Taotao deserves to die,\" there were other words carved: \"bedroom,\" \"bookshelf,\" \"hole.\" These words were tiny and crooked, barely visible without careful examination.","Fang Rui said, \"She probably left evidence hidden behind the bookshelf in their bedroom.\""]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: Sleeping Murder: The Flaw","paragraphs":["Fang Rui led the team to Zhang Mingli's house. Her home had bedrooms upstairs and downstairs, but only the side bedroom upstairs had a bookshelf, which was a wall-mounted one, not very large in size.","They dismantled the bookshelf and found a large hole in the wall, originally meant for an embedded electric meter box, which was later presumably moved, leaving a big hole. Inside the hole was a cassette tape and a shopping receipt.","The cassette tape had been stored for many years, and it was uncertain whether it had deteriorated.","The receipt listed the items purchased: two buckets of tung oil, one bucket of alcohol, and one bottle of disinfectant, dated August 7, 2004. However, it did not mention the buyer's name, only the store name: Sunshine Department Store.","The receipt was wrapped in plastic film.","\"Wang, take it for testing to see if there are any fingerprints on it.\"","\"Okay.\"","The cassette tape was unable to be played, but the black plastic tape was intact. Fang Rui sent the tape to the technical department to see if it could be repaired.","The fingerprint test results came out quickly. There were fingerprints from two people on the receipt, one of which matched Zhang Taotao's.","With the efforts of the technical department, the cassette tape was also successfully repaired.","Inside was a recording of an argument between Zhang Taotao and Zhang Huanhuan.","\"Brother, you lied to me! I read Li Bao's diary, he never cheated on me, he loved me deeply. The reason he neglected me during that time was because he and Mingli did a paternity test, and Mingli is not his daughter. I never cheated, so why isn't Mingli Li Bao's daughter? Brother, you switched my child, didn't you?\"","\"Huanhuan, I had no choice. The one-child policy was so strict, and our Zhang family only has me as the son. If I didn't have a son, our family's lineage would be cut off. Anyway, your child and my child both share our bloodline, so what's the big deal about switching them?\"","\"Brother, why did you slander Li Bao for cheating? You took away my son, why did you also destroy my family? I'm your own sister, why did you treat me like this?\"","\"That's because you two didn't love each other enough. Otherwise, how could I have easily sowed discord with just a few words? Li Bao was too petty, you should have divorced him long ago and found a better man to marry.\"","\"Brother, I've had enough of you. You ruined my sister's marriage, and now you won't even spare me. I'm going to turn myself in. I'd rather go to jail than give you another penny.\"","\"Huanhuan, you and I are in the same boat now. If you go to the police, we're both done for. You're a murderer, and I helped you bury the body. We'll both end up in prison.\"","\"Brother, please dig up Li Bao, I want to give him a proper burial. He didn't betray me, I can't let him be buried here like this.\"","\"No way! You'd better behave, or I'll kill your son.\"","The recording ended abruptly here.","These pieces of evidence were enough to prove that Zhang Taotao had switched the children and was involved in the burial.","Zhang Taotao was brought back to the interrogation room again.","Zhang, with his arms crossed, coldly looked at Zhang Taotao: \"Zhang Mingli has regained her memory and told us everything that happened at the time. There's no point in denying it anymore, just confess your crimes.\"","Zhang Taotao laughed at Zhang's words, \"Mingli has been amnesiac for so many years, and suddenly she remembers everything? And what can a six-year-old remember? Little comrade, your logic for solving cases isn't very good. How can we, ordinary people, trust you?\"","\"You—\"","Fang Rui placed the shopping receipt in front of him.","Zhang Taotao's smug smile froze. He had written this receipt to ask Zhang Huanhuan to reimburse the expenses. He didn't expect Zhang Huanhuan to keep it all these years and now the police had found it.","Zhang Taotao quickly calmed down. It didn't matter, there was no name on it. It had been so many years; the store certainly wouldn't remember him.","Fang Rui noticed Zhang Taotao's lips move, knowing he was about to make excuses, so he reminded him, \"There are your fingerprints on this receipt, you can't deny it.\"","\"I bought things for my sister, isn't that allowed? This receipt was for asking her to reimburse the expenses.\"","\"We also have a cassette tape.\"","Fang Rui played the recording in front of Zhang Taotao.","At first, Zhang Taotao remained composed, but the more he listened, the worse his expression became.","\"Officer, a recording can't be used as evidence, can it?\" Zhang Taotao still refused to admit it.","\"When a recording meets the conditions of authenticity, legality, and relevance, it can be used as valid evidence,\" Fang Rui rebutted, \"Wang Pandi's testimony can prove you were the mastermind behind the child switch, and this recording can corroborate that; the purchase receipt for the tung oil, the recording, and Zhang Mingli's statement can all prove you were involved in the case back then!\"","Zhang Taotao instinctively wanted to refute, but Zhang interrupted him, \"Even if you refuse to admit it, with these pieces of evidence, we can solve the case without your confession.\"","Faced with so much evidence, Zhang Taotao had no choice but to confess his crimes, \"Yes, I switched the children. But I'm the only son in our Zhang family, wanting a son to carry on the family line, is that wrong?\"","Zhang Taotao had consulted a lawyer. Switching children like this, the court wouldn't be too harsh. As long as he insisted that Zhang Huanhuan agreed to the switch, the court wouldn't sentence him too severely.","Fang Rui was amused by his righteous defense.","\"Yes, your family's lineage is noble, but you stole someone else's son, isn't that also someone else's lineage?\" Zhang mocked, \"If you can't have a son, it's probably because your ancestors think, with you as a descendant, they'd rather have the lineage cut off.\"","Zhang Taotao was so angry that his veins bulged, but he clenched his fists and remained calm.","\"Officers, I admit to switching the children. I need to educate you on some legal knowledge. Assisting in burying a body is punishable by up to three years in prison, or detention, or surveillance, with a maximum sentence not exceeding ten years, and the statute of limitations is fifteen years. This case has passed the statute of limitations. There's no need for you to investigate who buried the body, as the perpetrator won't be punished anyway.\"","Zhang Taotao smiled coldly.","He could go to prison for protecting the family lineage, which was a family honor. But he would not admit to any other crimes, as the police would never uncover the truth.","At that moment, the interrogation room door was knocked on.","Fang Rui paused the interrogation and went outside.","Outside was Mu Mian, full of excitement.","\"Fang Rui, my luck this time is really good. I've found evidence that can put Zhang Taotao, this scoundrel, behind bars.\"","Seeing Fang Rui go out but not returning for a long time, Zhang Taotao's hands kept rubbing, feeling increasingly anxious.","The door creaked open, and Fang Rui re-entered.","Zhang Taotao was startled by the sudden sound of the door opening. But he quickly regained his composure.","\"Zhang Taotao, do you know how Li Bao died?\"","\"How would I know that! I said, I don't know about this matter.\"","\"His cause of death was suffocation. Tung oil blocked his respiratory tract, preventing oxygen from entering his lungs, causing him to suffocate.\" Fang Rui said.","Zhang Taotao's face changed drastically.","\"Impossible! He was killed by falling! My sister pushed him down the stairs, and he hit the floor and died! My sister told me herself.\" Zhang Taotao denied vehemently, then regretted it, suspecting that Fang Rui had deliberately given him the wrong cause of death to provoke him.","Li Bao was clearly killed by falling, how could it be suffocation? Zhang Taotao recalled the feel of the body at the time, it was warm... Could it be that he had actually killed Li Bao himself?","\"We have to thank you for that. You did a thorough job of preserving the body, preventing it from completely decomposing, so we could find the real cause of death.\"","\"So what, do you have evidence?\"","\"Of course.\" Fang Rui stared at Zhang Taotao, \"We found your blood on the deceased.\""]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: Sleeping Murder: No Successor","paragraphs":["Zhang Taotao denied vehemently, \"Impossible! There couldn't be any blood. Even if there was, after so many years, the blood sample would have been contaminated. You're framing me!\"","\"That's why I said you preserved the corpse very well.\"","Zhang Taotao became agitated, \"What do you mean?\"","\"We found a mosquito encased in tung oil inside the victim's body.\" Fang Rui placed the photo in front of him, \"Inside the mosquito, we detected your blood.\"","\"Impossible! That's impossible!\"","\"When the crime occurred, that mosquito had sucked your blood, then fell into the tung oil, which you then poured into the victim's body,\" Fang Rui explained. \"Fortunately, under these conditions, the mosquito was preserved like a specimen, becoming evidence that identifies you as the murderer.\"","\"There can't be any evidence! You're bluffing! Using fake evidence to trick people - you police are breaking the law.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Mr. Zhang, I should remind you that the statute of limitations for premeditated murder is 20 years, and this case hasn't exceeded that limit. The current chain of evidence is sufficient to prove your guilt of premeditated murder. Even if you refuse to confess, we can solve this case without your confession.\"","Zhang Taotao had a mental storm in his head, realizing that denying his crime would be futile. So he quickly made a decision that would benefit himself.","\"I'll confess, but I have one condition.\"","Fang Rui looked at him and said, \"Let's hear it.\"","\"Please don't tell Ming Yuan about his true identity, alright? I don't want to hurt him.\"","\"Heh, you're just afraid of having no one to take care of you in your old age,\" Zhang scoffed mockingly.","Fang Rui said, \"Just tell us everything.\"","Thinking Fang Rui had agreed to his condition, Zhang Taotao began to confess his motive for murder.","\"Li Bao was inferior to me in every way. He was just a college graduate, an elementary school teacher, and a coward. But just because he got lucky with some demolition compensation, he suddenly looked down on me. When I asked to borrow money from him, he refused and accused me of leeching off my sister. I couldn't stand it, so I started taking revenge!","First, I spread rumors that he was having an affair, but surprisingly no one believed it. I had to write him letters with my left hand, telling him Ming Li wasn't his biological daughter. But this coward actually accepted the situation and didn't divorce. He still treated Ming Li like his precious daughter.","On the day of the incident, I went to borrow money from him again, but he refused. I instigated my sister to argue with him, and when she was about to run away, Li Bao tried to stop her. I pushed him, making my sister think she was responsible, then I pretended to help her bury the body.","After dealing with the corpse, my sister and I put on an act, making everyone believe Li Bao had eloped with someone.","I never meant to hurt my sister, but she was going to report me. I couldn't let such a traitor live. So I used some hallucinogenic mushrooms to make her have delusions, successfully getting her committed to a mental hospital.\"","Zhang Taotao was an extremely jealous person. He envied Li Bao and was jealous that his sister's family was better off than his, so he had to destroy them. Similarly, his older sister was wealthier than him, and he deliberately ruined her marriage, but she was smart enough to distance herself from him early on.","Despite this, he sent Zhang Mingli, his biological daughter, to his sister's house, knowing that his childless sister would likely leave her property to Zhang Mingli. Everything later happened as he had predicted.","\"I deliberately let Ming Li see this house, hoping to trigger a mental breakdown so she'd end up in a mental hospital like her mother. I never expected her to buy the house outright. Even more unexpected was that she would think she had killed someone,\" Zhang Taotao sighed, \"This is all fate! I accept it!\"","Zhang couldn't help but curse, \"Zhang Mingli is your biological daughter, how could you bear to let her spend her life in a mental hospital?\"","Zhang Taotao sneered coldly, \"She's just a daughter, what use is she anyway?\"","Zhang was speechless with anger.","Zhang Taotao looked at Fang Rui, \"Officer, you already promised me earlier that you wouldn't tell Ming Yuan the truth, you can't go back on your word.\"","\"Did I actually promise that?\" Fang Rui asked rhetorically.","\"You—\" Zhang Taotao suddenly realized he had been tricked by Fang Rui, who had only asked him to confess without actually agreeing to his condition.","\"I can guarantee that you won't have a son to care for you in your old age,\" Fang Rui said coldly.","The best way to punish such a demon was to take away what he valued most.","\"No, I can't be without a son, I can't let our Zhang family line end here. Officer, please, don't let Ming Yuan change his surname, I'm begging you,\" Zhang Taotao pleaded desperately.","Fang Rui ignored him and had the prison guards take him away.","Zhang Taotao's wife, Wang Yuanfang, was also arrested for child abduction and abandonment.","After the case was closed, Li Qiang came to the police station to claim Li Bao's remains. Zhang Mingli came with him, her eyes red with tears.","Looking at Li Bao's withered corpse, Zhang Mingli broke down in tears. She had forgotten her father for twenty whole years - such a wonderful father had been buried in the depths of her memory for twenty years, just as he had been buried in cement for twenty years, bearing various false accusations. How could such a good person suffer such a tragic fate?","Li Qiang, with tears in his eyes, bowed deeply to Fang Rui and his colleagues, \"Officers, thank you. If it weren't for you, my brother might never have been able to rest in peace. Thank you for uncovering the truth, bringing the real murderer to justice, and clearing my brother's name.\"","\"You're welcome, it's our duty,\" At this moment, Zhang felt immensely proud of his profession.","Fang Rui informed Li Qiang about how Zhang Mingyuan and Zhang Mingli's identities had been switched.","Zhang Mingli's face stiffened; she felt she no longer had the right to call Li Bao father. Such a wonderful father wasn't hers but Zhang Mingyuan's. He wasn't hers - her father was an evil man who had committed countless crimes.","\"Officers, after you left that day, I carefully went through my brother's belongings and found a diary. So I already knew that Ming Li wasn't my brother's biological child. But my brother believed that blood ties weren't that important - he raised Ming Li for six years, and she was his most beloved daughter. I respect my brother's wishes, and I will take good care of Ming Li.\"","Zhang Mingli burst into tears - even though she wasn't her father's biological daughter, she was still his most beloved child.","Fang Rui and Zhang had gone through all of Li Bao's belongings that day and hadn't found any diary. Li Qiang nodded at them. Fang Rui suddenly realized there was no diary at all - but Li Qiang understood his brother well, so he invented the diary story to comfort Zhang Mingli.","\"Ming Li, you will always be part of the Li family. Grandmother, your cousins, and I all welcome you back.\"","Zhang Mingli hugged Li Qiang tightly.","When Zhang Mingyuan learned of his true identity, he insisted on changing his surname to Li, wanting to claim his place in the Li family. Firstly, the Li family was wealthy, and secondly, his current parents' criminal records would affect his chances of becoming a civil servant.","Li Qiang had initially intended to help Zhang Mingyuan, but seeing his ulterior motives, he merely found him an ordinary job to dismiss him.","Zhang Mingyuan was furious about this and came to hate Zhang Taotao. He sold all the Zhang family property and left Jiangzhou City with all the money.","Li Qiang organized a grand and elaborate funeral for Li Bao, inviting all relatives from the main family. The rituals traditionally performed by sons were all carried out by Zhang Mingli.","Some elderly relatives complained, \"How can they let a girl carry the rice bamboo tube? That's only for sons to do, or nephews if there's no son. How can a daughter do it? This is so inauspicious! I'm leaving this funeral!\"","\"Uncle, please bear with it. Your son still needs Li Qiang's help with his job!\"","\"Even if Li Bao had no son, a daughter can't be a substitute. Li Qiang really doesn't understand tradition.\"","\"I heard Zhang Mingli isn't even Li Bao's biological daughter, and he has a son. Li Qiang deliberately prevents Li Bao's son from claiming his heritage just to seize Li Bao's farmland.\"","At the funeral banquet, Li Qiang announced to everyone, \"Ming Li was my brother's most beloved daughter. Now that my brother is gone, I will take care of her. My brother still has some farmland in our hometown, and all of it will be inherited by Ming Li.\"","Everyone below erupted into chaos, their faces visibly troubled. However, since Li Qiang was the most successful member of their family, they didn't dare to show their displeasure openly.","Zhang Mingli was sobbing uncontrollably; she would always be daddy's most beloved daughter, even though daddy was no longer there."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: One Hundred Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Scientist","paragraphs":["Mu Mian noticed that Chen Xue had been acting strangely these past few days, constantly arguing with thin air and displaying an ever-changing array of expressions.","Zhang had been sporting dark circles under his eyes lately. He'd been sleeping in the police station dormitory, where the bed was rock-hard and he had to endure his colleagues' snoring. To make matters worse, Chen Xue wasn't speaking to him, which made it even harder for him to sleep.","During lunch, Mu Mian and Fang Rui sat in the middle of the cafeteria, while Chen Xue sat in the upper left corner and Zhang in the lower right corner, forming a perfect diagonal line. Mu Mian and Fang Rui were positioned exactly in the middle of this line, maintaining an equal distance from both parties – a perfect balance.","Fang Rui thought this couldn't continue, or else he'd have to spend half of every day helping Mu Mian find the perfect seating position.","Mu Mian felt it was time for her to step in.","That evening after work, Fang Rui found Mu Mian frantically typing away at her computer.","\"Mu Mian, there's no case right now. What are you writing?\"","When Fang Rui tried to peek, Mu Mian quickly blocked the computer screen with her body. \"I haven't finished yet, don't look.\"","\"I already saw the bold title: '100 Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Pathologist.' Mu Mian, you're not writing this to convince me to marry you, are you?\"","\"Of course not. You already know the benefits of marrying a forensic pathologist,\" Mu Mian tilted her head back slightly, speaking with pride. \"I can help you solve cases, and you'll never have to worry about dying mysteriously.\"","\"...Then who are you writing this for?\"","\"Zhang's mother. I want to make her fall in love with the forensic pathologist profession, so Chen Xue won't have to quit her job to be with Officer Zhang.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian ruffled her hair in frustration, \"This is so hard to write. I've been thinking for ages and only came up with 49 reasons. My brain is about to short-circuit.\"","Fang Rui suggested, \"You could change the title to '49 Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Pathologist.'\"","Mu Mian stared at Fang Rui with wide eyes, wondering how she hadn't thought of such a brilliantly legitimate way to cut corners.","\"Fang Rui, you're a genius. Now that my report is done, we can leave work.\" After changing the title, Mu Mian suddenly thought of something and said to Fang Rui, \"Could you look it over? From a normal person's perspective, would this be convincing?\"","Fang Rui seriously read through Mu Mian's 49 benefits:","One: Forensic pathology is the most interesting profession in the world, allowing legal access to various corpses and the study of human anatomy. If you marry a forensic pathologist, you get free education about human anatomy.","Two: You'll never have to worry about your murder going unsolved. With a forensic pathologist in the family, you'll never have to worry about any family member dying under mysterious circumstances.","...","\"Fang Rui, would this convince you?\" Mu Mian asked, tilting her head.","\"Yes. Every single point is convincing.\"","Mu Mian was overjoyed and was about to print it when Fang Rui added, \"But if Zhang's mother reads this, she might think forensic pathology is the most terrifying profession in the world.\"","Mu Mian's head drooped in disappointment. \"Then what should we do? I don't want Chen Xue and Officer Zhang to be unhappy.\"","\"I'll help you revise it.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian immediately stood up and gave her seat to Fang Rui. She stood watching for a while until her legs got tired, then brought over Chen Xue's chair and sat next to Fang Rui.","\"Fang Rui, why did you delete the first point? I wrote it so well! And what's this you've written? It doesn't highlight the unique advantages of being a forensic pathologist at all... Oh, can we keep the second point? Please? Alright, I'll let you move it to the end.\"","Mu Mian kept leaning closer until she was practically resting her head on Fang Rui's shoulder while looking at the computer screen.","Feeling Mu Mian's head against him, Fang Rui's typing fingers froze.","\"Fang Rui, why did you stop? That last part was really good, very much my style. Keep writing!\"","\"Mm.\"","A little while later, Mu Mian clutched her stomach and complained, \"Fang Rui, I'm so hungry. But we've only written 22 points. We still need 27 more. When will we ever finish? Should we just stuff my original points in the middle to make up the numbers? People only really read the beginning and end of documents anyway, they just skim the middle.\"","Fang Rui went back to the title bar and changed \"49 Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Pathologist\" to \"22 Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Pathologist.\"","\"Fang Rui, I must say, you have a real talent for cutting corners.\"","\"...Let's go eat now.\"","\"I want the wonton skin from that place we went last time.\"","After making some final adjustments to the wording, Mu Mian printed the document and tucked it into a folder. Tomorrow was their day off, and she decided to visit Zhang's mother to educate her about the benefits of marrying a forensic pathologist.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian walked to the wonton shop in the next street over from the police station. The shop was small with only a few tables, but it was spotlessly clean and the food was excellent.","After ordering, Fang Rui and Mu Mian sat facing each other.","\"Fang Rui, can you come with me tomorrow? Chen Xue says Zhang's mother can be a bit fierce. I'm afraid that when I try to correct her cognitive errors, she might experience cognitive dissonance and hit me to save face.\"","Fang Rui couldn't help but laugh, \"You're such a scaredy-cat! Then why do you still want to go see Zhang's mother?\"","\"Chen Xue and Zhang are my friends, and I don't want them to be unhappy,\" Mu Mian said. \"I want them to make up so we can all eat together again. It's exhausting having to calculate midpoints every day.\"","\"Alright, I suppose I'll have to accompany you tomorrow.\"","\"Fang Rui, you're such a good person.\"","\"...Choose a different compliment.\" Being called a \"good person\" by Mu Mian wasn't exactly positive. Everyone who had received her \"good person card\" tended to end up committing crimes.","\"Fang Rui, you're so handsome.\" Mu Mian remembered that Zhang always seemed happy when Chen Xue complimented him like this.","\"...\"","When the wontons arrived, Mu Mian first broke them open and scooped out the meat filling, placing it in Fang Rui's bowl. Fang Rui then put the wonton skins in Mu Mian's bowl. Their movements were well-practiced, and soon there was a small bowl of meat filling and a large bowl of wonton skins on the table.","Fang Rui had also ordered a bowl of beef noodles. When the owner brought it over, he was amazed by their operation. He looked at Mu Mian and said, \"Young lady, if you just want wonton skins, you can tell me directly, and I'll make you a bowl with just the skins.\"","\"But then it would just be noodle skin. I like wonton skins, not noodle skins. They taste different,\" Mu Mian corrected the owner.","\"I could add some ground meat, and it would be the same.\"","Mu Mian shook her head, \"It's not the same. That would be noodle skin with ground meat.\"","The owner looked at Fang Rui, then at Mu Mian, and suddenly understood – he was being nosy. This was clearly just a couple's special way of sharing food.","The taste was indeed different – that bowl of wonton skins probably contained the flavor of love.","\"Fang Rui, can that owner change faces? He just showed several different emotions within one minute,\" Mu Mian gossiped quietly to Fang Rui.","\"Want some beef?\"","\"I don't eat it when it's diced... but you have so much beef in your bowl, you definitely can't finish it all. I suppose I'll have to help you eat some of it.\"","\"How does it taste?\"","\"Really good. I'll have another piece.\""]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Can I Steal a Household Register","paragraphs":["Mu Mian woke up early in the morning. She took special care with her hair and put on formal attire before going to knock on Fang Rui's door.","\"Fang Rui, open up! Don't tell me you're still in bed? We have important business today, get up quickly!\"","After Mu Mian knocked three times, Fang Rui opened the door with disheveled hair.","\"Good morning, Fang Rui,\" Mu Mian greeted him excitedly.","\"Good morning.\"","Mu Mian thought Fang Rui's messy hair might affect their persuasiveness, so she stood on her tiptoes and helped fix his hair.","\"I think you should dress more formally,\" Mu Mian said.","\"Mu Mian, it's six-thirty in the morning,\" Fang Rui reminded her helplessly, glancing at the clock inside. He noticed that Mu Mian had incredible drive - whenever she wanted to do something, she never seemed to feel tired.","\"There's an unreliable theory that says people's minds aren't very clear before 8 AM or after 10 PM, their logical thinking is weaker, and they're more susceptible to persuasion. I think this is the perfect time for Zhang's Mother to be convinced by us.\"","\"...Come in and sit down. Give me five minutes.\"","Mu Mian sat on the sofa munching on a sandwich, thinking the theory must be reliable since Fang Rui had been so easily convinced.","Fang Rui drove Mu Mian to Zhang's house. Having been there before, he knew Zhang's Mother had a habit of exercising early in the morning, so after parking at Zhang's residential complex, they went directly to the nearby square.","Fang Rui quickly spotted Zhang's Mother practicing Tai Chi.","Zhang's Mother used to practice martial arts and had even won championships, so her movements were fluid and carried the aura of a martial arts master.","\"Is that Zhang's Mother?\" Mu Mian asked with slightly trembling voice, eyes wide as she watched the practice.","\"Yes.\"","\"Her kung fu looks really impressive.\" Mu Mian was intimidated by Zhang's Mother's martial arts stance and hinted delicately to Fang Rui, \"They say Tai Chi is our country's most formidable martial art.\"","Mu Mian worried that Fang Rui wouldn't be able to handle Zhang's Mother in a fight. She hesitated - while Officer Zhang and Chen Xue's happiness was important, she didn't want to get beaten up.","Fang Rui had already read her thoughts from her expression and said helplessly, \"Mu Mian, Zhang's Mother is actually very nice. She won't hit anyone.\"","\"But Chen Xue said she's fierce.\"","After checking the photo on her phone and confirming their target, Mu Mian gave herself a mental pep talk, then gathered her courage and approached with her printed documents.","Standing a few meters away, Mu Mian introduced herself, \"Hello auntie, I'm Mu Mian, Zhang's colleague.\"","\"Good morning, auntie,\" Fang Rui also greeted Zhang's Mother.","Zhang's Mother glanced at Mu Mian and nodded, \"Hello, are you the genius forensic scientist from Zhang Qiang's department?\"","\"Yes. Chen Xue is also a very dedicated forensic scientist.\"","Zhang's Mother then greeted Fang Rui, \"Fang Rui, don't you live near the City Police Bureau? What brings you here?\"","\"We came specifically to see you.\"","\"To see me?\"","\"Auntie, why won't you let Chen Xue be a forensic scientist?\" Mu Mian asked softly.","\"I'm not forcing her to quit. I just asked her to choose between her job and my son.\" Zhang's Mother continued her graceful cloud hands movement while speaking.","Mu Mian took a few steps back, \"But Chen Xue really likes Officer Zhang, and she loves her job too. Could you please not break them up?\"","Zhang's Mother stopped her movements.","Mu Mian thought she was about to strike and quickly hid behind Fang Rui.","Zhang's Mother looked confused, \"Little Mu, what did Chen Xue tell you? Why do you seem so afraid of me?\"","\"You... please look at this. After reading it, you'll surely come to like the forensic science profession.\" Mu Mian carefully handed the documents to Zhang's Mother.","\"I don't care for such flowery writing. Just tell me directly what you want to say.\"","\"'22 Benefits of Marrying a Female Forensic Scientist.' First point: Forensic science is a civil service position with salary well above average, includes comprehensive benefits and pension, has high social status, and is a very respectable profession. The retirement pension is also substantial, so there's no worry about elderly care. And unless unlucky, the danger level is quite low...\"","Zhang's Mother stood with her mouth slightly open, staring at Mu Mian in amazement.","Mu Mian continued reciting from the paper: \"Second point: Officer Zhang is a criminal investigator, and Chen Xue is a forensic scientist. They make excellent work partners, their life rhythms align perfectly, they can understand each other's work, and they can often see each other at work (without affecting their normal duties). They're very compatible...\"","\"Did Zhang Qiang and Chen Xue send you as their spokesperson?\"","Mu Mian looked at her sincerely, \"I came on my own. They're my good friends, and I don't want them to be unhappy.\"","\"Well, you really are a good friend to them!\"","\"Thank you for the compliment. I didn't have many friends before, so I'm still learning how to be a good friend, but I'm trying my best.\"","\"...\"","Zhang's Mother glanced at the pages filled with text and suddenly felt a headache coming on. \"They've gone too far, knowing you don't understand social niceties yet having you do something like this.\"","\"I understand social niceties very well. And I haven't finished yet,\" Mu Mian protested dejectedly. \"The previous points were written by Fang Rui and aren't very convincing. They don't really highlight the unique advantages of being a forensic scientist. Would you like to hear the remaining points?\"","\"No, no, that's not necessary!\" Zhang's Mother quickly waved her hands and turned to Fang Rui, \"Fang Rui, tell Zhang Qiang that as an adult, he shouldn't run away from difficulties. How does running away from home solve anything? If he can't mediate such a small conflict, how will he handle marriage in the future?\"","Fang Rui was startled and asked, \"Auntie, you're not really against their marriage, are you?\"","\"What good would my opposition do? It's not like I'm the one getting married! But I think both Zhang Qiang and Chen Xue are too immature. Of course they don't have any conflicts now while they're in the honeymoon phase. But what about later? I created just a small obstacle for them, and they're already acting like it's life or death and talking about breaking up. This shows their relationship isn't solid enough yet.\"","Zhang's Mother saw things clearly: Chen Xue grew up in a single-parent family, was introverted, and quite sensitive; Zhang Qiang grew up pampered by his parents, was thick-skinned, and not very sensitive to others' emotions. Their personalities were too different - fine for dating, but not suitable for marriage.","\"It is solid,\" Mu Mian whispered in protest.","Zhang's Mother was amused by Mu Mian and asked, \"How do you know?\"","\"When they're together, I feel very out of place, like I can't join in. That's what love is. That's what movies say.\"","Zhang's Mother laughed even harder.","Mu Mian couldn't read her complex expression. She asked, \"Auntie, have I convinced you? Will you still oppose Officer Zhang and Chen Xue being together?\"","\"This isn't feudal times anymore, what good would my opposition do? If worst comes to worst, they could always steal the household registry and get married,\" Zhang's Mother complained unhappily. \"I just wanted to test them, and now I'm being made out to be the evil mother-in-law.\"","On the way back, Mu Mian asked, \"Fang Rui, is it illegal to steal a household registry?\"","\"Probably not.\"","\"How can stealing not be illegal? Fang Rui, what if I stole your household registry? Would that be illegal?\"","\"...Why would you want to steal my household registry?\"","Mu Mian looked at the sky, changing the subject, \"Fang Rui, the sky is so blue today.\"","\"Mu Mian, in our country, both people need to be present to get married. Even if you stole the household registry, you couldn't get married alone. Besides, stealing someone else's household registry is illegal.\"","\"I see. I don't know how to pick locks, and I'm afraid of heights so I couldn't climb through windows. I couldn't steal it anyway.\"","\"So you've thought about how to steal it?\"","\"Fang Rui, don't talk while driving.\"","Fang Rui couldn't understand why Mu Mian was so fixated on the idea of marrying him. He was afraid to ask why, worried that Mu Mian only wanted legal rights to his body after death."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Double Clues: Two Bodies","paragraphs":["The next day at work, as soon as Mu Mian arrived at the office, she noticed that the gloomy atmosphere that had been lingering in the office was gone. Chen Xue was humming while leisurely drinking coffee.","Mu Mian found it strange, as Chen Xue hadn't had coffee for a long time.","\"Mian Mian, I bought you milk tea. It's on your desk.\"","Mu Mian hadn't had milk tea for a long time either. She happily held the cup and asked curiously, \"Chen Xue, you seem very happy today.\"","Chen Xue took a sip of coffee and replied casually, \"Really? Aren't I the same as usual?\"","\"Before today, you've had a bitter face for a whole week,\" Mu Mian complained. \"When I told you jokes, you didn't even laugh. Even though there are two people in this office, I felt so lonely because you wouldn't talk to me.\"","\"Mian Mian, that's because your jokes were too dry.\"","\"Why are you laughing now? I wasn't even telling a joke.\"","\"Mian Mian, let me tell you something. I've gotten back together with Zhang,\" Chen Xue said mysteriously. \"Remember that fortune teller we met when we were investigating? We paid him to tell Zhang's mother that we were perfect for each other, practically made for each other. After the fortune teller convinced her, her attitude changed, and she stopped opposing our relationship. Aren't we clever?\"","\"That's wonderful that you've finally reconciled. You have no idea how hard it is to keep everyone happy.\" Mu Mian believed that the fortune teller's superstitious words couldn't have swayed Zhang's mother's opinion – it must have been what she had said to Zhang's mother yesterday morning that had worked, but she decided not to tell Chen Xue about this, keeping her achievement to herself.","\"Mian Mian, what are you secretly smiling about?\" Chen Xue caught Mu Mian's subtle expression.","\"Chen Xue, I discovered yesterday morning that I'm very good at persuading people,\" Mu Mian said proudly.","\"Are you sure? Do you have specific examples?\" Chen Xue saw Mu Mian about to speak and quickly interrupted, \"You can't use Fang Rui as an example, that doesn't count.\"","\"Fine.\" Mu Mian gave up trying to prove her point.","\"We have a case, let's hurry!\" Zhang walked in, telling them they had received an emergency call and needed to go to the scene.","\"Is there a body?\" Mu Mian asked.","\"Probably!\"","\"Probably?\"","\"The caller only reported seeing blood.\"","The crime scene was in the underground parking lot of the International Trade Mall in the city center.","The International Trade Mall was one of the largest shopping centers in Jiangzhou City, known for its high-end retail. Most of the stores were luxury brands, and the clientele was primarily wealthy.","Its underground parking lot was vast, with four entrances, each equipped with surveillance cameras, and all vehicles had to register at the entry and exit points. There were two internal entrances from the mall to the parking lot, both also equipped with cameras.","The incident involved a red Maserati sports car parked in a corner of the parking lot. The doors were shut tight, but blood had seeped through the door gaps, forming a small pool on the ground.","When the security guard came to inspect that morning, he saw the blood pool and immediately called the police, securing the scene.","\"Officers, I didn't go near the car. As soon as I saw the blood, I called the police right away,\" the security guard said.","Fang Rui first had the technical team check the footprints and fingerprints at the scene.","Mu Mian put on shoe covers and gloves, walked to the car door, and carefully opened it.","Inside sat a middle-aged man slumped over, wearing a business suit, appearing to be a businessman. His head was covered in blood. The blood had flowed down his forehead, and his face was obscured by dark red bloodstains, making his features difficult to distinguish.","The victim's legs were unnaturally curled up.","\"He must have had a habit of wearing a watch,\" Mu Mian held up the victim's hand, raising his wrist. \"There's a watch mark on his wrist, but the watch is missing.\"","Mu Mian continued: \"He should have been wearing a tie, but that's missing too.\"","The victim had no identification on him, and his phone was gone. Everything in the car had been cleaned out, even the car refrigerator had been removed.","\"Could this be a robbery-homicide?\" Zhang picked up a luxury shopping bag, but it was completely empty.","\"If it was a robbery, why kill the victim?\" Wang argued.","Mu Mian carefully examined the body's surface. The victim's corneas were slightly cloudy, and rigor mortis had set in throughout the body.","His clothes were disheveled, his shirt buttons weren't properly fastened, and there were bruises on his wrists and neck, likely from struggling and resisting. Apart from the head wound, there were no other external injuries on the victim's body.","Noticing his slightly long fingernails, Mu Mian examined them closely and found tissue fragments under the victim's skin. She took out tweezers and extracted the tissue samples.","Mu Mian also found white, viscous fluid in the car.","\"Based on the body temperature, the time of death should be between 10:00 and 10:30 last night.\"","Zhang looked at the car and muttered, \"Something's not right. He looks like an executive-level white-collar worker. Why would he drive a red car? Red is too flashy and doesn't suit someone his age.\"","Fang Rui agreed: \"This probably isn't the car he drove here. Look at the driver's seat position – he would have been sitting too high in it. This seat position is suitable for someone shorter. If he had been driving this car, this seat height would have been very uncomfortable for him.\"","Zhang analyzed, \"Did the killer move the victim here? Why would they do that?\"","\"No, the reason the victim is here is likely because he was engaging in certain activities with a lady,\" Chen Xue pointed to the collected white fluid. \"So this car probably belongs to that woman.\"","Fang Rui frowned. The car's owner had just had sexual relations with the victim; she wouldn't have just left her car behind. Even if there was an emergency requiring her to leave, wouldn't it have been faster to take her own car? Unless she was the killer, or more likely, she had also been killed.","\"Zhang, take some people and search the entire parking lot for any other bodies.\"","Everyone at the scene quickly understood and immediately began searching the entire parking lot.","They soon found a commercial vehicle in a nearby parking space. Looking through the windows, they could see a young woman sleeping in the back seat, but no matter how much they knocked on the windows, she showed no response.","Zhang found a fire extinguisher and forcefully broke the window. They opened the door through the broken window, and inside, the woman's clothes were disheveled, her face was pale, and there was a long strangulation mark on her fair neck.","Zhang touched her arm – it was cold and stiff.","He quickly waved to Mu Mian and Chen Xue, \"Mu Mian, come quickly, there's another victim here.\""]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Double Clues: The Identity of the Deceased","paragraphs":["The clothes of the female victim were in disarray; she was lying face down on the back seat of the car, her dress's zipper only halfway up.","Mu Mian examined the surface of the female victim's body. The ligature marks around the victim's neck formed a closed loop, with even depth and a dark color, and there were pressure marks at the back of her neck.","Chen Xue pointed at the marks on the victim's neck and said, \"These are typical ligature marks from strangulation. It's highly likely that the victim was strangled to death.\"","\"There are no abrasions on the wound, so the ligature that killed her must have been made of a soft material,\" Mu Mian thought, recalling that the male victim had lost his tie. She suspected that the tie might have been the murder weapon.","\"Could it be the tie?\" Zhang speculated.","\"It's possible.\"","\"If that's the case, the killer didn't bring any tools with him. It's likely a crime of passion,\" Wang analyzed.","Crimes of passion usually leave behind a lot of evidence.","The items inside the car had also been looted. The victim's phone was missing, and there were no items in the car that could identify the victim's identity.","Mu Mian noticed that the victim's right hand was clenched tightly, as if holding something. After prying it open, she found that the victim was holding a condom.","The team quickly deduced the sequence of events.","\"The scenario likely went like this: the two victims were having an affair in the red car when they realized they had no condoms. The female victim then got out and went to the black car to retrieve one. The killer took the opportunity to approach the red car and kill the male victim; then he used the victim's tie to strangle the female victim. The killer was probably following the victims,\" Fang Rui analyzed.","\"Could the killer be the female victim's husband or boyfriend? This looks like a scene of catching someone in the act. The motive could be a crime of passion,\" Zhang said, suggesting a high possibility of a love-related murder.","Fang Rui and his team reviewed the mall's surveillance footage and quickly spotted the two victims on the cameras leading to the underground parking lot.","Around 9:45 PM, the male victim first passed the parking lot entrance's camera, carrying two shopping bags. About a minute later, the female victim appeared with several luxury shopping bags. A man wearing a baseball cap, tall and dressed in black athletic wear with a black mask covering his face, followed closely behind her. The brim of his cap obscured his eyes, and the camera didn't capture his face.","At 10:41 PM, the camera captured the man in the baseball cap, now carrying a bulging black backpack, hurrying through the passage from the parking lot to the mall.","The police quickly identified this suspect. Although the camera didn't capture his face, the police had his physical characteristics: about 1.82 meters tall, male.","\"The car fridge isn't valuable, so the killer had no reason to take such a bulky, low-value item,\" Fang Rui analyzed. \"It's likely that something on it could incriminate the killer, so he had to take it with him. The suspect in the surveillance footage was carrying a lot of stuff, but he didn't seem strained, so it's unlikely to be the fridge. Let's search the trash cans in the parking lot to see if we can find it.\"","The mall's cleaning staff hadn't yet cleared the trash, but the police searched all the trash cans in the parking lot and found no fridge.","\"Maybe the killer's car was also parked in this lot, and he hid the fridge in his car and took it away,\" Wang speculated.","\"Then why didn't he put the other items in his car and take them all at once?\" Fang Rui countered.","\"Right.\"","The victims' identities were quickly confirmed. Both were regular customers of the mall, and a store clerk recognized them.","The male victim was Wang Yonghua, the procurement manager of Jianhua Engineering Company, aged 42, married with one son and one daughter; the female victim was Sun Xiaoning, the human resources director of the same company, aged 27, unmarried.","The police first contacted Wang Yonghua's wife to come and identify the body. She answered the phone.","Wang Yonghua's Wife coldly said, \"Wang Yonghua is dead? Finally, the heavens have taken him! Where did he die, on some woman's bed?\"","\"He was murdered!\"","\"Murdered? There should be plenty of suspects; he was such a scumbag that many people would want to kill him. Start by investigating the women around him. Where did he die?\"","\"In the underground parking lot of the mall.\"","\"Parking lot? No wonder we couldn't catch him cheating; he must have found a new place to cheat, in the mall's parking lot. Why are you contacting me? Do you want me to collect his body? He's not worth it!\"","Wang Yonghua's Wife was very indifferent and didn't seem inclined to come to identify the body. \"Contact his mistress, or mistresses, to collect his body. Do you need their contact information?\"","Zhang was stunned by Wang Yonghua's Wife's cold attitude. Could she have harbored resentment towards her husband and hired someone to kill him?","Zhang then called Wang Yonghua's mistress. The woman on the other end was gentle and started crying loudly upon hearing the news of Wang Yonghua's death. \"Woohoo, he promised to transfer a house to me, and now he's dead! Does his verbal promise still count? Can I still get the house?\"","\"Sorry, I'm a police officer, not a lawyer!\" Zhang interrupted her crying.","\"Then why are you calling me?\"","\"Do you have time to come and identify the body?\"","\"As a mistress, what right do I have to collect his body? You should contact his wife!\"","\"...\"","The phone went dead.","Zhang then called the other mistresses, but they all said they had only a financial relationship with Wang Yonghua and had no obligation to collect his body. The phone of the seventh mistress, however, was unreachable. Soon, Zhang found out why: Sun Xiaoning was the seventh mistress.","\"Zhang Qiang, no one is willing to come and identify Wang Yonghua's body?\" Li asked.","Zhang shrugged, \"Wang Yonghua's parents are already deceased, and his brother and sister have cut off contact with him. His women also refuse to come and identify the body. The deceased's character must have been pretty bad.\"","Sun Xiaoning was a local from Jiangzhou City. Her parents were workers living in the old part of the city, with average family conditions. Upon receiving the news, they quickly came to identify the body.","Fang Rui and Zhang took statements from them.","\"Has Sun Xiaoning had any recent conflicts with anyone?\" Fang Rui asked.","Sun's Father said, \"Not that I know of. My daughter works at a construction company as an office worker. She usually goes between the company and home. My daughter has a high EQ and gets along well with her colleagues and superiors. Many colleagues and leaders celebrated her birthday with her. She shouldn't have offended anyone.\"","Sun's Mother, tearfully, scrolled through Sun Xiaoning's photos on her phone, showing pictures taken at the company and during team-building activities. Sun Xiaoning was always smiling in the photos and was very beautiful.","However, Fang Rui and his team noticed that most of the people in the photos with Sun Xiaoning were men, with only a few photos including women, and those were group photos. Several photos showed Sun Xiaoning with Wang Yonghua."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: Double-Edged Clues: Evidence in the Nail","paragraphs":["\"Has your daughter exhibited any unusual behavior recently?\"","\"Not really. She goes to work and comes home as usual every day. However, Xiaoning recently got a boyfriend and often goes out on dates with him, coming back very late at night, sometimes not coming back at all,\" Sun's Mother said. \"We thought she's an adult now, so we didn't interfere much with her social life.\"","\"When did she start dating this boyfriend?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"About two months ago.\"","\"Boyfriend? Did she say her boyfriend is a boy?\" Zhang asked again to confirm.","Wang Yonghua is already in his forties, so it's unlikely he would be described as a boy. Could it be that the boyfriend Sun Xiaoning mentioned is someone else?","\"Yes, that's what she said,\" Sun's Mother replied, then added, \"Xiaoning has been acting a bit strange lately. She suddenly became very rich, bought a lot of luxury items, and even a car. When I asked her where the money came from, she said it was from stock trading and that we would soon live a good life. Could she have done something illegal? How could a girl suddenly earn so much money?\"","\"We are still investigating,\" Fang Rui replied.","Zhang asked, \"Do you know about your daughter's relationship with Wang Yonghua?\"","Sun Xiaoning's parents looked puzzled. \"Who is Wang Yonghua? We've never heard of him.\"","\"Didn't your daughter mention him?\"","\"No.\"","\"Have you seen your daughter's boyfriend?\"","Sun's Father said, \"No! My daughter never showed us a photo. She seems very fond of him, but when we asked about the boy's background, she wouldn't tell us.\"","Sun's Mother covered her face and burst into tears. \"It's all my fault. How could a girl suddenly have so much money? She must have gotten it through improper means. Waaah, when she was coming home late, why didn't I talk to her more and understand her situation better?\"","Sun's Father also started blaming himself and crying.","Zhang quickly handed them tissues.","In the autopsy room.","The female victim, apart from ligature marks on her neck and a few scratches on her back, had no other external injuries and no signs of resistance.","\"At the time of the incident, the victim probably got into the car to look for something, and the assailant strangled her from behind, killing her quickly,\" Chen Xue analyzed. \"The scratches on the victim's back were likely caused during sexual intercourse with the male victim, which explains why there were skin cells under the male victim's fingernails.\"","Mu Mian and her team had already extracted all the skin cells from the victim's fingernails. Mu Mian noticed that the victim's nails seemed to contain two types of skin cells: one fair and delicate, the other rougher.","The male victim's injuries were more complex. He had bruises from resistance, multiple contusions on his head, and a fractured skull on his forehead.","Mu Mian cut open the male victim's scalp and found that his frontal, left parietal, and left temporal bones were all depressed, with severe intracranial damage.","Mu Mian and Chen Xue carefully observed the morphology of the depressed fractures, finding five depressed areas, which were narrow and had a certain curvature.","Mu Mian had seen similar wound patterns in most of the domestic autopsy reports she had read, and the weapon used was a large wrench.","\"The weapon could be a large wrench,\" Mu Mian said.","\"Yes, if the wrench is held sideways and struck, it could cause such wounds,\" Chen Xue agreed.","Mu Mian then wiped the blood off the skull to further observe the wounds. She noticed some black substances in the depressed areas.","She used a cotton swab to wipe it and examined it closely.","\"This should be engine oil! When I was a kid and my bike's chain fell off, I would get engine oil all over my hands while fixing it,\" Chen Xue analyzed. \"How did the wrench get engine oil on it? Ah, this wrench was probably used for repairing cars! But ordinary people wouldn't keep a wrench in their car, and unless they were fixing the engine, it wouldn't get engine oil on it. Unless the assailant brought it themselves.\"","Chen Xue noticed Mu Mian silently watching her and began to doubt herself. \"Mian, did I get it wrong?\"","\"Chen Xue, I realize I lack some common sense. I don't know about those things. I don't have a bike, I've never had a chain fall off, and I don't have a car,\" Mu Mian sighed.","It seems she should watch more TV dramas. Fang Rui's mother recommended many family dramas to her the other day, saying they could broaden her perspective on solving cases. Mu Mian initially didn't want to watch them, but she felt she needed to learn some common sense.","\"Mian, that's why a team is necessary. We complement each other!\"","At the morning meeting the next day, Mu Mian reported the autopsy results.","\"The time of death for both victims was between 10:00 PM and 10:30 PM on June 23rd, the night before last.\"","\"The cause of death for the female victim, Sun Xiaoning, was strangulation. We detected semen on her body, which belongs to Wang Yonghua. She had three scratches on her back, caused by Wang Yonghua, as part of the skin cells we found under Wang Yonghua's fingernails belonged to Sun Xiaoning.\"","Mu Mian continued, \"The cause of death for the male victim was craniocerebral injury, resulting in subarachnoid hemorrhage. The weapon used to kill him was a wrench, and it should have had engine oil on it.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Whose skin cells are the other part under Wang Yonghua's fingernails from?\"","\"That's a good question,\" Mu Mian said excitedly. \"The skin cells under the victim's nails belong to two people, and the other person should be male.\"","\"Could it be that the victim scratched the assailant during the struggle?\" Zhang analyzed.","Mu Mian rebutted, \"If that were the case, why wouldn't the assailant clean up that evidence? Or just cut off the victim's fingers and take them away, so there would be no evidence left at all.\"","This assailant was too careless, making such a basic mistake.","Chen Xue said, \"Could it be that he acted on impulse and didn't think that far? Passion killings usually leave a lot of evidence.\"","Zhang had a bolder guess and said, \"Who benefits the most from Wang Yonghua's death? Definitely his wife! Could it be that his wife hired a hitman? I feel like his wife isn't at all sad or surprised about his death, as if she knew it would happen. If it was a professional killer, he wouldn't be afraid of leaving DNA evidence, as he would just flee after completing the job.\"","\"If his wife hired a killer, wouldn't she want to torture Sun Xiaoning severely? Usually, women hate the other woman the most, but the assailant only strangled Wang Xiaoning,\" Chen Xue analyzed. \"It seems the assailant hated Wang Yonghua more.\"","\"But Wang Yonghua's wife seems to have a good relationship with Wang Yonghua's other lovers; she even has their contact information. She doesn't seem to care about Wang Yonghua's other women.\""]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: Double Clues: The Art of Duplication","paragraphs":["The investigation quickly made a breakthrough. The police retrieved surveillance footage from key locations within the mall, and based on the height characteristics of the masked man, they quickly narrowed down the suspects to eight individuals.","One of the suspects caught Fang Rui's attention. This suspect had appeared in a group photo from Sun Xiaoning's company team-building event.","Fang Rui quickly discovered his identity. He was Chen Yuankun, a procurement officer in the procurement department of Jianhua Engineering Company, and the deceased Wang Yonghua was his direct supervisor.","Fang Rui brought Chen Yuankun to the interrogation room.","Chen Yuankun was dressed in a black suit, wearing black-rimmed glasses, a rigid young man, but he was quite handsome, somewhat resembling a popular celebrity.","He nervously clutched his trouser legs, \"Comrade police, why did you suddenly call me in? Is it because of that traffic violation incident from a while ago? But that should be handled by the traffic police, right?\"","Fang Rui scrutinized Chen Yuankun carefully. His hands and face showed no scratches. His skin was fair, but the man in the video had a wheat-colored complexion. His demeanor and posture also differed from the suspect in the video.","Fang Rui asked, \"Mr. Chen, do you know Sun Xiaoning?\"","Chen Yuankun squinted, trying to recall, and said, \"Not really. She's in the administrative department, and our work interactions are minimal. Occasionally, I need data from their department, but I usually deal with her subordinate, Lin.\"","\"How was the relationship between Wang Yonghua and Sun Xiaoning?\"","\"I'm not too sure about that.\"","\"Did Sun Xiaoning often attend your department's team-building activities?\"","\"I don't remember.\"","\"We've seen a photo of you with her.\"","\"Oh, I remember now. She did come a few times.\" Chen Yuankun lowered his voice, \"There were rumors in the office that our manager had an improper relationship with her. Manager Wang was quite promiscuous and often had unclear relationships with female colleagues in the company. I don't know if this gossip is true.\"","\"Where were you between 8 PM and 11 PM on the night of June 23rd?\"","\"On the 23rd? I got home around 7 PM, made dinner, and after eating, I had a video conference from around 9 PM to 10:30 PM. There was an issue with the goods provided by a supplier. The model and size of one type of steel were different from what I ordered, and the quantity of another type of building material was also wrong. This matter was very urgent, so I had to work overtime with the supplier's salesperson to handle it.\"","Zhang looked at him, not seeing any signs of lying, and there was no reason to fabricate such an easily debunked lie. However, the surveillance footage clearly showed him shopping in the mall during that time.","\"Are you sure you were at home during that time?\" Fang Rui questioned.","\"Yes, I remember very clearly. If you don't believe me, you can contact the supplier's salesperson; he can vouch for me.\" Chen Yuankun raised his voice, trying hard to defend himself.","\"But the mall's surveillance footage shows that you were shopping in the mall that night.\" Fang Rui stared at him, \"The surveillance camera captured it clearly; the man looks very much like you.\"","Chen Yuankun was shocked, \"Impossible! I was at home then, how could I be in the mall? And I haven't been to the mall in a long time.\"","Seeing him still denying it, Fang Rui had Zhang play the surveillance video for him.","Chen Yuankun's face grew paler as he watched, muttering, \"No, it's not possible. That's not me.\"","\"But his face is exactly like yours.\"","Chen Yuankun stared closely at the screen and then exclaimed happily, \"Comrade police, look, his hair is so rough and dyed; mine hasn't been dyed. This person isn't me; he just looks a bit like me.\"","Zhang compared the person in the surveillance video with Chen Yuankun. They looked almost identical, but the person in the video had slightly darker and yellower skin, yellow hair, and a rowdy demeanor, quite unlike Chen Yuankun.","Fang Rui asked, \"Mr. Chen, do you have a twin brother?\"","Chen Yuankun replied very confidently, \"No, my parents only had me. I've never heard of having any other brothers.\"","Fang Rui said, \"We found DNA samples at the scene that are suspected to belong to the murderer. Please cooperate with us for a DNA test.\"","\"Okay.\"","After letting Chen Yuankun leave, Fang Rui called the salesperson from the building material supplier.","\"Yes, I started a video conference with Manager Chen around 8 PM on the 23rd and it lasted until after 10 PM. We were checking the contracts because Manager Chen said there was a problem with the goods we provided and wanted to claim compensation.","I even went back to the factory to find the original documents and contracts. After checking, I found that it was their company's inspector who made a mistake. The inspector had checked the documents for the batch of goods arriving on the 24th, so the model and quantity were naturally mismatched. Manager Chen was very angry at the time, and after I explained, it didn't affect our subsequent cooperation with Jianhua.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Did you record the video conference?\"","\"No, this wasn't an official meeting, so we usually don't record it.\" the salesperson said.","\"Given that it involved contract disputes, it should have been an important meeting. Don't you record it to keep evidence?\" Fang Rui questioned.","\"This... we... I was in a hurry, so I didn't record it.\" the salesperson stammered.","\"Did you keep the video on throughout?\"","\"Of course. I have the start and end times of the video conference on my computer.\"","The salesperson was on a business trip out of town and had taken his computer with him. They would have to wait until he returned to investigate his computer.","After hanging up the phone, Zhang said, \"Could it be that the salesperson and Chen Yuankun colluded? Chen Yuankun certainly couldn't have been at home having a video conference with the salesperson while also going to the mall to kill someone, right? He doesn't have the ability to be in two places at once.\"","The DNA test results wouldn't be available for a while, so Fang Rui and Zhang went to Jianhua Engineering Company for further investigation.","The procurement department of the company wasn't large, with over ten employees, mostly young people, and the majority were female.","Wang Yonghua was an old-timer at the company and also the boss's brother-in-law, so despite his poor reputation and mediocre work ability, he still controlled the most lucrative procurement department.","Although Chen Yuankun was just a procurement officer and had only been with the company for two years, due to his prestigious university background and strong work ability, he quickly became Wang Yonghua's right-hand man. Their relationship was also very good, and Wang Yonghua often took Chen Yuankun to important dinners and meetings.","Fang Rui and Zhang used Wang Yonghua's office as a temporary interrogation room and questioned each employee in the department one by one.","These employees, though young, were well-versed in office politics and spoke very diplomatically.","\"What kind of person do you think Wang Yonghua is?\"","\"Our manager is diligent and responsible, kind-hearted, often mingling with employees, and is a very good leader.\"","\"What is the relationship between him and Sun Xiaoning?\"","\"Colleague relationship and cross-departmental superior-subordinate relationship.\"","\"How is the relationship between Chen Yuankun and Wang Yonghua?\"","The employee paused, his eyes rolling around, then said, \"Manager Wang values Yuankun a lot. Probably because he has the highest education and the strongest work ability.\" The tone was somewhat disdainful and sour.","After questioning several employees, they didn't find any useful clues.","Zhang looked around and found a female employee who seemed more outgoing and talkative, inviting her to Wang Yonghua's office.","The female employee was named Zhang Xiaoling. She came in and took the initiative to gossip, \"Comrades in blue, has our Manager Wang gotten into trouble? Did the neighboring department's Sun supervisor also get into trouble? Are you suspecting Yuankun is the murderer?\"","Fang Rui interrupted her, \"We ask, you answer, don't speculate, okay?\"","Zhang couldn't help but ask, \"How do you know all this?\"","\"I've already gathered the questions you asked. And I have a strong ability to integrate information.\"","\"......\"","\"Officer, Manager Wang and Supervisor Sun are having an extramarital affair. They hooked up about half a year ago. It was around that time when our manager asked me to order flowers for a Miss Sun. I immediately guessed it was for Sun Xiaoning. Later, I caught them kissing in the office, which confirmed my suspicions.\""]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Double Clues: Similar DNA","paragraphs":["Zhang asked, \"Miss Zhang, what's your position?\"","\"I was Manager Wang's former secretary.\"","\"Why former secretary?\"","Zhang Xiaoling shrugged, \"Because I leaked his gossip, which made him hold a grudge against me, so he found an excuse to transfer me. Now I'm Yuan Kun's purchasing assistant.\"","\"He didn't fire you?\"","\"The company owner is my grandfather.\"","\"...\" No wonder she dared to speak so freely - having backing really makes a difference!","Fang Rui asked, \"What's the relationship between Chen Yuankun and Sun Xiaoning?\"","\"Sun Xiaoning was obsessed with a male celebrity who looks very similar to Chen Yuankun, so she pursued Chen Yuankun for a while, but he wasn't interested in her.\" Zhang Xiaoling poured herself a cup of tea, then poured one for Fang Rui and the others. \"Sun Xiaoning doesn't have a good reputation in our company. Look, she's only 27 and already a supervisor with just a college diploma. She must have used improper means to get promoted.\"","Fang Rui interrupted her, \"Couldn't she have become a supervisor based on her abilities?\"","Zhang Xiaoling said disdainfully, \"Based on ability? Chen Yuankun has both education and capability, has worked here for two years, and is still just a mere purchasing clerk. In our company, ability is the least important thing. Our company is even more hierarchical than feudal society, with all promotion channels blocked by people with connections.\"","\"How's the relationship between Wang Yonghua and Chen Yuankun?\"","\"Well... I suspect there's something inappropriate between them!\" Zhang Xiaoling said mysteriously, \"I often see Chen Yuankun and Manager Wang alone in the office, and at night too!\"","Zhang exclaimed in surprise, \"You suspect they're... but Wang Yonghua's wife never mentioned him having male lovers!\"","\"Wang Yonghua wouldn't tell his wife everything. Think about it - Chen Yuankun has been at this company for two years, and Wang Yonghua never recognized his abilities, but suddenly started favoring him six months ago. What do you think is the reason?\"","Zhang countered, \"Following your logic, Chen Yuankun has been at this company for two years, why didn't Wang Yonghua notice his... good looks before?\"","\"Oh, that's a good point. Chen Yuankun is so handsome, if Manager Wang, that pervert, was interested in men, he would have made a move long ago. Maybe I was wrong? Were they really just discussing work in the office? That's strange though - how could someone like Manager Wang be so dedicated to work?\"","Fang Rui realized Chen Yuankun had lied in the interrogation room earlier - Sun Xiaoning had clearly pursued him, yet he claimed they weren't familiar. Why would he lie about such a small matter?","Zhang asked, \"How's Wang Yonghua's relationship with his wife?\"","\"Terrible, of course! But now they each do their own thing. His wife found herself a young boyfriend outside and doesn't pay much attention to him anymore. Recently his wife was pushing for divorce, apparently because she fell in love with that young man she's keeping and wants to marry him instead. Manager Wang naturally doesn't agree - if they divorce, he'll have to split half his assets with his wife, plus his wife made him a cuckold, and he can't swallow that.\"","Zhang continued asking, \"I heard Sun Xiaoning has a boyfriend, do you know about this?\"","\"Yes, she said she's dating a very handsome guy, but none of us have seen him. When we ask for photos, she won't show any. She's keeping it very secret. I suspect her boyfriend is actually Manager Wang. Haha, no wonder she can't show off a middle-aged greasy old man like him!\"","\"Thank you for your cooperation!\"","Zhang Xiaoling grabbed Zhang, \"Officer Zhang, let's exchange WeChat contacts. I feel like we really hit it off!\"","Zhang quickly waved his hands, \"No, no, my girlfriend is very strict.\"","\"Hmph, it's not like I'm interested in you,\" Zhang Xiaoling mumbled, her eyes fixed on Fang Rui.","\"...\"","After leaving Jianhua Engineering Company, Zhang increasingly felt that Chen Yuankun was the murderer.","\"Boss, do you think maybe Sun Xiaoning's boyfriend is Chen Yuankun, and he had Sun Xiaoning seduce Wang Yonghua, which led to Wang Yonghua favoring him?\"","Fang Rui thought this didn't make sense, \"If that's the case, how would Wang Yonghua's death benefit him? Would the new leader still favor him?\"","\"Oh, right. If that's the case, he wouldn't need to kill both victims. But no worries, once the DNA test results come back, we'll know if he's the killer or not.\"","When Fang Rui and his team returned to the station, the DNA test results were already out.","Mu Mian reported, \"Chen Yuankun's DNA doesn't completely match the DNA found at the crime scene.\"","Zhang seemed disappointed, \"So he's not the killer?\"","Mu Mian paused before continuing, \"But the similarity between the two DNA samples is 99%. Only identical twins could have such similarity. So the skin tissue left at the crime scene must be from Chen Yuankun's twin brother.\"","Zhang asked in surprise, \"Shouldn't twins' DNA be completely identical?\"","Mu Mian explained, \"Not necessarily. Identical twins form when a fertilized egg splits into two embryos during development, but DNA differences can occur during cell division, and environmental factors can also affect our genes. So identical twins' DNA isn't 100% similar.\"","\"No wonder the person in the mall looked exactly like Chen Yuankun but behaved differently,\" Zhang realized, but then frowned, \"But Chen Yuankun said he doesn't have a twin brother, and his household registration shows he's an only child.\"","They had investigated Chen Yuankun's household registration - he was a local resident, and his household registry showed he was an only child with both parents living, and he wasn't adopted."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Double Clues: The Third Party","paragraphs":["The technical department tried to match the surveillance footage with photos in the ID system but only found a match for Chen Yuankun.","\"Strange, why can't we find this person?\" Li wondered.","Fang Rui suggested, \"Could it be that he never had an ID card, or his ID photo hasn't been updated for a long time?\"","\"That's possible! If it's the former, that would be troublesome - an undocumented person would be hard to find. But these days, undocumented people should be quite rare, right?\"","Fang Rui decided to visit Chen Yuankun's home to look for clues.","Chen Yuankun's parents owned two storefronts and ran a small supermarket near the urban village.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to the supermarket run by Chen Yuankun's parents. His father was out purchasing stock, and only his mother was watching the store, arranging items on the shelves.","The back wall of the supermarket was covered with various certificates and awards - academic achievements, competition awards, and even an award for car model design. It was clear that Chen Yuankun was an exceptional student.","Zhang explained their purpose to Chen's mother.","Chen's mother's hand trembled, dropping the beverage bottle she was holding, which rolled slowly to Fang Rui's feet.","\"Officers, my Yuankun is a good child. He couldn't possibly commit a crime. He's been well-behaved since childhood, excellent in his studies, and is a graduate student at a prestigious university. How could he be involved in a murder case?\"","Fang Rui picked up the bottle and handed it back to her, \"Auntie, we just want to ask you about some details. How many children do you have?\"","\"I only have Yuankun now.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Are you sure you only gave birth to one child?\"","Chen's mother's expression became flustered, and she said quietly, \"Yes, just this one child.\"","\"Did you perhaps give birth to twins?\"","\"I... I...\"","\"Xiuying, what are you standing there for? Get back to arranging the shelves!\" Chen's father interrupted harshly as he entered carrying a box of goods.","With her husband's backing, Chen's mother became more assertive, denying, \"No, I never had twins!\"","Fang Rui reminded them, \"We have DNA samples from another child. With a DNA test, we can quickly determine if he's your child, so you'd better not lie.\"","Chen's mother instantly panicked, looking helplessly at her husband. But Chen's father was also stunned, saying in surprise, \"That child is still alive?\"","Realizing his slip, he tried to cover it up, \"We never had any news of him, we thought he had died.\"","Chen's mother, seeing this, covered her face and began crying, \"Yes, I had twins. But we gave the other child away. It was all because of that fortune teller's nonsense! When I gave birth to them, I almost died in labor, my father died in a car accident, and our small shop was destroyed by a flood. We consulted a fortune teller about what was happening.","The fortune teller said the twin brother was bringing us bad luck, and if we didn't send him away, our family would never know peace... so I gave him away...\"","Zhang angrily said, \"That was your child, and you gave him away just because of some fortune teller's words?\" Zhang thought these people were too superstitious!","\"Too many disasters happened then, we didn't dare take the risk, we couldn't afford to! What mother would willingly give up her child? I had no choice!\"","Chen's father remained silent.","Fang Rui asked, \"Did you have any news of him afterward?\"","\"No.\"","\"Don't you know who you gave him to?\" Zhang demanded.","\"I... I...\"","\"You didn't actually give him to anyone, you abandoned him, didn't you?\" Fang Rui asked. What he really wanted to ask was, did you try to kill him?","Chen's mother cried even louder, \"I was out of my mind then. On a cold winter day, I left the baby by the roadside, but when I went back to look for him later, he was gone. I've lived with regret all these years. Officers, do you know where he is?\"","Zhang replied helplessly, \"We're looking for him too.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Does Chen Yuankun know he has a twin brother?\"","\"No! We've kept it from him all this time.\"","Chen's mother grabbed Zhang, pleading, \"Officer, if you find him, could you take me to see him? I want to see him, to know if he's doing well.\"","Chen's father scolded her, \"Crying, always crying, you'll cry away all our good fortune! If the police are here, that harbinger of disaster must have done something wrong. You still want to see him? Aren't you afraid he'll bring death to you?\"","Zhang couldn't help but retort, \"No matter what, he's your flesh and blood. Not raising him is one thing, but calling him a harbinger of disaster - you don't deserve to be parents!\"","Zhang and Fang Rui were driven out of the supermarket. They then drove to Wang Yonghua and his wife's home.","Wang Yonghua's home was in an upscale community in the city center. After ringing the doorbell, a young woman opened the door. She was Wang Yonghua's wife, Li Meijia.","After learning why Fang Rui and Zhang were there, Li Meijia gave a contemptuous smirk and invited them in.","\"Officers, I knew you'd come looking for me. When a husband dies, the primary suspect is always the wife, even if that wife was thousands of miles away shopping in Paris at the time.\" Li Meijia said with a smile.","\"You were shopping in Paris on the evening of the 23rd?\" Zhang asked.","Li Meijia countered, \"Haven't you already checked my alibi?\"","\"...\" They had already ruled out Li Meijia as the direct perpetrator. She had flown abroad on the 21st and only returned early morning on the 24th.","Fang Rui noticed that the apartment seemed newly renovated, with new furniture and freshly painted walls. The living room featured a massive display case, filled not with books or artwork, but with various model cars.","\"As soon as I heard about his death, I had all the old furniture thrown out,\" Li Meijia explained. \"I wanted to erase every trace of him from this house.\"","\"Are you interested in cars?\" Fang Rui asked casually.","\"No, but the man I love is.\"","Li Meijia poured tea for Fang Rui and Zhang, then sat across from them. She took out a pack of cigarettes, offered them to Zhang and Fang Rui, and after they declined, lit one for herself.","\"Wang Yonghua liked cars?\" Zhang asked in surprise. \"I wouldn't have guessed he had that hobby.\"","Li Meijia rolled her eyes, \"Officer Zhang, are you trying to mock me?\"","\"...Aren't you going to try to hide your affair?\"","\"Would you not find out even if I tried to hide it?\" Li Meijia tapped her cigarette ash. \"I only need to keep up appearances in front of Wang Yonghua's family and his lawyer. Once I get his assets, I'm getting married right away. I want the whole world to know I made him a cuckold.\"","Zhang realized that Wang Yonghua's death had made Li Meijia a winner in life.","\"What's your boyfriend's name?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Ding Zhuangzhuang.\"","\"Do you have any photos of your boyfriend?\"","\"My boyfriend is very introverted and doesn't like having his picture taken. Besides, I couldn't keep photos of us together - if Wang Yonghua's family found them, they could use my affair to contest my inheritance.\"","\"Is this him?\" Fang Rui found the photo of the man from the surveillance video on his phone and showed it to Li Meijia.","Li Meijia's expression changed dramatically upon seeing it. She was clever enough to realize immediately that the man in the photo was a suspect. Just as she was about to deny knowing him, Fang Rui said, \"Ms. Li, your expression has already given you away.\"","\"Officers, my boyfriend is a very kind person, he's even a vegetarian, he couldn't possibly kill anyone! There must be some mistake!\" Li Meijia explained frantically. But clearly, she couldn't even convince herself with this explanation.","\"Where is he? Take us to him. We have DNA evidence, and once he cooperates with a DNA test, we can quickly determine if he's the killer or not.\""]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Double Clues: Evidence Conclusive","paragraphs":["Li Meijia stammered, \"I... I don't know where he is. I've never been to his home.\"","\"Ms. Li, if you continue to cover for him, we have reasonable grounds to suspect you as his accomplice in murder,\" Fang Rui said. \"So it's best if you cooperate with our investigation.\"","After some internal struggle, Li Meijia quickly made what she thought was the best choice.","She loved Ding Zhuangzhuang, but she loved her money more. She was about to inherit a large fortune, and with money, she could have any man she wanted. There was no need to protect a man who might not love her forever, all in the name of so-called love.","\"He's a mechanic at an auto repair shop,\" Li Meijia said. \"I met him when I was getting my car fixed there. I can take you to him!\"","Zhang whispered, \"Boss, Ding Zhuangzhuang is a mechanic, and there was engine oil on that wrench. Could he be the killer?\"","Li Meijia led Fang Rui and his team to an auto repair shop in the old district, but after searching the premises thoroughly, they couldn't find any trace of Ding Zhuangzhuang.","The shop owner said, \"Ding Zhuangzhuang hasn't shown up for work in several days. He doesn't respond to messages either. I don't know where he's gone. Yesterday was payday, and when I asked if he wanted his wages, he didn't reply to that either.\"","\"When did he stop coming to work?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"The 24th. He'd never skipped work before, but that day he didn't even call in sick. He just didn't show up, and his phone was unreachable.\"","\"Do you know where he lives?\"","\"Somewhere around here, I think. I don't know his exact address. That area behind us is full of migrant workers; he probably rents a place there. The rent is cheap in that area.\"","Fang Rui looked at Li Meijia.","Li Meijia quickly shook her head, \"I don't know where he lives either. He never let me drive him home or take me to his place. He said his place was too messy and not suitable for visitors.\"","Zhang couldn't help but ask, \"Ms. Li, what did you see in him?\"","\"His looks! He resembles a male celebrity I like. Plus, he has a great physique.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang went around showing Ding Zhuangzhuang's photo to nearby shop owners.","A breakfast shop owner recognized him, \"That young man lives in the leftmost room on the third floor of the building behind us. Has he done something wrong? Well, he's always been light-fingered. He stole my electric bike's battery half a month ago.\"","\"Why didn't you report it to the police?\"","\"I had no proof.\"","\"...How can you be sure it was him without evidence?\"","\"He looks like a troublemaker! With that bleached yellow hair, no proper job, never greeting anyone, and being from out of town. Last time when census workers came around, they knocked on his door for ages, but he wouldn't open it even though he was inside - I saw him smoking through the window. People like that must have a criminal record, why else wouldn't he have an ID card?\"","\"How do you know he doesn't have an ID?\"","\"The room he rents belongs to my aunt. When she asked for a copy of his ID card, he claimed he'd lost it. Then when she asked for his ID number, he just made up a string of numbers. We checked, and it was fake.\"","\"And you still rented to him?\"","\"It's 450 yuan a month. Better than leaving it empty. We have more rooms than tenants around here, so we can't be too picky.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui and Zhang found the building and went to the leftmost room on the third floor, but after knocking for a while, there was no response. Instead, his neighbor opened their door angrily.","\"What's with all the knocking? Don't you know you're disturbing everyone in broad daylight?\"","Fang Rui showed him Ding Zhuangzhuang's photo and asked, \"Does Ding Zhuangzhuang live here?\"","\"Oh, so that's his name! Yes, the person in the photo lives in that room.\" The neighbor lightly kicked the door, and it swung open. \"Go ahead and check if he's in there. Just stop knocking - you're interrupting my game.\"","With a bang, the neighbor shut his door.","Before Fang Rui and Zhang even entered the room, they could smell a pungent odor.","The curtains were drawn, and the room was pitch black. Fang Rui turned on the light to find the floor in complete disarray.","The floor was covered with various items - cardboard boxes, clothes, socks, and several liquor bottles, including one that appeared to be Maotai.","Under the bed, there seemed to be more items stuffed away, and from what was visible, there was a luxury handbag.","In the middle of all the garbage and clutter lay a man - it was Ding Zhuangzhuang, whom they had been searching for.","\"Boss, is Ding Zhuangzhuang dead?\"","Fang Rui approached him and checked for breathing, finding that he was still alive.","\"He's just drunk.\"","\"Boss, look at his hands!\" Zhang pointed at Ding Zhuangzhuang's hand, exclaiming, \"There are scratch marks on the back of his hand!\"","They quickly discovered a stash of luxury goods under the bed, including an expensive watch. Fang Rui also found two latest-model iPhones on the table.","Fang Rui called Wang and the others to come process the crime scene.","Li managed to crack the phones' lock codes, and the contact lists showed they belonged to Wang Yonghua and Sun Xiaoning.","\"Is he too arrogant or just completely clueless about avoiding detection?\" Li couldn't help but comment. \"Even common phone thieves know to flash their stolen phones, but he just removed the SIM cards without doing anything else to the phones. It's like he's leaving evidence for us to catch him.\"","Everyone shared the same confusion.","If Ding Zhuangzhuang was really the killer, he seemed incredibly stupid, not even bothering to hide the stolen goods, just leaving them scattered around.","After quite a while, when night had fallen, Ding Zhuangzhuang finally sobered up. His head felt like it was exploding with pain, and he struggled to open his eyes.","During the time they had waited for him to sober up, Fang Rui's team had sent Ding Zhuangzhuang's hair for DNA testing, and the results showed that the DNA from the crime scene matched his.","The luxury items in his room were also confirmed to be those purchased by Wang Yonghua and Sun Xiaoning that night.","Zhang gently patted his face, saying, \"Hey, wake up. We need you to explain some things.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang looked at Zhang with a vacant expression.","\"Is he still drunk?\" Zhang waved his hand in front of his eyes, but Ding Zhuangzhuang didn't respond.","Fang Rui picked up the Maotai bottle from the floor and discovered that it was labeled \"Maotai\" with slightly different characters. The packaging was identical to genuine Maotai, and the difference was nearly impossible to spot without careful inspection.","There was still a bit of liquor in the bottle. Fang Rui smelled it and detected the scent of poor-quality alcohol.","\"He might have drunk fake liquor - quick, call 120 and get him to the hospital!\""]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: Double Clues: Self-Contradiction","paragraphs":["After rushing Ding Zhuangzhuang to the hospital for emergency treatment, Fang Rui and his team searched Ding's home again. They found many stolen items but couldn't locate the wrench used to kill Wang Yonghua or the missing car refrigerator.","Zhang found a mobile phone under Ding Zhuangzhuang's pillow.","The phone didn't have many WeChat contacts, and the chat history only showed conversations with Wang Yonghua's wife Li Meijia and the other victim, Sun Xiaoning.","\"So Ding Zhuangzhuang was Sun Xiaoning's secret boyfriend,\" Zhang remarked, surprised yet finding it logical. \"Ding Zhuangzhuang looks almost identical to Chen Yuankun. Sun Xiaoning probably saw him as Chen Yuankun's replacement. Well, this suggests the murder motive was a crime of passion!\"","After reviewing the chat history between Ding Zhuangzhuang and Sun Xiaoning, their relationship became clear.","Six months ago, Ding Zhuangzhuang had added Sun Xiaoning on WeChat, claiming it was love at first sight. After establishing a relationship with her, he encouraged her to seduce Wang Yonghua to extract large sums of money from him.","Their plan was to accumulate 5 million yuan and then elope together. Since Sun Xiaoning's parents would never approve of her marrying a mechanic like Ding Zhuangzhuang, elopement was their only option.","Ding Zhuangzhuang's relationship with Li Meijia was more innocent. They only occasionally dined together, and when she offered to buy him a house, he refused. Even when she proposed marriage, he declined, saying he wasn't worthy of her.","A particular conversation between Ding Zhuangzhuang and Li Meijia caught their attention:","[Ding Zhuangzhuang: Sister Meijia, if necessary, just settle for less money and divorce him quickly. Life is about being happy!","Li Meijia: Absolutely not! I want to drain him of every penny. Why should I leave him money to spend on his mistresses? I won't swallow this anger.","Ding Zhuangzhuang: But if you insist on getting so much money, you'll have to keep dealing with him. You're not short of money, there's no need for this.","Li Meijia: So what if it drags on? I'm 10 years younger than him - I can outlast him!","Ding Zhuangzhuang: But you're not happy. Is money really that important?","Li Meijia: This isn't just about money - it's about my pride.","Ding Zhuangzhuang: Sister Meijia, I will protect you.]","Ding Zhuangzhuang's last message to Li Meijia was \"I will protect you.\"","\"Ding Zhuangzhuang seems to have a split personality - he exploited Sun Xiaoning and kept asking her for money, but acted so pure with Li Meijia. Could he have killed for Li Meijia?\" someone speculated about the murder motive.","\"It's possible! Li Meijia benefits the most from Wang Yonghua's death. Could Ding Zhuangzhuang be Li Meijia's weapon? I was wondering why she'd be interested in a mechanic - she probably used her beauty to seduce him into killing for her!\" Zhang analyzed.","Now with a motive established, the chain of evidence seemed complete.","However, everyone felt the case had been solved too easily - something didn't feel quite right.","Fang Rui recalled the repair shop owner's words and said, \"The shop owner mentioned he had contacted Ding Zhuangzhuang multiple times, so why isn't the owner in this phone's contacts?\"","\"Could the chat history have been deleted? No, if he was deleting anything, he would have deleted the chats with Li Meijia and Sun Xiaoning. Why delete the owner's messages? Could he have another phone?\"","They searched the entire house again, even checking the toilet tank, but found no other phone.","While searching through the trash, Fang Rui found a takeout box that had contained pork leg rice, according to the receipt. However, there were no food delivery apps on the phone, and the phone number on the receipt didn't match the one in this phone.","This all suggested Ding Zhuangzhuang must have another phone.","Fang Rui asked the technical department to check if any information had been deleted from this phone.","Fang Rui then took Mu Mian and the others to the repair shop to search for the murder weapon.","\"Little Ding's WeChat name was 'Scavenger,' not this. The profile picture is different too. This isn't his WeChat!\" the owner stated confidently.","Fang Rui noted down the WeChat account. He asked, \"Has the shop ever lost any repair tools? Like wrenches?\"","\"Last month we lost some tires. I found out an employee was stealing shop items to sell them! I fired him. I won't keep employees who steal!\"","\"When did Ding Zhuangzhuang start working here?\"","\"About six months ago. He had no ID card and couldn't find work. I felt sorry for him and took him in.\"","\"Why didn't he have an ID card?\"","\"He said he was an orphan, abandoned by his parents and taken in by a mentally ill woman. She never formally adopted him, and the villagers didn't care about the situation, so he couldn't get registered in the household system. When he was twelve, the woman died, and the villagers drove him out. He became homeless, surviving by collecting garbage. When he turned eighteen, he still couldn't find work without an ID card, so he kept wandering until he ended up here.","He always wanted to get an ID card, but without household registration or any way to prove who his parents were, he remained undocumented. You know, he's a hardworking young man, clever too - just dealt a cruel hand by fate. Officer, has he done something wrong? He doesn't seem like someone who would commit crimes. He's just a bit antisocial, but honest and kind-hearted.\"","Everyone present felt moved by the owner's account. They sympathized with the image of a child wandering homeless and rootless, then growing up only to be forced into working illegally due to lack of documentation.","Mu Mian's eyes welled up with tears. If her parents hadn't adopted her, she probably would have starved to death - she would never have collected garbage, preferring to starve rather than deal with the bacteria in trash bins.","Fang Rui asked, \"Can we examine their tool boxes?\"","\"Of course.\"","The employees put their toolboxes on the ground, and the owner brought out Ding Zhuangzhuang's as well. Fang Rui carefully inspected each toolbox. They all contained wrenches, and from the wear patterns and deterioration, these wrenches had clearly been used for a long time, covered in machine oil and rust, quite dirty.","Mu Mian sprayed luminol reagent in each toolbox, but none showed fluorescent reactions.","\"No blood traces,\" Mu Mian reported.","\"Did Ding Zhuangzhuang like to drink?\" Fang Rui asked the employees.","\"I don't think so. He never joined us when we went drinking. He's very introverted, doesn't talk much, likes to read. And he's extremely skilled at car repair.\"","Someone couldn't help but comment: \"Introverted? Would an introverted person dye their hair yellow? Would an introverted person two-time women?\"","\"His hair wasn't always like that. But since he's from out of town and people kept bullying him, he dyed it yellow so people would leave him alone. He's actually quite kind-hearted.\"","\"Is he vegetarian?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Vegetarian? He does like vegetables, but he eats meat too. He's not picky about food.\"","Fang Rui found this strange, as Li Meijia had said Ding Zhuangzhuang was vegetarian.","\"Has he shown any unusual behavior recently?\"","\"Nothing unusual. He goes straight home after work every day. We don't really know him that well. He's peculiar, and we can't really connect with him.\""]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Double Clues: No Confession","paragraphs":["Back at the bureau, Fang Rui called a case analysis meeting.","Chen Xue raised her doubts first: \"If the murder weapon wasn't randomly taken from the toolbox, why was there oil on the wrench? Was it an old discarded one? But from the crime scene, it seems like a crime of passion, so why would the killer specifically carry an unused tool? And if it was premeditated murder, why not buy a new wrench?\"","Everyone nodded in agreement. They also felt many pieces of evidence were contradictory.","\"He clearly had two phones, and the one with contacts to Li Meijia and Sun Xiaoning wasn't missing, but the other phone disappeared. If he was really the killer, shouldn't both phones have been disposed of?\"","\"Everyone at the repair shop said Ding Zhuangzhuang didn't have a drinking habit, but after the incident, he suddenly started drinking heavily, and it was fake alcohol too. Could this be a coincidence?\"","Everyone raised a series of questions, and an answer seemed to be emerging.","Mu Mian voiced that answer: \"Someone is framing him! This wasn't a crime of passion; it was a carefully planned murder.\"","\"If that's the case, the only person who could be framing him is Chen Yuankun. But why would Chen Yuankun do this? Ding Zhuangzhuang is already in such a miserable state, why would he frame him for murder?\"","\"Well, these are just our speculations, and we can't overturn the current chain of evidence,\" Chen Xue sighed, noting that the DNA evidence was conclusive.","\"Little Li, you and Old Zhang investigate the surveillance cameras around Chen Yuankun's house, see if he really stayed home all evening on the 23rd like he claims.\"","After being rushed to the hospital, Ding Zhuangzhuang was saved. The nurse gave him IV drips all night, and the next afternoon, the doctor called to say he had regained consciousness.","\"Fang Rui, can I go to the hospital with you?\"","\"Who do you want to visit?\"","\"I need to collect evidence from a living subject.\"","Chen Xue, who was nearby, said: \"Living evidence? Haven't we already tested his DNA? What other evidence do we need?\"","\"Chen Xue, you continue writing your report. Fang Rui and I can handle this.\"","\"...\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang opened his eyes at noon, but his mind wasn't clear. His left hand kept clapping at the air, his pupils were cloudy, and he appeared agitated.","Mu Mian's eyes focused on the scars on his left hand, but Ding Zhuangzhuang's constant movement made it difficult for her to observe clearly.","\"Why is he clapping at the air?\" Fang Rui thought the fake alcohol might have made him mentally unstable.","\"Fang Rui, you probably won't be able to get a statement from him. His current condition appears to be alcohol-induced dementia, his brain tissue is likely damaged, and if he's unlucky, he'll be like this for life,\" Mu Mian sighed. \"Fang Rui, hold his hand still, I can't see his scars clearly.\"","There were four finger scratch marks on the back of Ding Zhuangzhuang's hand, and the scars had scabbed over.","\"We found skin cells under three of Wang Yonghua's fingernails, but why are there four scratch marks on his hand?\" Fang Rui recalled the autopsy report and quickly understood what Mu Mian was confirming.","\"His hand wasn't scratched by Wang Yonghua!\" Mu Mian said. \"Wang Yonghua's fingernails were long and sharp, but these four scratch marks are wide. When we found the skin cells, I thought it was strange that there was no blood on the nails. Now it seems those skin cells were likely planted deliberately.\"","This evidence suggested that Ding Zhuangzhuang was very likely being framed.","Suddenly, Ding Zhuangzhuang looked behind Fang Rui and Mu Mian, shouting loudly: \"You're here?\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian both turned around but saw nothing.","Ding Zhuangzhuang started giggling at the air.","\"Do you remember your name?\" Fang Rui asked tentatively.","\"Camphor boy.\"","\"Your name is Camphor boy?\"","\"Hehe, you are, you are.\"","\"Do you remember what you were doing on the evening of the 23rd?\"","\"Someone was crying, so noisy,\" Ding Zhuangzhuang mumbled. \"He's back again. Hehe.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang had become mentally disturbed, and Fang Rui couldn't communicate with him at all.","Ding Zhuangzhuang's attending physician said: \"We've done an MRI of his head and detected organic brain changes that have led to central nervous system dysfunction. His memory and cognitive abilities will decline, and he might even display aggressive behavior.\"","\"Is there any way to return to normal through treatment?\"","\"This kind of damage is irreversible, there's no way to recover.\" The doctor looked at Fang Rui with an awkward expression. \"Officer Fang... have you found his family? His medical fees...\"","\"Didn't his parents come to the hospital yesterday?\" Fang Rui had already notified Chen's father and mother to come to the hospital.","\"No! No one has come to see him, let alone pay his fees.\"","\"I'll pay for him!\" Mu Mian said.","\"You'll pay? This isn't a small amount. He doesn't have medical insurance, so the expenses can't be reimbursed. This round of treatment alone will probably cost tens of thousands. You should still try to find his family.\"","\"He has no family,\" Mu Mian said softly. \"He's very pitiful, wandering alone since childhood. I'm very wealthy, so I'll pay for him.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian pulled Fang Rui to the payment window to pay Ding Zhuangzhuang's fees, but when it came time to pay, she discovered she only had a few hundred in her account. She looked at Fang Rui embarrassedly.","Fang Rui paid Ding Zhuangzhuang's fees, adding extra to cover his subsequent treatment. Whether Ding Zhuangzhuang was a criminal or not, Fang Rui was willing to pay this money because he was truly pitiful. Moreover, his situation was a result of both family and social failure.","That is, if his background story was true.","Fang Rui suddenly realized they hadn't verified Ding Zhuangzhuang's history. But there was no way to verify it - Ding Zhuangzhuang had no ID card and they didn't know where his hometown was.","\"Fang Rui, once I borrow money from my sister, I'll pay you back,\" Mu Mian said quietly.","\"No need, let's just consider it a joint charitable act.\"","\"But I didn't pay anything.\"","\"You contributed the intention, I contributed the money.\"","Mu Mian sighed: \"I supposedly receive a good salary every month, why has all the money disappeared?\"","Mu Mian hadn't paid much attention to her bank account balance, so it wasn't until now that she discovered she was living paycheck to paycheck.","When Chen Xue had previously mentioned living paycheck to paycheck, Mu Mian had mocked her, asking how such a good salary could be spent within a month. She hadn't expected to be in the same situation herself.","\"You often buy dissection tools and the latest medical equipment out of your own pocket, you like buying books and magazine subscriptions, and you're fond of Lego and puzzles. Oh, and you're passionate about giving gifts to others.\"","\"They gave me gifts first.\"","\"You've never given me a gift,\" Fang Rui said sourly.","Mu Mian felt wronged: \"Fang Rui, I want to give you the best gift in the world, but since the best gift doesn't exist, I'm sorry, I can't give you that gift.\"","\"Can't you give me an ordinary gift?\"","Mu Mian shook her head, \"No. You deserve the best.\"","\"...\" Because of this logical paradox, Fang Rui felt he would never receive a gift from Mu Mian in his lifetime.","At this moment, a mother and son pair walked down the opposite corridor - it was Chen's mother and Chen Yuankun.","Chen's mother recognized Fang Rui and approached him: \"Is my younger son hospitalized? Where is he? Officer, could you take me to see him?\"","Fang Rui pointed to the room they were facing and said: \"He's in there.\"","Chen's mother said to Chen Yuankun: \"Yuankun, you have a brother. He got lost when he was young, and now we've finally found him. You must treat him well, understand?\"","\"Yes, Mom, I understand.\"","Chen's mother turned and entered the hospital room.","Chen Yuankun watched her back, a look of contempt and disgust crossing his face. When he felt Fang Rui and Mu Mian's gaze, he quickly concealed his expression and followed his mother's footsteps."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Double Clues: Alibi","paragraphs":["\"He seems to really hate Ding Zhuangzhuang,\" Mu Mian whispered to Fang Rui. \"But Ding Zhuangzhuang was the one who was abandoned. Why would he hate Ding Zhuangzhuang?\"","Fang Rui also found it strange. Chen Yuankun had said he didn't know he had a twin brother, so why would he show such disgust towards Ding Zhuangzhuang?","Moreover, even though Chen Yuankun knew the police were present, he still displayed that kind of smile. It was very likely that he couldn't control his emotions and inadvertently revealed his true feelings.","Fang Rui thought of another possibility, \"Could it be that what he hates is his mother?\"","In the hospital room, Chen's Mother threw herself onto Ding Zhuangzhuang, crying heartbrokenly: \"My son, it's all mother's fault. Mother is so sorry. My son...\" Chen's Mother wanted to call his name, but she didn't know it, so she could only stop there.","Ding Zhuangzhuang maintained his vacant expression, extending his left hand to pat Chen's Mother's face intermittently.","Chen Yuankun stepped forward and grabbed Ding Zhuangzhuang's hand, \"Brother, have you been well all these years?\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang's body trembled, and he fearfully withdrew his hand.","\"Brother, come home with us. We'll take good care of you from now on.\"","The duty nurse came in to change Ding Zhuangzhuang's IV drip. Seeing his family members had arrived, she reminded them: \"Why did you family members take so long to come? Those two police officers outside have already paid several tens of thousands in medical fees for you. You should pay them back quickly. It's not easy for police officers to earn their salary, don't make them pay out of their own pockets.\"","Chen's Mother didn't respond and continued holding Ding Zhuangzhuang while crying.","Chen Yuankun also stood there without answering.","\"Are you all deaf?\"","Chen's Mother glared at the nurse, \"You're the one who's deaf.\"","The nurse suddenly seemed to understand something and rolled her eyes at both of them.","After Chen's Mother finished her intense crying, rationality took over again.","Ding Zhuangzhuang's mind was now damaged, and if she took him home to care for him, she would have to look after him for the rest of his life. Moreover, Ding Zhuangzhuang had an unlucky birth chart that would bring misfortune to his parents, which made Chen's Mother even more reluctant to take him home.","Chen's Mother walked out of the hospital room and said to Fang Rui and Mu Mian who were standing in the hallway: \"Officers, we'll be leaving now.\"","Mu Mian asked in confusion: \"He needs someone to take care of him now. Aren't you going to look after him?\"","Chen's Mother looked somewhat embarrassed and said, \"I need to watch over our supermarket. I have to go back.\"","\"Is your supermarket more important than your son?\"","\"He... he's not really my son.\"","\"You gave birth to him,\" Mu Mian emphasized angrily.","Chen's Mother was left speechless. Her expression became more guilty, and for a moment, she considered taking Ding Zhuangzhuang home to care for him, but she knew the children's father would never agree. He might even throw both her and this mentally challenged son out of the house. Moreover, if Chen Yuankun had such a mentally challenged brother, it would affect Chen Yuankun's future prospects.","Chen's Mother hardened her heart and said, \"I never raised him, so he's not my son.\"","\"If it were Chen Yuankun lying in there, would you take care of him?\" Fang Rui questioned.","Chen's Mother glanced at Chen Yuankun and said urgently, \"Yuankun is different. I raised him myself, and no matter what condition he's in, we would take care of him. But that person in there, I... I feel like a stranger to him.\"","After hearing his mother's words, Chen Yuankun turned to look at Ding Zhuangzhuang in the hospital room. His expression was blank as he coldly observed the man who looked identical to him.","\"Let's go home,\" Chen Yuankun said.","\"Yes, I need to go back and make dinner for your father. If I'm late, he'll scold me again.\" Chen's Mother didn't dare look at Fang Rui and Mu Mian anymore, and said quietly, \"Officers, we'll be leaving now.\"","After they left, Mu Mian said angrily, \"They might as well not have come at all!\"","\"She came to ease her own guilty conscience.\"","Recalling the scene in the hospital room, Fang Rui analyzed, \"When Chen Yuankun grabbed Ding Zhuangzhuang's hand earlier, Ding Zhuangzhuang showed an expression of fear. Could it be that Chen Yuankun did something to him?\"","\"Then they must have known each other before,\" Mu Mian remembered the recurring timeframe. \"Could they have met six months ago? Many important events happened six months ago.\"","Although Ding Zhuangzhuang was a suspect, he had just escaped mortal danger and couldn't be detained yet. Fang Rui assigned two officers to watch his room.","Fang Rui had Li check the surveillance footage near both Ding Zhuangzhuang's and Chen Yuankun's homes to see if they could find evidence of the two meeting.","The most crucial thing now was to break Chen Yuankun's alibi.","The next morning, the salesman who had been in the video conference with Chen Yuankun on the night of the incident returned from his business trip. Fang Rui and Zhang went to find him at his office in the factory.","This was a small-scale building materials factory that mainly produced various types of steel bars and metal construction materials, with only about a dozen employees. The salesman was called Li Deming, and his office was very basic.","\"Officers, look at the meeting records. During that time period, I really was in a video conference with Manager Chen.\" Li Deming opened his computer to show them the meeting time and list of participants.","Zhang asked, \"Isn't he just a purchasing agent? Why do you call him Manager Chen?\"","\"Oh, 'manager' is just a respectful term, it doesn't represent his actual position. Besides, he has the authority to make purchasing decisions. He decides whose goods to buy, so if he's not a manager, what is he?\"","\"Isn't Manager Wang his superior?\"","\"He's Manager Wang's right-hand man. Manager Wang listens to everything he says.\"","\"You really didn't record the video conference?\" Fang Rui asked.","Li Deming was an old hand at this, and he laughed it off, \"No, I was so flustered by his complaint at the time that I forgot to turn on the automatic recording function.\"","\"Wouldn't you be more likely to record the video when there's a complaint involved, to keep evidence? You've been in this business for so long, you shouldn't be this careless. Or was something said in the meeting that shouldn't have been?\"","Having his pretense exposed, Li Deming was stunned for a moment before admitting, \"Officers, I did record the video, but some of the content involves industry secrets. Please don't let this leak out.\"","\"Where's the video?\"","Li Deming opened his computer's D drive and clicked on a folder named \"New Files\" which contained various audio and video recordings. He clicked on one of them and the video began to play.","On the other end of the conference was Chen Yuankun, who appeared to have just taken a shower with a towel wrapped around his head. The background was his home with bright lights on. During the meeting, he would occasionally stand up and walk around.","At the beginning of the meeting, Chen Yuankun was very angry and started berating Li Deming. When Li Deming got tired of being scolded, he reminded him, \"Chen Yuankun, you took a ten percent commission from me. When there's a problem, you should help me solve it properly instead of yelling at me.\"","Chen Yuankun was taken aback, and his attitude improved considerably. Their communication became much smoother afterward.","Near the end of the video, Li Deming said, \"Manager Chen, another batch of goods will arrive tomorrow. There are some defective items in that batch that look unsightly, but the quality is fine. Give me the inspector's contact, I can handle him.\"","Chen Yuankun frowned slightly but didn't reply and ended the video call."]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Double Clues: Collaborative Murder","paragraphs":["After the video ended, Li Deming awkwardly rubbed his hands together, \"Officer, this is just how our industry works. It's part of our business ecosystem.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui copied the video and asked, \"Isn't a 10% commission a bit high?\"","Fang Rui had classmates in the Economic Crime Investigation Department who often complained to him about various bizarre forms of bribery. Kickbacks were an open secret in every industry - if you wanted to get orders, you had to provide benefits to the client's sales representatives. However, in traditional industries with low profit margins, kickbacks rarely reached 10%.","\"We have no choice - business is tough these days. Out of this 10% commission, 8% goes to his superior, and only 2% goes to him. The construction materials industry is too competitive. If I don't do this, I can't get any orders at all.\"","\"How do you know how their commission is distributed?\"","\"I got him drunk and sweet-talked him into telling me. He also mentioned that he's had enough of Wang Yonghua, and that he'll step over him to get ahead sooner or later.\"","Fang Rui exchanged glances with Zhang - could this be Chen Yuankun's motive for murder?","Zhang said, \"To make money, you must be cutting costs drastically. How can you guarantee the quality of products made this way?\"","\"Well... being cheap doesn't necessarily mean poor quality. We conduct quality inspections on every batch to ensure there are no problems. Accidents in the construction industry are no small matter - we wouldn't dare to be careless.\"","\"Why don't you negotiate directly with Manager Wang? Then you'd only need to pay 8% commission.\"","Li Deming sighed, \"You don't understand - without Manager Chen mediating, I couldn't get any orders even if I offered higher commission.\"","\"Is Chen Yuankun very capable at his job?\"","\"Although Manager Chen is young, he's very capable and well-versed in handling relationships. Working with him is very smooth.\"","After leaving the factory, Fang Rui analyzed, \"Chen Yuankun was promoted six months ago, likely because he could help Wang Yonghua make money. Could his motive for murder be an unfair split of the profits?\"","Zhang thought this was very possible, \"I have Zhang Xiaoling's contact information, I'll ask her about it.\"","From Zhang Xiaoling, they learned that Jianhua Construction Company had experienced a building collapse incident six months ago. During the investigation, company executives took the opportunity to conduct an anti-corruption campaign. The heads of both the project and business departments were found to have problems, but the procurement department's accounts were clean, so Wang Yonghua emerged unscathed from this storm.","It was from that time that Chen Yuankun began to receive Wang Yonghua's favor.","Back at the station, Fang Rui handed the video to the technical department for analysis.","After the results came out, Fang Rui called a case analysis meeting.","Li from the technical department said, \"The meeting video is authentic, not artificially synthesized. We can also rule out the possibility of Chen Yuankun faking the video background, because he moves around frequently, and any background manipulation would be easily detected.\"","\"If he was in a meeting then, how could he appear at the parking lot to commit murder? The person in the mall must have been Ding Zhuangzhuang. How else could he be in a meeting and killing someone at the same time?\" Zhang analyzed.","\"When you eliminate the impossible, whatever remains, however improbable, must be the answer,\" Mu Mian said. \"Could Chen Yuankun and Ding Zhuangzhuang be working together? One killing, while the other attended the meeting?\"","\"But Chen Yuankun has lighter skin, and Ding Zhuangzhuang is darker. And if they were working together, why would Chen Yuankun frame Ding Zhuangzhuang?\" someone objected.","\"Could it be that Chen Yuankun deceived Ding Zhuangzhuang? They appeared to be working together, but Chen Yuankun secretly left Ding Zhuangzhuang's DNA at the scene to frame him?\" Chen Xue speculated.","Fang Rui played the video again, letting everyone review the meeting content.","\"Chen Yuankun's expression seems off. When Li Deming mentioned kickbacks, he hesitated as if he didn't know about it. And when verifying the contract, Chen Yuankun had to check the contract to respond to Li Deming's points. If he had drafted the contract himself, why wouldn't he know its contents?\"","\"The lighting is very bright, making everyone's skin appear lighter.\"","\"It's quite disrespectful that he's wearing something on his head while meeting with partners. Could it be to hide his hair? He might actually be Ding Zhuangzhuang in disguise!\"","After repeated viewings, everyone noticed many inconsistencies.","\"Looking at it this way, Chen Yuankun was the killer. He had Ding Zhuangzhuang impersonate him while he committed the murder, and left Ding Zhuangzhuang's DNA samples at the scene,\" Zhang analyzed.","Mu Mian said, \"These are just our speculations. How can we prove all this?\"","Everyone fell silent. They could now be fairly certain that Chen Yuankun was likely the killer, but they had no evidence to prove it.","Li continued reporting on the surveillance results: \"There are few cameras near Ding Zhuangzhuang's home; there are also few cameras near Chen Yuankun's home. He lives in a newly built complex with inadequate infrastructure and no internal surveillance. There are multiple ways to enter the complex, so we couldn't find any useful leads from the surveillance footage.\"","Zhang said, \"Chen Yuankun moved four months ago. He used to live near his company, closer to downtown where there are many cameras. Could he have moved specifically to avoid surveillance?\"","After the meeting, Fang Rui discovered that a large sum of money had been refunded to his phone from the hospital. While he was wondering about this, Li Meijia showed up unannounced.","\"Officer Fang, can I apply to take care of Ding Zhuangzhuang at the hospital?\" Li Meijia requested. \"The police at the hospital said I need your permission to visit him.\"","\"Ms. Li, we have some questions for you.\"","Fang Rui took Li Meijia to the interrogation room. He placed printed chat records in front of her and asked, \"Did you ever hint to Ding Zhuangzhuang that you wanted Wang Yonghua dead?\"","\"Yes! But that was my thinking a month ago, I was just venting my emotions. Do you suspect I instructed Ding Zhuangzhuang to kill him?\"","Seeing that Fang Rui didn't believe her, Li Meijia continued, \"Officer Fang, you can ask Wang Yonghua's lawyer. A month ago, I signed a marital property agreement where Wang Yonghua agreed to give me 20% of his assets and 55% to our two children. I got custody of the children. With so much property coming to me, why would I want to have him killed?\"","Fang Rui and his team questioned Wang Yonghua's lawyer, who confirmed that Wang Yonghua and Li Meijia had indeed signed a marital property agreement with the distribution exactly as Li Meijia described.","After Wang Yonghua's death, Li Meijia only planned to take 75% of his assets, intending to distribute the remaining 25% among Wang Yonghua's mistresses. So she had no reason to kill Wang Yonghua.","Although Wang Yonghua was unfaithful in relationships, he was good to his children, which was why he agreed to sign that marital property agreement.","\"Did Ding Zhuangzhuang ever tell you about his past?\"","\"He rarely mentioned it. He had a difficult childhood - his foster mother was a mentally ill woman who often beat him. Later he wandered around and was bullied by others.\"","\"Did he mention where his hometown was?\"","\"I think it was in Dongcheng in the north. After learning his parents might be in Jiangzhou City, he wandered here. But he said he never found his parents. He was planning to leave this place, but he said meeting me made him want to stay.\" Li Meijia said.","Li Meijia had lost both parents at a young age and was passed around between relatives, enduring their cold treatment. Her life only improved after marrying Wang Yonghua. Initially, she was only attracted to Ding Zhuangzhuang's appearance, but after learning about his tragic past, she empathized with him and gradually fell in love.","Fang Rui sent Ding Zhuangzhuang's photo to the police in Dongcheng, asking if they recognized him.","They quickly replied with information.","\"His name isn't Ding Zhuangzhuang, it's Ding Wei. And even Ding Wei might be an alias. He was once a suspect in a fraud case.\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: Double Clues: The Other Side","paragraphs":["Fang Rui heard another version of Ding Zhuangzhuang's background from the Dongcheng Police Department.","\"He's not an orphan. His father was a factory owner, very wealthy. When he was 12, he ran away from home and joined a fraud gang, traveling around to scam people. When we caught him, he wasn't even sixteen yet, and since he was only an accomplice, we didn't pursue criminal charges.\"","\"Later, he used romance scams to deceive many girls, but those girls insisted they gave him money willingly. Since the amounts weren't large, no cases were filed.\"","\"What kind of personality does he have?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"He's extremely smooth and worldly. The kid is quite clever, just didn't use his smarts for good. When I met him, he was only fifteen, but he talked and acted like an adult. He even smoked and drank.\"","\"Why did he run away from home?\"","\"Rebellion, of course. When we tried to send him back home, he'd rather jump from the car than return. Besides, his parents had another child and didn't really want him anymore.\"","\"Do you have his fingerprints or DNA information?\"","\"We have his fingerprints.\"","After learning Ding Zhuangzhuang's true identity, everyone was stunned. None of them had imagined that his tragic background was fabricated to deceive people.","Mu Mian was the most upset, unable to believe she could still be scammed even with Fang Rui around.","\"I shouldn't have been so sympathetic.\"","Fang Rui consoled her: \"At least there's one less tragically suffering child in this world.\"","\"But there's one more despicable fraudster and two foolish victims.\"","Chen Xue asked puzzled: \"Where did you get two fools from? Weren't you the only one who got scammed?\"","Mu Mian pointed at Fang Rui.","Fang Rui added: \"The hospital refunded our medical expenses.\"","\"So there's another victim. Who else was foolish enough to fall for his scam?\"","\"Ms. Li.\"","Zhang sighed from the side: \"Don't tell me Ms. Li fell victim to a romance scam, losing both her heart and money?\"","Mu Mian started feeling sorry for Ms. Li again.","\"The auto repair shop staff said Ding Zhuangzhuang was introverted, which is completely different from what the Dongcheng police described!\" Chen Xue said puzzled.","Mu Mian had a bold theory: \"Could Chen Yuankun and Ding Zhuangzhuang have switched identities? Maybe the current Chen Yuankun isn't Chen Yuankun, and Ding Zhuangzhuang isn't Ding Zhuangzhuang.\"","\"But Ding Zhuangzhuang has many calluses on his hands, clearly from long-term manual labor. Besides, it would be easy to spot if a college student and an auto mechanic switched identities,\" Chen Xue argued.","Chen Xue had also suspected this possibility, but the gap between their identities was too large, making it too difficult to pretend to be each other.","\"What if they switched identities six months ago?\" Fang Rui said. \"Six months is enough time for two people to become familiar with each other's identities. Plus, Ding Zhuangzhuang has a fraud record, so he should be good at impersonation.\"","Chen Xue analyzed: \"Then Chen Yuankun, or rather Ding Zhuangzhuang pretending to be Chen Yuankun - could his motive for framing the fake Ding Zhuangzhuang be that he wanted the real Chen Yuankun to disappear, so he could take his place forever?\"","\"This sounds like something from a detective novel,\" Zhang commented. \"Good thing I don't have a twin brother, or I wouldn't even know if someone replaced me. Chen Xue, would you be able to recognize me if someone switched places with me?\"","Chen Xue looked at him helplessly, \"Of course. No one else in this world could be as silly as you.\"","\"Ah, so I'm unique in your heart.\"","\"...\"","Wang scoffed: \"It's work hours, mind the atmosphere and stop flirting! There are lots of people here.\"","Hearing Zhang's words, Mu Mian suddenly felt a sense of crisis. She grabbed Fang Rui's hand and examined it carefully.","\"Mu Mian, what are you doing?\"","\"I want to memorize your physical characteristics, so if anyone tries to replace you, I'll definitely notice. I'm not good at detecting lies, but I'm very good at remembering physical features. I've already memorized your face and hands, are there any other characteristics?\" Mu Mian reached out to pull at Fang Rui's clothes, but he stopped her.","Zhang looked at Wang, \"Say that last line again, louder.\"","\"It's not the same thing. Look at Forensic Mu's innocent eyes - she's just conducting academic research.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui brought Chen Yuankun to the interrogation room.","\"Officer, you've called me in again. Is there something else you want to ask?\" Chen Yuankun asked.","His expression was calm, showing none of the panic typical of suspects. Instead, he acted as if he was there for a business meeting.","\"You're vegetarian, right?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"What does that have to do with the case?\"","\"Please answer my question.\"","\"No.\"","\"So you eat meat, correct?\"","\"Yes.\"","Fang Rui gave Zhang a look, and Zhang placed a box of braised pork rice in front of Chen Yuankun. Zhang said, \"It's almost noon, we got you lunch.\"","Chen Yuankun crossed his arms and refused, \"Thank you, but I'm not hungry. I don't want to eat right now!\"","\"Is it that you don't want to eat, or you dare not eat?\"","\"Are you trying to torture a confession out of me? I'll file a complaint against you.\"","Zhang pointed to his police badge, \"Go ahead and complain about me. But what will you complain about? That we kindly provided lunch for a suspect? Or do you think eating meat is torture for you?\"","Chen Yuankun picked up the lunch box. He picked up a piece of meat and put it in his mouth, chewing forcefully, but his expression grew increasingly strained as he felt his stomach churning violently.","Seeing this, Zhang quickly put a trash can in front of him, \"If you can't eat it, spit it out quickly!\"","Chen Yuankun fought back his nausea and insisted, \"Now can you prove that I'm not vegetarian?\" Before he could finish speaking, he grabbed the trash can and started vomiting violently.","\"Look at you, why not just admit you're vegetarian? Why make yourself suffer?\" Zhang quickly handed him a cup of water. Chen Yuankun immediately used it to rinse his mouth, the meat's smell making him feel like dying.","After Chen Yuankun drank the water, Zhang took the paper cup and passed it to Wang who was waiting outside.","Once Chen Yuankun had recovered somewhat, Fang Rui asked, \"Li Meijia said the person she was dating was vegetarian. That person was you, wasn't it?\"","Chen Yuankun wanted to deny it, but he knew that Li Meijia had spent enough time with him to identify who her boyfriend was through such details.","He admitted, \"Yes. I loved her, even though she was my superior's wife. I didn't dare to date her openly, so I pretended to be a mechanic.\"","\"Why a mechanic, and not some other profession?\"","\"I made it up on the spot.\"","\"Because you're not Chen Yuankun, you're Ding Zhuangzhuang, or should we call you Ding Wei.\"","Upon hearing the name Ding Wei, Chen Yuankun's face showed anger, and he shouted forcefully, \"I'm not Ding Wei! I'm not! I am myself!\"","\"We've already obtained Ding Wei's fingerprints from the Dongcheng police.\"","Chen Yuankun froze, then became even more angry, \"I told you, I'm not Ding Wei! Don't call me by that name.\""]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Double Clues: Swapping Lives","paragraphs":["The fingerprint comparison results came back quickly. They revealed that the Chen Yuankun before them wasn't actually Chen Yuankun, but rather his twin brother, Ding Zhuangzhuang.","Fang Rui placed the report in front of the fake Chen Yuankun, who was actually Ding Zhuangzhuang.","Ding Zhuangzhuang gave it a cold glance and retorted, \"Yes, I switched identities with Chen Yuankun. So what? We were both tired of our lives, so we swapped. Is that a problem?\"","\"Why did you previously deny knowing each other?\"","\"I didn't want the identity swap to be exposed.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"On the night of the 23rd, did you kill Wang Yonghua and Sun Xiaoning, then frame the fake Ding Zhuangzhuang?\"","\"Of course not. I don't know why they died. Later, I heard my brother was hospitalized for drinking. I suspect he must have killed them because he hated those two people deeply. He must have drunk heavily out of fear after committing the murders.\"","\"Why did he hate them?\"","\"Wang Yonghua was jealous of my brother's higher education, so he deliberately oppressed him, picked on him, made him do various menial tasks, and even forced him to clean toilets. My brother has strong self-esteem but a weak personality. He didn't know how to fight back and could only endure silently. He eventually developed depression. He told me many times how much he hated Wang Yonghua and wished him dead.","As for Sun Xiaoning, she was nothing but a loose woman. She claimed to like my brother, gave him encouragement and comfort, gave him hope; but behind his back, she treated several male colleagues the same way and had many boyfriends. Later, when my brother discovered she was with Wang Yonghua, his world collapsed. He had a mental breakdown and almost committed suicide by jumping into the river. I was the one who saved him.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang seemed to have a good relationship with Chen Yuankun, constantly referring to him as \"brother.\" This confused Zhang - why would he want to frame Chen Yuankun?","However, Fang Rui noticed many holes in his story.","\"Why didn't your brother quit his job?\" Zhang asked.","\"Quit? He studied civil engineering. Do you know how difficult it is to find a decent job in his field that doesn't involve working at construction sites? Besides, that evil couple wouldn't have allowed him to quit!\"","\"How long have you known Chen Yuankun?\"","\"Three years. He went to Dongcheng for his graduation trip that year, where we met and recognized each other. Later, when I wasn't doing well in Dongcheng, he asked me to come here, saying he would earn money to support me. My brother is a good person - even if he killed someone, it was because others pushed him to it.\"","\"When did you start switching identities?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"Six months ago. The company started an anti-corruption campaign then, and my brother had evidence of Wang Yonghua's embezzlement. He didn't have the courage to report it, but he couldn't bear being an accomplice either, so his depression relapsed.","I told him I would take his place at work, and he could do whatever he liked, like traveling. But I never expected him to choose to become a mechanic, a lower-class person.\"","\"Why did you need to switch identities?\"","\"We were both dissatisfied with our lives and wanted to try each other's life, so we switched. My brother is a bookworm who can't do anything except study. His work life was unsuccessful, and he was played by women in relationships - he's a failure.","As for me, I just needed a degree and a decent identity. With these, I could become successful, just like now.\" Ding Zhuangzhuang's expression showed a hint of pride.","\"The person who had the video conference with the sales representative on the night of the 23rd was the real Chen Yuankun, right? Although his hair was wrapped in a towel, we analyzed the footage frame by frame and saw some blonde strands.\" Fang Rui placed the photo in front of him.","Ding Zhuangzhuang calmly explained, \"That's because that night, I was planning to disguise myself as a repairman to go on a date with Li Meijia. I had put on a wig, but suddenly received a message about a mistake with the goods, so I had to wrap my head and attend the meeting.\"","The explanation seemed reasonable. Fang Rui and his team didn't contradict it. They still didn't have enough evidence to prove he was the killer.","Ding Zhuangzhuang continued, \"Officers, I know you suspect I'm the murderer. But where's your evidence?\"","Seeing no response from Fang Rui and his team, he said smugly, \"You don't have any evidence, do you? So let's not waste each other's time.\"","\"The evidence is on that car refrigerator, isn't it?\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang's expression froze momentarily before he smiled, \"That's something you'll need to investigate. Officers, have you finished your questions? Can I leave now?\"","\"Certainly not. You're suspected of identity theft, and we'll place you under administrative detention,\" Fang Rui said.","Fang Rui planned to detain Ding Zhuangzhuang on this pretext to prevent him from committing more crimes, such as harming Chen's parents. Fang Rui remembered his expression at the hospital - he might not hate Chen Yuankun, but rather his biological parents.","Ding Zhuangzhuang's smug smile froze. He asked, \"My brother voluntarily switched identities with me. Is that illegal too?\"","\"How can you prove it was voluntary?\"","\"I...\"","\"He's become mentally impaired. You can't prove it now, can you?\"","All original paper contracts at Jianhua Company were kept in the company's archives. The police obtained all contracts handled by Chen Yuankun from the company's management. The handwriting on contracts from six months ago differed from those signed in the past six months.","Fingerprints were extracted from the contracts. The fingerprints on contracts from over six months ago matched those of Chen Yuankun in the hospital.","This further proved that the two had indeed switched identities six months ago.","Although Ding Zhuangzhuang admitted to switching identities with Chen Yuankun, he adamantly denied being the killer.","There wasn't enough evidence yet to prove who the killer was that night.","Fang Rui analyzed, \"When we mentioned the car refrigerator, Ding Zhuangzhuang hesitated for a moment. There might be some clues on it, and he probably hasn't disposed of it properly yet.\"","\"Could it be hidden in his house?\" Zhang suggested.","Fang Rui obtained a search warrant and first searched Chen Yuankun's home but found nothing. The room appeared to have been thoroughly cleaned, spotlessly clean.","When Chen's Mother learned that the person in the hospital was actually Chen Yuankun, she was stunned with horror, mumbling, \"Impossible, I couldn't have failed to recognize my own son.\"","\"Didn't you notice anything different about your son recently?\"","\"I... I've been busy with business.\"","She continued mumbling, \"This is retribution, all because of my sins!\"","When they went to search his supermarket, they had barely reached the entrance when they saw an ambulance parked outside, with doctors and nurses carrying out a blood-covered man.","Chen's Mother threw herself onto him, crying loudly, \"Husband, what happened to you? How did you get hurt like this?\"","\"What happened?\" Fang Rui asked the nurse.","\"He fell from a ladder while moving goods.\""]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: Double Clues: Can We Look at the Skull","paragraphs":["Chen's father was injured in the storage room at the back of the supermarket. The storage room was small and dimly lit. Goods were stacked layer upon layer, piled up high, making the storage room feel oppressive and cramped.","Chen's father fell from a ladder. From the scene's condition, it appeared that while he was climbing the ladder to retrieve a box of canned drinks, the second rung of the ladder broke, causing him to fall, and the goods in his hands fell too, hitting his head.","The ladder was made of welded stainless steel, poorly constructed, and the break occurred at a welding joint due to a failed weld seam.","Wang analyzed, \"Looking at the welding point, the weld is clean without oxidation or rust, suggesting it was likely welded recently. The exact cause of the weld failure needs further testing. Initial assessment suggests it's due to the welding material - I can see it's very poor quality metal with high brittleness.\"","\"Could Ding Zhuangzhuang have deliberately damaged the ladder to murder his father?\" Zhang speculated.","\"If that's the case, this Ding Zhuangzhuang is terrifying - how could he harm someone while being locked up?\" Wang sighed.","Fang Rui also suspected Ding Zhuangzhuang, thinking he must deeply hate Chen's father and mother after learning about his true identity.","The store had surveillance cameras. The footage showed Chen's father using the ladder earlier that morning without incident. No one else had entered the storage room that day except for Chen's father.","Ding Zhuangzhuang, who had been impersonating Chen Yuankun, had been in the storage room three days ago helping his father move goods. He hadn't returned to the supermarket since then.","Chen's mother had entered the storage room the previous morning to retrieve a box of instant noodles.","\"This should be an accident. Ding Zhuangzhuang hasn't been in the storage room these past few days, and Chen's father used the ladder frequently without incident,\" Wang analyzed.","Fang Rui repeatedly watched the surveillance footage. The camera could see one corner of the storage room, showing that it had been quite empty a few days ago, likely filled up recently due to frequent restocking.","\"The second rung would only be needed when reaching for goods on the top layer. It wasn't necessary for other times,\" Fang Rui theorized. \"The perpetrator might have calculated that Chen's father wouldn't climb that high in those days. By the time he fell, it would be days later, removing any suspicion from the perpetrator.\"","Fang Rui had Wang collect fingerprints from the ladder. However, only Chen's father's fingerprints were found.","Zhang exclaimed in surprise, \"Ding Zhuangzhuang must have helped his father move goods and used the ladder, yet there are no fingerprints from him - he must have wiped them off.\"","In the surveillance footage, Ding Zhuangzhuang wasn't wearing gloves while moving goods. The supermarket's cameras could partially see inside the storage room, and one frame showed Ding Zhuangzhuang using the ladder.","Chen's father's injuries were severe, but Chen's mother only took him to a nearby small hospital. After a night of emergency treatment, Chen's father passed away.","By the time Fang Rui and the others received the news, Chen's father had already been taken to the funeral home. When Fang Rui and Mu Mian arrived at the funeral home, Chen's father had already been cremated, his ashes placed in an urn.","Mu Mian complained to Fang Rui, \"We're too late. The body is gone.\"","\"They were too hasty,\" Fang Rui found it strange that Chen's mother didn't even bring her son to the hospital first, but instead rushed to cremate the body early in the morning. It seemed like she was trying to hide something.","Mu Mian, unwilling to give up, approached Chen's mother and the others, pointing at the urn that the staff was about to carry away. \"Usually, the skull doesn't completely burn during cremation. Though it might be inappropriate to ask, could I open the box to examine the deceased's skull?\"","Chen's mother, tears still in her eyes, looked horrified at the cute-looking girl before her.","Fang Rui explained, \"We suspect his death wasn't accidental but murder, so we want to investigate the cause of death.\"","\"Didn't the hospital issue a death report? Why don't you just ask them for it?\" Chen's father's brother complained.","\"But doctors specialize in saving lives, they're not experts in analyzing causes of death,\" Mu Mian said softly.","Mu Mian had already seen the death report; the doctor had only described the victim's injuries without detailed documentation of the wound conditions. Moreover, the human brain is complex, and without an autopsy, it's difficult to determine the cause and nature of injuries.","Of course, a cremated skull couldn't determine the cause of death either.","Chen's mother insisted, \"There's nothing to investigate. My husband fell from a ladder - it was an accident! Isn't arresting my son enough? Who else do you want to arrest?\"","\"Don't you want to know the true cause of your husband's death?\" Mu Mian tried to persuade her.","Chen's relatives glared angrily at Mu Mian before escorting Chen's mother to offer incense for Chen's father.","After they left, Mu Mian suddenly asked, \"Where will they bury the deceased?\"","Fang Rui replied helplessly, \"You're not thinking of digging up the grave, are you?\"","\"That's illegal! But I'm really curious about what a cremated skull looks like. They say it's snow-white, and the bones become very brittle. I want to tap it and feel its texture.\"","Mu Mian regretted not attending Ms. Jiang's cremation ceremony; otherwise, she could have seen cremated bones then.","\"...\"","Fang Rui found a deceased's relative who had few family members and made a deal with them to let Mu Mian in during the collection of the ashes.","\"Fang Rui, how did you manage that?\" Mu Mian asked excitedly.","\"When you go in, you can only look, not touch, understand?\"","\"Got it.\"","Minutes later, the funeral home staff witnessed an unusual scene. As he pulled the deceased's remains from the furnace, two family members knelt down wailing loudly, while a girl circled around the remains, seemingly studying the skull's shape with eager eyes.","If only she could touch it...","\"Young lady, shouldn't you be crying?\" the staff member couldn't help but remind her.","\"I'm afraid of disturbing him. He died so young; we should let him go peacefully.\"","The two family members cried even harder.","After leaving the funeral home, Mu Mian remarked, \"The color of the cremated skull was beautiful, truly snow-white. But that deceased person's skull shape wasn't attractive - he must have preferred sleeping on one side, causing his skull to become asymmetrical.\"","\"...\"","With the body gone and no crucial evidence to prove murder, the case couldn't be officially investigated.","However, Chen's mother's rush to cremate the body confirmed one thing: Chen's father's death was likely not accidental.","Fang Rui suddenly thought of a possibility - could Chen's mother be the one who wiped off the fingerprints? Perhaps she damaged the ladder and killed Chen's father, or maybe she was helping Ding Zhuangzhuang cover up evidence.","The investigation into the car refrigerator had made no progress.","Sun Xiaoning had once shared photos of the red car's interior on social media, through which they learned about the car refrigerator's appearance - it was pink with many decorative stickers.","The police had searched everywhere Chen Yuankun and Ding Zhuangzhuang had lived and worked, but found nothing.","\"Could the car refrigerator have never been taken away, but hidden in the parking lot instead?\" Mu Mian analyzed. \"The most dangerous place is often the safest place.\""]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: Double Clues: Key Evidence","paragraphs":["\"We've conducted an extensive search of the parking lot. We checked all the garbage bins and every corner of the parking lot, but found nothing! We've questioned the janitors and security guards, and they all said they hadn't seen this item,\" Zhang complained.","\"There's still one place we haven't searched,\" Fang Rui said. \"We haven't searched the cars.\"","\"But all those cars are locked. How could he put it inside? We've already checked under every car, and nothing was hidden there.\"","\"Didn't Ding Zhuangzhuang used to work at an auto repair shop? Could he be skilled at picking locks?\"","Zhang and the others went through the parking lot again with photos of the refrigerator, searching each car, even rechecking the vehicles that had left after the incident.","After spending an entire day, they finally identified a suspicious vehicle. Through the window, they could see something wrapped in a black plastic bag in the trunk. It was square-shaped and not very large.","The trunk's lock showed no signs of tampering.","Using the vehicle entry and exit records, they tracked down the car's owner. When contacted, the owner explained that he was one of the mall's shop owners and had been away on vacation, which was why the car had been parked there. He had a spare key at his shop.","After opening the trunk and removing the plastic bag, they found a pink mini-refrigerator - the very one that had disappeared from Sun Xiaoning's car.","Everyone's faces lit up with excitement, finally finding evidence to implicate Ding Zhuangzhuang.","Wang eagerly surrounded the refrigerator with his toolkit, \"Don't touch it! Let me check for fingerprints first.\"","\"He must have worn gloves while committing the murder. How could there possibly be fingerprint evidence?\" Zhang objected.","\"There are quite a few fingerprints here,\" Wang detected numerous prints on the refrigerator.","\"That only proves the refrigerator hasn't been wiped clean in a while.\"","\"...\"","After bringing the refrigerator back, Mu Mian sprayed luminol reagent both inside and outside. Soon, several small fluorescent reactions appeared on the exterior, appearing as droplet-sized spots - likely blood spatter.","\"There's blood,\" Chen Xue said excitedly.","But Mu Mian wasn't as optimistic. \"Chen Xue, do you remember how Wang Yonghua died?\"","\"He was struck on the head with a wrench.\"","\"This is blood spatter,\" Mu Mian reminded her.","\"Oh right, this could be Wang Yonghua's blood. Of course, the killer wouldn't be so careless as to injure himself during the crime and leave his DNA evidence at the scene.\"","Wang detected many fingerprints, belonging to eleven different people, but none matched either Ding Zhuangzhuang's or Chen Yuankun's prints.","\"Wang, I told you the killer wouldn't leave fingerprint evidence. Wearing gloves during a crime is basic criminal knowledge,\" Zhang sighed.","Wang gave him a side-eye. \"So, you think my work is meaningless?\"","\"Of course not. Some criminals are stupid and don't know the basics.\"","\"...\"","The blood test results came back quickly. As Mu Mian had predicted, the blood on the refrigerator's exterior belonged to one person - Wang Yonghua.","\"If there's no evidence on the refrigerator, why did Ding Zhuangzhuang hide it?\" Zhang complained.","\"Besides fingerprints and DNA samples, what other evidence could prove his identity? And this evidence would need to be difficult to destroy and intrinsically linked to the entire refrigerator.\"","Everyone was deeply disappointed. They had thought finding the refrigerator would provide evidence to convict Ding Zhuangzhuang, but they came up empty-handed.","\"We've only checked the outside of the refrigerator, not the inside,\" Fang Rui said.","\"We did check the inside... wait, you mean we should take the refrigerator apart?\"","Fang Rui handed the refrigerator to the technical department, asking them to dismantle it for clues.","There were new developments in Chen's father's ladder death case. Shop owners near the supermarket reported hearing welding sounds the morning before Chen's father's accident. That morning, Chen's father had gone out to restock inventory, Chen Yuankun wasn't at the supermarket, and only Chen's Mother was there.","The answer seemed obvious - Chen's Mother was likely the one who damaged the ladder. But now the body was gone, making an autopsy impossible, and there was no crucial evidence to prove Chen's Mother had deliberately sabotaged the ladder.","The next day, the technical department completed their examination of the refrigerator and issued a report.","\"The internal components were doused with water, causing a short circuit that completely destroyed the refrigerator.\"","They still found no fingerprints or blood traces inside. However, they discovered something unusual about one of the components.","\"This... appears to be a listening device. It can record sound and transmit it to other devices through the cloud. It also stores recordings locally. But since it was connected to the refrigerator's circuitry, it was damaged in the short circuit.\"","\"Can it be fixed?\"","\"We'll try.\"","Thanks to the technical department's efforts, the listening device was soon repaired. They played the most recent recording:","\"Chen Yuankun, I've treated you well, groomed you as my successor. Why did you kill me?\" Wang Yonghua's breathing was heavy as he spoke weakly.","\"Because I'm not Chen Yuankun. After you die, I can be Chen Yuankun forever.\" The other voice was triumphant.","\"You're not Chen Yuankun? Who are you really?\"","\"You're about to die, so I'll let you know the truth. I'm Ding Zhuangzhuang. I slept with your wife, oh, and Sun Xiaoning too - I used her and discarded her... The lowlife scum you looked down on now holds your fate in his hands.\"","\"Please, don't kill me... don't kill me!\"","The sound suddenly stopped, and after a long pause, a voice said, \"Almost forgot, there's a listening device here!\"","The recording abruptly ended. Ding Zhuangzhuang must have poured water into the refrigerator, causing the short circuit that stopped the recording.","The technical team traced the terminal device through the listening device to a laptop computer. Further investigation confirmed it was Ding Zhuangzhuang's work laptop.","They obtained Ding Zhuangzhuang's laptop, and although he had deleted all the recordings, the technical department recovered his browser history and found the platform and account he used to receive the recordings.","The recordings were stored in the cloud - they just needed to log into the account to download them again.","The account usage records showed that Ding Zhuangzhuang had been monitoring Sun Xiaoning and Wang Yonghua for three months. There were numerous recordings, and Fang Rui's team randomly listened to a few.","One recording from six months ago revealed Sun Xiaoning and Wang Yonghua plotting to hire someone to murder Li Meijia.","Zhang wondered, \"Why did Ding Zhuangzhuang really kill him? It couldn't have been for Li Meijia, right? He doesn't seem like the romantic type.\"","Wang excitedly said, \"Why don't we just talk to him and find out?\""]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Double Clues: Confession","paragraphs":["Ding Zhuangzhuang was brought to the interrogation room once again.","He hung his head, eyes fixed on the floor, hands tightly clasped together.","He knew the police must have obtained evidence of his crimes; otherwise, they wouldn't have called him in for another interrogation.","Before Fang Rui and Zhang could speak, Ding Zhuangzhuang asked, \"Did you find that refrigerator?\"","\"Yes, we did. And we found the listening device hidden inside it.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang smiled wryly, mocking himself, \"Ah, my luck has always been terrible.\"","\"Crime always leaves evidence behind. You thought you planned a perfect murder, but there are always flaws in the execution.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang looked at Fang Rui and Zhang, asking softly, \"Does every crime get punished? Then why didn't that couple face any consequences for abandoning me? They didn't just abandon me - it was winter, and they threw me, just an infant, into freezing lake water. I nearly died.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang fell silent. In those days, many children were abandoned or killed for various reasons, and those parents were never punished.","Ding Zhuangzhuang kept his head down, his voice muffled, \"Crimes that go undiscovered never get punished. Those people don't even suffer from guilty consciences.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Did you frame Chen Yuankun for murder as revenge against the Chen family?\"","\"Of course not. My revenge against the Chen family was sabotaging the ladder, causing that couple's downfall.\"","Zhang exclaimed, \"You damaged that ladder?\"","\"Four days ago, I deliberately told that woman the ladder was broken and offered to fix it. I broke the rung near the top. The warehouse wasn't very full then, but when they restocked to a certain level, they would need to climb to that height, and then fall from the ladder. Whether it was either of them who fell, my goal would be achieved.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Which rung of the ladder did you break?\"","Instead of answering that question, Ding Zhuangzhuang continued explaining his motives for murder: \"I killed Wang Yonghua because he called me bottom-feeding trash. I worked so hard to survive - what right did he have to humiliate me? What right did that parasite, who rose through family connections and generational privilege, have to insult me?","Two weeks ago, he discovered I was taking kickbacks behind his back and demanded I hand over all the money within a week. That pushed me over the edge. Why? Hadn't I helped him make enough money already? I couldn't accept it, so I killed him. Sun Xiaoning was just collateral damage.\"","Fang Rui noticed Ding Zhuangzhuang avoiding his question and realized he must be covering for Chen's mother. But why would he protect her when he hated her so much?","Fang Rui challenged him: \"You said before that Chen Yuankun had evidence of his corruption. Couldn't you have used that to threaten him instead? And didn't he say before his death that he saw you as his successor? Would he really pressure you over such a small amount of money?\"","There were many contradictions in Ding Zhuangzhuang's story.","\"I had already handed over that evidence to Wang Yonghua as a gesture of loyalty. He was a company executive - it would have been effortless for him to destroy me and blacklist me from the entire industry. I had no choice but to kill him since he was in my way.\"","\"Why did you frame Chen Yuankun?\"","\"A murder case needs a culprit, doesn't it? I thought if I provided you with a suspect, you would stop investigating. I underestimated the capabilities of the Jiangzhou City police.\"","Zhang asked puzzledly, \"You always called Chen Yuankun 'brother.' How could you bear to poison him with fake alcohol?\"","\"My brother was indeed good to me - he was the kindest person in my life. But he was the one who first suggested switching identities with me, letting me experience his life. He was tired of his oppressive corporate life and wanted to trade places; then when he couldn't adapt to life among the lower class, he wanted to switch back. Why?","He enjoyed twenty-plus years of a blessed life, so why would he only let me enjoy it for half a year? I could have done even better, become someone more outstanding than him!","Initially, I only planned to use fake alcohol to make my brother mentally impaired. That's how I damaged my adoptive parents' son - no one ever found out. Then Wang Yonghua started pressuring me. That's when I came up with a brilliant plan: I would kill Wang Yonghua, frame my brother, and make them both disappear. Then I could openly continue being Chen Yuankun.\"","Zhang exclaimed in shock, \"You also harmed your adoptive parents' child?\"","\"You've investigated me, so you should know I used to be called Ding Wei, but that wasn't my name - it belonged to my adoptive parents' real son. Their three-year-old son was kidnapped, and they bought me from human traffickers to replace him.","Until I was twelve, I thought I was their biological son, and those were the happiest years of my life. Then their son was found by the police. That's when my life's nightmare began.","When their biological son returned, my adoptive parents' attitude toward me changed immediately. They took back my name, Ding Wei, and renamed me Ding Zhuangzhuang, but didn't register me in the household registry.","Though they still kept me, they often allowed their biological son to abuse me. One day, they killed my little black dog that I had raised for many years - after their real Ding Wei returned, that dog was my only companion. They even tricked me into eating its meat. Since then, I haven't been able to eat any meat.","I couldn't bear this abuse, so I ran away. Before leaving, I tricked that child into drinking high-concentration methanol, which left him mentally impaired. Anyone who hurt me would never get away with it.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang recounted these past events expressionlessly, as if telling someone else's story.","\"Please describe how you committed the murders.\"","\"I had installed a listening device in Sun Xiaoning's car long ago. I wanted to record evidence of her infidelity to ruin her reputation - she had deceived my brother's feelings, and I wanted to restore his honor. Later, I discovered Wang Yonghua frequently got into this car, which gave me many unexpected discoveries.","On the day of the incident, I learned they were going to the mall that evening and then meet in the underground parking lot. I knew my chance had come. After following them to the parking lot, I put on a raincoat and shoe covers, then killed Wang Yonghua with an oil-stained wrench. Then I took Wang Yonghua's tie and went to another car to strangle Sun Xiaoning.","Everything went smoothly, but I forgot about the listening device in the car, and I left evidence while taunting Wang Yonghua. I wanted to remove the listening device, but it was installed inside the refrigerator, and I couldn't get it out quickly. I could only take the refrigerator with me. The refrigerator was too large and conspicuous to carry, so I found a car that looked like it had been parked for a long time, used a master key to open the trunk, and put the refrigerator inside.","As for my brother's situation, I first tricked him by saying I wanted to teach Wang Yonghua a lesson but needed his help to create an alibi. He agreed - he felt guilty towards me, so he always fulfilled all my requests. While my brother was asleep, I scratched him to get his DNA. After the murders, I tricked him into drinking fake alcohol, then planted some luxury items taken from the crime scene in his room to frame him for the murders.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang described the crime process in detail, largely matching the police's theories.","However, Fang Rui found it unusual - Ding Zhuangzhuang wasn't the type to be compliant and submissive, so why was he confessing in such detail?"]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: Double Clues: Not Your Fault","paragraphs":["Fang Rui asked, \"What about Li Meijia? You heard Wang Yonghua and Sun Xiaoning plotting to have her murdered through the listening device. Didn't you tell her about this?\"","\"Why should I care about her affairs? Initially, I wanted to scam some small money from her because she seemed rich and naive. After switching identities with my brother, I wasn't satisfied with small amounts anymore. I continued dating her using Ding Zhuangzhuang's identity. For someone from the upper class like her, appearing vulnerable was the best way to win her over. I planned to play the long game and catch a big fish - after her divorce, I would marry her and then swindle all her property.\"","\"Actually, you killed for Li Meijia, didn't you? Sun Xiaoning never deceived your brother's feelings; you made it all up. At first, you thought Wang Yonghua only had Sun Xiaoning as a mistress. You seduced Sun Xiaoning and encouraged her to elope with you, actually intending to protect Li Meijia's marriage, right?\" Fang Rui speculated.","Ding Zhuangzhuang showed a contemptuous smile. \"Ridiculous. I'm not some lovesick fool. Why would I commit a crime for a woman?\"","\"Because you felt she was the only person who loved you unconditionally.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang's eyes gradually reddened, but he held his head high and insisted, \"Someone like me stopped expecting love long ago. I killed for myself, to regain my dignity, to have an identity that could stand in the sunlight.\"","Fang Rui communicated further with the Dongcheng police.","\"Yes, Ding Zhuangzhuang's adoptive parents had lost a child who was kidnapped. When they found him, he was already mentally impaired - the traffickers had beaten him until he became mentally disabled.\"","Zhang was puzzled: \"Why did Ding Zhuangzhuang claim he had drugged that child into disability?\"","Fang Rui couldn't understand why Ding Zhuangzhuang kept lying.","\"He's admitted to his crimes, so why does he keep telling these meaningless lies?\"","Mu Mian analyzed, \"Could he have pathological lying disorder? When the frontal lobe function is weakened, they can't judge the accuracy of their own words, leading to constant lying, and their lies seem very real. He must be skilled at fraud.\"","\"Yes, he was a fraudster before.\"","Zhang speculated, \"Then maybe his brother wasn't actually disabled by his drugs either?\"","Fang Rui interrogated Ding Zhuangzhuang again.","\"Your adoptive parents' child wasn't disabled by your drugs. Why are you lying?\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang paused, then said, \"Because I wish I had been the one who disabled him. I hate him; he ruined my life.\"","\"Actually, you didn't trick your brother into drinking fake alcohol either, did you?\"","Earlier at the hospital, Mu Mian had examined Chen Yuankun's mouth and found no injuries. If someone had forced him to drink, there would definitely have been wounds in his mouth. The fake alcohol had such a strong taste that no normal person would drink it, let alone that much.","\"Officer, I've confessed everything that needs to be confessed. You have the statement you want, and all the evidence is there. I'd like some quiet time now.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang fell silent.","Chen Yuankun had indeed suffered psychological abuse from Wang Yonghua and developed severe depression. They exchanged identities to give each other a chance at a different life.","Ding Zhuangzhuang's original plan was to leave his brother's DNA at the scene. After investigation, the police would find that his brother might have been framed, and he, pretending to be Chen Yuankun, would also be a suspect. Since they had switched identities and looked almost identical, it would be impossible to determine who the real killer was, and both would eventually be released without charges.","But his brother was too kind-hearted. He thought Ding Zhuangzhuang had killed for him and was consumed by deep guilt. His brother deliberately drank the fake alcohol, attempting to fake a suicide from guilt and take all the blame, but instead of dying, he became mentally disabled.","There was no need to tell the police this. He wanted his brother to be seen as a pitiful victim, unrelated to the case.","Regarding Chen's father's case, Fang Rui provided relevant evidence, and the prosecutor's office determined that Chen's mother was unlikely to be the perpetrator due to insufficient evidence, so they declined to prosecute.","After Ding Zhuangzhuang was sent to detention, Li Meijia visited him immediately.","\"Why did you kill him?\" Li Meijia asked in confusion. \"I had already told you that Wang Yonghua and I were about to divorce. Why did you still kill him?\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang said expressionlessly, \"It has nothing to do with you. Don't come anymore. I don't want to see you.\"","\"Ding Zhuangzhuang, we were so close to getting married.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang knew clearly that they could never marry. The gap between them was too wide - he was a sinful person who had done many bad things, while Li Meijia could live happily in the sunlight.","But when Li Meijia told him she wanted to marry him, he felt the whole world become warm.","Having that moment of warmth was enough.","Ding Zhuangzhuang said emotionlessly, \"I was with you to scam your money. You looked rich and naive, and my specialty was conning women out of their money. I'm a fraud. Everything I told you was a lie. All those tragic experiences that made you sympathize with me were made up to deceive you.\"","Li Meijia covered her face and burst into tears.","\"Go. Make yourself stronger. Don't rely on men - they're all unreliable like me.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang's memory returned to two weeks before he killed Wang Yonghua.","He had heard Wang Yonghua telling Sun Xiaoning through the listening device: \"Xiaoning, that property agreement was just to pacify that old woman. Don't worry, I'll make her give everything back.\"","\"How will you do that?\"","\"I'll hire someone to kill her in a car accident! I know someone who can handle this for just a million yuan. That old woman has life insurance with my two children as beneficiaries. When she dies, we'll get a huge payout.\"","\"Isn't that too cruel?\"","\"If I don't do this, I'll become a pauper.\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang closed his eyes. He couldn't admit his true motive for killing. He didn't want Li Meijia to have any connection to this case. Someone as wonderful as her should have nothing to do with evil.","Li Meijia left the detention center. The sunlight fell on her face as she looked up at it, murmuring, \"I'm finally free!\"","The next moment, her expression darkened. She had lost someone who truly loved her.","Chen's mother also visited Ding Zhuangzhuang at the detention center. Looking at the man sitting across from her, she couldn't tell whether he was Chen Yuankun or Ding Zhuangzhuang.","\"Son, it's mother's fault. I'm sorry, I let you suffer for so many years...\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang interrupted her: \"Just take good care of my brother in the hospital. There's a bank card in my brother's drawer, the PIN is his birthday. That money should be enough for you to live out your lives.\"","\"I will.\"","\"Then... goodbye!\" Ding Zhuangzhuang realized he had nothing to talk about with his birth mother.","\"Child, do you hate your mother?\"","Ding Zhuangzhuang held back his tears. When his adoptive parents had thrown him out, he had countless times imagined that if only he could find his birth parents, he could live a happy life.","But in the process of searching for them, he had done countless wrong things just to survive. He had become a person full of sin, so when he finally found his parents, he didn't dare reveal his identity.","Later, he discovered that he had actually been abandoned. He had felt hatred and resentment, but he could only accept fate's mockery once again.","He nodded and said softly, \"You had no choice. I don't blame you.\"","She was just a weak and powerless woman who could neither fight against superstitious feudal beliefs nor resist her husband."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: Proposal Time","paragraphs":["As the Qixi Festival approached, Zhang was planning something big.","After work, everyone except Chen Xue and the out-of-town Lin Sen gathered in the conference room, with even people from other departments joining in, making the room instantly crowded.","Zhang handed out milk tea to everyone one by one, then shyly said, \"I plan to propose to Chen Xue tomorrow, and I want everyone to help me brainstorm how to make the proposal romantic.\"","Mu Mian took a sip of her milk tea and asked confusedly, \"Why not propose tonight? It's best to propose before going to bed. Usually, people's minds aren't as clear at night, making them more likely to agree to requests.\"","\"...Because tomorrow is Qixi, Valentine's Day, which has special significance.\"","Mu Mian exclaimed in surprise, \"You have to choose a day to propose?\"","\"Of course. Choosing a good day is very important.\"","Mu Mian summarized the first reason for her own failed proposal to Fang Rui: she didn't choose the right day.","Mu Mian suggested, \"Then why not propose tonight? Give Chen Xue a surprise, no, a huge surprise. Many people propose on Qixi, so the day isn't that special.\"","Zhang found Mu Mian's suggestion quite reasonable, but—","\"Tonight is too rushed; I haven't prepared everything yet.\" Zhang looked at everyone, \"Please help me come up with some creative ideas.\"","Mu Mian summarized her second reason for the failed proposal: she hadn't made sufficient preparations. Creating a romantic atmosphere in advance was necessary.","Wang suggested, \"Why not take Chen Xue to the rooftop to watch the stars tomorrow night, and then propose with a ring made of dogtail grass?\"","\"Watching the stars is quite romantic, but there are not only many stars on the rooftop but also lots of mosquitoes.\"","\"A ring made of dogtail grass? That's way too shabby.\"","\"That's called creativity. Diamond rings are too cliché. In idol dramas, the male leads always propose with dogtail grass—romantic, eco-friendly, and close to nature.\" Wang defended his idea.","\"That won't work,\" Zhang dismissed Wang's suggestion and asked others, \"Any other ideas?\"","Wen from the finance department suggested, \"Why not take Chen Xue for a walk and lead her to a osmanthus tree, then propose with a ring made from a soda can pull-tab? We'll shake the osmanthus flowers around you, creating a shower of osmanthus petals. Guaranteed to be unforgettable.\"","\"That sounds romantic.\"","Mu Mian couldn't help but remind them, \"Destroying greenery is against the law.\"","Zhang rejected the idea, as they couldn't break the law.","Zhang looked at Fang Rui, thinking the boss might have a reliable idea.","Sitting next to Fang Rui, Mu Mian thought Zhang was looking at her and offered her suggestion.","\"We can design a series of puzzles, each containing clues, but they should be simple so Chen Xue can solve them. These clues will guide Chen Xue step by step to the proposal location...\"","Zhang's eyes lit up and said to Mu Mian, \"That's a good idea. Then what?\"","\"The proposal location is the dissection room. When Chen Xue arrives, she'll see you lying on the dissection table, buried in roses. She'll be very sad, crying as she digs you out of the flowers.","At that moment, you suddenly 'come back to life' and sit up, presenting a ring made of bones, asking if she'll marry you. Then we'll all raise our scalpels and chant, 'Chen Xue, say yes, say yes...'\"","\"......\"","\"......\"","Zhang rubbed his forehead, wondering why he had expected anything normal from Mu Mian's response.","Wen laughed, \"Hahaha, Mu Mian, you're killing me. Under those circumstances, Chen Xue wouldn't dare refuse, right?\"","Wang curiously asked, \"How do you make a ring out of bones?\"","\"You can piece together finger bones into a circle, then polish and wax them.\"","Zhang emphasized, \"You don't need to think about the ring; I've already bought a diamond ring.\"","He pulled an exquisite ring box from his pocket, opened it, and showed it to everyone.","“Ah, what is that? It's blinding me,” Wang covered his eyes and made an exaggerated expression, “Take it away, quickly!”","Wen praised, \"Wow, that diamond is huge. Zhang, you've really spent a fortune.\"","\"That's right, I saved for years to buy this. I want to give Chen Xue the best proposal ring.\"","Wang reminded him, \"Zhang, you've spent all your salary now; what will you buy for the wedding ring?\"","\"Uh... My parents have already saved money for my 'wife fund.'\"","\"......\"","Mu Mian whispered her suggestion, \"Officer Zhang, you should have bought a gold bracelet. Chen Xue says diamonds aren't worth keeping; only wasteful people buy them. However, gold always appreciates and can be passed down as a family heirloom.\"","Zhang frowned, \"Really? Will Chen Xue think I'm too wasteful?\"","Wen rebutted, \"No, no girl doesn't like diamonds.\"","“Wen, your logic isn't precise; it's too absolute. I don't like diamonds.”","\"You like gold?\"","Mu Mian shook her head; she liked bones, various animal specimens, and corpses, but most people couldn't accept such hobbies, so Mu Mian decided not to reveal them.","Everyone came up with many more ideas, but none were feasible.","Zhang decided to go with a romantic but uncreative proposal: simply proposing with the big diamond ring.","Qixi happened to be on a Saturday, so they had the weekend off and didn't need to work.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian were paired up to help Zhang buy roses for the proposal setup.","They didn't go to a flower shop but to a wholesale flower market. There were no middlemen, so the prices were half of what they would be at a flower shop, and the flowers were fresher. However, the shop owner's attitude wasn't great, taking a long time to attend to them.","\"You want ninety-nine roses?\" The owner glanced at Mu Mian next to Fang Rui, \"For your girlfriend? I should mention, we don't do packaging here.\"","Mu Mian said, \"No need for packaging.\" They would use the roses to create a heart shape on the ground, so packaging wasn't necessary.","\"Then wait a moment.\"","The owner whispered to an employee, \"That guy doesn't look poor, yet he's not buying flowers from a shop; he's coming here for wholesale. How shrewd.\"","\"Exactly, how can his girlfriend stand it? Too stingy!\"","Mu Mian asked the owner confusedly, \"Aren't the flowers in the shops sourced from here? What's the difference?\"","The owner's face stiffened. She hadn't expected them to hear her so clearly.","\"We like the flowers, not the fancy packaging.\"","Mu Mian pulled Fang Rui, \"Let's go to another shop.\"","\"Okay.\"","They were about to head to another store when a flower farmer stopped them, \"Are you looking to buy roses? My flower field is nearby; if you buy from me, it'll be even cheaper.\"","\"Then please take us there.\"","The flower field was vast, but with Qixi approaching, the demand for flowers had surged, leaving the field mostly barren, with mostly buds remaining. In one corner, there were still a small patch of unpicked red roses, blooming beautifully.","\"Fang Rui, do you think there might be the Little Prince's rose here?\"","\"Maybe. If the Little Prince is here too.\"","When a breeze blew, the red roses swayed gently in the wind.","\"Fang Rui, you're so silly. The Little Prince is a character from a novel, and his rose is on another planet.\"","\"......\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian added a bit more money, and the farmer allowed them to pick the flowers themselves. After spending most of the day, they finally found ninety-nine roses of similar size and shape.","\"Mu Mian, let's head back.\"","Mu Mian's attention, however, was caught by a large cluster of yellow chrysanthemums. She said, \"Can I have a bouquet of those?\""]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: Confession","paragraphs":["Before Fang Rui could answer, the flower seller warned, \"Young lady, these flowers are used for mourning the dead. It's not auspicious. Why do you want to pick them? There are many other beautiful flowers over there you can look at instead.\"","Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui and said, \"I think they're beautiful.\"","Fang Rui smiled, \"Go ahead and pick them.\"","The flower seller was dumbfounded. Well, these young people in love these days really had no taboos when romance clouded their judgment.","Mu Mian picked about a dozen flowers and tied them together with a plastic strip. While Mu Mian thought the bouquet was perfect, Fang Rui inserted a red rose in the center of the bundle.","\"Mu Mian, this is for you.\"","\"Fang Rui, don't you think it clashes with the other pretty yellow flowers?\" Mu Mian's OCD was acting up, and she had to resist the urge to pull it out.","\"I think it looks nice this way.\"","\"No, it ruins the aesthetic of the bouquet.\"","\"This is my gift to you. It's like the rose from The Little Prince.\"","\"Fine, I'll reluctantly accept its presence.\"","On their way to the parking lot, Fang Rui and Mu Mian drew many curious stares. Fang Rui was carrying ninety-nine roses, while Mu Mian beside him held a bunch of yellow chrysanthemums. People couldn't understand what kind of couple they were.","When they arrived at Zhang's house, the others had almost finished decorating. The house looked romantic, with balloon hearts and flowers on the walls, and cloud-shaped colored lights replacing the regular ones.","\"The roses are here, let's arrange them into a heart shape!\" Wang directed. \"Make it bigger!\"","In no time, the entire proposal venue was set up.","After lunch, everyone faced a dilemma.","\"How do we trick Chen Xue into coming here?\"","Everyone looked at Mu Mian.","Mu Mian said, \"You all know I'm not good at lying.\"","\"That's exactly why she won't be suspicious if you do it.\"","Mu Mian called Chen Xue, but before she could speak, Chen Xue started talking.","\"Mian Mian, want to watch a movie this afternoon? There's this new romance film that's supposedly really melodramatic. It'll definitely be a brain-teaser for you. Want to come with me? Zhang said he's busy today and can't go with me.\"","\"Chen Xue, Officer Zhang, he...\"","\"What about him?\"","\"You should come to his house and see. Sister Wen is driving over to pick you up. Try to stay calm.\" They had thoughtfully arranged a driver to prevent Chen Xue from having an accident in case she got worried.","\"Mian Mian, what happened to him?\"","\"Just come quickly, or else...\"","\"I'm coming right away.\"","Wen's acting was far better than Mu Mian's. Under her skillful performance, Chen Xue almost believed Zhang had met with a terrible accident.","She stumbled through the door only to find flower petals floating in the air and Zhang kneeling on one knee in the center of a heart made of roses.","\"Chen Xue, will... will you marry me?\" Zhang nervously asked, holding up the ring box.","Everyone cheered from the sidelines, \"Say yes, say yes...\"","Chen Xue stood silently looking at him, not saying a word.","Everyone froze, worried they had somehow ruined the proposal.","\"Chen Xue, it's okay, when you're ready to marry me, I'll...\" Zhang said dejectedly.","Chen Xue threw herself into Zhang's arms. \"You scared me to death! What would I do without you?\"","\"So... will you marry me?\"","\"Of course.\" Chen Xue extended her finger toward him.","Zhang quickly slipped the ring onto Chen Xue's finger as she covered her face, beaming with joy.","Mu Mian was confused. Chen Xue had said she didn't like diamonds and preferred gold, yet she seemed so happy receiving a diamond ring.","Mu Mian quietly tugged at Fang Rui's sleeve. \"Do you like diamonds? I have a big one that Senior Yi Nian gave me. If you like it, I can give it to you.\"","\"Why did he give you a diamond?\"","\"Back then, I wanted to be a necromancer, but I didn't have a crystal. So he gave me one for my birthday. Do you like diamonds?\"","\"Why do you want to give me a diamond?\"","Mu Mian handed him a party popper. \"Quick, pull it! We need to shower them with streamers now.\"","After Zhang's proposal ceremony ended, everyone left, leaving the couple to their romantic moment.","\"It's only three in the afternoon, shall we go watch a movie?\" Fang Rui suggested.","\"Sure. Let's watch that brain-teaser movie Chen Xue mentioned.\"","Mu Mian texted Chen Xue asking for the movie title, but Chen Xue sent her the QR code for the tickets directly.","The movie was called \"Warm Winter,\" which made Fang Rui think of old melodramas.","At the theater, Fang Rui fell silent as he looked at the movie poster showing two men and one woman.","Mu Mian excitedly said, \"Here's the first mystery – which of these two male characters is the female lead's boyfriend?\"","The theater was packed and lively, mostly with couples.","At the beginning of the movie, everyone was engaged in the plot, but after a while, some people started playing with their phones. Soon after, couples began cuddling, and few people were actually watching the movie.","Mu Mian watched intently, memorizing every shot and every line of dialogue, but she still couldn't understand the movie's logic or what the director was trying to convey.","The girl sitting next to Mu Mian kept complaining to her boyfriend, \"Look at what movie you picked! Is this even a romance? What are they filming? I can't understand anything.\"","\"Hey, we're not here to watch the movie, we're here for a date.\"","\"But this background noise is polluting my ears.\"","Mu Mian turned to Fang Rui and said, \"This isn't just a romance movie.\"","\"Do you still want to watch it?\"","\"Of course! I rarely see such a brain-teasing movie. This director is amazing – he managed to create four couples from just three people. That's incredible.\"","The people around them looked at Mu Mian with newfound respect. How could she find this terrible movie brain-teasing? No, how could she even watch it seriously and analyze it? What kind of extraordinary mind did she have?","The girl next to Mu Mian asked puzzled, \"Where are the four couples?\"","\"Her with him, her with him again, him with him, and all three of them together.\"","\"...Impressive, you really understand permutations and combinations. Come to think of it, maybe that's what the director intended.\"","After the movie, Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to dinner.","After driving back to their building, Fang Rui invited Mu Mian for a walk.","To match the Qixi Festival atmosphere, colored lanterns hung along the street, and trees were wrapped in fairy lights, creating a dreamlike scene.","Mu Mian found the colored lights hurt her eyes.","Fang Rui suddenly felt this romantic atmosphere was perfect for confessing his feelings.","He first took Mu Mian's hand, and she naturally held his back.","Fang Rui nervously began, \"Mu Mian, I li-\"","Slap!","Mu Mian's palm connected with his face. She opened her hand to show him what she'd caught. \"There was a mosquito.\"","\"...\"","\"Fang Rui, what were you going to say?\"","\"There are too many mosquitoes. Let's not walk anymore. Let's go back,\" Fang Rui said.","Today wasn't suitable for a confession.","\"Okay, that movie was so mind-bending, my brain is short-circuiting. I need to rest properly.\"","Back home, Mu Mian put her yellow flowers in a vase. Seeing the red rose, she felt it didn't match the others, so she found another vase for it.","Suddenly, Mu Mian wondered why Fang Rui had given her a rose.","Roses symbolize love, and only couples give each other roses.","Following this logic, she could deduce that – Fang Rui liked her.","Mu Mian grabbed the rose and ran to knock on Fang Rui's door.","\"Fang Rui, open up, quick!\"","After a moment, Fang Rui opened the door, his hair still dripping – he must have been in the shower.","Mu Mian held up the rose and asked, \"Fang Rui, why did you give me a rose?\"","Fang Rui looked at her and smiled, \"Mu Mian, why do you think?\"","\"Because you... like me.\"","\"Wrong answer.\"","Mu Mian lowered her head dejectedly, overwhelmed by immense sadness. No wonder Fang Rui hadn't accepted her proposal – he didn't like her after all.","Fang Rui looked down at her and said softly, \"Mu Mian, I love you. Not like – love. Romantic love.\"","Mu Mian stood stunned for a long while, then lifted her head, her eyes bright as she looked at Fang Rui.","She spoke with utmost sincerity: \"Fang Rui, I love you too, not in an ordinary way, but in a unique way. It's like in a field of countless roses, the Little Prince only loves his one special rose. That's exactly how I love you.\"","Well... he had become a rose.","\"Mu Mian, may I hug you now?\"","\"Yes.\"","After a moment, Mu Mian changed her mind: \"Fang Rui, although I really like you, I'm not very comfortable with people hugging me... well, okay, you can hug me for a bit longer... Fang Rui, you've been hugging me for too long.\"","Fang Rui released Mu Mian, saying with a hurt expression: \"I only hugged you for one minute.\"","\"That's already broken the historical record.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian handed the rose to Fang Rui: \"Fang Rui, I'm giving you this rose that represents love.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Mu Mian felt relieved inside, finally finding a reasonable way to dispose of this rose - it had been diminishing the beauty of those little yellow flowers when placed together with them."]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: Happy Qixi Festival","paragraphs":["After being confessed to by Mu Mian, Fang Rui couldn't sleep that night. He couldn't help but post on his Moments (WeChat social feed).","[Happy Chinese Valentine's Day. From her.]","The picture showed that rose.","Soon, Fang Rui's Moments became lively with comments.","The Director was the first to see Fang Rui's post and commented: \"Fang Rui, has your account been hacked? @Li, check what's going on. How could Fang Rui post something so bizarre? We must catch whoever hacked his account!\"","Li: \"@Director Reporting sir, after verification, the post was made by Captain Fang himself. Report complete.\"","Director: \"@Li You finished checking in less than 30 seconds? That's not even enough time to boot up your computer. Li, you can't be this careless with your work.\"","Li: \"@Director Because I asked him directly.\"","Fang Rui: \"I posted it myself.\"","Director: \"Congratulations, congratulations!\"","Li: \"Congratulations boss on finally finding love.\"","Zhang: \"Congratulations boss on getting a girlfriend.\"","Chen Xue: \"Haha, my ship has finally sailed!\"","Finance Wen: \"@Chen Xue Haven't they been together for almost half a year? Why is everyone so excited?\"","Chen Xue: \"@Wen Before we were just shipping them, but now it's official! How can that be the same?\"","Finance Wen: \"Congratulations, congratulations.\"","Captain Li: \"Fang Rui, you're terrible at dating! How could you let a young lady give you flowers? Come on, private message me, I'll teach you how to date properly.\"","Zhang: \"@Captain Li Don't just teach Captain Fang, we all want to learn!\"","Captain Li: \"@Zhang You still need to learn? You're better at it than me. I often copy ideas from your Moments posts.\"","Wang: \"Let's make a group chat, this is affecting our image.\"","Li: \"Only friends can see Moments posts. What's the point of making a group when it'll be just us anyway? Though we could kick the Director out, hahaha.\"","Director: \"@Li I'm still here.\"","Director: \"@Captain Li You better not teach anyone. Your dating history made me anxious just watching it.\"","Captain Li: \"Well... at least I've stepped on all the mines already.\"","Li: \"Director, I was just joking! [Cute and innocent.jpg]\"","Wang: \"Hehe, Chinese Valentine's Day is a good day, everyone's found love.\"","Li: \"@Wang I suspect you're taking a dig at me.\"","Wang: \"@Li You should reflect on why you're still single when even the boss and Dr. Mu are coupled up.\"","Li: \"@Wang Because they found each other.\"","Wang: \"Being witty won't get you a girlfriend! You need to socialize more, don't just be a tech nerd.\"","Mu Mian: \"Yes, I gave him that! [Proud.jpg]\"","Wang: \"We know!\"","Zhang: \"No need to emphasize!\"","Li: \"Keep emphasizing and you're just showing off!\"","Lin Sen: \"Call me brother-in-law.\"","Mu Mian: \"@Lin Sen Brother-in-law.\"","Wang: \"Haha.\"","Li: \"Hahaha.\"","Zhang: \"Hahahaha.\"","Zhang: \"Why wasn't my proposal post this lively? Why did you all just like it without commenting?\"","Li: \"@Zhang Because you two show off your love every day, we're not interested in your gossip anymore. This is the boss's first time showing affection, it caught us off guard, we have to make it lively to give him face.\"","Fang Rui: \"Thanks for all the well wishes above.\"","Wang: \"Alright, alright, it's late, time to sleep. I need to drive my girlfriend to work the day after tomorrow.\"","Li: \"If work is the day after tomorrow, why sleep early tonight?\"","Chen Xue: \"Because he's bragging about having a girlfriend.\"","Li: \"Ahh, just a lonely single dog who can't sleep.\"","Finance Wen: \"Add another single dog.\"","Chen Xue: \"Why don't you two get together?\"","The Director quickly jumped in to break up the potential match: \"No way! One knows finance, the other knows technology; if they get together, our financial system's risk factor would be too high!\"","Chen Xue: \"Director, you're so strategic, truly worthy of being our leader.\"","Li: \"Director, don't worry, we're not compatible.\"","Finance Wen: \"Director, don't worry, we have different interests.\"","Everyone had an enjoyable Chinese Valentine's Day evening.","Fang Rui somewhat regretted posting that Moments update. After posting, it wasn't just his gossip-loving colleagues, but his classmates, relatives, and even his superiors who all sent their warm regards.","However, these congratulations reinforced one fact: he had a girlfriend now.","Mu Mian told her hacker friend about having a boyfriend. Her friend asked puzzled, \"Didn't you already have a boyfriend?\"","\"Why would you think that?\"","\"Look through our chat history, the name 'Fang Rui' appears so frequently, and you even sent me his photo, which I said was handsome. I thought he was already your boyfriend.\"","\"He wasn't then. But he is now.\"","\"That's good. After I got a girlfriend, I worried you wouldn't find a boyfriend and might end up alone.\"","\"I used to be scared of that too, but Fang Rui said he'll stay with me, so I'm not scared anymore.\"","\"Now neither of us will end up alone!\"","\"Yes.\"","Mu Mian told Shen Xiyin about this. Her sister wasn't surprised and said, \"Little Mian, you've grown up.\"","\"Sister, now that I have love, does that make me normal?\"","\"When you have love, whether you're normal or not doesn't matter anymore, because in his eyes, you'll be unique.\"","Mu Mian thought for a while, then sent emails to her adoptive father's lab seniors. They had joked before that if Mu Mian ever got a boyfriend, she must tell them.","She had promised. Being someone who keeps her promises, she sent emails to each of them. When she saw Jiang Yinian's email address, she thought for a moment, then sent him one too.","She waited for a long time, but none of the seniors replied. Mu Mian knew they probably wouldn't respond anymore. Since her adoptive parents passed away, she hadn't been able to contact them. Her sister also refused to mention them.","Perhaps they no longer used those lab-affiliated email addresses, or perhaps after her adoptive father's death, the bond connecting them had broken, and they no longer wanted to deal with their troublesome junior. Either way, they had lost contact.","Ding dong, an email came in from Jiang Yinian.","[Mu Mian, I'm glad you've found your own love. Wishing you happiness.]","Mu Mian replied: [Thank you. I hope you can find your own love too.]","Jiang Yinian didn't reply again.","Although they had confirmed their relationship, Fang Rui and Mu Mian's interactions remained largely the same as before. Mu Mian didn't blush when seeing Fang Rui, and he didn't look at her with lovey-dovey eyes. To outsiders, they still appeared like purely professional colleagues.","But in the morning when leaving home, Mu Mian's greeting changed from \"Fang Rui, good morning\" to \"boyfriend, good morning.\"","Mu Mian said: \"Fang Rui, from now on your name equals boyfriend, so when I call your name, it's the same as calling you boyfriend. So I'll still say, Fang Rui, good morning.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Fang Rui, you haven't said 'girlfriend, good morning' to me yet.\"","\"Girlfriend, good morning.\"","\"From now on, my name equals girlfriend, understand?\"","\"Mu Mian, good morning.\"","On Monday at work, Fang Rui bought milk tea for Zhang and the others. They sensibly accepted without teasing.","Firstly, there wasn't much to tease about - Fang Rui and Mu Mian weren't as openly affectionate as Zhang and Chen Xue. Secondly, they had already been warned by Fang Rui, and their 2000-word self-criticism reports weren't finished yet.","During the morning meeting, Wang shuffled into the conference room with a battered face. His left cheek had several scratch marks.","Zhang exclaimed in surprise: \"Wang, weren't you dropping your girlfriend at work this morning? How did your face get scratched up like this? Who did it? How dare they assault a police officer - aren't you going to report it?\"","Li reminded him: \"He is the police.\"","\"Well, there was a medical dispute at Shu's hospital entrance. A female family member lost control and tried to attack a nurse. I couldn't just stand by, so I intervened, and this is what happened.\"","Chen Xue asked: \"Is your girlfriend okay?\"","\"With me here, how could anything happen to her? That female family member just lost her child, and I felt sorry for her, so I didn't pursue her responsibility. Her husband took her away.\"","At this moment, the dispatcher informed them that they had received an emergency call. A medical accident had occurred at Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital, and the patient's family member was insisting it was a murder case, demanding police intervention.","Zhang asked Wang, \"Which hospital does your girlfriend work as a nurse at?\"","\"It's the same hospital where this incident happened. I wonder if the person who called the police was that woman from earlier? She seemed mentally unstable.\""]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: Death Angel: Medical Dispute","paragraphs":["Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital is a comprehensive tertiary hospital located in the city center. It is renowned for treating strokes, with elderly patients making up a large proportion of its patients. As a result, this hospital experiences more frequent medical disputes than other hospitals.","The person who called the police was a female family member named Feng Xiaonan. She was originally an elementary school teacher, and her husband was a business manager. They had a lovely child named Li Yang, and they used to be a happy family of three. However, a car accident destroyed their happiness.","Feng Xiaonan looked haggard, with sunken cheeks and dark circles under her eyes. Her clothes suggested she was financially well-off, but her hair was dirty, and she appeared disheveled.","\"Officer, my son is dead. Someone killed him. The doctors said he could live for at least another six months. But last night, my son suddenly stopped breathing. The doctors said his condition deteriorated, but I don't believe it. Someone must have murdered him!\" Feng Xiaonan cried.","Li Yang's attending physician, Doctor Zhang, clarified: \"Officer, her son was in a vegetative state. Who would murder someone in a vegetative state? She insists her son was murdered. Given her son's condition, it was already a miracle he lived this long.\"","\"Does being in a vegetative state mean he's not human? Does it mean he doesn't have the right to live? Although my son couldn't speak or move, he could hear me talking. He was still alive. Why did you take away his right to live?\"","Doctor Zhang stepped back, frightened. He explained helplessly, \"Ms. Feng, I've explained countless times that he passed away due to his deteriorating condition.\"","\"That's just an excuse. You doctors and nurses are all in this together. You all killed my child.\"","Feng Xiaonan's husband, Li Ruiqing, held her back to prevent her from harming the doctor: \"Officer, my wife might be having some mental issues. I'm sorry you had to come here for nothing. My wife probably reported a false alarm because she's not thinking straight after our child's death.\"","He turned to the doctor: \"Doctor Zhang, I'm sorry. I'll take my wife home now.\"","After their son's accident, Feng Xiaonan blamed herself for not watching him carefully enough. She took care of him day and night, not wanting to miss any chance for his recovery. When he died, her mental state began to collapse.","Doctor Zhang said, \"I can let this go this time, but please take your wife to see a psychiatrist soon. We can't have these disturbances every day.\"","\"Li Ruiqing, your son is dead, and you're defending his murderers! Where is your conscience?\" Feng Xiaonan tried to scratch Li Ruiqing but was restrained by Fang Rui and his colleagues.","Feng Xiaonan said, \"Officer, the person who killed my son was Li Lingling, the nurse on duty in the Neurosurgery Ward of Building 7. She's the distant niece of the driver who caused the accident. That driver didn't want to keep paying for my son's treatment, so he instructed Li Lingling to kill my child. My poor baby...\"","Li Ruiqing scolded her: \"Xiaonan, don't make baseless accusations. She could sue us for defamation. Li Lingling wasn't even working last night. How could she have killed Yang?\"","\"Li Ruiqing, why are you protecting the murderer? She is the killer! Yang was killed by her!\"","Fang Rui turned to Li Ruiqing and said, \"Mr. Li, please explain the situation in detail.\"","\"Two weeks ago, my son Yang was playing with his toys in front of our house when a car suddenly lost control and drove into our yard, hitting him. After emergency treatment, my son survived but became vegetative.","The doctors said that if we maintained his vital signs with equipment, our son could live for another six months, maybe longer if he was lucky. He was our only son, and even though he was in a vegetative state, we didn't give up on treatment and kept taking care of him. My wife took care of him day and night for over two weeks, but unexpectedly, at around eight o'clock the night before last, our son suddenly stopped breathing.","The doctors told us his condition had deteriorated. They explained the reasons, but it was all medical terminology that my wife couldn't understand, so she became convinced someone deliberately killed our son.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Where is your son's body?\"","\"The hospital has hidden it. They won't let me see my son,\" Feng Xiaonan shouted.","Li Ruiqing quickly explained, \"No, the child's body is in the morgue. My wife is too emotional, and I was afraid seeing our child's body would traumatize her further. I was worried she might do something rash, so I've been preventing her from seeing him.\"","\"Li Ruiqing, do you think I'm crazy? You're the crazy one! They killed my child, and no one will give me justice, yet you think I'm crazy. You don't love Yang. Do you have another child somewhere else?\" Feng Xiaonan demanded.","Fang Rui first calmed Feng Xiaonan down, then said to her, \"Ms. Feng, we will investigate the cause of your child's death. You need to stay calm and provide as much information as possible so we can help you uncover the truth.\"","Feng Xiaonan wiped her face, trying to maintain composure: \"Yes, I can't let people think I'm crazy. If I'm crazy, no one will believe me or help me get justice.\" She looked at Fang Rui and his colleagues: \"Officers, you must help me. You're my only hope.\"","\"Will you go with my colleagues to give a statement?\"","\"Yes.\"","Fang Rui had two female officers take her back to give a statement.","After Feng Xiaonan left, Li Ruiqing said, \"Officers, I'm sorry for troubling you. After that car accident, my wife's mental state became unstable, and she became paranoid. Our son probably died naturally. His head was severely injured in the crash, with brain matter exposed. He wasn't going to live long anyway. But my wife kept believing he could be cured and wouldn't give up on treatment.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Mr. Li, you seem reluctant for us to investigate. Why?\"","\"Who would murder a vegetative patient? Especially a child?\"","\"Doesn't the driver who caused the accident have a motive?\"","Li Ruiqing fell silent.","Fang Rui said, \"Take us to see your child's body first.\"","\"Alright.\"","The morgue was in the basement of Building 7 of the inpatient department, accessible only by service elevator. The lighting was dim, and there was a strange smell in the air.","It was divided into a freezer area and a temporary storage area for bodies. Li Ruiqing pointed to one of the transport beds and said, \"The child is there.\" He seemed afraid to approach.","Mu Mian lifted the white sheet covering the bed, but there was only a teddy bear, no body. The bear had a wristband attached to its paw with Li Yang's name and hospital information.","Mu Mian asked, \"Where's the body? Has someone stolen it?\""]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Death Angel: Who Stole the Corpse","paragraphs":["Li Ruiqing's face changed as he hurriedly walked over. He wanted to touch the teddy bear but was stopped by Fang Rui, \"Mr. Li, you're not wearing gloves, please don't touch it.\"","\"This teddy bear belongs to Yangyang. I gave it to him on his seventh birthday,\" Li Ruiqing said, staring at the teddy bear. He mumbled, \"Yangyang's body was right here. I brought it here with the nurse. How could it suddenly disappear?\"","Fang Rui looked at nurse Chen Li. She was the nurse on duty in Yangyang's ward that night, and she had helped Li Ruiqing transport the body to the morgue.","Chen Li stammered, \"I brought the body here with Mr. Li. I'm certain we placed it on this bed. Mr. Li said Yangyang loved this teddy bear the most, so we put it in Yangyang's arms. Why is only the teddy bear left now?\"","The morgue didn't hold many bodies. Most deceased patients were sent directly to the funeral home for cremation. Only bodies involved in medical disputes or those unclaimed by family members were temporarily stored here.","Li Yang passed away around eight o'clock on August 9th, two nights ago. Feng Xiaonan refused to send her child to the funeral home, holding onto his body all night long.","The next morning at 9:10, Li Ruiqing and nurse Chen Li took advantage of Feng Xiaonan being asleep to secretly move the child's body to the morgue.","Originally, Li Ruiqing had planned to send the child directly for cremation, but the hospital feared trouble from Feng Xiaonan. They worried that without the body, the situation might become complicated, so they temporarily placed it in the morgue while waiting for the forensic examiner.","They searched the entire morgue but couldn't find Yangyang's body.","Fortunately, there were security cameras installed in the hallway outside the morgue and in the service elevator.","\"Let's check the surveillance footage. We'll definitely find who moved the body.\"","Li and Zhang went to the security room to review the footage, while Fang Rui and Mu Mian questioned nurse Chen Li and Li Ruiqing separately.","They started with Chen Li.","Before Fang Rui could ask anything, Chen Li spoke first: \"Officer, do you think Yangyang's mother, Feng Xiaonan, might have taken his body? She's mentally unstable and loves her child so much. She's the most likely suspect.\"","Mu Mian replied, \"If she had taken him, she would have been holding the body during her confrontation with the hospital.\" Noticing Chen Li's strange expression, she added, \"That's how it always happens in TV dramas.\"","\"Then there are no suspects. Who would steal a child's body?\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Aren't there any doctors in your hospital who might have a particular interest in corpses?\"","\"Our doctors aren't perverts. They're only interested in treating living patients.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Did the child's father visit often to care for him?\"","\"Yangyang's father rarely came. He was extremely busy with work. He would occasionally visit in the evenings but only stay for an hour or two. Most of the time, it was just the child's mother and grandmother taking turns caring for him.","You know, I think Yangyang's mother's mental illness was brought on by stress. It's already heartbreaking enough when your child is hurt, and any mother would feel guilty. But her mother-in-law would aggressively criticize everything she did every day. She even blamed her for not watching the child properly, saying that's what led to the accident. Combined with the exhaustion of caring for her child day and night, Feng Xiaonan was practically broken.\"","Chen Li, being a mother herself, deeply empathized with Feng Xiaonan. She even worried that at this rate, Feng Xiaonan might be the one to die first.","\"So the mother spent most of the time caring for the child?\"","\"Yes. The grandmother would come during the day, but she mostly just complained and watched dramas on her phone. Basically, Yangyang's mother did all the care herself. She was very responsible. Despite Yangyang being bedridden for so long, he never developed bedsores and was always kept clean. She took better care of him than professional caregivers would have.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"After Yangyang passed away, didn't his grandmother come to make trouble?\"","\"No. I found it strange too. Yangyang's grandmother is usually so confrontational, yet she hasn't come to the hospital to cause a scene. Instead, it was the seemingly gentle and timid mother who did.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"What was Yangyang's condition like before he passed?\"","\"I was on duty then. Around eight o'clock, Yangyang's mother ran to the nurse's station saying her child wasn't breathing. When I got to the ward and saw the child's unusual color, I immediately called for doctors to attempt resuscitation, but it was unsuccessful.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Wasn't he on a cardiac monitor?\"","\"Yes, he was.\"","\"Didn't you notice when his heart rate and breathing became irregular? Didn't the machine alarm?\"","Chen Li looked embarrassed and explained, \"That night we had another patient in emergency care, and the entire nurse's station was busy. I was changing IV bags for other patients and didn't notice the abnormal readings immediately.\"","Li Ruiqing received a phone call about an urgent matter and left immediately, so they couldn't complete his questioning.","After the interviews, Fang Rui and Mu Mian went to the security office to find Li and the others.","They were still reviewing the surveillance footage.","Zhang analyzed, \"Could this actually be a murder case? Why else would the child's body suddenly disappear? Whoever took the body must not want us investigating the cause of death.\"","Mu Mian agreed, \"It's possible. Common causes of death for patients in vegetative states are infection and organ failure, which usually show a gradual progression. It's unusual for death to occur without warning. Li Yang's death was too sudden.\"","\"Who could have taken the body? It must be either Li Yang's family or a doctor.\"","Zhang said, \"Don't you think Li Ruiqing's attitude is strange? His child died, yet he's so calm. And when his child's body was stolen, he barely showed any anger? If it were me, I'd turn the hospital upside down looking for my child's body.\"","Mu Mian countered, \"Some people just remain calm when facing death, like me.\"","\"Mian Mian, you're not representative,\" Chen Xue said.","Wang thought more practically: \"Well, they probably cried themselves numb when the accident first happened, and now it's more like relief. Think about it - how difficult is it to care for a child in a vegetative state? It costs money and energy. The child's death might be a release for both the child and the parents. He's probably thinking about the accident compensation money. Once money enters the picture, he might not feel as sad.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Li Ruiqing doesn't seem to want us investigating the cause of death. Even if he doesn't care about his child, wouldn't he care about money? If this escalates, the hospital would likely pay to settle the matter. Why isn't he making a fuss with his wife?\"","\"Could it be that he loves his child so much that he doesn't want to profit from the situation?\"","\"That's unlikely. The nurse said he rarely came to the hospital to care for the child.\"","After this analysis, everyone felt something was off about Li Ruiqing.","\"Let's stop discussing and find who took the body first,\" Mu Mian urged.","\"We're looking.\"","Not many people had accessed the morgue, and most visits were made by nurses accompanied by family members. Very few went in alone. They quickly identified one suspicious person.","The person wore a loose white coat and was tall and thin. Their face was covered by a mask, and they had thick, fluffy hair that made their head appear large.","This person entered the morgue alone at 12:08 PM yesterday with empty hands, stayed for about seven minutes, and then left.","\"They didn't carry out a body. Could it still be in the morgue?\""]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: Death Angel: Black Gray","paragraphs":["Fang Rui contacted the hospital staff, who dispatched several medical personnel to assist the police in searching the bodies.","The bodies in the freezer were all stored in body bags.","This time, they pulled out all the bodies from the freezer, opened the bags one by one for inspection, and eventually found Yangyang's body in one of the compartments. Yangyang's body was placed in the same body bag as an elderly man's body, positioned near the man's legs. If they hadn't opened the bag, they wouldn't have noticed that a child's body was hidden inside.","During the first inspection, they had opened the body bag and saw the elderly man's body, so they didn't check further, never realizing that Yangyang's body was inside.","Zhang said, \"Could Yangyang's death really have been a medical accident? Otherwise, why would the doctor hide the body?\"","Li analyzed, \"It's also possible that someone disguised as a doctor to steal the body. Look, the white coat he was wearing was too big and didn't fit well.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Zhang, Li, you two go investigate this matter.\"","\"Okay.\"","Mu Mian took out a new body bag, placed Yangyang's body inside, and took it back.","Fang Rui invited Li Ruiqing to the interrogation room.","\"Mr. Li, we have found your son's body.\"","\"Is... is that so? That's great, great.\" Li Ruiqing said absent-mindedly.","He sat nervously in the chair, his head lowered in guilt, not daring to meet Fang Rui's gaze.","\"Mr. Li, don't you want to know who hid your son's body?\"","\"Who was it? Could it be the doctor? They didn't want my wife to cause a scene, didn't want you to find out the cause of death, so they hid my son's body.\" Li Ruiqing speculated.","\"Mr. Li, where were you yesterday at noon?\" Fang Rui asked.","\"I... I was with my wife. I was afraid she would get emotional and try to commit suicide, so I stayed with her, trying to console her.\"","\"Did you buy a wig?\"","\"No.\"","\"The owner of the wig shop closest to the hospital said you bought a wig there, claiming it was for your wife who has terminal cancer. The hospital's surveillance footage shows you sneaking into the doctor's office yesterday at noon. Did you steal the doctor's white coat?\"","\"I...\"","Confronted with various pieces of evidence, Li Ruiqing could no longer argue.","\"Mr. Li, why did you hide your child's body?\"","Li Ruiqing hugged his head, his expression pained. His mouth opened and closed, and finally, he admitted, \"Yes, I hid the child's body. Yesterday at noon, I took advantage of the doctors going to a meeting and stole a white coat to disguise myself as a doctor, then hid my child's body in the freezer. It was me. You can arrest me.\"","\"Why did you hide the child's body?\" Fang Rui repeated.","Li Ruiqing remained silent.","\"Because you knew the child didn't die a natural death, but was murdered, right?\"","Li Ruiqing still didn't speak.","\"If you continue to remain silent, we will have no choice but to suspect that your child's death is connected to you.\"","\"I... I have nothing to say.\" Li Ruiqing opened his mouth, as if to say something, but then closed it again.","Fang Rui detained Li Ruiqing temporarily on the charge of stealing a corpse.","Zhang wondered, \"I don't think Li Ruiqing killed Yangyang. He wasn't even there the day Yangyang died, but why did he hide the body?\"","Fang Rui said, \"He might have been protecting someone.\"","When Feng Xiaonan learned that her husband had hidden their child's body, her emotions flared up again. She muttered to the air, \"Li Ruiqing killed Yangyang. He has another woman outside, he doesn't need this child anymore, he thinks Yangyang is a burden...\"","\"You mean he cheated?\"","\"It must be so.\"","Feng Xiaonan's mental state was too poor, so Fang Rui and the others had no choice but to contact her parents to take her back.","In the autopsy room.","Mu Mian carefully read the death record provided by the doctor.","The cause of death given was: Intracranial infection leading to increased intracranial pressure, resulting in brain herniation.","The death diagnosis was: Severe traumatic brain injury, left temporal subdural hematoma; bilateral frontal, temporal, and right parietal lobe contusions; traumatic subarachnoid hemorrhage; scalp hematoma.","The death record showed: On August 9th, at 19:52, the patient's vital signs became abnormal, with cardiac arrest, cyanosis of the lips, difficulty breathing, and dilated pupils. After resuscitation, the patient died at 20:46 that evening.","After the body was thawed, Mu Mian began the autopsy.","The deceased's face and fingers were cyanotic, and there were pinpoint hemorrhages in the conjunctiva, which could initially suggest that the deceased likely died from asphyxiation, or at least experienced a period of asphyxiation.","Mu Mian examined the deceased's mouth and nose, finding no foreign objects. However, she discovered some black ash-like substances in the respiratory tract. These substances were small, blocky, and very thin.","Mu Mian used a cotton swab to wipe some of the black ash and examined it closely under the light.","Mu Mian said, \"This seems to be the residue of something that has burned.\"","Chen Xue observed for a while and then said, \"It looks like plant ash. Could this stuff have blocked the deceased's airway, causing his death? Who put this into Yangyang's airway? That's too malicious! Isn't this premeditated murder?\"","Mu Mian cut open the deceased's abdominal cavity, starting with the trachea and lungs, where she found a small amount of black substances.","Mu Mian then removed the deceased's stomach, cut it open, and found many black substances attached to the gastric mucosa.","Chen Xue said, \"There's also stuff in the lungs and stomach? Could it be that when someone fed the deceased these things, some accidentally fell into the airway, causing asphyxiation?\"","Chen Xue suddenly thought of something. \"Could it have been his family who fed him this?\""]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: The Angel of Death: The Killer","paragraphs":["At the case analysis meeting, Mu Mian reported the autopsy results.","\"The cause of the deceased's death was bleeding in the brainstem. This would damage the respiratory center, preventing the deceased from breathing on their own,\" Mu Mian explained. \"There are many causes of brainstem hemorrhage, including any factors that raise blood pressure, such as emotional distress, strenuous activity, excessive drinking, and constipation.\"","\"So, what caused the deceased's blood pressure to rise?\" someone asked.","Mu Mian replied, \"We found that the deceased's adrenaline levels were abnormally high, three times that of a normal person. Elevated adrenaline can cause blood pressure to rise. However, this could also be the result of adrenaline injection during medical resuscitation.","We detected some black ash-like substances in the deceased's body. It is weakly alkaline, and we are still analyzing what it is.","We also found cinnabar in the deceased's body. Cinnabar is both a traditional Chinese medicine and a toxic substance. Excessive intake can lead to mercury poisoning and affect the central nervous system.\"","Mu Mian displayed photos of the black substances on the screen.","\"Could it be the residue of some toxic herbal medicine? Or perhaps ash from burning mugwort? It's said that mugwort ash can be used in medicine,\" someone suggested.","Chen Xue added, \"I also suspect it might be some kind of plant ash.\"","\"But who would feed such a thing to a child, especially a comatose one? It seems like they were deliberately trying to harm him,\" another person commented.","Mu Mian said, \"It's unlikely to be medicinal residue. It appears to be ash formed from the combustion of a fiber-rich substance.\"","Zhang suddenly chimed in, \"Could it be ash from a talisman? In our area, some very superstitious people go to temples to get talismans when their children are ill. They burn the talisman into ash and mix it with water to drink. It's said to be very effective. The talismans are usually drawn with cinnabar. Maybe Yangyang's family is also superstitious and secretly fed him talisman water?\"","Others seemed to agree with Zhang's theory. If the child's condition worsened due to drinking talisman water, it would explain why Li Ruiqing hid the child's body and didn't want the police to investigate.","Li questioned, \"Comatose patients are usually maintained with IVs. How could someone feed him anything?\"","Chen Xue replied, \"Comatose patients still need nutrition. They are typically fed through a gastric tube with liquid food like rice porridge or protein powder. It's likely that Yangyang's family fed him talisman water secretly, without the doctor's knowledge.\"","\"Then, the person who fed him the talisman water is probably the child's grandmother or grandmother-in-law?\" Zhang speculated. \"Only older generations would be so superstitious.\"","As they finished the meeting and left the conference room, they heard that an elderly woman was causing a commotion at the police station entrance.","\"You heartless people, how could you arrest my son? My grandson just died, and instead of investigating the hospital's doctors and nurses, you arrest my son... You're all in cahoots with the hospital, making things difficult for us ordinary folks...\"","The woman was Yangyang's grandmother, Sun Guixiang, in her sixties, wearing a worn-out outfit, sitting on the ground at the police station entrance, crying and cursing.","A crowd of onlookers had gathered, with some even filming with their phones.","\"Old lady, is what you're saying true?\" an onlooker asked.","\"My grandson suddenly passed away, and the hospital won't give us any explanation. My son and daughter-in-law went to the hospital to seek justice, but the police sided with the doctors and arrested my son. We're the victims here! My grandson's body is still warm, and they're already bullying us...\" she wailed.","The onlookers felt sympathy for the poor old woman.","Fang Rui and Zhang hurried to the police station entrance to calm Sun Guixiang.","Zhang reached out to help her up. \"Grandma Sun, let's talk inside, okay? It's hot out here, and we can get you some water.\"","Sun Guixiang swatted his hand away. \"Inside? Do you think I'll come out alive? My son went in to cooperate with your investigation, and you locked him up. Are you planning to lock me up too?\"","Fang Rui explained, \"We detained him because he broke the law.\"","An onlooker asked, \"What law did he break? You need to explain in detail. Just because you say he broke the law doesn't make it so.\"","Fang Rui replied, \"I'm sorry, but we cannot disclose our work details to the public.\"","The crowd began murmuring among themselves. Some whispered, \"If the procedures are correct, why can't they be transparent?\"","Zhang was speechless. They didn't disclose details because they were afraid of online backlash.","Sun Guixiang, finding support in the crowd, became more assertive. She addressed the onlookers, \"Come, everyone, judge for yourselves. Yangyang is my grandson. My son has the right to handle Yangyang's body as he sees fit, doesn't he? My son is Yangyang's father. What law did he break by hiding Yangyang's body?\"","The onlookers were stunned into silence.","Zhang exclaimed in surprise, \"You knew your son hid your grandson's body?\"","\"Of course I knew. I told him to do it. Are you going to arrest me too?\"","The sympathy the onlookers had for the old woman vanished upon hearing her confession.","\"Officers, arrest this old lady quickly. Maybe she killed her grandson herself.\"","\"Exactly, I've never seen such an arrogant criminal.\"","\"This old lady doesn't look like a good person. She has a fierce face.\"","Sun Guixiang was furious at this comment. She pointed at the young man who insulted her. \"My grandson is the lifeblood of our family. Why would I harm him? You little wretch, slandering an old woman like me, do you have no conscience?\"","Fang Rui called for two officers to take Sun Guixiang inside.","With the disruptive woman gone, the onlookers were about to disperse when Zhang stopped them.","\"Please delete the videos you just took. Don't spread them. It's not good for the image. Thank you for cooperating.\"","\"Oh, officers, you're in the right. What are you afraid of?\"","\"Exactly, let's post this old lady's tantrum online and shame her. Officers, don't worry, I'll blur your faces.\"","Zhang's tone became firm. \"Please cooperate with our work.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Deleted, deleted.\"","Zhang made sure everyone deleted their videos and repeatedly emphasized that spreading misleading videos online would result in severe legal consequences.","Once brought to the interrogation room, Sun Guixiang realized she might have said the wrong thing and started crying again. \"Officers, please have mercy on my family. My grandson is gone, and I can't lose my son too... Oh, heavens, you can't treat an old woman like me this way...\"","Fang Rui and Zhang watched her quietly as she cried. When she finally stopped, Fang Rui asked, \"What did you feed Yangyang the night he died?\""]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: The Angel of Death: Divine Water","paragraphs":["“I didn’t feed him anything. It was always Feng Xiaonan who fed him.” When mentioning her daughter-in-law, Sun Guixiang’s anger flared up instantly. She cursed, “My grandson was killed by Feng Xiaonan, that jinx.”","“Why do you say she caused his death?”","“Feng Xiaonan’s horoscope clashes with my grandson’s. She’s the one who’s cursed him. Oh, I’ve been telling my son to remarry, but he wouldn’t listen. Now look, the child is gone...”","Fang Rui interrupted her: “Did you secretly feed the child some ritual water that night?”","Sun Guixiang’s eyes darted around. She denied it, “No! What talisman water? I don’t know anything about it. I didn’t feed him anything!”","“Your son said it was you who fed him.” Fang Rui decided to bluff her.","“Did he say that? He’s grown bold, daring to accuse his own mother,” Sun Guixiang exploded in rage. “Where is Li Ruiqing being held? I’m going to drag him out and beat him to death for being such an ungrateful son!”","“So you admit you fed him talisman water?”","“Officer, this wasn’t just any talisman water. It was specially made by a master. The talisman was burned into ash and mixed with the master’s sacred water. It’s said to cure any illness. I spent thousands of yuan on it. The master told me that as long as the child drank it, no matter what illness he had, it would be cured immediately. That evening, while my daughter-in-law was in the bathroom, I secretly fed the child a big bowl of talisman water.","Soon after, the child showed some reaction—his eyelids were twitching. But a little while later, Feng Xiaonan said the child had stopped breathing. It wasn’t me who killed my grandson. It was the hospital’s fault, or maybe it was Feng Xiaonan’s curse.”","Zhang was furious. “The talisman was drawn with cinnabar. Haven’t you watched TV? They always say in dramas that cinnabar is poisonous!”","“I asked the nurse. The nurse said it was okay to feed him. I asked her, and she said it was fine.”","“Which nurse said that? We’ll take you to the hospital right now, and you can point her out.”","“All the nurses in the hospital wear the same uniforms and look similar. I can’t remember which one it was now.”","Zhang cut her off. “Stop trying to shift the blame to others. If you hadn’t fed the child random things, causing the food to go into his airway, he wouldn’t have died so suddenly.”","“Yangyang wasn’t going to live much longer anyway. Whether he died early or late, it was going to happen. He was lying in bed all day, what’s the difference between that and being dead?” Sun Guixiang muttered.","She knew it was wrong to feed the child random things, but she thought, what if the sacred water worked? Even if it didn’t work and the child died, it wouldn’t be a loss. After all, the child was a vegetable; living or dead, it was all the same. Dying would actually make things easier. Her son could have another child, and she wouldn’t have to worry about not having a grandson.","Zhang was both angered and amused by her brazenness. Sun Guixiang had killed her own grandson and showed no remorse. Such a person was truly terrifying.","When Li Ruiqing learned that the police had discovered Sun Guixiang’s act of feeding talisman water, he admitted his motive for hiding the body: “That’s my mother. I couldn’t just stand by and watch her go to jail. I had to hide the body.”","“You didn’t inform the doctors about this during the emergency treatment?” Fang Rui asked.","Li Ruiqing stammered, “My mom was scared out of her wits. She... she didn’t dare tell the doctors.”","“If you had told them, the child might have been saved!” Zhang exclaimed angrily.","“Even if he was saved, he’d still be a vegetable.” Li Ruiqing muttered softly.","“...” The malicious thoughts between mother and son were eerily aligned. Zhang couldn’t help but wonder if they had intentionally used the talisman water to kill Yangyang.","“It’s all Feng Xiaonan’s fault. If she hadn’t made a fuss, none of this would have happened.”","Fang Rui retorted, “So you could just shift the blame to others and feel justified blaming the hospital or Feng Xiaonan for not taking good care of him?”","“I...”","“Yangyang’s car accident happened in your courtyard, which was surrounded by walls. If that car hadn’t lost control and crashed through the wall, Yangyang wouldn’t have been involved. The driver of the car is the one responsible for the accident. Feng Xiaonan had no responsibility at all. Yet you’re blaming her for Yangyang’s accident. Don’t you think that’s too cruel for a mother who loves her child?”","Li Ruiqing had nothing to say. In fact, he and his family knew Feng Xiaonan was innocent, but they were afraid she would abandon them and refuse to take care of Yangyang. So, they kept piling on the guilt, hoping to make her feel responsible and force her to stay and care for Yangyang.","When Feng Xiaonan learned the truth about her child’s death, she broke down in tears. She had thought of many reasons, even suspecting that her mother-in-law and husband had secretly killed Yangyang. But she never expected it was because her mother-in-law had fed him talisman water.","Right after Yangyang’s accident, her mother-in-law suggested feeding him talisman water to speed up his recovery. Despite her strong objections, she thought her mother-in-law had given up on the idea. She never imagined that Yangyang would still die because of this superstitious practice.","Feng Xiaonan filed for divorce from Li Ruiqing. She couldn’t continue living with such a man. After Yangyang’s accident, he had used work as an excuse to avoid coming to the hospital to care for their child. She had tolerated it for the sake of their child.","Now that Yangyang was gone, there was no point in continuing this marriage.","After work, Fang Rui and Mu Mian headed home together. As they got into the car, Fang Rui noticed Mu Mian’s mood was off.","“Mu Mian, what’s wrong?”","“Yangyang’s death might not have been caused by that bowl of talisman water.”","“What else could it be?”","“When a patient stops breathing or has cardiac arrest, adrenaline is usually injected for emergency treatment. But excessive adrenaline can cause high blood pressure. Patients with cerebral hemorrhage should not be given adrenaline for resuscitation.","But we found that Yangyang’s adrenaline levels were three times higher than normal. Elevated adrenaline can raise blood pressure, which could cause or worsen cerebral hemorrhage.”","Fang Rui asked, “Are you saying this might be a medical malpractice case?”","“I’m not sure. The doctor gave me the treatment records, and it shows that adrenaline wasn’t used during the resuscitation. I don’t know why his adrenaline levels were abnormal. There could be many reasons. It’s very difficult to determine the cause of death in cases like his, with severe traumatic brain injury.”","The next day, Mu Mian shared this information with Yangyang’s attending doctor, who denied it: “During the resuscitation, Yangyang had already stopped breathing. We didn’t use any medication on him.”","“Then why were his adrenaline levels abnormal?”","“Patients with severe traumatic brain injury often have complications that can cause abnormal hormone secretion. It’s difficult to determine the cause of death in such cases. Yangyang’s death could have been caused by multiple factors, making it hard to pinpoint the exact cause.”","Mu Mian insisted, “Can you provide the infusion list?”","“Are you suspecting Yangyang’s death was due to medical malpractice? But I’m certain that none of the medications I prescribed contained adrenaline.”","Mu Mian asked, “But don’t you think Yangyang’s death was rather sudden?”","“Patients with such severe conditions aren’t like ordinary people. They are at risk of death at any moment.” Yangyang’s attending doctor thought for a moment and said, “Our hospital has already formed an investigation team to look into this matter. If there was indeed a medical malpractice, we will provide an explanation to Yangyang’s family.”","Two days later, the hospital’s investigation results came out. The treatment process for Yangyang had followed the medical procedures, and there was no medical malpractice."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Death Angel: The Deceased Elder","paragraphs":["The hospital provided the police with detailed investigation procedures and medical records, which proved that Yangyang's death was not a medical accident.","Yangyang's attending physician had never prescribed epinephrine, and the entire treatment process was very standardized.","This investigation result was within Fang Rui and their expectations.","\"If it's not a medical accident, could it be intentional murder?\" Fang Rui speculated.","Zhang said, \"Someone who could use epinephrine to kill is most likely a healthcare worker, but they had no grudge against Yangyang. Why would they want to kill him?\"","Chen Xue said, \"Didn't they say before that the relative of the hit-and-run driver works at that hospital? Could it be her?\"","\"She wasn't on duty that night. The medical expenses for Yangyang were being paid by the insurance company, so the hit-and-run driver had no motive to kill him,\" Fang Rui replied.","\"There's another possibility,\" Lin Sen said.","\"What possibility?\"","\"There is a type of serial killer who are healthcare workers, and their targets are usually patients. There was a serial killer abroad who was a nurse. During her time working in the hospital, she killed over 300 patients, making her the most prolific serial killer.\"","Mu Mian said, \"Yes, her motive for killing was to free up hospital beds. Her story was even adapted into a movie called 'The Good Nurse,' which is a bit ironic, isn't it?\"","\"To kill patients just to free up beds?\" Zhang exclaimed, \"That motive is too absurd!\"","Lin Sen said, \"Don't try to understand serial killers, because as a normal person, you won't be able to grasp their logic.\"","Chen Xue was puzzled, \"She killed over 300 people, and the hospital never noticed?\"","Mu Mian said, \"Chen Xue, if a professional doctor wants to kill his patient, it's very easy. Many patients die without anyone knowing the truth.\" Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui, \"So having a forensic scientist in the family is very important.\"","Fang Rui smiled helplessly.","Mu Mian then looked at Chen Xue and continued to explain, \"That nurse worked in several hospitals. She wasn't undetected; rather, when she was discovered, it was always considered a medical accident.\"","Chen Xue speculated, \"Could the killer also be someone who doesn't want to waste medical resources, so they targeted comatose patients?\"","\"But this hospital has only had one comatose patient die recently,\" Fang Rui said.","\"With only one victim, we can't determine the serial killer's criteria for selecting targets,\" Lin Sen said, pausing slightly, \"If there really is a serial killer in that hospital, they will likely be tempted to kill again.\"","\"Can't we prevent it in advance?\"","Lin Sen said, \"Have the hospital provide me with the death data from all their departments recently. If there's an abnormal death rate among certain patients, the killer is likely targeting them. Of course, this is all based on the assumption that such a serial killer exists.\"","\"My goodness, then they're like the Grim Reaper, freely taking lives?\"","After the morning meeting, they received another police report. The incident occurred in a village on the outskirts of the city, but the jurisdiction belonged to Jiangzhou City.","Fang Rui and the team drove to the village. It was a poor village, and it was only in recent years, with the help of the government, that a narrow cement road was built. Most of the houses in the village were single-story bungalows, though they were all painted white.","The village was surrounded by large fields, and most villagers made a living by farming or working outside the village.","They parked their car outside a two-story building. The house had two floors, but the second floor was unfinished. It had a large courtyard enclosed by a wall, with several jujube trees planted inside.","They walked into the courtyard, which was crowded with people. The deceased was an 85-year-old lady who had seven children: three sons and four daughters. Her children had also had many children, so their family was quite large. After the old lady's death, her children immediately gathered from all over.","There was a tradition of vigil in this area. If they didn't send the old lady off properly, not only would they be criticized by the villagers, but they would also have bad luck for years.","The people were standing in several groups, and the groups didn't talk to each other. Some had tears in their eyes, while others looked angry, indicating a family with many grudges and not very harmonious.","Seeing Fang Rui enter, the eldest son, Ye Jianzhong, immediately came forward and said, \"Police officer, I called the police. I suspect that my younger brother, Ye Jianmin, and his family abused and murdered my mother with carbon monoxide!\"","\"Why do you say that?\"","The eldest son said, \"When I was young, I was a barefoot doctor and knew some medical skills. After death, the face turns white due to the cessation of blood circulation, but my mother's face was red, and she had vomited before her death. There was also a fire bowl in the room, so I can't help but suspect that my mother was murdered.\"","Ye Jianmin immediately came forward to argue, \"Eldest brother, it's not right for you to do this. I've taken care of our paralyzed mother for two years. If I had bad intentions, could she have lived for two years? You're calling the police on me? You're not showing any brotherly love at all!\"","Ye Meiying, the third child, tried to mediate, \"Big brother, Jianmin couldn't have killed mom, so don't make a fuss. If this gets out of hand, everyone's face will be affected.\"","Ye Jianzhong accused, \"Am I making a fuss? In the middle of summer, why did you put a fire bowl for the old lady? Who would roast themselves in the summer? Jianmin, you didn't want to take care of mom, so you used this method to kill her, right? If you didn't want to take care of her, you could have sent her to my house. As long as I have food, mom won't go hungry.\"","Ye Jianmin muttered, \"The fire bowl wasn't ours! Maybe she wanted to roast herself and got up to do it herself?\"","The eldest son laughed angrily, \"Mom had a stroke and was paralyzed. How could she possibly get up? You're full of lies! Police officer, look at his attitude. If my mom wasn't killed by him, I'll die right here.\"","The fourth child chimed in, \"Jianmin, how you and your wife treated mom, the neighbors have already told us. Today, this matter won't be settled until it's cleared up.\"","\"Oh, you still know that mom was bedridden? In the past two years, who among you visited? Now you blame us for not taking good care of her? You take good care of her, why don't you do it yourself? It's easy to say nice things. Look at what you've done. Now you blame me, blame my wife, where were you before?\"","Ye Jianqing, the sixth child, said, \"Mom's house was given to you. If it wasn't you taking care of her, who would it be? One must have conscience.\"","This house was built by me. I admit that the land use rights belong to my parents, but you didn’t come back to build houses, so my parents could only stay with us. I’ve also said that I can compensate you with money, and we can take turns taking care of mom, but you said no.","“Is this just about the homestead? Mom also took care of your kids for so many years!”","Mu Mian, seeing them argue without end, tried to interject several times but couldn't interrupt them. She looked at Fang Rui.","\"Where is your mother's body?\" Fang Rui asked loudly.","The eldest son led them to a low house behind them, pushed open the wooden door, and said, \"My mother's body is inside. She lived here before her death. Jianmin, this is how you took care of mom, letting her live in such a place!\"","This house was originally a firewood house, converted into a room. The walls weren't painted, the ground was uneven and hadn't been paved with cement, and there was only one window, making it poorly lit and ventilated.","As soon as Fang Rui and the others entered, they smelled a strange odor, a mix of excrement and mildew.","The room was surprisingly tidy, perhaps because the old lady had almost nothing except a cabinet. Next to the old lady's bed was a fire bowl with some unburned charcoal."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: The Angel of Death: The \"Murderer\" Who Was Filial","paragraphs":["The elderly woman had already been dressed in traditional Chinese funeral attire. Her cheeks were flushed, her lips shriveled and cherry-colored, and her body was stiff.","Mu Mian lifted her eyelid. The old woman had suffered from severe cataracts during her lifetime, and her eyes were cloudy, so Mu Mian couldn't observe the condition of her eyeballs.","Mu Mian pressed her skin, and soon redness and swelling appeared. This suggested that she might have died from severe carbon monoxide poisoning.","The old woman's body had multiple bedsores, and her skin was ulcerated in several places, emitting a foul odor.","Mu Mian pried open the deceased's mouth and found a coin inside. Mu Mian asked in confusion, \"Why did you put a coin in her mouth?\"","It's our custom. It's called 'han kou qian' (literally \"mouth coin\"), which means putting a coin in the mouth.","\"Remove it!\"","\"You'll have to help us put it back later.\"","Mu Mian then examined the deceased's mouth and found a thick, oily substance inside.","Mu Mian asked angrily, \"What did you feed her?\"","\"It's cooked muzi oil. It's our custom that when an elderly person is about to pass away, they must be fed this. This way, they can leave smoothly.\" Ye Jianzhong explained.","Mu Mian said, \"So this is 'sending off the dying oil'?\" Typically, elderly people near death have difficulty breathing and rely on mouth breathing, so they gasp heavily. This oil, when swallowed, could block the airway and accelerate their death.","\"...\"","\"How did you determine that she was about to pass away?\"","Ye Jianmin, the fifth brother, said, \"I was the one who sent my mother off. At that time, only my daughter and I were there. My mother's throat kept making gurgling sounds. I heard that's what happens before the elderly pass away, so I quickly fed her this oil. Soon after, she passed away.\"","Ye Jianzhong angrily retorted, \"It must be because of something you did. How could Mother pass away without waiting for us to return? She hadn't even seen her great-grandchild yet! If it weren't for your tricks, Mother would have held on until we got back!\"","This was what angered Ye Jianzhong the most. His fifth brother had deprived him of the chance to see their mother off, and he would surely be ridiculed by the villagers.","\"What's so great about a great-grandchild? Will the great-grandchild come to her bedside to take care of her?\" Ye Jianmin's wife said sarcastically. \"It's better to have a granddaughter. At least a granddaughter would visit her grandmother every day and talk to her.\"","Ye Jianzhong instantly exploded, \"This is a matter of the Ye family. What right does a woman from another family have to speak? Ye Jianmin, your wife really needs to be disciplined.\"","Ye Jianmin's wife wasn't afraid of him and retorted directly, \"Yes, I'm an outsider. But when you forced me to take care of your mother, I wasn't an outsider anymore? You Ye family members are all useless, always fighting within the family. With so many of you, you couldn't even take care of an elderly mother. I'm ashamed for you!\"","\"Stop arguing,\" Ye Yu, Ye Jianmin's daughter, suddenly shouted. \"You argued when Grandma was alive, and you're still arguing after she's gone! Can't you be quiet for a while and let Grandma leave peacefully? Grandma didn't want to hear you talk!\"","Ye Yu, who was in sixth grade, was very sensible, but her eyes were swollen from crying. She had been raised by her grandmother and had a deep bond with her.","Ye Meiying patted her head and scolded, \"Adults are talking. What right does a child like you have to interrupt? Ye Jianmin, look at how you're raising your daughter. She has no manners!\"","\"My daughter visits her grandmother every day. She's more filial than you, the daughter. You have no manners. Grandma used to love you the most, but after she became paralyzed, did you ever take care of her for a single day? You're not even as good as my daughter, the granddaughter!\"","\"I'm a daughter. It's not my responsibility to care for the elderly. That's the sons' job.\"","Seeing that they didn't stop but instead argued even more fiercely, Ye Yu covered her face and ran out.","Wang noticed several clear fingerprints on the brazier. They found a box of charcoal in the room, and there were also fingerprints on the box.","Mu Mian took out a body bag. The old woman's children, hearing the sound of the zipper, stopped arguing and asked, \"Miss, what are you doing?\"","\"We need to take the deceased's body back for an autopsy,\" Mu Mian said.","\"No way!\"","The eldest brother, Ye Jianzhong, said, \"An autopsy? Are you that incompetent, coroner? Can't you prove that our mother died from carbon monoxide poisoning based on these signs? Why do you need an autopsy?\"","\"We're withdrawing the report. Police officers, you can go back now.\"","The group suddenly became united, pulling on the body bag in Mu Mian's hands.","Mu Mian asked in confusion, \"Don't you want to know how your mother died?\"","No one answered. In fact, they didn't really care how their mother died. When they found out about her death, their first reaction was to breathe a sigh of relief, followed by sadness. The eldest brother had reported the case because he had a grudge against the fifth brother and wanted to frame him.","On the matter of not autopsying the body, the seven siblings reached an unprecedented consensus. After some discussion, the eldest brother, Ye Jianzhong, took out a pack of Zhonghua cigarettes and offered it to Fang Rui. \"Police officer, can this matter just be dropped?\"","Fang Rui didn't take the cigarette. \"I'm sorry, but since a report has been filed, we must investigate.\"","\"You can't just report that we made a mistake? Look, police officer, let's have a meal in the city. Can we just drop this matter? You can't autopsy our mother's body. If her body isn't intact, it will affect our family's feng shui.\"","Fang Rui said, \"You're so superstitious. Don't you worry that your mother's ghost will haunt you after her death?\"","\"Who says we're not filial? We didn't visit her because...\"","Fang Rui interrupted their excuses, \"We must take the body back.\"","At this, the old woman's children all stood in front of her bed.","The husband of Ye Meilin, the second sister, was a court clerk. He stepped forward and said, \"Police officers, you need the family's consent to perform an autopsy. We don't agree now. If you forcibly take the body, we will file a complaint. I know your superiors...\"","As the stalemate continued, Wang said to Fang Rui, \"Boss, let's go outside for a moment.\"","Fang Rui and the others went outside. After ensuring that those inside couldn't hear them, Wang whispered, \"Based on the size of the fingerprints, they might belong to a child.\" As he spoke, Wang looked toward the roadside, where Ye Yu was crouching and crying.","Zhang whispered, \"Are you saying Ye Yu lit the brazier? But she had a good relationship with her grandmother. Why would she do that?\"","No one wanted to think ill of a primary school student. But they couldn't figure out why she would do such a thing.","\"Maybe she thought her grandmother was suffering and wanted to help her find relief,\" Chen Xue speculated. Chen Xue's grandmother had passed away after suffering a stroke, and she had often said she wanted to die while lying in bed. Seeing an elderly person suffer so much on the bed, sometimes one might want to help them find relief.","Mu Mian disagreed, \"No, she might have wanted to warm her grandmother.\"","Chen Xue said, \"But it's summer. Who needs a fire?\"","\"Maybe her grandmother had a cold? Elderly people perceive temperature differently from young people. Even in summer, they might feel cold,\" Mu Mian explained.","Everyone agreed with Mu Mian's speculation. Zhang asked, \"So what do we do with this case? Do we still investigate?\"","Fang Rui said, \"Let's not let those people inside know about this for now.\"","The others nodded, \"Understood.\"","Those inside were not easy to deal with. If they found out about this, they might drive Ye Yu to despair. If this was just an accident, Ye Yu was still a child. This incident shouldn't tarnish her life.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian walked up to Ye Yu.","Feeling the sunlight blocked, Ye Yu looked up. Seeing the police in front of her, she shrank in fear, then mustered her courage and said, \"Officer, I killed my grandmother. I didn't mean to. Are you here to arrest me?\""]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: Death Angel: Serial Killer","paragraphs":["Mu Mian asked, \"Why did you light the brazier?\"","Ye Yu wiped away her tears and whispered, \"Last night, Grandma suddenly told me she was freezing all over. I went to tell my parents, but they ignored me. My uncle and my dad haven't paid their share of Grandma's support this month, so they didn't want to take care of her anymore.","Grandma was really cold, shivering all over. I found a brazier and charcoal in her room. I burned the charcoal. It's my fault Grandma died. I had opened the window and placed a bowl of water nearby, but I don't know why it ended up killing her...\"","As Ye Yu spoke, she grew more and more upset. She felt deeply guilty and afraid. She didn't dare tell her family, yet she was tormented by her conscience. So, she decided to turn herself in to the police.","Being locked up in prison seemed better than facing judgment from her own family.","She extended her hands toward Fang Rui and Mu Mian, \"Officer, please take me away. My teacher said that if you do something wrong, you need to be punished.\"","Fang Rui crouched down and comforted her, \"Ye Yu, this was an accident, not your fault. You are a very filial child.\"","Ye Yu became even more upset, \"Sob... I really didn't mean it. I don't know why it happened. I just wanted to make Grandma warm. I should have given my own blanket to Grandma, but I was afraid my mom would scold me. She doesn't allow me to be nice to Grandma...\"","Mu Mian looked down at Ye Yu and said very seriously, \"Your grandma didn't die from carbon monoxide poisoning. She was very sick, which is why she felt cold even in the summer. She died from her illness.\"","Ye Yu's eyes were filled with tears, sparkling, \"Really? But my uncle said Grandma died because of the brazier.\"","Mu Mian replied, \"I'm a forensic scientist, and I'm very professional. Plus, I never lie.\"","Ye Yu said, \"Sister, you're so amazing. You're a forensic scientist.\"","\"Thank you for the compliment.\"","\"When I grow up, I want to become a doctor so that there will be no more paralyzed people in the world. Or maybe a scientist. I want to develop a robot that can take care of patients. That way, when people get old, they will receive thoughtful care. I will also give those robots features so they can chat with Grandma, tell stories, and sing her favorite Huangmei Opera...\"","As she spoke, tears streamed down Ye Yu's face, \"If only I could grow up faster, then I could take care of Grandma and make her happy every day.\"","\"Your dream is very noble,\" Mu Mian praised.","“But I'm not good at math. The nurse said that people who aren't good at math can't become doctors or scientists.”","Mu Mian said, \"Math is simple; you just need to work hard to learn it. Or you can work hard to make money and become rich. Then you can hire doctors and scientists to work for you, and they will fulfill your dreams.\"","Ye Yu stared at Mu Mian, \"How can I become rich?\"","\"I don't know. I don't want to make money, so I haven't researched how to become rich. But there's a shortcut: if you have a very rich father, you can inherit his wealth when he dies and become rich.\"","\"But my dad is poor.\"","\"So you can't take that shortcut. You need to study hard or work hard to make money.\"","“Forensic sister, you’re a very interesting person. Thank you for telling jokes to comfort me.”","Mu Mian turned to look at Fang Rui, her eyes questioning: I wasn't telling jokes; I was seriously comforting her.","Fang Rui smiled helplessly.","He asked Ye Yu, \"You said the window was closed when your grandma died?\"","\"Yes, and the brazier was closer to Grandma.\"","Fang Rui had a sinister but plausible guess. It was likely that Ye Yu's parents had deliberately closed the window. That way, they wouldn't have to take care of the paralyzed old woman anymore. However, there were no surveillance cameras, and no evidence to prove they had intentionally closed the window.","He couldn't even be sure if Ye Yu's story was true. When the old woman died, was the window open or closed?","Ye's family refused to let Mu Mian take the body away. Under Mu Mian's insistence, they agreed to let her take some blood samples from the deceased for testing.","Mu Mian also found a bag of medicine at the head of the old woman's bed. It contained some blood pressure medication and stomach medicine.","Inside the bag was a bottle of ibuprofen. Mu Mian opened the bottle and found a few pills left, but they weren't painkillers. Instead, they were replaced with some light green tablets.","The bag had the words \"Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital\" and the hospital's logo printed on it.","Fang Rui noticed a sign on the wall outside Ye's house. It read: \"Support Unit: Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital; Support Personnel: Zhang Yingying.\"","This village was a poor one. The city had implemented a policy where local hospitals formed support relationships with these impoverished villages, regularly sending medical staff to provide free medicine or home visits.","Fang Rui found Ye Jianmin and asked, \"Does the hospital have medical staff visiting often?\"","\"Not often. Maybe once every one or two months. But they do call frequently to ask about my mom's condition.\"","\"Is it someone named Zhang Yingying?\"","\"There's a female doctor surnamed Zhang and a nurse. The nurse comes often but always wears a mask. They don't talk much with us and leave after a short while.\" Ye Jianmin replied.","The police eventually classified the case as an accidental death caused by heating with charcoal.","As Fang Rui and the others were about to drive away, the funeral home's vehicle arrived at the village entrance.","Accompanied by the wailing of the extended family, the staff loaded the old woman's body onto the vehicle. Her descendants knelt on the cold concrete ground, their tear-filled eyes watching the vehicle leave. This might have been their most filial moment.","Ye Yu didn't cry. She quietly watched her grandma leave. In a daze, she seemed to see her grandma smiling at her.","In the car, Chen Xue sighed, \"This old lady had seven children, struggling to raise them all, but her many descendants couldn't allow her to enjoy her old age.\"","\"Long illness makes even filial children turn cold,\" someone remarked.","Everyone fell silent. This old woman was just one of countless paralyzed elders, enduring not only the pain of illness but also the quarrels and curses from their children, living without dignity.","Back at the bureau, Mu Mian sent the old woman's blood for testing. The light green tablets were also sent for toxicological analysis.","Lin Sen's investigation into the hospital had made progress. He discovered that the death rate in the neurology department of that hospital was 20% higher than the same period last year. Most patients in the neurology department were stroke patients.","Stroke patients naturally had a high mortality rate, mostly elderly with diabetes, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol. They were at high risk, so sudden deaths wouldn't attract much attention.","Lin Sen shared this finding with Fang Rui and Mu Mian.","Mu Mian said, \"Could it be due to the temperature drop? The average temperature in Jiangzhou City this summer was 1.5 degrees Celsius lower than last year. Temperature is also an important factor affecting blood pressure levels. When it's cold, more people have strokes because cold causes blood vessels to constrict and blood pressure to rise. Similarly, the death rate of stroke patients also increases.\"","\"But their hospitalization rate hasn't increased.\"","Mu Mian said, \"So, it's likely that there's a sick killer targeting stroke patients in that hospital.\" She thought of Yangyang and today's deceased, then added, \"More precisely, their target is paralyzed patients.\"","Lin Sen agreed, \"It's possible that they believe their killings are a form of liberation for those patients.\"","Fang Rui said, \"But just relying on data analysis, the hospital won't believe there's a psychopathic killer among their staff, right?\"","\"They might have already lost control. Eventually, the hospital will have to admit there is indeed such a killer.\""]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: Death Angel: The Third Victim","paragraphs":["The next day, Fang Rui noticed that Wang, who was usually punctual, was late for work. Just as he was about to call to ask what was going on, Wang's call came through.","\"Boss, I need to report a crime!\"","\"Aren't you a policeman yourself?\"","\"There's another medical disturbance. They're threatening to attack the doctor and my girlfriend. You need to bring people over quickly,\" Wang's voice suddenly became softer, \"Hey, hey, don't get physical. I'm a police officer. Let's talk this out... Don't push me. I've trained, and if you push me again, I'll fight back...\"","The phone suddenly disconnected.","Fang Rui quickly gathered his team and headed to the Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital. The scene of the disturbance was in Ward 806 of the Neurology Department on the 8th floor of Building 7 in the inpatient department.","Six or seven family members of a patient had cornered two doctors and a nurse inside the ward, with Wang shielding his girlfriend Chen Shu in front of him.","The family members weren't physically attacking anyone, but they were blocking the way, preventing the medical staff from leaving the ward.","Seeing the police arrive, the leader, a young man, said, \"Officer, we're not here to cause trouble. We just want the doctors to explain how my grandfather passed away.\"","Doctor Zhang Yingying, looking helpless, replied, \"Mr. Sun, I've explained this to you many times. This was an unexpected situation, and we're still investigating the cause.\"","\"You're just fooling us. The internet says that your hospital recently caused the death of a little boy, and not only did you not give an explanation, but you also had the police arrest the family members.\"","Fang Rui explained, \"We detained that family member because he hid the body, which hindered our investigation.\"","\"Officer, you must look into this properly. Why did my grandfather suddenly pass away? He was fine the day before, and there's no reason for him to be gone the next day. And the caregiver said it happened while he was on an IV drip.\"","The grandson of the deceased pulled a bottle of liquid out of a bag, \"This is the IV drip my grandfather was on. I was afraid the hospital would tamper with it, so I secretly kept it.\"","Fang Rui put on gloves and placed the bottle into an evidence bag.","Doctor Zhang said, \"They couldn't have tampered with the IV drip to frame our hospital, could they?\"","\"What could we do? We don't know anything about medicine!\"","Fang Rui addressed the family members, \"We will conduct an investigation. But you are not allowed to cause trouble.\"","\"Officer, we'll leave it to you then.\"","Fang Rui learned that the attending doctor of the deceased was Zhang Yingying. Interestingly, the assistant doctor for the Ye family's old grandmother was also named Zhang Yingying.","Fang Rui asked Zhang Yingying, \"Doctor Zhang, do you know Ye Jianmin?\"","Doctor Zhang squinted and thought for a moment, then said, \"No, I don't.\"","“Isn't he one of your assisted individuals?”","\"Oh, you mean him. Yes, I know him.\"","\"His mother passed away, do you know that?\"","\"Is that so? It's been a busy half-year, and I haven't been to his place much.\"","Mu Mian examined the body of the deceased. The patient had been staying in the intensive care unit, where three elderly patients, all bedridden, were cared for by caregivers.","The deceased was named Sun Guanghua, who had been bedridden for years. He was emaciated, with sunken cheeks and lips, and his skin was covered in age spots. The sheets and blanket were wet—he had sweated profusely before his death.","From the external features of the body, Mu Mian could not determine the cause of death.","Mu Mian requested to take the body back for further examination, but the family of Sun Guanghua firmly refused.","\"No, you can't dissect my father's body. It's very disrespectful to him.\" Sun Guanghua's son blocked the way.","Mu Mian said, \"Without dissecting the body, I can't determine the exact cause of death.\"","\"Aren't you a forensic doctor? Can't you do that?\" Sun Guanghua's son looked at Fang Rui, \"Officer, this young lady is too inexperienced. You should get an older forensic doctor!\"","Doctor Zhang said, \"Even if you brought Song Ci (a famous historical forensic doctor) here, it wouldn't help! Without dissecting the body, there's no way to know the cause of your father's death.\"","The family members of Sun Guanghua huddled together and whispered for a while, then Sun Guanghua's son came forward and insisted, \"I don't care. My father's death was definitely caused by the hospital, but you are not allowed to dissect his body!\"","The family members surrounded the bed, shielding the body and firmly preventing Fang Rui and his team from getting close.","Mu Mian compromised, \"Then can we take the body for an MRI? I also need to draw blood samples for testing.\"","\"That's fine! Forensic doctor, you must help us find the real cause of my father's death!\"","Doctor Zhang said, \"Mu Mian, I can accompany you for the investigation.\"","\"Okay.\"","After Mu Mian and Chen Xue left, Fang Rui and his team questioned the caregivers. The three elderly patients in the ward were all cared for by male caregivers.","Sun Guanghua's caregiver said, \"At around three in the morning, Mr. Sun suddenly started sweating profusely. I called the nurse, who took a long time to arrive. Then she went to get the doctor. Doctor Zhang wasn't on duty that night; it was another male doctor. He took a look and said to check the blood sugar and do a blood test to see what was going on. The nurse said the blood sugar was very low, so she changed the IV drip. Then, while Mr. Sun was on the drip, he fell into a coma and soon stopped breathing.\"","The other caregivers also said, \"Mr. Sun's blood sugar had always been normal before, but it suddenly dropped like that last night, which was quite strange.\"","Wang said, \"Sun Guanghua's children are quite filial. They've never given up on his treatment despite him being bedridden for so many years.\"","The caregivers chuckled but didn't respond.","Wang felt there was something special in their laughter and asked, \"Did I say something wrong?\"","One of the caregivers whispered, \"Officer, you're thinking too highly of people. This old man's retirement salary is over fifteen thousand yuan, and most of the medical expenses are covered by insurance. After deducting the four thousand yuan for the caregiver, the rest is split among his children.\"","Wang was stunned.","\"These old people are kept alive by medication. If the respirator and drugs are stopped, they usually don't survive more than a day. But their children still desperately try to keep them alive. Is it because of their conscience? No, it's for the benefit. If these old people left behind an inheritance, they'd be gone by now!\"","Leaving the ward, Wang sighed, \"Alas, human nature can't withstand the test of interest.\"","With Doctor Zhang's help, Mu Mian and her team were able to use the green channel and quickly completed various tests on the body.","They then returned the body to the ward.","In the corridor on the 8th floor, a middle-aged male doctor saw Chen Xue and paused, suddenly calling out to her, \"Xiao Xue, why are you here?\"","Doctor Zhang addressed the man, \"Director Chen.\"","Chen Xue didn't respond.","Director Chen looked awkwardly at Chen Xue for a moment before leaving.","Doctor Zhang asked, \"Chen Xue, are you related to Director Chen?\"","Chen Xue shook her head, \"No, I have no relationship with him. I don't know him.\"","\"Alright.\"","After returning the body to Sun Guanghua's family, Mu Mian and Chen Xue sat on the chairs in the corridor, waiting for the test reports.","Mu Mian whispered, \"Chen Xue, why did you lie just now?\"","Chen Xue laughed helplessly, \"Was it that obvious?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Mian Mian, that man is my father, but he cheated on my mother and abandoned our family. I hate him. So I didn't want others to know about our relationship.\"","\"Alright, I'll keep it a secret for you.\" Mu Mian thought for a moment and comforted her, \"He's very unfortunate because he lost a very excellent forensic doctor as a daughter.\"","\"Mian Mian, thank you for comforting me. But he doesn't think I'm excellent. When I was little, I wasn't a good student, and he often said I didn't seem like his daughter. He said my mother's inferior genes ruined his superior genes, and his child should have been a genius.\" Chen Xue spoke calmly.","Later, Chen Xue worked very hard to study. She thought she had become good enough, but when she met Mu Mian, she realized the gap between ordinary people and geniuses. However, she didn't envy Mu Mian, because Mu Mian was also working hard to be normal.","\"He's not a good father!\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Chen Xue, you need to forget what he said.\"","\"I'll try to forget.\""]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: The Angel of Death: The Suspect","paragraphs":["During the morning meeting, Mu Mian reported the autopsy results of the deceased, Sun Guanghua.","\"The cause of Sun Guanghua's death was an intentional injection of insulin, which interacted with other medications in his body, causing a disruption in his blood sugar levels,\" Mu Mian paused and explained, \"However, the deceased did not have diabetes, and no doctor had prescribed insulin for him.\"","Mu Mian continued, \"We detected insulin in the IV bottle provided by the deceased's family, and the concentration was not low.\"","Fang Rui suggested, \"In that ward, there is a patient with diabetes. Could it be that the nurse mixed up their medications?\"","Chen Xue rebutted, \"Although insulin can be administered intravenously for short-term use, hospitals rarely do so. It is usually injected subcutaneously.","We investigated and found that the other patient in the ward receives insulin subcutaneously, so the probability of a medication mix-up is very low.\"","Zhang sighed, \"So, is this a medical accident or intentional murder?\"","Dr. Zhang Yingying, Sun Guanghua's attending physician, was shocked when she learned the cause of his death: \"I never prescribed insulin for him. How could there be an abnormal amount of insulin in his body?\"","\"What medications did you prescribe for him?\"","Dr. Zhang printed out the medication list and handed it to Fang Rui and Mu Mian.","\"Who was the nurse responsible for administering medications to Sun Guanghua that night?\"","\"Li Xiaolan. We were afraid the family might cause her trouble, so we've had her on leave for the past few days. Do you need to question her? I can call her in.\"","Dr. Zhang added, \"But this incident probably has little to do with Li Xiaolan. The intravenous medications are centrally prepared and delivered by the Intravenous Medication Preparation Center. If there's a problem, it's their responsibility. Officers, you should investigate them first.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang then went to the Intravenous Medication Preparation Center to gather information.","The pharmacists there felt wronged: \"We prepared the medications according to the doctor's prescription. The entire preparation process was error-free, and insulin would not have been included. Insulin is rarely administered intravenously; we wouldn't make such a basic mistake. There are surveillance cameras here, so feel free to check.","Could it be that the medications were tampered with during transport to the inpatient department? Or perhaps they were switched at the nursing station.\"","The issue was once again pushed back to the inpatient department.","Dr. Zhang speculated, \"Could it be that the patient's family injected him with insulin and then added it to the IV bottle, deliberately framing the hospital to demand compensation? Insulin is not a controlled drug and is easy to obtain. What if the family staged this themselves?\"","Fang Rui rebutted, \"When the patient died, his family was not in the hospital; it was the caregiver who was taking care of him.\"","\"Then could it have been the caregiver...?\"","Fang Rui interrupted, \"If the patient died, the caregiver would lose his job and have to find a new employer. What benefit would that bring him? There are other caregivers in the ward; if he tampered with the medications, it would be easy to get caught.\"","Fang Rui and his team had already investigated this caregiver. He had cared for many bedridden patients and was a professional with a good reputation. Most of the patients he cared for died naturally after their families decided to stop treatment. Therefore, the caregiver had little motive or possibility of committing murder.","This caregiver was also unlikely to be the serial killer, as he had only cared for this one patient in the past six months.","Dr. Zhang had nothing more to say.","Fang Rui then asked, \"Who was the nurse that accompanied you to Ye Jianmin's home for the house call?\"","\"Li Xiaolan. What does this have to do with Ye Jianmin?\" Dr. Zhang was puzzled. She didn't understand why Fang Rui kept mentioning that impoverished patient.","\"Please call Li Xiaolan in; we have some questions for her.\"","Dr. Zhang asked the head nurse to call Li Xiaolan and have her come to the hospital to cooperate with the investigation.","The hospital also immediately initiated a medical accident investigation.","Fang Rui then questioned Nurse Chen Shu, who was the girlfriend of Xiao Wang, and they had met during a previous dinner gathering.","\"Captain Fang, Forensic Doctor Mu,\" Chen Shu greeted Fang Rui and Mu Mian warmly.","She was a lovely girl with big, beautiful eyes and a cheerful demeanor, often smiling. Mu Mian had a good impression of her.","Fang Rui asked, \"Nurse Chen, were you responsible for patient 18?\"","\"Yes. Li Xiaolan and I are in the same team and we rotate shifts. This week, I worked the day shift, and she worked the night shift,\" Chen Shu replied.","\"How is Li Xiaolan's work performance?\"","Chen Shu said, \"She has a great personality, is outgoing, and very talkative. She's very patient with patients, and she gets along well with the caregivers and patients in the ward.","It's just that she can be a bit careless. She once almost caused a medical accident by taking the wrong medication, and the head nurse caught it. She was reprimanded for that. If she weren't the director's relative, she would have been fired long ago.\"","Other nurses also complained that Li Xiaolan's work performance was poor and that she often received complaints.","The head nurse said, \"Last time, she was supposed to draw arterial blood for a blood gas analysis, but she missed the artery five times in a row and was scolded by the patient's family. She's always causing trouble; she's just not very reliable.\"","Chen Shu tried to defend her, \"That patient was very old, and his veins were hard to find. It's not entirely her fault.\"","\"Well, how come we can find them? She just doesn't have the ability. This time, she injected insulin into a patient whose blood sugar was already low. What's the difference between that and intentional murder?\"","The hospital set up a special office for Fang Rui and the medical accident investigation team to conduct their interviews.","Li Xiaolan was a young nurse, having graduated only a year ago. Upon hearing that the police wanted to question her, she was panic-stricken.","She explained tearfully, \"Officers, I don't know what happened. He just suddenly... I immediately called the on-duty doctor...\"","\"Describe the situation at that time.\"","\"That night, around three o'clock, the caregiver suddenly pressed the call button, saying the patient was showing abnormal symptoms. I immediately went to get the on-duty doctor. The doctor said to check his blood pressure, blood sugar, and draw blood for a routine test. After checking his blood sugar, I found it was very low. The doctor said to give him some glucose, so I did as instructed.\"","The on-duty doctor confirmed, \"Yes, that's what I said, but who knew she would be so stupid as to add insulin to the IV bag.\"","\"No, I didn't add insulin! I'm not that clueless. The patient was already hypoglycemic; why would I give him insulin? Besides, the doctor didn't prescribe it, so where would I get the insulin to add? Someone must be framing me!\"","The on-duty doctor rolled his eyes, \"That's not certain. You've made basic mistakes more than once. What stupid thing haven't you done?\"","Li Xiaolan cried aggrievedly, \"I was just out of school then; you didn't teach me properly, so how could I not make mistakes? I rarely make mistakes now.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Are there any other people who could have access to the IV bag?\"","\"Any nurse in the nursing station could.\"","The police investigated the hospital's medication delivery process. The preparation center would prepare the medications for the day by around nine in the morning and deliver them to the nursing station.","The prepared medications were stored in a room at the nursing station, where any nurse could access them. This means that all the nurses in that department had the opportunity to tamper with the medications."]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Death Angel: The Culprit Revealed","paragraphs":["After returning to the station, Fang Rui convened a case analysis meeting.","Fang Rui analyzed, \"This doesn't seem to be a medical accident but a murder. The hospital's medication process is very standardized, so it's unlikely they would make such a basic mistake as pouring insulin into an IV bottle.\"","Zhang said, \"So Lin Sen was right; there really is a serial killer in the hospital. If it weren't for the patient's family making a big fuss, this case wouldn't have come to light.\"","Lin Sen, displeased, corrected, \"Please replace 'guessed' with 'analyzed.' Otherwise, it makes me seem very unprofessional.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui said, \"I don't think Li Xiaolan is the murderer. The killer wouldn't be so foolish as to target a patient during their own shift.\"","Zhang agreed, \"And Li Xiaolan has poor psychological resilience. Such a person wouldn't be able to become a serial killer.\"","Mu Mian said, \"Insulin can be purchased online and at pharmacies, so it's difficult for us to trace the source of the drug. However, adrenaline is a controlled substance. If Yang Yang's death is also connected to this killer, then she must have stolen adrenaline meant for someone else. Following this lead, we might be able to catch the killer.\"","Fang Rui agreed, \"And since Yang Yang was hospitalized in the neurosurgery ward on the sixth floor, if the killer tampered with the medication, they would have had to go to the nurses' station there. We can check the surveillance footage to see if any nurses from other departments visited the nurses' station on the day Yang Yang died.\"","Fang Rui thought of Grandma Ye and added, \"Could the killer also have been to the Ye household?\"","Chen Xue said, \"It's possible! Ye Yu mentioned that her grandmother suddenly felt very cold that night. Could it be that the killer gave her some kind of drug, causing her to feel that way? The carbon monoxide poisoning was an accident, which just happened to cover up her crime.\"","Mu Mian said, \"The deceased's blood showed no abnormalities; she died from carbon monoxide poisoning. However, that light green pill is a bit suspicious. Its composition is still being analyzed. We'll discuss it further once we have the results.\"","Fang Rui decided to divide the investigation. Mu Mian and Chen Xue would look into the hospital's adrenaline usage; Li and the others would check the surveillance footage.","Fang Rui and Zhang drove to the Ye household. Ye Jianmin was out working in the fields, leaving only his daughter, Ye Yu, at home.","Zhang asked, \"Ye Yu, do you recognize the nurse who often came to your house to treat your grandmother?\"","Ye Yu looked at Fang Rui and Zhang. After thinking for a moment, she nodded, \"I recognize her.\"","\"Is it her?\" Fang Rui showed Ye Yu a photo of Li Xiaolan.","\"Yes, it's her.\"","\"Are you sure?\"","Ye Yu nodded.","At that moment, Ye Jianmin returned. Seeing the police again, he was a bit annoyed, \"Officers, why are you here again?\"","\"Was the nurse who often visited your home her?\"","\"No, she only came once. The nurse who came frequently was someone else. That nurse had bigger, rounder eyes, very beautiful eyes, not her!\"","Li Xiaolan had single eyelids and puffy eyes, making her eyes smaller than normal.","Fang Rui showed Ye Jianmin photos of all the nurses from the neurology department, \"Mr. Ye, can you identify which nurse it was?\"","Ye Jianmin carefully examined the photos and immediately shook his head, \"They all look the same to me; how can I tell? That nurse always wore a mask, so I can't remember her face, just that her eyes were big. You should ask my daughter; she definitely knows. She was quite close to that nurse.\"","Hearing Ye Jianmin's words, Ye Yu looked down at her toes, visibly flustered, as her earlier lie had been exposed.","Zhang handed Ye Yu a chocolate and crouched beside her, softly saying, \"Can you tell the police uncle who the nurse sister was? We need to find her urgently. Here are some photos; can you help us identify her?\"","Ye Yu didn't take the chocolate and remained silent.","Ye Jianmin kicked her, \"Are you mute? I'm asking you something; answer them!\"","Fang Rui glared at him, \"What are you doing kicking a child? In front of the police, you dare to abuse your child?\"","\"Oh, I was just in a hurry. This child has a strange temper; if I don't hit her, she won't tell the truth.\"","Ye Yu still didn't speak. After a few seconds, she extended her finger and pointed to a photo of one of the nurses.","The nurse was named Zhang Shan.","Zhang said, \"Ye Yu, thank you.\"","On the way back, Fang Rui drove, while Zhang analyzed the photos, \"It seems Zhang Shan's involvement is quite suspicious.\"","\"It's not her.\"","\"Boss, are you saying Ye Yu was lying to us?\"","\"Ye Jianmin said the nurse's eyes were bigger than Li Xiaolan's, but this nurse has single eyelids and not particularly big eyes. Ye Yu probably just pointed at a random photo.\"","\"No wonder she didn't take my chocolate. But why didn't she tell the truth? She doesn't even know why we're looking for that nurse.\"","\"Maybe she does. So she's protecting that nurse.\"","\"Should we go back and press Ye Yu for more information?\"","Fang Rui said, \"If she doesn't want to speak, pressing her won't help.\"","Zhang suddenly had a theory, \"Could it be that the nurse incited Ye Yu to use the charcoal method to kill her grandmother?\"","\"It's possible.\" Fang Rui recalled that when Ye Yu confessed to them, she specifically mentioned opening the window and placing a bowl of water, indicating she knew charcoal burning could cause carbon monoxide poisoning.","Zhang idly flipped through the photos of the nurses, joking, \"Xiao Wang's girlfriend also has pretty big eyes. Among these, her eyes are the most beautiful.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang suddenly fell silent.","Fang Rui said, \"To avoid suspicion, Xiao Wang shouldn't be involved in this case.\"","\"But Chen Shu is such a nice person; how could she be a psychopathic killer? She's usually very kind.\"","\"She's currently a suspect.\"","Mu Mian and Chen Xue questioned hospital staff. Mu Mian discovered a loophole: during emergencies, doctors usually administer adrenaline based on the patient's condition, not using an entire vial. This means that after using half a vial, the remaining portion would be disposed of as medical waste.","The killer likely collected adrenaline this way.","Li's surveillance investigation also made progress. There was a camera in the neurosurgery nurses' station.","The camera captured footage of a nurse entering the medication storage room at 12:31 PM on the day Yang Yang died. She stayed for about two minutes before leaving.","At that moment, Yang Yang's grandmother walked by the nurses' station carrying a thermos. She stopped the nurse and spoke to her. The nurse smiled and answered her question.","The camera then captured the nurse's face. Although she was wearing a mask, Li immediately recognized her.","\"How could it be her?\" Li exclaimed in surprise.","Li hurriedly went to inform Fang Rui and the others of this development.","\"Captain Fang, I've found a suspect,\" Li reported, \"The surveillance footage shows that on the day Yang Yang died, she visited the neurosurgery nurses' station. But she's a nurse from the neurology department; why would she go to the sixth floor? She even spoke with Yang Yang's grandmother.\"","\"Who's the suspect?\"","\"Chen Shu... Xiao Wang's girlfriend.\""]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: Death Angel: The Crime Process","paragraphs":["The police investigation had not yet concluded, but the hospital had already classified Sun Guanghua's death as a medical accident and fired the night shift nurse, Li Xiaolan, while also disciplining the on-duty doctor.","The hospital reached a private settlement with Sun Guanghua's family, who received a substantial compensation payment and decided not to sue the hospital.","However, the case had already been filed and was under investigation, so it wasn't something the family could simply withdraw.","Fang Rui applied for a search warrant to search Chen Shu's home.","Chen Shu rented a one-bedroom apartment near the hospital. The place was small but neat, with minimal furniture. There was a bookshelf filled with medical-related books.","\"Boss, her medical kit contains a lot of controlled substances,\" Zhang reported after finding a medical box under Chen Shu's bed, which was neatly arranged with various medications.","Mu Mian and Chen Xue inspected the box, discovering medications such as epinephrine, insulin, and Demerol, along with many painkillers—likely all stolen from the hospital by Chen Shu.","Mu Mian casually flipped through the books on the shelf. Most were related to neuroscience, not the kind of popular science books one might expect, but filled with experimental data and dry theoretical explanations. One of the books was even written by Mu Mian's father. These complex, theory-heavy books seemed beyond the comprehension of a nurse.","However, the books were heavily annotated with underlined passages and detailed notes, indicating someone had studied them thoroughly. The elegant handwriting suggested the notes were made by a woman.","They also found an album in Chen Shu's bedroom drawer.","As Fang Rui flipped through it, Mu Mian leaned in, noticing the man in the photos looked familiar.","In the photos, Chen Shu and the man were building a snowman in a snowy landscape, looking very happy.","\"Mu Mian, do you recognize this man?\" Fang Rui handed the album to Mu Mian for a closer look.","\"Yes, he's Director Chen from the neurology department,\" Mu Mian replied, glancing at Chen Xue, knowing she had also recognized the man.","Chen Xue showed no emotion, but Mu Mian thought she might feel a bit envious and sad, as Chen Xue's father had never accompanied her to build a snowman.","Mu Mian suddenly felt a pang of sadness herself, as she had never built a snowman with her father either. Back then, she was very afraid of the cold, so when her father and sister built snowmen, she stayed inside the warm house, unwilling to go out. But she watched the snowman from the window; it was beautiful.","\"Fang Rui, the next time it snows, I'll go with you to build a snowman.\"","\"You want to build a snowman too?\"","\"Yes.\"","Zhang chimed in, \"But Jiangzhou City hardly ever snows. You might not get the chance.\"","\"...\"","As they went through the entire album, they noticed another middle-aged woman in the photos. The woman was always seated in a wheelchair, her expression cold and detached.","Mu Mian speculated, \"This woman might be a vegetable.\"","Zhang conjectured, \"Director Chen is probably Chen Shu's father, and this woman is her mother. Her mother is a vegetable. Could it be that because Chen Shu's mother has been a vegetable for so long, suffering from chronic pain, Chen Shu's psychology has been warped?\"","Everyone agreed with Zhang's theory.","While Fang Rui and the others continued their search, Mu Mian quietly comforted Chen Xue, \"She may have a father, but now she's become a twisted killer, while you are an excellent assistant to the forensic pathologist. Chen Xue, you don't need to envy her.\"","\"Mu Mian, I'm not envious. But why am I an excellent assistant to the forensic pathologist, and not an excellent forensic pathologist assistant?\"","\"Alright, I believe you're not feeling too sad. You spotted my language trap, which proves your thinking hasn't been affected by emotions.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian packed all the books from Chen Shu's shelf into evidence boxes, planning to take them back for a closer examination. She wanted to study Chen Shu's notes.","When Fang Rui and Zhang went to the hospital to find Chen Shu, she was in a patient's room, patiently checking an elderly man's back for bedsores.","Seeing Fang Rui and the others, Chen Shu paused but said, \"Can you let me finish my work first?\"","\"Of course.\"","After finishing the examination, Chen Shu told the patient's family, \"He now has bedsores. If not properly cared for, they will worsen.","You must remember to turn him every half hour, preferably while he's lying on his side, and frequently pat his back to promote blood circulation. If you're unsure, you can scan the QR code on the wall for nursing tutorial videos.\"","The family member pocketed their phone and said casually: \"Got it. I've already watched the videos. I turn him often.\"","Chen Shu looked at the old man with sympathy but quickly composed herself, telling Fang Rui and the others, \"Give me a little more time. I need to hand over my work to my colleague.\"","\"Alright.\"","Chen Shu explained the situation to the nurse supervisor and then handed over her duties to another nurse.","She was very thorough, and the other nurse couldn't help but complain, \"Chen Shu, you're only going away for half a day. Why are you acting like you're leaving forever?\"","Chen Shu smiled at her. \"Goodbye.\" Then she said to Fang Rui and Zhang, \"We can go now.\"","Zhang felt a bit sad, though he hadn't interacted much with Chen Shu. He had a good impression of her.","Wang often bragged about his girlfriend in front of them. In Wang's eyes, she was a kind and lovely angel in white. If not for the evidence, Zhang wouldn't have believed Chen Shu could cruelly kill her patients.","In the interrogation room,","Chen Shu sat quietly across from Fang Rui and Zhang, her face still wearing a smile.","Fang Rui asked, \"Chen Shu, why did you go to the neurology ward nurse's station the day Yangyang died?\"","Chen Shu replied, \"I went to borrow something. No one was there, so I went in and took it.\"","Why did you tell Yangyang's grandmother that she could feed Yangyang talisman water?","\"I didn't—\"","Fang Rui interrupted her, \"The surveillance footage captured you talking to Yangyang's grandmother. And Yangyang's grandmother recognized you.\"","Chen Shu's smile faltered, and she stopped defending herself.","\"We found many medications in your home: epinephrine, insulin, and Demerol... Did you use these to kill many innocent elderly people?\"","\"I didn't kill them. I was helping them find release. You've seen it yourselves; those old people lie in bed every day, kept alive by medication, with no dignity. They want to die, but they can't. Their freedom to die has been taken away. I was helping them, helping them find release.\"","\"How can you be sure they didn't want to live?\"","Their desperate, helpless eyes told me. They've lost their ability to move, even to express their thoughts verbally, but their brains are clear. Their eyes begged me to help them find release. They were so pitiful; I couldn't refuse them. Chen Shu said, \"When they died, their faces were filled with smiles. They were thanking me!\"","\"Why did you kill Yangyang?\"","\"Yangyang was my 10th patient. There was no chance he would wake up; his life had no meaning. But if he had lived, his mother might have collapsed from caring for him and committed suicide. That day, as I passed his room, I heard him say, 'Help my mom.' I agreed. I knew that only if he died completely could his mother live.\"","\"I injected epinephrine into his IV bag. Coincidentally, Yangyang's grandmother asked me if she could feed him talisman water. I thought maybe she had also heard his call and wanted to help him find release, so I told her, 'Yes.'","Later, as you've discovered, Yangyang died. It might have been due to a rise in blood pressure causing a cerebral hemorrhage, or it might have been caused by his grandmother's talisman water. It doesn't matter. He died, finding release, and his mother found release, able to live her own life.","You see, I did a great good, didn't I?\"","\"Are you sure you heard Yangyang speak?\" Fang Rui felt Chen Shu's mental state might be unstable, otherwise, how could she hear a vegetable speak?"]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Death Angel: Fabricated Motives","paragraphs":["“It’s not something I heard with my ears, but with my heart,” Chen Shu said, pointing to her chest. “I can empathize deeply with them, so I can hear their inner voices.”","Fang Rui continued, “Did you incite Ye Yu to kill her grandmother by burning charcoal?”","Chen Shu immediately defended herself, “That was an accident. Ye Yu only wanted to help her grandmother stay warm. No one intended to kill her.”","She went on, “Ye Yu’s grandmother had heart disease, and I had originally planned to kill her with digoxin. But when she had her first attack, she begged for her life with all her strength. The scene of her desperate struggle to survive shocked me.","“I couldn’t understand it. She lived such a miserable life, paralyzed in bed, blind, and her children didn’t care for her. Yet, she still wanted to live. I couldn’t comprehend why someone would want to live in such a dehumanizing condition.","“Later, I thought this might be the resilience of life. Or perhaps, for this elderly woman who had endured so much hardship, the pain she was experiencing wasn’t much compared to what she had already been through. She had lived through far more painful and humiliating situations in her life.","“I only kill the elderly who truly wish to die, so I abandoned my plan to murder her!”","Chen Shu’s words were convincing, but Fang Rui sensed something was off.","First, neighbors of Ye Yu’s grandmother had reported that she often complained about her children’s lack of filial piety, saying she was an old, unwanted burden who wished she could die sooner. This suggested that Ye Yu’s grandmother had suicidal tendencies.","Second, if Chen Shu didn’t want to kill Ye Yu’s grandmother, why did she continue to visit the Ye household multiple times under the guise of being from a hospital?","Since Chen Shu had already admitted to her crimes, why would she lie about Ye Yu’s grandmother? Fang Rui speculated that Chen Shu might be trying to protect Ye Yu and cover up the truth.","He exchanged a glance with Lin Sen, who also seemed to think she was lying.","Fang Rui asked, “What about Sun Guanghua?”","“I killed him. I added insulin to his IV bag. His blood sugar was already low, and I used a large dose of insulin, causing his blood sugar to drop rapidly.","“He often told me how much pain he was in, how his whole body hurt, and how he wanted to die quickly. He begged his children to let him return home, but they refused. So, I had to help him ‘go home’ this way.”","After detailing the murder process, Chen Shu smiled. She didn’t feel she had committed a crime.","She asked, “Am I guilty for helping those desperate lives end?”","Lin Sen countered, “How do you know if they were truly desperate, or if they were just temporarily unable to bear the pain and wanted to die? When people are in pain, they may have suicidal thoughts, but once the pain subsides, they might want to live again!","“How do you determine if they are completely hopeless? If you placed a poison and a painkiller in front of them, which do you think they would choose?”","This is also one of the reasons why euthanasia is not yet legalized—because we cannot determine if someone truly wants to die or if they are merely seeking an escape from their suffering.","Chen Shu retorted passionately, “You’ve never taken care of those paralyzed patients, so you don’t understand them! You can’t empathize with them! I’ve taken care of many such patients, I understand their despair and pain.”","Chen Shu calmed herself down and said, “The first person I killed was my grandmother. She had been bedridden for over three years. When I went home during summer vacation, I found her lying on a bed soaked in feces and urine. She was emaciated and moaning in pain. When she saw me, she pleaded with her eyes for me to kill her!","“I didn’t use any drugs or deceptive methods. I smothered her with a blanket when no one was around. No one noticed. Her children’s first reaction was to dress her in funeral clothes and quickly send her body for cremation.","“Later, when I started working in the hospital, I killed many elderly people, but no one ever discovered it. If it weren’t for Ye Yu’s mother making a fuss, it might never have been found out. Even if someone suspected the cause of death, they wouldn’t investigate deeply. In their eyes, the death of these patients was a relief.”","After leaving the interrogation room, Lin Sen said, “She’s probably lying. The story about her grandmother is likely fabricated.”","Fang Rui immediately investigated Chen Shu’s background.","The investigation quickly yielded results.","Chen Shu’s grandmother had passed away when she was just one year old. There was no way she could have killed her grandmother herself.","Chen Shu’s mother had given birth to her out of wedlock. Later, Chen Shu’s mother was involved in a car accident and became a vegetable. Her mother’s household registration had not been canceled, which indicated she was likely still alive.","Zhang wondered, “Why would she fabricate her own experiences?”","Lin Sen analyzed, “I need to correct my earlier assumption. She’s probably not a psychopathic killer. She fabricated her experiences to justify her motives for murder, thereby concealing her true motives.”","“What could her true motive be?”","Mu Mian said, “It might have something to do with those light green pills. We’ve already conducted toxicological tests on those pills, and they’re not poisonous. After analyzing their composition, we found they are quite complex and do not match any existing drugs on the market. It’s a completely new synthetic drug.","“It contains gangliosides and nerve growth factors, which are essential for brain nerve regeneration. It’s reasonable to suspect that this drug is meant to repair brain damage. The people Chen Shu killed were likely test subjects for this drug.”","Fang Rui added, “Previously, the autistic patients at Star Home were also used as test subjects. Could there be a connection between the two?”","Everyone fell silent. If this was true, then Chen Shu certainly wasn’t acting alone.","Fang Rui interrogated Chen Shu again.","Fang Rui asked, “We found a light green pill on Ye Yu’s grandmother’s bed. Did you give it to her?”","“No. What light green pill? I don’t know anything about it. I never gave her such a pill.”","Fang Rui said, “Ye Yu has already told us everything.”","“What did she tell you?” Chen Shu scoffed. “There’s no such thing. What could she possibly tell you? Are you trying to trick me into confessing?”","“The elderly you killed were all used as test subjects for your drug, weren’t they? Who are your accomplices?”","“I don’t know what you’re talking about.”","“What is that drug used for?”","“Fang Rui, I’ve already admitted my crimes and explained my motives and the process. If you continue to press me, you’ll be accused of mistreating a suspect. I’ll hire a lawyer to sue you!”"]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: The Angel of Death: Faith","paragraphs":["Regardless of what Fang Rui and the others asked, Chen Shu remained silent, not willing to say a single extra word.","Fang Rui had no choice but to pause the interrogation.","Zhang suggested, \"Why don't we let Wang go and ask? Maybe Chen Shu will reveal something. I feel like Chen Shu has feelings for Wang. Perhaps if Wang tries to persuade her, it might work.\"","Wang also pleaded, \"I know Chen Shu. She's a very kind person. It's likely that someone forced her to do these things. Let me try to talk to her; she might tell us the truth.\"","Chen Xue couldn't help but pour cold water on the idea, \"Wang, she's using you. She probably doesn't even love...\"","Wang interrupted Chen Xue, \"Let me try!\"","Fang Rui eventually agreed to let Wang see Chen Shu. However, there had to be two people present during the interrogation, so Fang Rui accompanied him.","Chen Xue poured a cup of water and handed it to Wang, \"Chen Shu has been locked up for so long; she might be a bit thirsty.\"","\"Thank you.\"","With heavy steps, Wang followed Fang Rui into the interrogation room.","Chen Shu's eyes were originally dull, but when she saw Wang enter, her pupils slightly dilated. She paused for a moment, then smiled.","Wang handed her the water, \"Have some water.\"","Chen Shu drank a mouthful of water, placed the cup down, and then looked at Wang again. She said, \"Wang Yu, I thought you wouldn't want to see me again.\"","Wang asked, \"Chen Shu, why did you kill those patients?\"","\"I thought you'd first question me about why I lied to you.\"","\"I'm a police officer. In my heart, my job is more important.\"","\"I've said it many times. I wasn't killing them; I was helping them find release. If I were paralyzed in bed, I would have no hesitation in killing myself. People should live freely and with dignity.\"","\"Chen Shu, was someone forcing you to do this? Did they threaten you to kill? Who is the person behind you?\" Wang urgently pressed.","He still couldn't believe that the usually kind and patient Chen Shu, who had such a gentle demeanor with patients, could cruelly kill so many of them.","She was clearly an angel in white, how could she have turned into a devil who kills?","\"No one forced me. Everything I did was voluntary. And I wasn't committing a crime; I was doing something very great and meaningful. The law shouldn't judge me,\" Chen Shu softly said.","\"Chen Shu, you often told me before that although taking care of patients was tiring, and you often got scolded and bullied by their families, when you saw those patients healthy and discharged, you felt your work was very meaningful. Why have you become like this now?\"","Chen Shu looked away, no longer meeting Wang's gaze. \"I'm not kind at all. What you saw before was just my disguise. It's your stereotype that beautified my image. You thought I was an angel in white, but I'm not. There are no angels in this world.\"","\"Wang Yu, I don't like you. Being with you was just to find out how you police solve cases. Understanding your procedures better allowed me to cover my tracks more effectively. I was just using you.\"","Wang stared blankly at Chen Shu, \"So all those promises you made to me, were they all fake?\"","\"Wang Yu, you're such a fool. Are all police officers this naive? But I think your colleagues are quite smart. You should learn from them in the future and stop being so gullible.\"","Wang couldn't help but ask, \"Chen Shu, did you ever like me?\"","Chen Shu looked into Wang's eyes and saw her cold face reflected in his pupils. She said, \"Of course not. There's nothing about you that I could like.\"","Wang looked at her with a sad expression, \"At least, we were friends, right?\"","Chen Shu didn't answer, but her cold expression seemed to answer.","\"Can you tell us the real reason why you killed those paralyzed patients? Is it related to that light green drug? Were you using those patients to test the drug?\"","\"I've already said, I was helping them find release. But since you don't believe me, I have nothing more to say.\"","Wang held Chen Shu's hand and pleaded, \"Chen Shu, you're a very kind person. Why did you do that? What exactly is that light green drug? If you confess now, there's still a chance to make amends. Chen Shu, don't make a bigger mistake.\"","\"You're wasting your time. I will never tell you the truth. Because I can't betray my faith.\"","\"What faith?\"","You're lucky; you've never experienced moments of despair. When you're in despair, you start to have faith. You yearn for miracles to happen.","\"What does that drug have to do with your faith?\"","Chen Shu picked up the cup and drank some water. She looked down at the paper cup and said slowly, \"Wang Yu, I hope you can find someone who truly loves you.\"","\"Wang Yu, goodbye!\"","Chen Shu returned to her silent mode again. No matter how Wang questioned her, she no longer spoke.","After leaving the interrogation room, Wang's nose tingled, and he suddenly felt like crying. He had liked Chen Shu so much, but it turned out everything was fake, even the girl he liked was just a facade of Chen Shu.","Zhang patted his own shoulder and said to Wang, \"Zhang Qiang lends you a shoulder to lean on.\"","Wang leaned on Zhang's shoulder and cried loudly, \"She said she was just using me, that she never liked me. Sob, I even wanted to propose to her and spend my life with her.\"","\"Wang, no criminal would like a police officer. If she liked a police officer, she wouldn't commit crimes. However, in this life, one always has to endure some pain from love. Just try to look at it positively.\"","\"She also called me stupid. Where am I stupid?\"","\"Love lowers your IQ. Look, you even fell for a criminal... Of course, it's not your fault. Her sweet appearance is too deceiving.\"","\"Sob, she wasn't willing to turn over a new leaf for me.\"","\"What else could you expect? She doesn't love you, so how could she turn over a new leaf for you? She didn't drag you down the wrong path, which is already kind to you.\"","\"Zhang Qiang, you're the devil!\"","Mu Mian comforted, \"Officer Wang, I think Chen Shu likes you. It's just that criminals and police officers have no future, so she said she doesn't like you.\"","Wang's eyes lit up as he looked at Mu Mian, \"Really?\"","\"Fake. Do you think Mu Mian knows anything?\" Zhang said.","Wang looked at Mu Mian's pure eyes, untouched by the world's impurities, and cried even louder. Only Mu Mian would think that Chen Shu liked him, because Mu Mian couldn't recognize lies.","Mu Mian whispered to Fang Rui, \"My words were clearly correct, so why did Officer Zhang say I was wrong? Does he have a problem with me?\"","\"Mu Mian, some hurts are better dealt with quickly than lingering.\"","\"I don't understand.\"","\"If Wang knew Chen Shu loved him, he would never forget her in this lifetime. He wouldn't be able to move on from this relationship.\"","\"What happens if he can't move on?\"","\"He would be in pain. He wouldn't be able to love anyone else.\"","\"Why does he have to love someone else?\"","Fang Rui replied, \"Otherwise, he would end up alone in his old age.\"","\"Fang Rui, if I die, would you love someone else?\"","\"No.\"","\"Aren't you afraid of ending up alone in your old age?\"","\"I won't end up alone in my old age.\"","Since Chen Shu refused to disclose the real motive behind the murders, she couldn't be kept in the interrogation room indefinitely. Fang Rui had to send her to the detention center first.","Since Chen Shu wouldn't talk, Fang Rui decided to investigate her computer and phone, hoping to find useful clues by looking into her social connections.","Li carefully inspected Chen Shu's computer and said, \"This laptop is brand new, with almost no usage traces. It seems to be a recently purchased computer. The phone, however, looks like it's been used for a long time.\"","Chen Shu's phone was an older model, and from the wear and tear, it seemed she had been using it for many years.","Her social media had many contacts, mostly her colleagues from the hospital and her college classmates. The chat records were mostly about trivial life matters and complaints about strange patients and their difficult family members at work.","From the chat logs, it is evident that Chen Shu is an outgoing and optimistic person. She frequently comforts her colleagues and actively participates in various activities. She has many friends and is quite talkative. However, she rarely discusses medical topics with others.","Fang Rui focused on the chat logs between Chen Shu and Director Chen.","He noticed that Chen Shu and Director Chen had a distant relationship. They rarely called each other and mostly communicated via text messages, with each interaction being work-related. They didn't seem to have a father-daughter relationship.","Zhang analyzed, \"What exactly is the relationship between Chen Shu and Director Chen? They took a family photo, but based on the chat logs, they don't seem very close.\""]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: Angel of Death: Death by Poisoning","paragraphs":["Li nodded in agreement, \"Chen Shu's mother never married Director Chen. She has always been single. So, what is Chen Shu's relationship with Director Chen? Why do they have a photo together?\"","Chen Xue, who had been lost in thought, suddenly spoke up, \"Chen Shu's mother was Director Chen's first love. She cheated on him, fell for someone else, and left him. But she ended up with the wrong person and got pregnant out of wedlock, giving birth to Chen Shu. Later, Chen Shu's mother was in a car accident and became semi-vegetative. She was completely paralyzed, unable to move, but could still speak and respond to external stimuli. Director Chen, heartbroken for his first love, abandoned his own family to take care of Chen Shu and her mother.\"","Everyone looked at Chen Xue in surprise.","Zhang asked, puzzled, \"Chen Xue, how do you know all this so clearly?\"","Li nudged Zhang, \"Haven't you noticed? All three of them share the surname Chen.\"","Chen Xue sighed, \"Yes, it's exactly what you're thinking. It's a very dramatic story.\"","Mu Mian analyzed, \"Chen Shu's mother must be a patient with severe brain damage. And the patients Chen Shu killed all had varying degrees of brain lesions. Could it be that Chen Shu, in an attempt to cure her mother, made a deal with some medical institution, using these patients as test subjects for experimental drugs?\"","Everyone agreed with Mu Mian's speculation.","Fang Rui added, \"Chen Shu once said that when you're in despair, you start to believe in faith. Could her faith be that medical institution? Does she believe the drugs they're developing can cure her mother?\"","\"That might be why she's cooperating with that institution.\"","\"But what is the name of that institution?\"","The tech team examined Chen Shu's phone and recovered some deleted pictures and messages. The photos were all ordinary scenery shots with no clues. However, they did find something in the chat records.","\"How does Chen Shu know Bai Jing?\" Zhang exclaimed in surprise.","Hearing Bai Jing's name, Fang Rui and Mu Mian exchanged glances. In the case of the Cat Fetus Killer, Bai Jing had allegedly manipulated Chen Hui to exact revenge on her father. Could she be involved in Chen Shu's case as well? Was she manipulating Chen Shu into committing these crimes?","The recovered chat records showed that Bai Jing had once been Chen Shu's friend, but after the medical dispute involving Sun Guanghua's family, Chen Shu deleted Bai Jing from her contacts and wiped their chat history.","From the recovered chats, Bai Jing often arranged to meet Chen Shu at a café called \"Left Bank Coffee.\" The chats were brief, mostly about setting up meeting times and locations, but they had been in contact for over two years.","Chen Xue speculated, \"Bai Jing works at a psychological clinic. Could she have been providing counseling to Chen Shu?\"","Mu Mian countered, \"But Bai Jing isn't qualified to conduct independent psychological counseling. And counseling sessions usually don't take place in public places like cafés.\"","\"Then why did they meet so often?\"","At that moment, Fang Rui received a call from the prison guard escorting Chen Shu.","The guard shouted anxiously, \"Captain Fang, something's happened to the prisoner. She suddenly started foaming at the mouth and convulsing. We're rushing her to the nearest hospital for emergency treatment.\"","Hearing the conversation, Mu Mian gestured for Fang Rui to hand her the phone.","Mu Mian asked, \"Is she having a seizure?\"","\"We don't know. I was about to ask you if she has any medical history.\"","\"First, tilt her head to the side to prevent secretions from causing choking. Is her convulsion severe? Very severe? Then find a spoon or something to put in her mouth to keep her from biting her tongue.\"","\"Got it.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Which hospital are you taking her to?\"","\"Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital.\"","Fang Rui was about to suggest they switch hospitals when the guard added, \"It's the closest one. We've already contacted the hospital.\"","Fang Rui decided not to insist.","\"What happened? What's wrong with Chen Shu?\" Wang asked anxiously.","\"We don't know yet. Let's go to the hospital and see.\"","Fang Rui and the others immediately drove to the hospital, arriving just as the prison van pulled up. The emergency department doctors and nurses were already waiting at the entrance. They lifted Chen Shu out of the vehicle.","Mu Mian noticed that Chen Shu had already lost consciousness. She had foam at the corners of her mouth, and her body was cyanotic. It didn't look like a seizure.","\"She's been poisoned.\"","The doctor asked, \"Did she attempt suicide by poisoning? What kind of poison did she take?\"","The guard replied, bewildered, \"You're asking me? I'm not a doctor. How would I know what poison she took? She just suddenly collapsed like this. I didn't see her take any poison!\"","Unable to determine the exact poison, the doctors followed the standard procedure for treating poisoning and sent her for gastric lavage. However, during the process, Chen Shu stopped breathing.","The doctor declared her death, \"I'm sorry, we couldn't save her. She likely ingested a highly toxic neurotoxin.\"","Wang's eyes welled up with tears. He slowly walked over to Chen Shu's hospital bed, wanting to hold her body, but Mu Mian stopped him.","\"Officer Wang, I'm sorry, but you can't touch her yet. I need to take her back for an autopsy.\"","Hearing the guard describe Chen Shu's symptoms, Mu Mian had already guessed that she might not survive. She had wisely prepared a body bag in advance.","Mu Mian and Chen Xue placed Chen Shu's body into the bag.","\"Officer Wang, you can now hold her body through the bag,\" Mu Mian said.","Wang didn't reach out to hold her. He struggled to suppress his emotions, \"Mu Mian, is Chen Shu really gone?\"","\"Yes. She has been declared brain dead.\"","Fang Rui carefully questioned the guards about what had happened.","The guard escorting her said, \"We don't know what happened. After she got in the van, she didn't eat anything. Then, suddenly, her expression turned pained. We asked her what was wrong, but she didn't answer.","After a while, foam started pouring from her mouth, and her body began convulsing. We realized something was wrong and rushed her to the hospital.\"","The driver added, \"There's surveillance in the van. She really didn't eat anything. Meng was sitting right next to her, watching her the whole time.\"","The guard added, \"When we called for an ambulance, she said, 'It's no use. I'm already beyond saving.'\"","Fang Rui found it strange. Before entering the interrogation room, a female officer had thoroughly searched Chen Shu. She had no dangerous items on her—not even hairpins or necklaces. How could she have been poisoned?"]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Angel of Death: Doubts","paragraphs":["Mu Mian performed an autopsy on Chen Shu's body. There were no obvious external injuries or needle marks on Chen Shu, leading to the preliminary conclusion that she had indeed died from poisoning.","Chen Xue said, \"Mian Mian, don't you think Chen Shu's condition resembles Lin Qianjie's? Could she have also died from ingesting tetramine?\"","Mu Mian agreed, \"I also suspect that tetramine is what poisoned her.\"","However, Mu Mian was puzzled. How could it be tetramine?","Chen Xue wondered, \"Before she entered the interrogation room, a female officer had already searched her and found no poison on her. So how did she obtain the poison and ingest it to commit suicide? The food she ate inside was also provided by our department, so it couldn’t have been tampered with.\"","Chen Xue picked up Chen Shu's clothes and examined them carefully. No suspicious items were found in the pockets. She then untied the hair tie from Chen Shu's hair. The hair tie was made of cotton and showed no traces of hidden poison.","Mu Mian said, \"There are many ways to hide poison, such as concealing it under fingernails, in the ears, or swallowing it in a capsule to delay its effects. Another method is to soak clothing in a poison solution...\"","Chen Xue nodded, \"That makes sense. We need to thoroughly inspect all of Chen Shu's belongings to see if there are any traces of poison.\"","It would take time for the toxicology report to come out. Only after receiving the results would Mu Mian know exactly what poison Chen Shu had ingested and how she had been poisoned.","Chen Shu had eaten lunch and drank two glasses of water at the police station. The disposable utensils she used, which were still in the trash and hadn’t been discarded, were also sent for toxicology testing.","The next day, the toxicology results came out. As Mu Mian and the others had suspected, the poison that killed Chen Shu was tetramine. Traces of tetramine were detected on the collar of the clothes Chen Shu had worn that day; no poison was found on any other items.","\"How could it be tetramine?\" Zhang wondered. \"It’s not easy to obtain. Why would Chen Shu use such a poison to commit suicide?\"","Fang Rui also found it strange, \"Chen Shu had access to so many controlled substances from the hospital. Why didn’t she steal something from there to use for suicide instead of buying tetramine?\"","Mu Mian speculated, \"It’s possible because the drugs available in the hospital aren’t as lethal and could be easily treated. Tetramine, on the other hand, is highly toxic, and even a small amount can be fatal.\"","\"Then how did she bring the poison in?\"","Mu Mian explained, \"We detected tetramine on her collar. If she really did commit suicide, it’s reasonable to assume she soaked her collar in a tetramine solution beforehand, allowing her to evade detection during the search.\"","Li questioned, \"If she wanted to commit suicide, why didn’t she do it earlier? Why wait so long in the interrogation room? Why not kill herself before we arrested her? That way, we wouldn’t have been able to question her at all. The timing of her suicide is strange.\"","Chen Xue countered, \"She didn’t know we had solid evidence against her. If our evidence had been insufficient, she might have walked free. But when she realized we had undeniable proof of her crimes and that she couldn’t talk her way out, she gave up completely.\"","Wang chimed in, \"Chen Shu once told me that people should live freely. She probably didn’t want to be imprisoned, so she chose to take her own life.\"","Zhang added, \"The prison guards also mentioned that Chen Shu told them not to call for emergency help, as she was beyond saving. That suggests she did commit suicide.\"","Fang Rui still had doubts, \"But how did she know we would arrest her at the hospital that day?\"","\"Could it be that she wore clothes soaked in poison every day? If she were arrested, she could use the tetramine to kill herself,\" Li speculated.","With Chen Shu dead, the only way forward was to investigate her social connections for potential clues.","The police examined Chen Shu’s bank accounts. Her transaction history was brief, with deposits only from her hospital salary and no suspicious income.","She had almost no savings, and no cash was found at her home. This suggested that Chen Shu likely wasn’t motivated by money in committing these acts.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to the hospital to speak with Director Chen, but the nurses informed them that Director Chen had gone out of town for an academic conference and wouldn’t return for a week.","Fang Rui managed to reach Director Chen by phone.","\"Officer, what do you need from me?\" Director Chen’s tone was impatient.","\"Do you know Chen Shu?\"","\"Yes, she was a nurse in our department. Why?\"","\"She’s dead. As her family member, could you come to the police station to identify her body?\"","Director Chen replied coldly, \"Who told you I’m her family member? Just because we share the same surname doesn’t mean we’re related. If you don’t believe me, go ahead and run a DNA test to see if she’s my daughter.\"","\"We found photos of you, Chen Shu, and her mother at her home. If you’re not related, why would those photos exist?\"","\"Those are just photos of me with patients and their families. Is there anything else? If not, I have work to attend to.\"","Before Fang Rui could respond, Director Chen hung up.","Zhang complained, \"Director Chen is so irresponsible. Even if Chen Shu wasn’t his biological daughter, she was still his stepdaughter. How can he be so indifferent to her death? Could he have been the one who pushed Chen Shu to harm those patients? Now that Chen Shu’s dead, he’s quick to distance himself.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Chen Shu couldn’t have carried out the drug experiments alone. Medical tests would have revealed abnormalities, so there must be an accomplice within the hospital.\"","Fang Rui wanted to investigate further, but the hospital was uncooperative. They refused to provide patient treatment records and even threatened to file a complaint against the police if they continued to \"harass\" their doctors and nurses.","Zhang sighed, \"Could it be that the hospital collaborated directly with that medical institution, and Chen Shu was just a scapegoat?\"","Fang Rui thought it unlikely that the hospital was directly involved, but he was certain there was an accomplice within the hospital.","Fang Rui investigated Director Chen’s bank accounts but found no unusual income. In fact, Director Chen’s account balance was only a few thousand yuan.","Upon further investigation, they discovered that while Director Chen earned a high income, he owned only an old unit-assigned apartment and had almost no savings.","He spent his money on helping patients, often covering medical expenses for rural patients and volunteering in impoverished areas. Director Chen was not only highly skilled in medicine but also had exceptional medical ethics."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: Angel of Death: The Threat","paragraphs":["During the morning meeting, after learning about Director Chen's deeds, everyone turned their attention to Chen Xue.","Li couldn't help but praise, \"Chen Xue, even though your father failed the family, he was a good doctor.\"","Chen Xue remained silent, feeling somewhat surprised. She couldn't connect the cold and distant father from her childhood with the kind and professional doctor she was hearing about now.","Fang Rui analyzed, \"Although Director Chen's character seems impeccable, Chen Shu once said that this was her faith. So, their motive for doing this must not have been for personal gain but for some higher ideal. Director Chen is still a suspect.\"","\"The Star Home case also involves illegal drug trials. When we investigated, we only traced it back to a shell company,\" Chen Xue added. \"Could these two cases be connected? Could the people behind the shell company have instructed Chen Shu to do this?\"","Zhang sighed, \"What if we investigate further and only end up tracing it back to another shell company?\"","Fang Rui decided to look into the relationship between Chen Shu and Bai Jing.","There were two coffee shops in Jiangzhou City called \"Left Bank Coffee,\" but both owners confirmed that Chen Shu and Bai Jing had never visited their stores.","Chen Shu's chat records showed that half a month ago, they had agreed to meet at a coffee shop. However, surveillance footage from both stores over the past two months showed no sign of them, and there were no payment records from Chen Shu's account.","Fang Rui speculated, \"Could 'Left Bank Coffee' not be an actual coffee shop but a code name they agreed upon?\"","Zhang agreed, \"That's possible! So why did Bai Jing and Chen Shu meet so often? Could Bai Jing have been assigning tasks to Chen Shu? If so, Bai Jing might be a liaison and could know a lot of things.\"","To avoid alerting anyone, they decided not to bring Bai Jing in for questioning but to investigate her privately instead.","Bai Jing's personal records were straightforward. She graduated from Jiangzhou University with a degree in psychology, spent over a year unemployed after graduation, then worked as a social worker in the Ziweili Residential Area for half a year before returning to Jiangzhou University to pursue a master's degree in psychology.","The only notable detail was that her father was the renowned psychologist, Professor Bai.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian drove to the \"Lingxi\" Psychological Clinic where Bai Jing worked.","On the way, Mu Mian said, \"There are suspicious points about Chen Shu's death. Although we detected rat poison on her clothes, there was no saliva on her collar. If she had intended to commit suicide by ingesting poison from her collar, the most convenient method would have been to put the collar directly in her mouth. That would have left saliva traces.\"","\"Could she have soaked the collar in a cup of water?\"","\"There was no rat poison detected in the cup or the lunchbox. Also, I checked the surveillance footage, and her collar wasn't wet.\"","Fang Rui frowned, \"That's strange. If she didn't ingest the poison from her collar, she was likely poisoned by someone else. But there was no poison detected on the utensils. So how did she get poisoned?\"","\"Exactly, it's very puzzling. If she committed suicide, why didn't she just ingest the poison directly from her collar? If she was poisoned by someone else, how did the killer manage to poison her in the police station, and why was rat poison found on her collar?\"","\"Could it be that some of the poison dripped onto her collar when she drank it?\"","Mu Mian frowned, \"But no poison was detected in the cup or on the utensils.\"","Fang Rui suspected that someone within their team might have tampered with the evidence.","Mu Mian worried, \"If Bai Jing is one of the masterminds, could she harm my sister?\"","Fang Rui replied, \"She likely approached your sister with a purpose. Your parents were scientists. Could your sister have their research materials? Maybe that's why Bai Jing got close to her.\"","Mu Mian said, \"It's possible. My father's last research project was on Alzheimer's disease. But my seniors said that since the foundational paper in the Alzheimer's field was fraudulent, all research based on those findings was flawed. Why would Bai Jing want a bunch of flawed research data?\"","Fang Rui felt that Mu Mian wasn't entirely clear about her parents' work.","When they arrived at the \"Lingxi\" Psychological Clinic, the receptionist recognized Mu Mian and greeted her warmly, \"Mu Mian, are you here to see your sister?\"","\"Yes,\" Mu Mian replied.","The receptionist noticed Fang Rui and was slightly surprised, \"Is this your friend?\"","Mu Mian corrected her, \"This is my boyfriend, Fang Rui.\"","Fang Rui greeted her, \"Hello.\"","\"Hello. Mu Mian, I didn't know you had a boyfriend, and such a handsome one too!\"","The receptionist was surprised. It was rare for someone with autism to form normal intimate relationships, so she hadn't expected Mu Mian to have a boyfriend. Still, she was happy for her.","\"Thank you. Sister Feng, I hope you find a boyfriend soon too.\"","\"...I'll try!\" the receptionist said, \"Please wait in the rest area.\"","\"Alright.\"","The receptionist brought them water.","Mu Mian asked, \"Has Bai Jing been coming to the clinic often recently?\"","At the mention of Bai Jing, the receptionist's expression changed, and she said with annoyance, \"Yes, she comes often. It's so annoying.\"","\"You don't like her?\"","\"She's a scheming, manipulative woman who has driven away several counseling assistants. I don't like her much,\" the receptionist, a straightforward girl, complained. \"You should avoid her. She might seem nice, but she's extremely jealous and can't stand anyone doing better than her.\"","\"Did Chen Shu ever come to see her?\"","\"Who's Chen Shu? We don't have a client by that name!\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Does Bai Jing usually behave unusually?\"","\"Unusual behavior? Not really. She just likes to play mind games. But she's clever, and the therapists like her. Our boss especially values her...\"","The receptionist lowered her voice, \"But your sister is smart. She saw through Bai Jing's act and no longer lets her be an assistant.\"","\"Sister Feng.\"","Hearing Bai Jing's voice behind her, the receptionist was startled. She awkwardly turned to face Bai Jing.","Bai Jing smiled at her, \"What were you talking about? I heard my name.\"","\"Nothing... nothing! Oh, I have some work to do. I'll head back now,\" the receptionist said before scurrying away.","Bai Jing smiled at Mu Mian, \"Mu Mian, it's been a while.\" She then looked at Fang Rui, \"Officer Fang, long time no see!\"","Mu Mian and Fang Rui ignored her. First, they didn't want Bai Jing to know they were investigating her, and second, if Bai Jing was indeed involved in the case, they wouldn't get any useful information from her.","Seeing that Fang Rui and Mu Mian were ignoring her, Bai Jing's smile faded. \"Aren't you here to see me?\"","It seemed Bai Jing already knew the police were investigating her. Fang Rui decided to be direct, \"Do you know Chen Shu?\"","\"Yes, we were good friends. I was deeply saddened by her death. However, she made mistakes and had to face the consequences.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Chen Shu didn't commit suicide. She was killed by your people, wasn't she?\"","Bai Jing didn't answer.","\"Is the Star Home incident also connected to you?\"","\"Officer Fang, you've already solved the case, caught the culprit, and established the motive and process. Just close the case. Let it end here,\" Bai Jing said.","\"Will you stop your criminal activities?\"","Bai Jing remained silent.","\"You won't stop. Then our investigation won't stop either.\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian were seated, while Bai Jing stood, looking down at them with a condescending air. \"I've given you a friendly warning. If you don't accept it, then I can only wish you good luck.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"If we continue investigating, what will you do?\"","Bai Jing was momentarily taken aback. \"Why should I tell you?\"","\"If you don't tell us the consequences, how can we decide whether to continue investigating?\" Mu Mian looked at her sincerely.","\"Damn autistic person!\" Bai Jing snorted coldly and turned to leave."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: The Angel of Death: Jiang Miao Group","paragraphs":["Watching Bai Jing's retreating figure, Mu Mian sighed, \"Ah, I really am not good at fishing for information.\"","Fang Rui rubbed his forehead. Could this even be called fishing for information? It was more like straightforward, sincere questioning.","Mu Mian asked, \"Fang Rui, what do you think they'll do if we keep investigating?\"","\"If Chen Shu was killed inside the police station, there must be someone on the inside working for them,\" Fang Rui replied. \"Before we expose the mole, we shouldn't reveal our progress to anyone. Let's pretend we've stopped investigating this case for now and find a way to uncover the mole.\"","Mu Mian speculated, \"Could it be Wang? Did Chen Shu lead him astray? But how could Wang get his hands on rat poison?\"","Fang Rui wasn't entirely sure either. If there really was a mole planted by the mastermind, who could it be? Was it Wang? He had been in the interrogation room and had contact with Chen Shu, making him the most likely suspect. But many people had interacted with Chen Shu that day, and all of them were under suspicion.","Suddenly, Mu Mian had an idea. \"Maybe it wasn't bought but stolen! When Lin Qianjie died, we retrieved a bag of rat poison from Lu Tian's house. Could someone have stolen some of it then? If so, that person must have planned this long ago. Oh no, what if they're planning to poison me? And you too, since you always eat my cooking.\"","\"It's unlikely, but we should be more careful from now on,\" Fang Rui said.","At that moment, Shen Xiyin finished her consultation. She was surprised to see Mu Mian and Fang Rui waiting for her.","\"Mu Mian, why are you here to see me?\"","Shen Xiyin had been very busy lately. The psychology department at Jiangzhou University was conducting a research project: a cognitive ability survey of adolescents in Jiangzhou City. They had designed a series of tests to assess the cognitive abilities of primary and secondary school students and were collecting data.","Basic cognitive abilities included attention, memory, perception, reasoning, and cognitive flexibility. These tests were based on psychological experimental paradigms and had been computerized to improve data collection efficiency, but organizing the data was still a massive task.","Mu Mian asked, \"Sister, why did you stop letting Bai Jing be your assistant?\"","Shen Xiyin replied, \"Because I caught her snooping through my computer. Although there wasn't anything important on it, I don't like people invading my privacy. She crossed a line.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Why would Bai Jing snoop through your computer?\"","\"I suspect someone put her up to it. She wasn't randomly searching through my files; she went straight to a specific folder on my D drive. I tend to store important files there, and only a few close friends know about this habit of mine, but none of them know Bai Jing.\"","Mu Mian pouted, \"I didn't know you had that habit either.\"","Shen Xiyin smiled helplessly, \"That's because you're not interested in my work.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Do you suspect someone you know instructed her?\"","\"Yes, I suspect it was Jiang Yinian. He knows me well. He could probably guess my computer password, and he knows where I like to store important files.\"","Mu Mian added, \"I know your password too—it's my initials plus your birthday.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"What kind of information would Jiang Yinian want from you?\"","\"I'm not sure. I don't have much research data. I focus on psychotherapy and rarely engage in research. The only research-related material I have is part of the data from our cognitive ability survey. Other than that, there's nothing significant.\"","Fang Rui probed, \"Could it have something to do with your parents' research?\"","Mu Mian countered, \"Jiang Yinian was Dad's favorite student. He probably knows more about Dad's work than you do, Sister. What could he possibly get from you?\"","\"My father was developing a drug to treat Alzheimer's disease, but their research failed. At the time, they couldn't figure out why. A few years ago, the foundational paper on Alzheimer's was exposed as fraudulent, and I think that's why their research failed,\" Shen Xiyin sighed. \"I never imagined my father and his team would waste over a decade because of a fake paper.\"","Mu Mian, worried Fang Rui wouldn't understand, explained further, \"The Alzheimer's research community widely accepts the 'amyloid hypothesis': Alzheimer's is caused by the accumulation of Aβ plaques. Based on this hypothesis, my father's team developed a drug that could repair a certain protein, reduce Aβ*56 deposits, and slow the progression of Alzheimer's. But since the paper supporting this hypothesis was fraudulent, my father's drug failed in clinical trials.","Of course, my father wasn't the only one unlucky. Almost every Alzheimer's researcher wasted over a decade of their lives because of this flawed hypothesis. This shows how important honesty is in the scientific community. I, for one, am very honest.\"","Fang Rui chuckled, \"So that's why you've never been good at lying?\"","\"I've gotten a little better now because the real world requires a lot of white lies.\"","Shen Xiyin added, \"A friend told me that Jiang Yinian's Jiangmiao Group has replicated many expensive foreign drugs over the years. They've been sued multiple times by foreign pharmaceutical companies, but they've managed to evade legal consequences by tweaking the formulas and adding traditional Chinese medicine components. Many companies haven't been able to hold them accountable.\"","Mu Mian said, \"Jiang Yinian once told me that innovation is the most important thing in research, and copying others' work is shameful. Why would he do something like this?\"","\"Maybe, for him now, making money is more important,\" Shen Xiyin said sarcastically.","Fang Rui looked into Jiang Yinian. He was the largest shareholder of Jiangmiao Group, but the company's operations were managed by professional executives.","Jiang Yinian had invested heavily in building a private laboratory, hiring many young medical graduates from prestigious universities, but he had never publicly announced any research findings.","Jiangmiao Group was founded by Jiang Yinian's cousin, who had been a criminal psychology expert before inheriting the family fortune and switching careers to establish the medical group. A few years later, he and his wife passed away, and Jiang Yinian inherited all their assets.","In addition to private hospitals and pharmaceutical companies, Jiangmiao Group frequently funded various research projects and collaborated with universities, giving it a good reputation and significant influence.","Fang Rui increasingly felt that Jiangmiao Group was shady. He even suspected that Jiang Yun's death had been orchestrated by Jiang Yinian so that he could gain control of the Lin family's assets as Lin Qianyan's guardian.","Fang Rui asked Mu Mian, \"What kind of person is Jiang Yinian?\"","Mu Mian thought for a moment and said, \"Dad said he was a genius. He loved research and once said he would give everything for his work. But he's changed now. He probably loves money more.\" Her tone was tinged with regret.","Fang Rui realized that investigating Jiangmiao Group wouldn't be easy. First, there was no legitimate reason to do so, and second, if they alerted the company, they might destroy all evidence immediately.","For now, their priority was to uncover the killer of Chen Shu—the mole within the police station."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: Rainbow Mouse","paragraphs":["The next day at work, Mu Mian walked into the office carrying a beautifully wrapped box.","\"Mu Mian, who sent you a gift?\" Chen Xue asked curiously, eyeing the box.","Mu Mian placed the box in front of Chen Xue and said, \"Chen Xue, open it. We're about to have a group of adorable little companions.\"","\"Adorable little companions? And a whole group of them?\"","Chen Xue had a bad feeling about this. She slowly opened the box, and as soon as she saw what was inside, she let out a loud scream.","\"Ah, Mu Mian, why did you bring a bunch of white mice to work? I hate white mice!\"","Inside the box was a glass container with several white mice curled up inside, making little \"squeak, squeak\" noises.","\"Chen Xue, you're a medical student. How can you be afraid of white mice?\" Mu Mian said, picking up the box and placing it on her desk to prevent the mice from being frightened by Chen Xue.","Chen Xue crossed her arms and said, \"I'm not afraid. I just dislike all living rodents. If I had to dissect them, I’d be fine with that.\"","Mu Mian picked up one of the white mice and held it in her palm. \"Chen Xue, look, this one is really cute. Don’t worry, it’s not aggressive anymore. It’s a bit of a silly mouse. Can you guess why it’s become so silly?\"","\"Unless it’s a corpse, don’t let them appear in front of me!\"","Mu Mian sighed sadly. \"Alright. Poor little guys, you’ve been banished by a beautiful but mouse-hating forensic sister. Sigh, I’ll have to find a new place for you.\"","Chen Xue sensed trouble. \"Mu Mian, you’re not planning to keep them long-term, are you? Why do you suddenly want to keep pets?\"","\"Of course. I’ve adopted them, so I’m responsible for them. But they’re not pets—they’re test subjects.\"","Mu Mian carried the box to Fang Rui’s office.","Only Fang Rui and Zhang were in the office.","Zhang’s suspicion of being an undercover agent had been preliminarily ruled out.","First, because when the rat poison was brought back, Zhang was one of the few who hadn’t come into contact with it, so he had no opportunity to steal it. Second, during Chen Shu’s interrogation, Zhang wasn’t involved and didn’t have any private contact with Chen Shu. Additionally, Zhang came from a good background, making it unlikely he’d be corrupted, and he wasn’t clever or steady enough to handle undercover work.","Zhang was peering through the glass at the mice running through a maze, puzzled. \"Mu Mian, I thought you didn’t like animals. Why are you keeping a bunch of mice?\"","\"Officer Zhang, don’t scare them. And I don’t dislike animals,\" Mu Mian said, pulling Zhang away. \"Also, don’t call them mice. They have names.\"","\"What are their names?\"","\"This one is Rainbow One, that one is Rainbow Two... and the smartest one is Rainbow Seven.\"","\"What... does that have to do with rainbows?\"","Chen Xue pointed at the mice’s heads. \"Look at the colors on their heads. If you see them as a group, you’ll notice they form a rainbow.\"","\"...\"","Inside the glass container were seven white mice, each with a patch of dyed fur on their heads—red, orange, green... purple. Together, they formed a rainbow.","Upon closer inspection, some of the mice had scars on their heads, as if their scalps had been cut open.","\"I dyed their fur to cover the scars and make it easier to tell them apart.\"","\"Why not name them Little Red, Little Orange, or something like that? Those names sound cuter,\" Zhang suggested.","\"Those names are too anthropomorphic. I’m worried you’ll develop feelings for them and think what I’m doing to them is too cruel.\"","\"Don’t worry, there’s no way we’d develop feelings for a bunch of mice. But why do some of them look sickly and not very bright?\"","Mu Mian explained, \"Rainbow One to Four are mice with brain damage. I removed part of their brain tissue... Rainbow One and Two are control groups; Three and Four are also control groups.","Rainbow Five is a normal mouse, very average. Rainbow Six is a naturally dull mouse—it’s been trained many times but still can’t figure out how to navigate the maze. Rainbow Seven is a genius mouse—it can quickly solve any unfamiliar maze and get the food.\"","Zhang stared at Mu Mian, dumbfounded. While others kept pets for fun, Mu Mian seemed to be conducting research.","Fang Rui asked, \"Are you using them to test the effects of that drug?\"","\"Yes. I’ve already sent the drug to a professional testing agency for analysis, but they don’t know what it’s for. They even suspect it’s a half-finished product.","The clinical effects of the drug are more obvious on living subjects. It’s hard to deduce from a corpse what the drug is actually for, so I’ve decided to test it on these mice.\"","Zhang praised her, \"Mu Mian, if you weren’t a forensic scientist, you’d definitely make a great researcher.\"","\"I prefer being a forensic scientist because I get to work with a lot of corpses. My dad said being a researcher is hard—you need a lot of funding first, and only then do you need a smart brain.\"","\"...\"","Zhang pointed at the box. \"Alright, we’ve seen your rainbow mice. You can take them back to your office now.\"","Mu Mian didn’t say anything, just quietly looked at Fang Rui and Zhang.","\"Mu Mian, you’re not planning to leave them here, are you?\"","\"Is that okay? Chen Xue doesn’t like them. She won’t let me keep them in my office.\"","Fang Rui said, \"It’s fine.\"","Zhang suggested, \"Why not put them in the conference room? It’s spacious, has good air circulation, and is quiet.\"","\"But no one will be watching them. I’m worried they might get hurt.\"","Zhang rolled his eyes. \"They’re in a glass container. What harm could come to them? Overeating until they burst? Or fighting to the death?\"","\"Officer Zhang, you’re overthinking it. Some of these mice are smart, and some are dumb. If they’re kept together, the dumb ones might get bullied and not get enough food. I should assign them separate living spaces and food.\"","\"...Meticulous!\"","Mu Mian quickly used cardboard to divide the container into seven compartments, ensuring each mouse had its own comfortable space.","In the end, Mu Mian decided to place the mice on a small table at the back of the conference room. Fang Rui helped her move the glass container there.","The conference room was empty. Mu Mian whispered to Fang Rui, \"These mice aren’t actually for drug testing. The mice for drug testing are at my house.\"","\"You’re using these mice as bait to lure out the undercover agent?\" Fang Rui asked.","Mu Mian nodded. \"The undercover agent definitely doesn’t want us to know the effects of that drug, so they might try to harm these innocent mice. I’ve installed a pinhole camera on the glass container, and there’s also a camera at the conference room door. If someone tries to kill these mice, they’ll be caught on camera.\"","\"Mu Mian, not bad. You’re learning to use cunning tactics now?\"","Mu Mian corrected him, \"It’s strategy. It’s called ‘waiting for the rabbit,’ no, ‘the willing fish,’ no, what’s it called again...\"","\"It’s called ‘luring the tiger out of the mountain.’\"","Mu Mian looked at the mice and said to Fang Rui, \"They have names too. This one is Neon One, that one is Neon Two... and the smartest one is Neon Seven.\"","\"Got it. We’ll remember them.\"","Mu Mian whispered to the mice, \"If you’re murdered, I’ll definitely avenge you. I’ll remember you.\"","The mice squeaked as they ate, perhaps in response to Mu Mian’s words."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: The Split-Brain Case: The Dead Child","paragraphs":["Mu Mian's little mice not only escaped harm but, under the care of everyone, especially Zhang, turned into a group of plump rodents.","The once smartest of them, Rainbow Seven, now refuses to navigate mazes for food.","Mu Mian poked Rainbow Seven's head and sighed, \"A comfortable environment can dull a mouse's intelligence!\"","\"Could it be that it was never particularly smart but just had a keen sense of smell?\" Fang Rui suggested.","\"Of course not. The food I placed at the maze exit had no scent,\" Mu Mian pondered. \"Should I install an electric shock device to give them a little danger now and then, to boost their motivation to solve mazes?\"","Mu Mian felt someone's resentful gaze on her.","She turned around and saw it was Zhang.","\"Mu Mian, how could you be so cruel? You want to electrocute them?\" Zhang scolded.","Mu Mian explained, \"Psychologists do this all the time. Skinner's theory of operant conditioning was developed through 'abusing' mice. Electric shocks are a common way to apply stimuli.\"","Zhang stood protectively in front of the glass enclosure and corrected her, \"They have names. Call them by their names—Little Red, Little Orange... Little Purple. Come on, Uncle will play some music to soothe your frightened little hearts.\"","Over the days, Zhang had come to treat these mice as pets.","Mu Mian whispered to Fang Rui, \"I told you not to give the mice overly anthropomorphic names. It makes people too attached. See, this is what happens.\"","Fang Rui smiled helplessly.","Two weeks later, Mu Mian's undercover bait plan ended in failure.","On Monday morning, as Fang Rui and Mu Mian were on their way to work, they received a notification: a child's body had been found in the greenery by the roadside in the suburbs.","The scene was a small flower bed by the road. A sanitation worker had discovered the body while cleaning in the morning. At first, he thought it was an abandoned child, but upon picking it up, he noticed the baby's eyes were closed, unresponsive, and the body had a faint odor.","He checked the child's heart and found no heartbeat or breath. Realizing it might be a death, he immediately called the police.","Arriving at the scene, Mu Mian saw the deceased's body placed by the roadside.","The victim was a very young boy, no more than two years old based on his height. He was dressed in light blue cotton pajamas and wore a black knitted hat with a cartoon character on it.","His abdomen was slightly swollen, and his back showed signs of greenish decomposition. Mu Mian lifted the child's eyelids—his corneas were heavily clouded, and black spots had appeared on the sclera. The body emitted a faint stench of decay.","\"The ambient temperature is 27°C, and the body temperature is 30.5°C. Based on other postmortem signs, the time of death is over 24 hours ago,\" Mu Mian noted.","The child's appearance was unusual—wide-set eyes, small eye slits, upward-slanting outer corners, a flat nose, and stubby fingers. Mu Mian noticed some deformities in his hand bones.","Chen Xue remarked, \"This child looks strange, not like a normal child. Could he have Down syndrome?\"","Down syndrome, also known as trisomy 21, is caused by an extra chromosome 21. Children with this condition have distinct facial features, delayed growth, physical deformities, congenital heart diseases, and intellectual disabilities.","Mu Mian agreed, \"Yes, this is likely a child with Down syndrome. His height is 61.5 cm, and children with Down syndrome are generally shorter than average. Based on his height, he's probably between one and a half to two years old.\"","\"Could it be that his parents didn't want to raise him and abandoned him here?\" Zhang speculated.","Mu Mian was puzzled, \"Isn't Down syndrome detectable through prenatal screening? It's a standard part of prenatal care. Why would his mother have given birth to him? Moreover, 60% of Down syndrome fetuses miscarry early on. Without medical intervention, it's unlikely he would have survived.\"","Chen Xue added, \"Doctors usually advise mothers to terminate such pregnancies. But I've heard of extreme cases where mothers, out of deep love for their child, choose to give birth despite knowing about genetic issues.\"","Zhang said, \"But a child with such disabilities wouldn't have a happy life. This kind of maternal love seems too blind.\"","Mu Mian noticed a faint smell of blood on the child, but upon closer inspection, she found no external injuries. Then, she removed the small hat on the child's head, revealing a bald scalp.","\"His skull has been cut open,\" Mu Mian announced.","Everyone turned to look. The child's hair had been shaved, and a ring of black stitches, crooked like a centipede, circled the top of his head.","Suddenly, they realized this might not be a simple case of child abandonment.","\"Did this child undergo brain surgery?\" Zhang asked in shock.","\"The technique is professional, but this wasn't a surgery. The wound shows no signs of healing, meaning the scalp was cut after death,\" Mu Mian explained. \"No doctor would perform surgery on a dead patient.\"","Fang Rui speculated, \"Could it be that a doctor performed an autopsy to determine the cause of death?\"","\"Possibly.\"","Mu Mian checked the child's eyelids and mouth. There were no foreign objects in the mouth, and no signs of compression on the neck. \"We can preliminarily rule out mechanical asphyxiation. Based on the body's condition, it doesn't seem like death by poisoning either.\"","Mu Mian placed the child's body in a body bag, and she and Chen Xue loaded it into the car. They drove back, eager to uncover what had happened to this child.","Her intuition told her that the killer might have taken something from the body.","Fang Rui carefully examined the surroundings. The flower bed was next to a service road, surrounded by vast, sparsely populated wasteland. However, it was near the intersection of several provincial highways, with a gas station and a water station nearby. At night, many trucks parked in the area.","This wasn't an ideal place to dump a body.","There were no surveillance cameras near the flower bed, but the road had several speed cameras.","The road had heavy traffic, being close to a highway entrance, with many large trucks passing through. Investigating these vehicles would be challenging.","Zhang speculated, \"Could it be that the child's mother, driven mad by grief, wandered here and left the child in the flower bed?\"","Wang found Zhang's theory somewhat plausible but also absurd. He couldn't help but say, \"Have you been watching too many dramas?\"","\"Think about it. A child's body is so small. It would be easy to dispose of it unnoticed—put it in a suitcase, dump it in a ravine, or throw it into the sea. Even burying it would be better than leaving it in a flower bed. If the killer had any sense, they wouldn't have dumped the body here.\"","Wang was convinced. \"That makes sense!\"","Fang Rui said, \"What if the person who killed the child and the one who dumped the body are not the same?\"","\"Then what was the dumper trying to achieve? To draw our attention? Why not leave the body in the city center to create a media frenzy?\"","Fang Rui replied, \"Let's start by identifying the child. His appearance is distinctive, and with Down syndrome, such children are rare. It should be easy to find out who he is.\"","At that moment, Wang called out, \"Come and look at this!\"","Everyone gathered around and saw a symbol \"დ\" drawn in the soil of the flower bed. The symbol was dark red, seemingly written in blood.","After taking a photo of the symbol, Wang sprayed it with luminol, and it fluoresced.","\"This symbol was written in blood.\""]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: The Split-Brain Case: The Stolen Half of the Brain","paragraphs":["The small body of the deceased was laid flat on the cold autopsy table.","Mu Mian’s mood was heavier than usual, as this was the youngest human body she had ever dissected, and it was also a child with Down syndrome.","Mu Mian did not start by dissecting the head of the deceased. Instead, she first cut open the chest and abdominal cavities, removing the internal organs. She began by examining the heart, scrutinizing it carefully.","Chen Xue asked curiously, “Mu Mian, why didn’t you start with the head?”","“Because I need to determine the cause of death first.”","“The skull has been cut open, so shouldn’t we first confirm if the cause of death was mechanical injury? It’s possible the victim died from massive blood loss or brain tissue damage.”","Mu Mian emphasized again, “The wound on the scalp shows no signs of vital reaction. This means the scalp was cut after death. Additionally, the lividity on the body is quite pronounced. If the cause of death were massive blood loss, the lividity would be lighter. The deceased was a child with Down syndrome, who often suffer from various congenital diseases, the most common being congenital heart disease.”","Lividity is formed by the deposition of red blood cells after death. If the deceased had lost too much blood, resulting in a significant loss of red blood cells, the lividity would appear lighter.","Chen Xue said, “Do you suspect the child died suddenly from an illness?”","“It’s possible.”","Mu Mian noticed that the deceased’s ventricles were thicker than those of an average person, and one of the heart valves had an abnormal structure.","Further pathological testing of the heart would be needed to confirm whether there were any issues. Mu Mian sent the heart to a testing facility for pathological analysis.","Pathological testing is a tedious process and takes a considerable amount of time. This was why Mu Mian had chosen to dissect the internal organs first.","“Finally, it’s time to examine the brain,” Mu Mian said excitedly.","She carefully cut open the sutures on the head. The stitches were made with ordinary black thread, not medical-grade, but the knotting and sewing technique suggested the person who had stitched it had some clinical experience.","After removing the sutures, Mu Mian carefully peeled back the scalp, separating the subcutaneous tissue to reveal the skull.","The skull had already been sawed open with an electric saw. Mu Mian lifted the cranial bone and discovered that only half of the brain tissue remained inside the cranial cavity.","The perpetrator had severed the corpus callosum, which connects the two hemispheres of the brain, splitting the brain into two parts. They had then taken the left hemisphere of the deceased’s brain.","Chen Xue was stunned.","“The perpetrator actually took the brain tissue, and only the left hemisphere? Why would someone take the brain of a deceased child?” Chen Xue exclaimed in shock.","Mu Mian replied, “It could be for research purposes. They could make brain slices to observe pathological changes.”","“Then why only take half?”","“Maybe the left hemisphere had some research value,” Mu Mian said as she removed the remaining half of the brain tissue, now deeply intrigued by it.","Chen Xue looked at the brain and said, “This reminds me of a famous medical experiment—the split-brain experiment. Sperry, in an attempt to treat epilepsy, severed the corpus callosum of a patient. While the patient’s seizures stopped, they lost the ability to control their behavior. This patient became known as the ‘split-brain person.’ Could the perpetrator be replicating this experiment?”","Sperry’s split-brain experiment demonstrated that the human brain is divided into two hemispheres: the left hemisphere receives sensory information from the right side of the body and controls movements on the right side, while the right hemisphere handles sensory information from the left side and controls movements on the left. Severing the connection between the two hemispheres renders a person unable to control their behavior.","“But what value would replicating this experiment have?” Mu Mian wondered. “The division of labor between the brain’s hemispheres has already been thoroughly studied. Moreover, the perpetrator removed the left hemisphere after the victim’s death. They wouldn’t be able to observe any behavioral changes in a dead person.”","“True. Taking the brain of a dead person would only be useful for pathological research,” Chen Xue agreed.","Mu Mian thought for a moment and said, “There’s another possibility: the perpetrator didn’t want us to know what pathological changes had occurred in the left hemisphere, so they took it.”","“Then why didn’t they destroy the entire body? The child’s body was so small; they could have disposed of it in many other ways,” Chen Xue analyzed.","Mu Mian looked at the cranial cavity, equally puzzled about the perpetrator’s motives.","She sent the right hemisphere of the brain for pathological testing as well, to determine if there were any abnormalities in the brain tissue.","**Case Analysis Meeting**","The pathological test results were not yet available, so Mu Mian simply reported the preliminary findings from the autopsy.","“Initial findings suggest two possible causes of death: first, sudden death due to illness. The child may have had congenital heart disease and died from a heart attack. Second, the brain may have developed a pathological condition that damaged vital centers. The pathological report isn’t ready yet, so I can’t determine the exact cause of death at this time.”","Mu Mian continued, “The perpetrator sawed open the skull and removed the left hemisphere of the brain. Both the suturing and the craniotomy were performed with precision, suggesting the perpetrator has extensive clinical experience. In fact, they might even be a neurosurgeon.”","Mu Mian displayed a photo of the cranial cavity on the screen.","Everyone stared in disbelief at the image of the skull, now missing half of its brain.","Zhang asked, “Why did the perpetrator only take half of the brain? Wouldn’t it have been easier to take the whole brain?”","Mu Mian replied, “I find it strange too. The perpetrator’s actions are contradictory.”","“Could they be mentally unstable?”","Lin Sen said, “If that’s the case, they might strike again.”","Wang reported the forensic findings: “In the flowerbed, we found two sets of footprints. One belonged to the sanitation worker who reported the case, and the other was a size 41. The shoe print pattern doesn’t match any known brand. The child’s clothing only had the fingerprints of the person who reported the case.”","Fang Rui displayed a photo on the screen. In the soil of the flowerbed, the perpetrator had written a symbol, “დ,” in blood. The handwriting was neat, and the symbol was slightly larger than a thumb.","“Tests confirmed that the blood used to write the symbol belonged to the victim,” Chen Xue reported.","The team searched online for the symbol but found no specific explanation. It seemed to be a symbol created by the perpetrator, possibly meaningless."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: The Split-Brain Case: The Man Who Should Have Died","paragraphs":["“Why did the killer leave this symbol? Is it a provocation to the police? But this symbol doesn’t seem threatening at all,” Lin Sen said.","“This might be his criminal signature. Many criminals, especially serial killers, like to leave their unique mark at the crime scene,” Lin Sen explained.","A criminal signature refers to the unique and personalized behavior an offender exhibits during the commission of a crime. These actions are not necessary for completing the crime but are done to satisfy a special psychological need. It’s also crucial evidence in linking serial murder cases.","Fang Rui asked, “Lin Sen, do you suspect he’ll strike again?”","“Yes. We can’t analyze his criminal behavior and motives using conventional investigative logic. It’s highly likely that he’s acting based on his criminal delusions, which often lack logic or realism. That’s why his actions appear so chaotic.”","Fang Rui and his team investigated the vehicles passing through the highway, but due to the heavy traffic, no useful leads were found.","Fang Rui and Zhang then visited the gas station near the crime scene.","The gas station was about 1,200 meters from the flowerbed where the body was discovered. Fang Rui first asked the gas station manager for the surveillance footage from the entrance and then began questioning the staff.","“Between September 14th and 15th, did you notice any suspicious vehicles around here?” Fang Rui asked.","The sanitation worker had reported the body on the morning of September 15th.","One of the male employees, wearing glasses, replied, “What counts as a suspicious vehicle? Speeding? Illegal U-turns? There’s no traffic camera here, so a lot of drivers break the rules.”","“Yes! Tell me the license plate numbers or any distinctive features of the cars.”","“I’ve already reported them on the traffic app,” he said, opening his phone to show Fang Rui and Zhang his report history. “These are the vehicles.”","The employee’s father had died in a car accident caused by a drunk driver, so he harbored a deep hatred for traffic violations.","Zhang noted down the car models and license plate numbers.","“Over the past two days, have you seen any cars parked along the roadside here?”","“Parking is prohibited here, and this area is mostly wasteland. Passengers wouldn’t get out here. Even if a driver needed to stop urgently, they could park at our gas station or the nearby water station. Trucks often park there overnight.”","A female employee suddenly spoke up, “Actually, I did see a white car parked on the roadside one night.”","“When was that?”","“It was around 9 PM on the 14th. I remember it clearly because something happened at home that day, and I swapped shifts with a colleague. I was riding my electric scooter past that section of the road, just before the turn to the service road.","“From a distance, I saw the white car parked there. At first, I thought it had broken down, so I went over to check. But as soon as the driver saw me approaching, they started the car. The driver seemed like a beginner—they turned the steering wheel the wrong way and hit the curb. I’m not sure if the car was damaged.”","“Do you remember the license plate number?”","The female employee shook her head. “No, it was too dark, and there were no streetlights. I only remember it was a white car with a green license plate.”","“Can you identify the car model?”","“It didn’t have a brand logo. Probably a generic domestic car, a very common-looking sedan.”","“Thank you for the information. If you remember anything else, please contact us immediately,” Zhang said, handing over his contact details.","“No problem. If I recall anything else, I’ll definitely let you know.”","Fang Rui and Zhang then visited the water station. However, since the water station was surrounded by a wall, the road was a blind spot, and the employees there couldn’t provide any useful information.","Following the female employee’s description, Fang Rui and Zhang inspected the curbs along the road. Soon, they found a spot with white paint scrapes. The location was about 500 meters from the flowerbed where the body was discovered.","Zhang found it strange. “Why didn’t he just park near the flowerbed? Carrying the body to the flowerbed would have taken a few minutes. Wasn’t he afraid of being seen by passing vehicles?”","Fang Rui was also puzzled. He speculated, “Maybe after parking, the killer realized it wasn’t a good spot to dump the body, so he moved further ahead?”","“But there’s an identical flowerbed right here.”","Fang Rui decided not to dwell on the question. “Let’s focus on finding that white car. Its front bumper is likely chipped, and with a green license plate, it’s probably a white new energy vehicle. Let’s have Li and the team check the surveillance footage for a car matching these features.”","“Got it.”","Fang Rui also asked the household registration department to investigate the victim’s identity.","The victim was a child with Down syndrome, with a very distinctive appearance. However, after Fang Rui’s team issued a missing person notice, no one came forward to identify the body. There were also no recent reports of a missing child.","Fang Rui sent people to visit major hospitals in Jiangzhou City. However, the pediatric staff at these hospitals all stated they had never seen the child.","Logically, children with Down syndrome are prone to illnesses, and the victim was suspected to have congenital heart disease. It was unlikely he had never visited a hospital.","Zhang said, “We’ve spread the word through multiple channels, and the local TV station aired the missing person notice, but there’s been no feedback. This is very unusual. His appearance is so distinctive—anyone who’s seen him would remember him. How could no one recognize him? Could he be from out of town and just arrived here, so no one knows him?”","“But he must have a guardian. He’s been missing for two or three days. Why hasn’t his guardian reported him missing?”","“Could he have been trafficked?” someone suggested, but quickly dismissed the idea. “But who would traffic a child with Down syndrome? No buyer would want a child with obvious health issues.”","Mu Mian quietly interjected, “There is a possibility. If someone wanted to study Down syndrome, they might buy such a child.”","Zhang exclaimed, “Could this child have been kept hidden for research, never seen by outsiders?”","Chen Xue countered, “This isn’t a TV drama. Even if someone wanted to study Down syndrome, they could openly seek consent from the child’s parents. There’s no need to lock the child away.”","Seeing that Fang Rui and the team were struggling to identify the child, Mu Mian decided to pass the time by matching the child’s DNA with the police database.","To her surprise, she found a match. The two DNA samples were strikingly similar, suggesting a likely mother-son relationship.","Chen Xue leaned over and asked, “Mu Mian, what are you doing?”","Mu Mian switched her computer screen and pointed at it. “I’m writing my observation diary about my lab mice.”","“Oh, I saw you looking surprised and thought there was a breakthrough in the case.”","Mu Mian sighed. “I was surprised. Rainbow No. 7 has gained more weight than the other mice. It’s no longer a genius mouse.”","“Are you going to abandon it?”","“Of course not. It may not be a genius, but it’s a happy mouse now. Officer Zhang says happy people gain weight—it’s called ‘a relaxed mind leads to a plump body.’ Chen Xue, you’re so thin. You must lack happiness.”","Chen Xue smiled helplessly. “Mu Mian, if you had to choose between intelligence and happiness, which would you pick?”","“Intelligence isn’t a choice—it’s mostly determined by genes. But happiness is a choice. So, I can have both intelligence and happiness!”","“...”"]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: The Split-Brain Case: Deception","paragraphs":["After work, Fang Rui drove Mu Mian home. When they arrived at her doorstep, Mu Mian suddenly looked at him with a mysterious expression and said, \"Fang Rui, let's go to your place. I have something important to tell you.\"","\"Something important? What is it?\" Fang Rui's heart raced. He couldn't help but wonder if Mu Mian was about to propose to him again. If she did, should he agree this time?","\"We'll talk inside. This isn't something that can be explained in a sentence or two.\"","\"Isn't it just a matter of one sentence?\"","\"Of course not. How can such an important matter be summed up in one sentence? Fang Rui, hurry up and open the door,\" Mu Mian urged.","\"Alright.\"","Mu Mian had Fang Rui sit on the couch while she sat across from him.","Fang Rui felt a little nervous.","Mu Mian pulled out a black folder from her bag and handed it to Fang Rui. \"Go ahead and open it. There's a surprise inside.\"","The folder had no writing on the cover. Fang Rui asked, \"What is this? It's not a marriage agreement, is it?\"","Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui and shook her head in disappointment. \"Fang Rui, with such a special murder case happening right now, you're still thinking about marriage? You're so unprofessional!\"","Fang Rui retorted, \"Then who was it that came to me in the middle of the night to discuss a case and ended up proposing to me? You have a history, so it's only natural for me to misinterpret your actions.\"","Mu Mian, feeling guilty, changed the subject. \"Fang Rui, just read the report.\"","\"Can't you just tell me the results?\"","\"Of course not. I need to train your reading and comprehension skills, or your IQ might degrade like Rainbow Seven. Besides, seeing it for yourself will have a greater impact.\"","After reading the report, Fang Rui furrowed his brows. The report was indeed impactful.","A child who should have died long ago had actually survived for over a year, only to become the victim of another murder case.","Fang Rui exclaimed in shock, \"How can this be Li Yan's child? Wasn't her child killed by Chen Hui and put into a jar? Why is this child still alive?\"","The DNA sample matching the child came from a victim named Li Yan, the first victim in the Cat Fetus Murder case.","Mu Mian explained, \"Li Yan was eight months pregnant at the time. If the child was born prematurely, it's possible for it to have survived. Back then, I extracted DNA from the fetuses in the jar, and their DNA didn't match the DNA of the three victims. The child of the victim wasn't in the jar.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Why didn't you tell me about this back then?\"","\"At the time, I thought it wasn't important. The parents of those children didn't care about them, so they wouldn't care about their remains either. Besides, we weren't close back then. You were always so harsh with me, and I was a little scared of you,\" Mu Mian said softly.","\"Was I really that harsh with you?\"","\"Yes! You never smiled at me.\"","\"You were always asking me for corpses back then. How could I smile at you? And even though I was so harsh, it didn't stop your interest in my corpses.\"","\"Later, I still asked you for them, but you started smiling at me often,\" Mu Mian said, tilting her head with a hint of pride. \"You liked me back then, didn't you?\"","\"Yes. So when did you start liking me?\"","Mu Mian lowered her head. \"I don't know. But I just like you, really like you.\"","Fang Rui quickly noticed a contradiction. He asked, \"Mu Mian, if you thought the children's remains weren't important, why did you test their DNA? Didn't you do it to help find their parents?\"","Mu Mian nodded. \"Yes. But Chen Xue told me that their parents wouldn't care about the children's remains. I thought her words made sense, so I ended up going out for a meal with her.\"","They both fell silent.","Fang Rui asked again, \"When did you and Chen Xue become so close?\"","Fang Rui had noticed that Mu Mian and Chen Xue had suddenly become very close. Given Mu Mian's personality, making friends was incredibly difficult. Yet, Chen Xue had been unusually tolerant of her.","\"About a week after I started working. I don't know why, but Chen Xue always invited me to chat. She taught me a lot about social norms, even did my horoscope, and bought me milk tea. Slowly, we became friends.\"","They fell silent again.","Chen Xue also had a motive for murder. Chen Shu's mother had caused Chen Xue to lose her father and her happy family.","But if Chen Xue's initial intention in getting close to Mu Mian wasn't pure, then her motive for killing Chen Shu wasn't jealousy or hatred. It was more likely that someone behind the scenes had instructed her to do these things.","She and Chen Shu might belong to the same organization. Chen Xue was afraid that Chen Shu, driven by emotions, would reveal the truth to Wang, so she poisoned Chen Shu.","But Fang Rui couldn't understand why Chen Xue would be so kind to Mu Mian if she was a mole. Was getting close to Mu Mian also part of her mission?","Mu Mian felt a little sad. Chen Xue was a good friend to her, and she couldn't believe that Chen Xue's kindness was built on lies. She couldn't accept that Chen Xue might be a murderer.","\"Fang Rui, could all of this just be a coincidence? Chen Xue... she wouldn't lie to me, right?\" But Mu Mian knew very well that making friends on her own was incredibly difficult.","Mu Mian remembered her university days when she had a few good friends. They were kind to her, patiently listened to her scientific explanations, and tolerated her quirks. She thought she had finally made real friends.","Later, she found out that those people had befriended her because her sister had given them many benefits.","Mu Mian had confronted them, asking why they had deceived her. They all gave similar answers: if it weren't for the benefits, no one would willingly take care of someone unconditionally.","\"Fang Rui, I should have realized. Someone like me, so troublesome, how could anyone willingly be my friend?\" Mu Mian's eyes grew moist.","Fang Rui hugged Mu Mian and comforted her, \"You're not troublesome at all. Look, you even have a boyfriend now.\"","\"Fang Rui, are you lying to me too?\" Mu Mian was scared. Even though she had learned to recognize lies, humans were too skilled at deception. Lies were nested within lies, truth and lies intertwined, and Mu Mian found it hard to distinguish between them.","\"Of course not,\" Fang Rui said, taking Mu Mian's hand and placing it on his chest. \"Mu Mian, feel my heartbeat. My heart won't lie to you.\"","\"I believe you,\" Mu Mian said, resting her head on his chest and feeling his strong, steady heartbeat. \"But Fang Rui, lies come from the brain, not the heart.\"","\"...\"","Mu Mian's emotions gradually calmed down, and she thought of the person most affected by Chen Xue's lies.","\"Fang Rui, what about Officer Zhang? If he finds out that Chen Xue has been deceiving him, how heartbroken will he be? He's already planned the wedding and even invited me to be a bridesmaid.\"","Fang Rui thought of Officer Zhang, who was always so cheerful. He couldn't imagine how devastated Zhang would be if he learned the truth.","Fang Rui said, \"Let's not let Chen Xue know that we suspect her. We'll see if we can find some clues from her.\"","Mu Mian asked, \"Should we tell Officer Zhang?\"","Fang Rui hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Not yet!\"","Zhang's acting skills were poor, and his feelings for Chen Xue were so deep. If they told him, it would likely alert Chen Xue."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: The Split-Brain Case: Suspicious Vehicle","paragraphs":["Mu Mian quickly composed herself and began analyzing the case with Fang Rui.","If the children of the victims in the \"Cat Fetus\" case were still alive, the nature of the case would be entirely different.","Fang Rui speculated, \"So, Chen Hui's true motive for committing the crime might have been to steal the pregnant women's children, and placing cats inside the victims was just a diversion to throw the police off track. However, Chen Hui's mental illness doesn't seem fabricated. If his sole intention was to steal the children, wouldn't he, as an obstetrician, have access to more discreet and safer methods?\"","Mu Mian agreed with Fang Rui's analysis. Chen Hui's mental issues were likely genuine; he truly believed he could be reborn as a cat.","Mu Mian added, \"Could it be that Bai Jing and the organization behind her are using Chen Hui to steal those children? But the same question arises: why wouldn't they adopt a more covert approach? They could have simply bought the children or hired someone to abduct them after birth. That way, they wouldn't attract our investigation.\"","Fang Rui said, \"It's possible that the victims were also insiders, and they wanted to silence them. When we investigated Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital, we found that the first two victims had repeatedly considered abortions. The hospital told us it was because they knew they were carrying girls and, due to their preference for sons, didn't want to keep them.","Now, it seems more likely that they knew there was something wrong with the babies they were carrying, which is why they wanted to terminate the pregnancies. But what's strange is that Chen Hui was the one who stopped them from having abortions. This suggests that Chen Hui might also be an insider. Could he be part of that organization too?\"","Fang Rui decided to dig deeper into Chen Hui's background.","They used their phones to look up information about the hospital where Chen Hui had worked—Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital.","Fang Rui said, \"This hospital was once affiliated with the Jiangmiao Group, but about a year and a half ago, shortly after the 'Cat Fetus' case concluded, it was sold off and severed ties with the Jiangmiao Group.\"","\"So, it's highly likely that the Jiangmiao Group was using this hospital for illegal research.\"","The next day, Mu Mian received the pathological test report for the deceased. Since the victim's identity remained unknown, he had no name, so Mu Mian gave him one: Little Tang No. 1.","Given that more than one child had gone missing in the \"Cat Fetus\" case, Mu Mian suspected that a second unidentified body might appear.","At the morning meeting, Mu Mian reported the findings: \"The pathological test results show that Little Tang No. 1 had a congenital heart defect, and his condition was severe. He most likely died of a sudden heart attack.\"","\"A sudden heart attack? So, the killer might not have directly caused his death but merely disposed of the body?\"","Mu Mian replied, \"Not necessarily. The killer could have used physical means to induce the heart attack.\" The reason she mentioned physical means was that neither the toxicology nor blood tests revealed any abnormalities.","\"If the victim died of a heart condition, why would the killer remove half of his brain? If it was about the heart, wouldn't they have taken the diseased heart instead?\" Zhang asked, puzzled.","Mu Mian explained, \"Children with Down syndrome often have severe intellectual disabilities, so their brains might hold research value.\"","Fang Rui said, \"Since we can't deduce the killer's motive, let's set that aside for now and focus on the existing clues. An eyewitness reported seeing a suspicious vehicle, so we'll start by investigating that car.\"","After the meeting, Zhang was surprised to find that Mu Mian had bought him milk tea and a small cake, while everyone else received coffee—even Fang Rui got coffee.","Zhang was both flustered and flattered. \"Mu Mian, why did you suddenly buy me cake? It's not my birthday. This is so strange. Are you trying to ask me for a favor? Just say it—I’d never refuse you.\"","Mu Mian gave Zhang a sympathetic look and then sipped her milk tea. She frowned; it was too sweet. She shouldn’t have ordered it with sugar.","\"Oh no, did my little ones die?\" Zhang rushed to check the glass tank where he kept his white mice, but they were alive and well, even more energetic than Mu Mian.","Zhang turned to Fang Rui. \"Boss, what's wrong with Mu Mian? I'm feeling a bit uneasy. Why is she suddenly being so nice to me?\"","Fang Rui replied, \"I don’t like milk tea or cake.\"","\"Ah, I thought I was getting special treatment from Mu Mian. Turns out it's just that,\" Zhang said, a hint of disappointment on his face, though he felt relieved. \"Well, I’ll enjoy it then. Honestly, this cake is pretty good. Mu Mian, where did you buy it? Send me the shop's name.\"","Mu Mian sent him the shop's name.","\"What? Is this cake made of gold? Why is it so expensive?\"","Mu Mian sighed. She finally understood why Rainbow No. 7 seemed so happy. Being a little clueless did seem to make life easier.","\"Mian Mian, what's wrong? Why are you sighing?\" Chen Xue asked.","Mu Mian pointed at the milk tea. \"It's awful.\"","\"Why didn’t you ask me to order for you? You always like what I pick.\"","\"But I can’t always rely on you to order for me,\" Mu Mian said softly.","\"Why not?\"","\"Once you marry Officer Zhang, I can’t keep bothering you.\"","Chen Xue glanced at the engagement ring on her finger and didn’t respond.","Mu Mian took another sip of the milk tea. The sweetness filled her mouth, but she still felt a deep sadness. It seemed she was getting better at lying now.","Fang Rui and Zhang went to Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital to investigate.","Fang Rui didn’t tell the team that the deceased was the child of Li Yan, a victim in the \"Cat Fetus\" case, and he didn’t officially link the two cases.","He fabricated a reason, saying that an informant had provided a lead—someone had seen the child at Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital.","When Zhang saw the hospital's sign, he exclaimed, \"Isn’t this the hospital where Chen Hui used to work?\"","They parked in the hospital's lot.","Zhang remarked, \"This is a private hospital for sure. The doctors and patients' families here must be wealthy—look at all these luxury cars.\"","Fang Rui scanned the area and noticed that most of the cars were high-end brands. In the corner of the parking lot, he spotted a white domestic car with a green license plate, standing out among the luxury vehicles.","Fang Rui walked over to inspect the car and noticed that some paint had been scraped off the right side of the front bumper.","Zhang's face lit up. \"Boss, the paint on this car is chipped. Could this be the car the eyewitness saw?\"","\"Send the license plate number to Li and check if this car appears in the surveillance footage.\"","\"Got it.\" Zhang took photos of the car from various angles and sent them to Li.","Fang Rui and Zhang questioned the doctors and nurses at the hospital, but none of them recognized the child.","Fang Rui then asked the receptionist, \"Whose car is this?\"","The nurse looked at Fang Rui warily and hesitated to answer.","\"I need him to move his car.\"","The nurse relaxed and said, \"It belongs to Vice President Liu Qiangmin.\"","Zhang was surprised. \"Your vice president drives this kind of car?\" It wasn’t that Zhang looked down on it, but cars often symbolized social status. At a certain level, people were expected to drive something more prestigious.","The nurse retorted, \"What’s wrong with driving this car? Don’t look down on people. Our Vice President Liu doesn’t care about superficial things. He’s the face of our hospital, the 'top hand' in obstetrics. With his income, he could buy any car he wants, but he prefers domestic cars over imported ones.\"","\"Sorry, sorry, I was just joking. I actually think domestic cars offer great value for money,\" Zhang said, immediately feeling a newfound respect for Vice President Liu.","Just then, Li sent them a message.","[This car with the license plate was captured by a traffic camera near the area at 8:42 PM on the 14th and again at 9:36 PM at another traffic camera. This means the car was in the area where the body was dumped between 8:42 PM and 9:35 PM.]","This matched the eyewitness's testimony perfectly.","Fang Rui found it strange. The distance between the two traffic cameras was less than three kilometers, and fifteen minutes would have been more than enough time to dump the body and flee the scene. Why had the killer lingered in this area for so long?"]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: The Split-Brain Case: The Suspect","paragraphs":["Fang Rui asked, \"Where is Director Liu's office?\"","\"On the third floor, left side, second to last room.\"","Fang Rui and Zhang found Director Liu's office and knocked on the door. A voice from inside called out, \"Come in!\"","Director Liu's office was simply decorated, with many banners hanging on the walls, such as \"Skilled and Compassionate,\" \"Grateful for the Safe Delivery of Mother and Child, Praising Medical Virtue,\" and \"Exemplary Medical Ethics, Renowned Expertise.\" These banners reflected his excellent medical skills and moral character.","Director Liu was a middle-aged man in his forties, not very tall, quite thin, with a receding hairline and a kind, approachable face.","He was writing a report when he saw Fang Rui and Zhang. Frowning, he asked, \"Who are you? What do you want?\"","They showed their badges and explained their purpose.","Upon learning they were police officers, Director Liu's frown deepened. \"Officers, what do you need from me?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Director Liu, where were you between 8 PM and 10 PM on the night of September 14th?\"","\"September 14th? Let me think... I got home a little after six that day and stayed in all evening. I didn't go out.\"","\"Can anyone confirm that?\"","Director Liu grew angry. \"What are you implying? Are you suspecting me?\"","Fang Rui said, \"Why are you lying? Surveillance footage shows your car near the highway entrance on the national road around 8 PM that night.\"","\"That's impossible! I haven't left the city recently. How could my car be near the highway entrance? Are you sure you're not mistaken?\"","Fang Rui handed Director Liu a photo from the surveillance footage.","Upon seeing the photo, Director Liu was visibly shocked. He muttered, \"This can't be. My car couldn't have been on that road. I've never been there! That's not my car!\"","Fang Rui pressed, \"You said you were at home that night. Can you provide any evidence to prove it?\"","Director Liu's eyes darted nervously. He stammered, \"I'm divorced, and I live alone. There's no one to confirm my whereabouts.\"","\"Doesn't your residential complex or elevator have surveillance cameras?\"","\"No, I live in an older neighborhood. There are no cameras.\"","As Fang Rui was about to press further, someone barged into the office. It was Director Wang, the head of the hospital. He had a beer belly and a stern expression as he entered.","After understanding the situation, he said, \"Officers, Director Liu is in charge of technical matters and doesn't handle hospital management. If you want to investigate something, you should come to me. Why are you giving Director Liu such a hard time?\"","Zhang retorted, \"We're not giving him a hard time. We're just verifying his alibi.\"","\"Director Liu is an honest man. What could he possibly have to do with a crime?\"","Director Liu chimed in, \"I wasn't there. It has nothing to do with me.\"","\"Officers, let's discuss this in the meeting room,\" Director Wang said, noticing Director Liu's nervous demeanor and quickly stepping in to defuse the situation.","Fang Rui and Zhang had no choice but to follow Director Wang to the meeting room.","Director Wang busied himself making tea, but Fang Rui interrupted him and asked directly, \"Director Wang, does your hospital offer Down syndrome screening as part of prenatal checkups?\"","Director Wang insisted on serving the tea first. After sitting down on the sofa, he replied leisurely, \"Yes, it's a standard part of prenatal care. We also offer genetic screening to detect various hereditary diseases, in line with the eugenics policy.\"","\"Have any pregnant women at your hospital been diagnosed with Down syndrome in their fetuses?\"","\"Of course! The incidence rate of Down syndrome is higher than one in a thousand. We detect several cases every year, but under medical advice, most women choose to terminate the pregnancy. So the child with Down syndrome you're investigating couldn't have been born in our hospital. You should check other hospitals.\"","Director Wang assumed Fang Rui was investigating a medical malpractice case and was eager to distance the hospital from any responsibility.","Zhang said, \"But someone claimed to have seen the child at your hospital.\"","\"Who said that? Have them come forward, and I'll confront them directly.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Can you provide us with a list of the pregnant women who were diagnosed with Down syndrome?\"","\"Well... that involves patient privacy. We can't disclose that information. Officers, I've already told you, no child with Down syndrome was born in our hospital. You're wasting your time here. You should check the public hospitals. Their patient base is more diverse, and it's possible that some women didn't undergo prenatal screening or that the screening failed to detect Down syndrome, resulting in such a birth.\"","Fang Rui said, \"If you don't provide the list, we'll have no choice but to obtain a search warrant.\"","Hearing this, Director Wang immediately changed his tone. \"As responsible citizens, we have a duty to cooperate with the police in solving cases. No problem, I'll have the nurse in charge of records print out the list of pregnant women and their medical files. If you need any other data, just let us know. We'll fully cooperate.\"","Fang Rui quickly obtained the list of pregnant women, but Li Yan's name was not on it. He had previously investigated Li Yan's prenatal reports, which showed that her fetus was healthy. This proved that someone had tampered with Li Yan's prenatal records.","After leaving the hospital, Zhang said, \"Boss, Director Liu is definitely lying. He probably wasn't at home that night.\"","\"Let's check out his residential complex.\"","\"Got it.\"","Director Liu had previously worked at the First Affiliated Hospital of the City before moving to Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital. He lived in a residential complex allocated to him by the First Affiliated Hospital. Since he owned the property, he was allowed to keep it even after changing jobs.","\"Seems like Director Liu is content with a modest lifestyle,\" Zhang remarked. \"He's a director now, yet he still lives in such an old neighborhood.\"","Fang Rui noticed that the complex had surveillance cameras.","He asked the security guard at the entrance, \"Are these cameras operational?\"","\"Yes, they were installed a few months ago.\"","Fang Rui showed his badge and asked, \"Can you help us pull up the surveillance footage from the 14th?\"","\"Sure, no problem.\"","The security guard, a chatty middle-aged man, struck up a conversation with Zhang while retrieving the footage.","Zhang made up a story, \"Do you know Director Liu? I heard he's an excellent obstetrician. My relative wants to deliver at his hospital. Do you think we could schedule an appointment with him? Would a gift help?\"","\"Don't waste your time. Director Liu never accepts gifts.\"","\"He's truly a doctor with high moral standards.\"","The security guard chuckled but didn't say more.","Zhang asked, \"Am I wrong?\"","\"Not entirely. His medical skills are indeed good, but his character... well, that's another story.\"","\"Why do you say that?\"","The guard lowered his voice, \"He and his wife got divorced. Guess why? He had an affair with a woman in her twenties. If I hadn't overheard his wife arguing with him, I'd never have guessed that someone who seems so honest could be like that!\"","\"But he lives in this shabby place. He probably doesn't have much money. What would the mistress see in him?\"","\"Do you think a hospital director could be poor? Forget his salary—just think about the red envelopes and kickbacks he must receive. He may live in this dump and drive a beat-up car, but who knows? His house might be stuffed with cash.\"","Zhang asked curiously, \"How do you know he has cash hidden at home?\"","\"Isn't that how it always is in TV dramas? They look poor, but when you lift the mattress, there's a pile of cash underneath.\"","\"...\"","\"Director Liu's son did terribly in school but still went abroad to study. Where did the money come from? As soon as he divorced his wife, she also went abroad and even bought a house there. Where did that money come from?\"","\"Couldn't his wife have earned it?\"","\"His wife was a homemaker. How could she have made that much money?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Did you see Director Liu return home on the 14th?\"","Without hesitation, the guard replied, \"No!\"","\"How can you be so sure?\"","\"I haven't seen Director Liu drive back for several days. Ever since his divorce, he's been coming back less often.\" The guard winked. \"You can probably guess why.\"","Zhang asked, \"Do you know where he went?\"","The guard muttered, \"I'm just a lowly security guard. How would I know?\"","\"...\" Zhang was speechless. Didn’t you already know enough?","After returning to the bureau, they carefully reviewed the surveillance footage from the neighborhood. The footage showed that Director Liu’s car had not returned to the community."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: The Split-Brain Case: Bloodstains","paragraphs":["After obtaining a search warrant, the police inspected Liu Qiangmin's car.","When Dean Liu learned that Fang Rui and his team were going to search his car, he stood in front of the vehicle, looking bewildered, and asked, \"Officers, why are you searching my car? I haven’t violated any traffic rules recently. Shouldn’t traffic violations be handled by the traffic police?\"","\"You are suspected of being involved in a murder case.\"","\"A murder case? How is that possible?\"","The forensic team carefully examined Dean Liu's car. The scratches on the front of the car showed no signs of oxidation, indicating they were recent.","The color and texture of the car paint were similar to the traces left on the curb. Wang collected soil samples from the tires and conducted a thorough inspection of the entire vehicle.","\"Boss, look, there's blood in the trunk.\"","Near the outer edge of the trunk, there was a small drop-like bloodstain.","Dean Liu turned pale upon seeing the bloodstain. Pointing at it, he stammered, \"How did this blood get in my trunk? Officers, I didn’t do this. I have no idea how it got there.\"","Wang collected a sample of the bloodstain from the trunk.","After analysis, the blood was confirmed to belong to the victim.","Dean Liu was taken to the interrogation room.","Fang Rui placed a photo of the victim in front of him and asked again, \"Dean Liu, are you sure you don’t know this child?\"","Dean Liu carefully examined the photo of the child and shook his head. \"I don’t know him! This child looks so unusual. If I had seen him before, I would definitely remember. Officer, could someone have maliciously reported me? Tell me who it is, and I’ll confront them.\"","\"Why is there blood from this child in your trunk?\" Fang Rui pressed.","Dean Liu vehemently defended himself. \"The blood belongs to this child? I don’t know how that happened. I’ve never seen him before. And why would I want to kill a child?\"","Fang Rui continued, \"On the night of the 14th, surveillance footage captured your car at the scene where the body was dumped. But you claim you were at home that night. How do you explain that?\"","\"I... I was at home!\" Dean Liu looked panicked.","\"Dean Liu, you’d better stop lying! We’ve already investigated your neighborhood. The surveillance footage shows you never returned home that day.\"","Dean Liu hesitated for a moment before finally confessing, \"I was at home, but it was at my girlfriend’s place. Since my divorce, I rarely stay at my own house. I usually stay at my girlfriend’s.\"","\"At your girlfriend’s? Then why did you give us a false address earlier? Don’t waste our time with lies!\"","\"Officer, I’m telling the truth this time. I didn’t tell the truth earlier because she’s my mistress, a recent college graduate. I was afraid people would gossip about my personal life and ruin my reputation. That’s why I lied when you asked. I didn’t think I’d get involved in a murder case. If I had known, I would’ve told the truth from the start.\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Can your girlfriend corroborate your story?\"","\"Y-yes. I was with her the whole night.\"","\"Were you in the same room?\"","\"O-of course!\"","Zhang interjected, \"You’re not lying again, are you? Why are you stuttering?\"","\"I stutter when I’m nervous. Officer, look at my nerves. I don’t have the guts to commit a crime.\"","\"Where was your car parked on the night of the 14th?\"","\"In the underground parking lot of my girlfriend’s apartment complex. There are surveillance cameras there. You can check the footage. I drove there after work and left the next morning.\"","Liu Qiangmin’s girlfriend lived in Dongjiang Yujing, a mid-range residential complex in the city. While the property prices weren’t exorbitant, the complex was new and had excellent infrastructure.","Fang Rui sent Li and Old Zhang to the security office to retrieve the surveillance footage from the parking lot entrance, while he and Zhang went to Liu Qiangmin’s girlfriend’s apartment.","The door was opened by a very beautiful young woman wearing a loose dress, clearly several months pregnant. She was Liu Qiangmin’s girlfriend, Wang Yuqing, a 23-year-old dance major who had recently graduated from college.","\"Who are you looking for?\" Seeing Fang Rui glance at her belly, she immediately covered it and took a few steps back, eyeing them warily. \"What do you want with my baby?\"","Fang Rui and Zhang showed their badges. \"We’re police officers. We need to ask you a few questions.\"","Upon learning their identities, Wang Yuqing closed the door behind her. Standing in the doorway, she said irritably, \"I haven’t done anything wrong. Why are you here?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Can we come inside?\"","\"No, it’s not convenient. I’m alone here, and you’re two men. How can I feel safe letting you in? If you have something to say, say it here at the door.\"","Zhang pointed to the body camera. \"We’re police officers. The entire process is being recorded. What could we possibly do to you?\"","Wang Yuqing rolled her eyes. \"Who knows? Every profession has its bad apples. Better safe than sorry.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui asked, \"Do you know Liu Qiangmin, the hospital dean?\"","Wang Yuqing replied, \"Yes, he’s my boyfriend.\"","\"Where was he on the night of the 14th?\"","Wang Yuqing answered without hesitation, \"He was here, of course.\"","Zhang questioned, \"Are you sure? Can you prove it?\"","\"Ever since I got pregnant, he’s been coming here every day to take care of me. He was definitely with me that night. If you don’t believe me, check the surveillance footage!\" Wang Yuqing pointed toward the elevator exit. \"There’s a camera right there. Go take a look.\"","After leaving Wang Yuqing’s apartment, Zhang said, \"I didn’t think there was anything suspicious about her place at first, but the way she kept us out makes me think there’s something she’s hiding.\"","Fang Rui agreed. \"The moment she found out we were police, she shut the door. That suggests there’s something in her home she doesn’t want us to see.\"","Zhang speculated, \"Do you think she’s hiding billions in cash that Liu Qiangmin embezzled?\"","\"Cash is unlikely, but the interior decor might reveal Liu Qiangmin’s true financial status.\"","\"We’re not from the economic crimes division. Why would she be so scared if it’s not about money? Maybe Liu Qiangmin embezzled so much that they’re paranoid.\"","Fang Rui also found it strange. Even if the interior was luxurious, that didn’t necessarily mean Liu Qiangmin was corrupt. As the vice dean of a private hospital, it was normal for him to have a high income. Why wouldn’t they let them in?","\"Wang Yuqing’s attitude is very suspicious. When we asked about her boyfriend’s alibi, she didn’t even seem curious about what case he was involved in. If their relationship wasn’t good, why would Liu Qiangmin spend so much time with her? If it was good, why aren’t they married? And she doesn’t seem very concerned about him.\"","Li retrieved the surveillance footage. After reviewing it, they discovered that at 6:23 PM on the 14th, Liu Qiangmin’s car entered the underground parking lot. At 7:30 AM on the 15th, his car left the parking lot.","The surveillance footage captured the driver’s face. Although the image wasn’t very clear, it was evident that the person driving into the complex was indeed Liu Qiangmin."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: The Split-Brain Case: Alibi","paragraphs":["The underground parking lot had only one exit. The car couldn’t have avoided the surveillance and left the underground parking lot.","There was also surveillance at the entrance of the residential complex, which confirmed that Director Liu had driven out of the complex the next morning.","This meant that after the car entered the underground parking lot at 6:23 PM, it hadn’t left the complex that night.","The elevator in the building where Wang Yuqing lived was also equipped with surveillance, which showed that Director Liu had taken the elevator upstairs at 6:31 PM and didn’t leave until the next morning.","All of this proved that Director Liu couldn’t have driven out of the complex on the night of the 14th. So why did the car appear at the crime scene where the body was dumped?","Fang Rui held a case analysis meeting.","Li exclaimed in frustration, “How is this possible? The traffic surveillance clearly shows that the car appeared on that road. Multiple cameras captured it, and the license plate was clearly visible. The car model matches too. But the surveillance from the complex also clearly shows that the car never left. How could the car be in two places at once?”","Wang said, “The car’s trunk tested positive for the victim’s blood, which proves it was the car used to dump the body. But Director Liu has an alibi. Could someone have stolen his car to commit the crime?”","“But how did they avoid the surveillance and steal the car?”","Everyone was puzzled. They were so close to catching the killer, but suddenly, the suspect had an alibi.","“Could there be some underground passage in that complex that allows someone to secretly drive the car out?” someone asked.","Wang replied, “That underground parking lot has only one exit and one entrance, not even a ventilation window. There’s no way the car could have left without being caught on camera.”","Zhang suggested, “What if the killer modified the car? Like adding stickers or changing the license plate?”","“That’s unlikely. I’ve already taken screenshots of all the cars entering and leaving the complex on the night of the 14th, and there’s no vehicle with a similar model.”","Suddenly, Fang Rui realized why the killer had lingered at the crime scene for so long.","Fang Rui analyzed, “This white car is a very common model. It would be easy to buy an identical one. Could the car at the crime scene be a decoy, with the killer swapping the license plate for Director Liu’s? The killer stayed at the crime scene for over half an hour, which is highly unusual. It’s possible he was deliberately waiting for witnesses to see his car.”","Zhang suddenly understood, “I thought the killer was being careless, letting witnesses see his car and even hitting the curb, damaging the paint and leaving obvious marks. But he was actually trying to mislead us.”","Wang said, “But there was blood in the trunk of Director Liu’s car.”","Mu Mian added, “The blood in the trunk was in a dripping pattern. If it had gotten there from the body being placed in the trunk, it wouldn’t look like that. Also, when we found the victim’s body, there was no blood on his hat. This suggests that someone might have deliberately dripped blood into the trunk.”","Fang Rui said, “So the killer likely had access to the car. Let’s carefully review the parking lot surveillance and see if we can spot any suspicious individuals.”","Lin Sen analyzed, “If the killer wanted to frame Director Liu, why did he take the victim’s brain and leave that symbol?”","Fang Rui replied, “Could he be trying to lead us to investigate Director Liu?”","Zhang speculated, “Could it be that Director Liu embezzled a lot of public funds, and the killer couldn’t stand it, so he used a child’s body to lead us to investigate him?”","Mu Mian said, “I don’t think it’s about embezzlement.”","“Why are you so sure?”","Mu Mian explained, “My intuition tells me that this killer is someone with a strong medical ambition. He’s not doing this for money. I suspect Director Liu might have done something unethical in his profession.”","After the meeting, Fang Rui and Mu Mian stayed behind in the conference room for a private discussion.","Fang Rui said, “The chief had someone tail Chen Xue, but she hasn’t shown any unusual behavior recently, nor has she met with any suspicious individuals.”","Fang Rui had already reported to the chief that Chen Xue might be an undercover agent. The chief thought it was unlikely, but just to be safe, he assigned two newly transferred officers to follow her.","Mu Mian said, “I sent Chen Xue a link with a Trojan virus, and my hacker friend infiltrated her phone and computer, but we didn’t find any useful clues. Chen Xue’s inner world is quite rich—she loves watching dramas and gossip news. There’s no one suspicious in her contacts either.”","Mu Mian had been monitoring Chen Xue’s phone for several days, but after work, all she did was call Zhang and watch dramas or gossip news. There was nothing unusual.","They couldn’t help but wonder if they had been wrong to suspect Chen Xue. But there were too many coincidences.","When Mu Mian returned to the office, Chen Xue teased her, “Mian Mian, why have you been spending so much time with Fang Rui lately?”","“Because he’s my boyfriend. You and Officer Zhang used to do the same.”","“Did we?”","“You two were always together.”","“Hahaha, I guess we set a bad example.”","Example? Mu Mian suddenly realized that much of her understanding of love came from observing Chen Xue and Zhang’s interactions. They had indeed set an example for her.","Fang Rui investigated Director Liu’s detailed background. He had worked at a public hospital for over a decade before switching to Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital. His medical skills were excellent, so he quickly rose to the position of vice president.","To Fang Rui’s surprise, Director Liu had once been Chen Hui’s mentor. The nurses said they had a good relationship, and Director Liu held Chen Hui in high regard.","Fang Rui obtained a search warrant and conducted a search of Director Liu’s girlfriend, Wang Yuqing’s home.","When a large group of police officers showed up at her door, Wang Yuqing looked annoyed. “Officers, haven’t I already testified for Director Liu? What are you doing here? This is my home. Even if Director Liu did something wrong, it has nothing to do with me. You have no right to barge into my house.”","“Here’s the search warrant.”","Seeing the search warrant, Wang Yuqing grew nervous. She said, “Officers, my house is a bit messy. If you’re looking for something, I can help you find it. There’s no need for you to come in.”","“Please cooperate with our work.”","Wang Yuqing eventually let them in.","The interior of the house was simply decorated, with nothing extravagant. The place wasn’t messy either; it was quite clean. There were no luxury items or anything suspicious.","“Why were you so adamant about keeping us out?” Zhang questioned Wang Yuqing.","“I... I have social anxiety. I don’t like people coming into my home.”","It was a three-bedroom, one-living-room apartment with two bedrooms and a study. Fang Rui noticed that both bedrooms had beds, and both showed signs of being slept in.","“Do you sleep in separate rooms?”","“Yes. I’m four months pregnant, so it’s not convenient to share a bed.”","Fang Rui found that the second bedroom was Director Liu’s room. They searched the room but found nothing suspicious.","“What are these pills?” Someone found several bottles of medicine in Director Liu’s drawer, labeled in English.","Wang Yuqing took the bottles and examined them, then shook her head. “I don’t know what these are. He doesn’t seem to have any illnesses. Why would he be taking these?”","Fang Rui recognized one of the bottles. Lin Qianjie’s drawer had the same pills—they were for erectile dysfunction.","“Take all these pills back with us.”","Zhang tried to get some information out of Wang Yuqing. “Director Liu is divorced now, and you’re pregnant with his child. Why aren’t you married to him?” Zhang noticed that Wang Yuqing wasn’t wearing a ring, which suggested that Director Liu had no intention of marrying her.","Wang Yuqing rolled her eyes. “Why are you, a police officer, so nosy?”","“...I’m just trying to advise you to see through this scumbag’s true colors and not waste your time on him. You’re pregnant, and he still won’t marry you. Isn’t he just using you as a baby-making machine?”","Perhaps these words struck a nerve with Wang Yuqing. Her expression changed slightly, and she retorted angrily at Zhang, \"What's it to you? I'm happy to be a baby-making machine, is that so wrong?\"","\"...\"","Zhang felt that Wang Yuqing probably didn’t like Director Liu. But that was understandable—how could a young girl like her be interested in a middle-aged man? Was it his age? Moreover, there were rumors that the man might not even be capable!","After searching the place, they found nothing related to the deceased and had no choice but to leave.","Before leaving, Fang Rui glanced at Wang Yuqing's belly. A strange suspicion crossed his mind: if Director Liu was taking potency pills, could the child in her belly really be his? Would it even be a healthy child?","Fang Rui asked, \"Do you go for regular prenatal checkups?\"","\"Of course. The baby's father works at Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital, so he arranges everything perfectly for each checkup.\"","\"Is your baby healthy?\"","\"Absolutely. This baby is very healthy.\"","Fang Rui found her response a bit odd. Shouldn’t she have said, \"My baby is healthy\"? Why did she say, \"This baby\"?"]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: The Split-Brain Case: Surrogacy","paragraphs":["The surveillance footage from the parking lot of Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital did not capture any suspicious individuals approaching Director Liu's car, and the underground parking lot of Dongjiang Yujing Residential Complex was not equipped with surveillance cameras.","Fang Rui suspected that the perpetrator likely tampered with Director Liu's car trunk in the underground parking lot of the residential complex.","However, after reviewing the surveillance footage, no suspects involved in framing Director Liu were identified.","Director Liu was known for his low-profile and mild temperament, rarely getting into conflicts with others, let alone making enemies. Investigations into his social connections also failed to uncover any suspects.","Most of the people he knew and interacted with were from the medical field, and many of his friends were surgeons. These individuals were skilled in performing surgical procedures and had the capability to cut open a skull and remove half of a deceased person's brain.","Since Director Liu had a solid alibi, the police had no choice but to release him.","Fang Rui still found him suspicious, so he assigned Zhang and Dong, who often worked in the field, to keep an eye on him, also ensuring his safety.","The medications found in Director Liu's drawer were sent for testing.","After the test results came out, Mu Mian said, \"These medications are for treating issues related to sexual performance. If these are his, it's likely that he has lost his fertility.\"","Fang Rui looked at the test report in surprise and asked, \"Then how did Director Liu get Wang Yuqing pregnant?\"","Mu Mian sighed, \"Fang Rui, you're being dense. Of course, it was through surgery. Artificial insemination can also result in pregnancy.\"","\"But he already has a son. The success rate of artificial insemination isn't high, so why would he spend a fortune to have another child?\"","Mu Mian looked at Fang Rui and blinked.","\"What is it?\"","Mu Mian made a bitter face, \"I can't answer such a complicated question.\"","Wang, who was standing nearby, chimed in, \"Well, no wealthy man would ever complain about having too many sons. The more children, the better.\"","\"...\"","Fang Rui investigated Wang Yuqing's background. She came from a poor family and often took on part-time jobs during college, but she maintained her integrity and earned money through legitimate means. Her classmates and friends described her as having strong morals and self-esteem, making it unlikely that she would interfere in someone else's marriage.","Although Wang Yuqing had visited Anqi Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital multiple times for prenatal checkups, the nurses and doctors there were unaware that she was Director Liu's mistress. They also had no idea how Wang Yuqing and Director Liu had met.","Fang Rui contacted Wang Yuqing's college roommate over the phone. She was Wang Yuqing's closest friend, but they had rarely been in touch over the past six months.","Fang Rui asked, \"Do you know about Wang Yuqing and Liu Qiangmin's relationship?\"","\"Who is Liu Qiangmin? I've never heard Yuqing mention him.\"","\"He's Wang Yuqing's boyfriend, and she's pregnant with his child. Didn't you know about this?\"","\"Yuqing is pregnant? That can't be!\"","\"You weren't aware of this?\"","\"We haven't been in touch much recently. Six months ago, Yuqing told me she found a job that only required her to work for ten months, and she would earn 600,000 yuan. I thought she had been scammed and advised her not to take the job. After that, she stopped contacting me. Could it be that she became someone's mistress?\"","After hearing Wang Yuqing's roommate's account and considering Wang Yuqing's strange behavior, Fang Rui began to suspect that Wang Yuqing might not be Director Liu's mistress but rather a surrogate mother.","This would explain why Wang Yuqing didn't let them into her house—she was likely afraid they would realize she and Director Liu weren't in a romantic relationship.","She never referred to the child in her womb as \"my child,\" possibly because the child was only being carried by her and didn't belong to her.","Fang Rui invited Wang Yuqing to the interrogation room.","Wang Yuqing sat on the chair, visibly annoyed, and said, \"Officer, I'm pregnant. On a rainy day like this, couldn't you have come to my place to ask your questions? Why drag me here? If something happens to me and I lose the baby, can you afford to take responsibility?\"","Fang Rui asked, \"What is your relationship with Liu Qiangmin?\"","Wang Yuqing replied irritably, \"Officer, have you lost your memory? I've told you many times, he's my boyfriend.\"","Fang Rui continued, \"Is the child in your womb yours?\"","Wang Yuqing's expression changed slightly, but she quickly masked it by brushing her hair and rolling her eyes at Fang Rui.","\"Officer, why are you asking such stupid questions? The child is in my womb. If it's not mine, whose could it be?\"","\"Then please accompany us to the hospital. We need to conduct a paternity test to determine if you and the fetus are biologically related.\"","\"Officer, you have no right to demand this from me. It violates my privacy.\"","\"You are suspected of illegal surrogacy. We are asking for a paternity test to gather evidence. You are obligated to cooperate.\"","Wang Yuqing turned pale and became visibly flustered. After hesitating for a few seconds, she finally chose to confess.","\"Officer, I admit it. I am a surrogate for Liu Qiangmin. I don't know who the child's mother is, but the doctors implanted the fertilized egg into my body through surgery. To better care for the child, Liu Qiangmin bought me an apartment, and he lived with me to take care of me.\"","\"You're so young. There are many ways to earn money. Why did you agree to something like this?\"","\"I had no choice. My family is poor, and my father is sick. We needed a large sum of money for his treatment. I couldn't just watch my father die!","When I was at my wit's end, I saw his job posting online. I thought, compared to selling myself, carrying someone else's child wasn't so bad. After all, women are meant to have children.\"","\"Liu Qiangmin already has a son. Why did he need you to be a surrogate?\"","\"He told me his wife cheated on him, and his child isn't biologically his. He desperately wanted a child of his own, but he's infertile. That's why he asked me to be a surrogate. That's also why I dared to live with him. Since he has fertility issues, he couldn't do anything to me.\"","\"How does he treat the child in your womb?\"","\"Very well. He takes me to his hospital for prenatal checkups every two weeks, terrified that something might happen to the child. He also bought me a lot of nutritional supplements, saying I must give birth to a healthy child this time.\"","\"This time? Has he had other surrogates before?\"","\"I'm not entirely sure, but I think so. He mentioned that this time he would personally supervise me to ensure there were no mistakes.\"","\"Is he very worried about the child's well-being?\"","\"He seems to have some mental issues. He's extremely anxious about this child. He repeatedly emphasized that I must follow his dietary plan and wouldn't let me go out casually.\"","\"Does he exhibit any other unusual behavior?\"","\"Not really. He's a decent person, just a bit controlling and overly concerned about the child. But that's understandable. He's infertile, and after going through the trouble of artificial insemination, he naturally wants to treasure this child.\""]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: The Split-Brain Case: Car Accident","paragraphs":["After leaving the interrogation room, Fang Rui and Mu Mian discussed the case.","Fang Rui said, \"Could it be that the killer went through so much trouble to frame Director Liu just to let us know that Director Liu was involved in illegal surrogacy?\"","Mu Mian speculated, \"Could he be using this child for some kind of experiment? A typical pregnant woman wouldn’t need to undergo such frequent prenatal checkups.\"","Fang Rui arranged for Wang Yuqing to have a prenatal checkup to see if there were any issues with the fetus. He also ordered a paternity test to determine whether the child was Director Liu's.","Under Fang Rui's urging, the hospital expedited the results.","The prenatal checkup results showed that the child was healthy, and the Down syndrome screening came back negative.","However, the paternity test revealed that the child was not Director Liu's; there was no blood relation between the fetus and Director Liu.","Fang Rui decided to bring Director Liu back for questioning to find out what was going on.","Since the night before last, Typhoon \"Little Raccoon\" had made landfall in Jiangzhou City, bringing continuous heavy rain. The city was shrouded in a gray haze, and the streets were flooded.","Zhang and Dong had been staking out Director Liu for two days and a night. After being released from the police station, Director Liu had returned to work at the hospital and maintained a routine between the hospital and his home.","Zhang couldn’t help but admire Director Liu's dedication to his work.","Zhang quipped, \"How does a workaholic like him even have time to have an affair?\"","Dong replied, \"That’s not unusual. Competence and character don’t always go hand in hand. A lot of highly capable people lack moral integrity. We need to look at this objectively.\"","\"True, that makes sense,\" Zhang conceded.","Dong then teased, \"Zhang Qiang, when are you getting married? I’m waiting to drink at your wedding banquet.\"","\"Soon, probably by the end of the year. You’ll have to be one of my groomsmen. I plan to have a whole squad of groomsmen to make the wedding lively.\"","\"You’re such a show-off.\"","\"Well, you only get married once. Might as well make it a grand celebration.\"","\"Don’t worry, we’ll make sure it’s a blast. Wang is even more of a show-off than you, but lately, he’s been quiet and not as lively. He’s matured a lot. I think he’s nursing a broken heart!\"","\"Yeah, seeing Wang like this breaks my heart. Without him chattering away, the world feels too quiet.\"","After Chen Shu's death, Wang had been in a slump for a while, but he quickly regained his drive and threw himself into his work. However, he no longer enjoyed chatting with others and had lost his sense of humor.","Dong glanced out the car window. \"The rain seems to have lightened up a bit. Keep an eye out while I go grab some boxed meals. It’ll be rush hour soon, and it’ll get crowded.\"","\"Go ahead. I’ll call you if anything happens. Oh, and grab me a bottle of water while you’re at it.\"","\"Got it.\"","Fang Rui called Zhang to instruct him to bring Director Liu back for questioning, but Zhang’s phone kept going unanswered.","Fang Rui then called Dong, Zhang’s partner. Fortunately, Dong answered almost immediately.","\"Captain Fang, what’s up?\"","\"Why isn’t Zhang answering his phone?\"","\"I’m out buying boxed meals. Zhang’s still staking out the hospital entrance. He probably has his phone on silent and didn’t hear it. I’ll be back in the car soon. Do you need to relay something to him?\"","The sound of raindrops hitting the pavement created a chaotic, irritating noise.","\"Bring Liu Qiangmin back. We’ve uncovered new leads and need to question him.\"","\"Got it. We’ll bring him back right away.\"","Fang Rui and Mu Mian were still discussing the case when Zhang called. \"Boss, the suspect is likely...\"","Mu Mian leaned in to listen, but Zhang’s voice abruptly cut off, replaced by a loud \"bang.\"","\"Zhang, what’s going on over there?\" Fang Rui asked anxiously.","\"Officer Zhang, can you hear me?\"","The call ended with a series of beeps.","Mu Mian said, \"That sounded like a car crash...\"","Both of them felt a sense of foreboding.","Fang Rui called Dong again, and the call connected quickly. Fang Rui and Mu Mian breathed a sigh of relief. If Dong could answer, Zhang was probably fine too.","Fang Rui asked, \"What’s happening over there? Why did Zhang hang up on me?\"","\"Captain Fang, Zhang just texted me saying Liu Qiangmin suddenly drove away from the hospital. He was worried about losing him, so he followed in his car.\"","\"Where is he now?\"","\"I’m not sure. I’ve hailed a taxi and am trying to catch up to Zhang.\"","The sense of unease grew stronger. Fang Rui’s instincts told him that something had likely happened to Zhang. He kept calling Zhang’s phone, but all he heard was the cold, automated voice.","\"The number you have dialed is currently unavailable. Please try again later...\"","Fang Rui contacted a friend in the traffic police, who informed him that a major accident had occurred near Jiangzhou University Second Affiliated Hospital, leaving two drivers seriously injured.","The friend sent Fang Rui photos of the accident.","Fang Rui froze when he saw the familiar car—it was Zhang’s. The other car, which had been completely wrecked, belonged to Director Liu.","Both of them had been involved in the crash.","Fang Rui and Mu Mian were about to inform Chen Xue when her phone rang.","\"Hello, are you Zhang Qiang’s girlfriend?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Zhang Qiang has been in a car accident and is currently in critical condition at the First Affiliated Hospital of the City. Please come as soon as possible.\"","The words seemed to cast a spell, instantly petrifying Chen Xue. She stood frozen, unable to think or respond.","\"Can you hear me?\"","\"Ma’am, are you there?\"","When no response came, the person on the other end said to someone nearby, \"This call isn’t going through. Let’s try the next one.\"","Mu Mian spoke into the phone, \"We understand. We’ll be there right away.\"","\"Please hurry!\"","\"Chen Xue, let’s go to the hospital,\" Mu Mian said, her eyes reddening. She tried to reassure her, \"Officer Zhang probably just had a minor accident. The roads have been terrible with all this rain. Accidents happen.\"","Chen Xue remained silent.","Mu Mian couldn’t read Chen Xue’s expression—or perhaps there was no expression to read. But she could feel that Chen Xue was drowning in sorrow, overwhelmed to the point of suffocation.","Mu Mian thought for a moment, then reached out and hugged Chen Xue tightly. \"Chen Xue, Officer Zhang needs you right now. You can’t lose your composure.\"","Chen Xue clung to Mu Mian like a drowning person grasping at a lifeline. \"Mian Mian, tell me Zhang Qiang won’t die.\"","\"The doctor didn’t say his condition is critical. He’ll be fine,\" Mu Mian said, her voice choked with emotion. \"It’s probably like last time—just a minor injury, like a sprained ankle.\"","\"Mian Mian, I never thought he could die.\"","Mu Mian whispered, \"Everyone dies eventually. But Officer Zhang won’t die so soon. He’s a Libra, and Libras have been having good luck lately.\"","\"Mian Mian, astrology is nonsense. But you’re a genius. If you say he won’t die, then he won’t die.\""]}]);
